\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I will not back down\u8217\'20\'19: Biden vows executive action if Senate cannot pass climate bill \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly in New York, Chris Stein and Adam Gabbatt (earlier) \par \uc2 5,801 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 July 2022\par 20:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President urges Senate to pass legislation amid Manchin oppositionSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 After more than a year of negotiations, was today the beginning of the end for Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 long-running effort to pass a spending bill improving America\u8217\'20\'19s social services? It very well may have been, after Senator Joe Manchin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-biden-israel-saudi-arabia-middle-east-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62d1760a8f08bee7e09c6a6e#block-62d1760a8f08bee7e09c6a6e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nixed provisions to raise taxes and fight climate change}}}\uc2 , and President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  called on Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-biden-israel-saudi-arabia-middle-east-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62d1b8a38f08b970599b728a#block-62d1b8a38f08b970599b728a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to pass a narrow agreement that would lower drug costs and extend health insurance subsidies}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 * Democrats in the House passed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-biden-israel-saudi-arabia-middle-east-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62d1a0248f08b970599b715b#block-62d1a0248f08b970599b715b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-biden-israel-saudi-arabia-middle-east-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62d1a3c58f08b970599b7192#block-62d1a3c58f08b970599b7192"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bills}}}\uc2  to preserve access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, but they are unlikely to pass the Senate due to Republican opposition.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-biden-israel-saudi-arabia-middle-east-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d1b1698f08b970599b7242#block-62d1b1698f08b970599b7242"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden fist bumped}}}\uc2  Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman after arriving in the country, drawing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-biden-israel-saudi-arabia-middle-east-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d1bdaf8f08bee7e09c6e83#block-62d1bdaf8f08bee7e09c6e83"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a rebuke from The Washington Post\u8217\'20\'19s publisher}}}\uc2 . Jamal Khashoggi, who was murdered in an operation US intelligence concluded the crown prince approved, wrote for the newspaper. The president later said he brought up Khashoggi\u8217\'20\'19s murder with MBS.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2 , a former top advisor to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-biden-israel-saudi-arabia-middle-east-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d17fa38f086e8f93696f79#block-62d17fa38f086e8f93696f79"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined a plea deal from federal prosecutors}}}\uc2  over his refusal to cooperate with the January 6 committee.\par \par \uc2 * A House committee announced it would take up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-biden-israel-saudi-arabia-middle-east-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d183058f08b970599b6f7c#block-62d183058f08b970599b6f7c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Democratic proposal to ban assault weapons}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * A deposition of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his children {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-biden-israel-saudi-arabia-middle-east-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d18cb58f086e8f93697089#block-62d18cb58f086e8f93697089"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was postponed}}}\uc2  due to the death of his first wife \uc2 Ivana Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * A Georgia district attorney has warned some Republicans lawmakers in the state that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-biden-israel-saudi-arabia-middle-east-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d194158f086e8f93697102#block-62d194158f086e8f93697102"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they could be indicted}}}\uc2  for their role in helping \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  overturn the results of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 In Riyadh, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was also asked about Joe Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s apparent torpedoing of Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 attempt to pass spending legislation targeting the climate crisis, healthcare and other party priorities before the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Asked for \u8220\'20\'1Cyour message to those Americans right now who were looking for that relief that would have a wide impact as it affects the climate and energy specifically\u8221\'20\'1D, the president said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going away. I\u8217\'20\'19m using every power I have as president to continue to fulfill my pledge to move toward dealing with global warming.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On his way out of the short and slightly testy briefing, Biden was asked if he thought Manchin, a West Virginia Democrat who has nonetheless stymied his party\u8217\'20\'19s agenda over and over again, had been \u8220\'20\'1Cnegotiating in good faith\u8221\'20\'1D over the spending deal and its climate-related provisions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t negotiate with Joe Manchin,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s true that Manchin has been talking to \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  of New York, the Democratic Senate majority leader, this time.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s also true that Manchin has an outsized influence on Democratic policy priorities in the 50-50 Senate and has been at the centre of almost every legislative drama since Biden took back the White House.\par \par \uc2 In their book Peril, about the end of Trump and the beginning of Biden, Bob Woodward and Robert Costa of the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  devote considerable space to Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s machinations around the $1.9tn Covid relief package Biden got through in March 2021.\par \par \uc2 At one point, they write, Biden told the senator: \u8220\'20\'1CJoe, please don\u8217\'20\'19t kill my bill.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He didn\u8217\'20\'19t. That time.\par \par \uc2 More:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-funding-tax-hikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden pledges executive action after Joe Manchin scuppers climate agenda}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 U.S. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  attends a news conference in Jeddah, Saudi Arabia on July 15, 2022. Photograph: Evelyn Hockstein/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Speaking from Jeddah, Saudi Arabia, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said he brought up the murder of Jamal Khashoggi when he met with Saudi crown prince \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2  earlier today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C I made my view crystal clear. I said very straightforwardly, for an American president to be silent on an issue of human rights, is this consistent... with who we are and who I am? I will always stand up for our values,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Asked how the crown prince responded, Biden replied, \u8220\'20\'1CHe basically said that he he was not personally responsible for it. I indicated I thought he was\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The president has previously said he wanted to make Saudi Arabia a \u8220\'20\'1Cpariah state\u8221\'20\'1D for the murder, and was asked if he wanted to take those words back. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t regret anything that I said. What happened to Khashoggi was outrageous,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 committee sets prime-time hearing for Thursday\par \par \uc2 The House committee investigating the January 6 insurrection has announced its next hearing for 8 pm eastern time on Thursday, July 21.\par \par \uc2 enltrJust in: Jan. 6 committee formally announces eighth hearing on Thursday, July 21 at 8p ET\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1548019782481428491?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The lawmakers are expected to explore what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was doing as the Capitol was attacked.\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: Jan. 6 committee member \uc2 Elaine Luria\uc2  on CNN confirms {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GuardianUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GuardianUS}}}\uc2  reporting that she and \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  will lead the eighth hearing, taking place in prime time next week, about how Trump did nothing during the 187mins of the Capitol attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1547421731748552704?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 The publisher of \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2  has condemned \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s fist bump with Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s Crown Prince \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2 , whom US intelligence concluded ordered the operation that resulted in the murder of Jamal Khasshogi, a contributor to the newspaper.\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/l2EDKZOLsS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/l2EDKZOLsS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kristine Coratti Kelly (@kriscoratti) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kriscoratti/status/1548021942199787522?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden, who is visiting Saudi Arabia, will address the press in about 20 minutes, according to CNN. The event was not previously scheduled.\par \par \uc2 enltrIn a last minute addition to his schedule, President Biden will address reporters at 3:30 ET/10:30 P.M. local following his meeting with the Saudi crown prince.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1548021438036135936?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden calls for Senate to pass bill lowering drug costs, vows executive action on climate change\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has just issued a statement calling on the Senate to pass legislation that would lower prescription drug prices and extend health insurance subsidies, while vowing to sign executive orders meant to fight climate change. The announcement comes after Democratic senator Joe Manchin said yesterday he would not support legislation intended to curb America\u8217\'20\'19s carbon emissions, nor new tax proposals to offset its costs. His statement was the latest complication for Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 long-running efforts to pass a major spending bill despite their narrow majority in Congress, where they can afford to lose no votes in the Senate and few in the House. While the initial proposals for the bill released last year showed it would address a host of the party\u8217\'20\'19s priorities, it is now set to be much narrower in scope.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/07/15/statement-by-president-joe-biden-5/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s statement}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Action on climate change and clean energy remains more urgent than ever.\par \par \uc2 So let me be clear: if the Senate will not move to tackle the climate crisis and strengthen our domestic clean energy industry, I will take strong executive action to meet this moment. My actions will create jobs, improve our energy security, bolster domestic manufacturing and supply chains, protect us from oil and gas price hikes in the future, and address climate change. I will not back down: the opportunity to create jobs and build a clean energy future is too important to relent.\par \par \uc2 Health care is also critical. After decades of fierce opposition from powerful special interests, Democrats have come together, beaten back the pharmaceutical industry and are prepared to give Medicare the power to negotiate lower drug prices and to prevent an increase in health insurance premiums for millions of families with coverage under the Affordable Care Act. Families all over the nation will sleep easier if Congress takes this action. The Senate should move forward, pass it before the August recess, and get it to my desk so I can sign it.=\par \par \uc2 This will not only lower the cost of prescription drugs and health care for families, it will reduce the deficit and help fight inflation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is making his controversial visit to Saudi Arabia, with an increase in oil production seen as the goal. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/bethan-mckernan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bethan McKernan}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Three years after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  vowed to make {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/saudiarabia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saudi Arabia}}}\uc2  a pariah state over the assassination of a prominent dissident, the US president greeted Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman with a fist bump as his administration attempts to reset relations and stabilise global oil markets.\par \par \uc2 Whereas \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was personally welcomed to the conservative Gulf kingdom on his first presidential visit by King Salman, Biden was met on the tarmac on Friday evening by the governor of Mecca and the Saudi ambassador to the US in a subdued ceremony before travelling to the city\u8217\'20\'19s al-Salam palace, where he held talks with the 86-year-old king and his powerful heir, \uc2 Prince Mohammed\uc2 , before a working meeting.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/15/fist-bumps-as-joe-biden-arrives-to-reset-ties-with-pariah-saudi-arabia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fist bumps as Joe Biden arrives to reset ties with \u8216\'20\'18pariah\u8217\'20\'19 Saudi Arabia}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Last week, we learned that \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , who\u8217\'20\'19s the Republican nominee for a Senate seat in Georgia, lied to his own campaign team about how many children he had. This is not his only misstep, but the longtime friend of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continues to have the support of Georgia Republicans. The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Jonathan Freedland speaks to Roger Sollenberger of the Daily Beast about why Walker might prove a fatal blow for the GOP in November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 The passage of two bills preserving the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to temporarily buoy Democrats, even if both bills are extremely unlikely to pass the Senate.\par \par \uc2 One thing is clear though: the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is not going away.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democrats-eager-to-talk-about-abortion-in-campaign-ads-as-gop-shies-away-from-issue-11657886401?st=8ej7jkclsqtpxcj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Wall Street Journal}}}\uc2 , Democrats are \u8220\'20\'1Cincreasingly talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their midterm campaign advertising,\u8221\'20\'1D while Republicans are shying away from the issue.\par \par \uc2 In June the Supreme Court reversed the Roe v Wade ruling which enshrined the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in federal law.\par \par \uc2 On Friday almost all House Republicans voted against the bills which would restore and protect access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 but the GOP is out of step with Americans, a majority of whom {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2022/06/13/about-six-in-ten-americans-say-abortion-should-be-legal-in-all-or-most-cases-2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 think \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  should be legal}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the November mid-term elections, Democrats seem to be tying Republicans to the reversal of Roe v Wade, the WSJ reported:\par \par \uc2 [An analysis] of broadcast and national cable data from the ad-tracking firm AdImpact shows more than a third of all spots aired by Democrats and their allies in congressional and gubernatorial campaigns from July 1-12 have mentioned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/inflation-gets-a-starring-role-in-gop-congressional-campaign-ads-11648373402?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are focusing their ads on inflation}}}\uc2 , which voters have consistently cited as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/inflation-is-taking-biggest-toll-on-nonwhite-voters-wsj-poll-shows-11647255601?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their top concern}}}\uc2  heading into November\u8217\'20\'19s elections. Less than 3% of all spots run by GOP candidates and their allies during that period included the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue, the analysis showed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Second bill preserving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights passes House\par \par \uc2 A second bill protecting the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has passed the US House.\par \par \uc2 HR 8297, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/house-bill/8297/text?r=1&s=1\"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ensuring Access to \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Act of 2022}}}\uc2 , passed by 223 votes to 205 no votes. Three Republicans did not vote.\par \par \uc2 The bill would prohibit restrictions on out-of-state travel for the purpose of obtaining an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  service.\par \par \uc2 Like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-biden-israel-saudi-arabia-middle-east-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d1a0248f08b970599b715b#block-62d1a0248f08b970599b715b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HR 8296}}}\uc2 , the bill is likely to fail in the Senate, where there is not enough support for either bill to survive the 60-vote filibuster threshold. There are 50 Republicans in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 enltr223-205: House passes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access legislation prohibiting restrictions blocking out of state travel to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in response to Supreme Court overturning Roe v. Wade.3 Republicans joined all Democrats in voting Yes.Ensuring Access to \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Act now heads to Senate. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/a3nAuTLnvp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/a3nAuTLnvp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Craig Caplan (@CraigCaplan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CraigCaplan/status/1548000819077062656?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.21pm BST\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights bill passes the House\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2  has approved a law which would preserve access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide at the federal level \u8211\'20\'13 but the bill is still expected to fail in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 HR 8296, the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act of 2022, passed the House by 219 yes votes to 210 no votes. Two members did not vote.\par \par \uc2 The law would preserve access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after the Supreme Court struck down Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 The bill is expected to fail in the Senate, however. In May {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/05/11/politics/senate-abortion-rights-vote-roe-v-wade/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a vote in the Senate failed}}}\uc2 , with Joe Manchin, the Democrat who has repeatedly blocked his own party\u8217\'20\'19s legislative efforts, joining Republicans to vote the bill down by 51 votes to 49.\par \par \uc2 The House will now consider another \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights bill, HR8297 \u8211\'20\'13 the Ensuring Access to \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Act of 2022. That bill would protect individual\u8217\'20\'19s right to travel for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Democratic congresswomen hold a news conference on Friday in support of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills. Photograph: Jonathan Ernst/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legislative agenda is reeling after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-biden-israel-saudi-arabia-middle-east-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62d1760a8f08bee7e09c6a6e#block-62d1760a8f08bee7e09c6a6e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a crucial senator said he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t support proposals to address climate change or raise taxes to pay for it}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-biden-israel-saudi-arabia-middle-east-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d186598f08bee7e09c6b94#block-62d186598f08bee7e09c6b94"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats in the House are moving to pass a measure to codify \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here is what has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2 , a former top advisor to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-biden-israel-saudi-arabia-middle-east-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d17fa38f086e8f93696f79#block-62d17fa38f086e8f93696f79"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined a plea deal from federal prosecutors}}}\uc2  over his refusal to cooperate with the January 6 committee.\par \par \uc2 * A House committee announced it would take up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-biden-israel-saudi-arabia-middle-east-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d183058f08b970599b6f7c#block-62d183058f08b970599b6f7c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Democratic proposal to ban assault weapons}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * A deposition of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his children {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-biden-israel-saudi-arabia-middle-east-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d18cb58f086e8f93697089#block-62d18cb58f086e8f93697089"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was postponed}}}\uc2  due to the death of his first wife \uc2 Ivana Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * A Georgia district attorney has warned some Republicans lawmakers in the state that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-biden-israel-saudi-arabia-middle-east-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d194158f086e8f93697102#block-62d194158f086e8f93697102"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they could be indicted}}}\uc2  for their role in helping \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  overturn the results of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 House lawmakers have taken to the floor to speak for and against a proposal from the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leadership to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide.\par \par \uc2 The speeches split along party lines, with Republicans decrying the bill and Democrats casting it as a necessary response to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision last month overturning Roe v. Wade and handing states the power to ban the procedure outright.\par \par \uc2 California Democrat Barbara Lee condemned Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 proposals to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, asking, \u8220\'20\'1CWhat in the world is this?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. Barbara Lee (D-CA) directly addresses Republicans during debate on bill protecting right to travel for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re trying to take away people\u8217\'20\'19s right to travel. What in the world is this? Is this America? \u8230\'20\'26 They come for me today, they\u8217\'20\'19re coming for you tomorrow.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Qkv7at6h9m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Qkv7at6h9m}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1547979276653277185?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Brian Mast\uc2 , a Republican from Florida, put a $20 bill on the table and said to Democrats, \u8220\'20\'1CAny one of you or your colleagues wants to speak up and tell us when life begins, it\u8217\'20\'19s sitting here for you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrPelosi and her allies are pushing for bills that would allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the very last moment before birth.\par \par \uc2 I asked if they can tell me when a life begins, but I was met with silence. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xytK5yUYza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xytK5yUYza}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Brian Mast\uc2  (@RepBrianMast) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepBrianMast/status/1547981820351881216?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Georgia district attorney has sent \u8220\'20\'1Ctarget\u8221\'20\'1D letters to prominent Republicans in the state, warning them they could face indictments for their attempt to help \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  overturn the results of the 2020 election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.yahoo.com/exclusive-fulton-county-da-sends-target-letters-to-trump-allies-in-georgia-investigation-152517469.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Yahoo! News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , the Democratic district attorney for Fulton county, which includes the capital and largest city Atlanta, has sent the letters to Republicans including Burt Jones, a state senator who is standing as Georgia governor \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate in this year\u8217\'20\'19s election, and David Shafer, chair of the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican party, as well as state senator Brandon Beach.\par \par \uc2 According to the report:\par \par \uc2 Jones and Shafer were among those who participate in a closed-door meeting at the state Capitol on Dec. 14, 2020, in which 16 Georgia Republicans selected themselves as the electors for the state, although they had no legal basis for doing so. Shafer, according to a source who was present, presided over the meeting, conducting it as though it was an official proceeding, in which those present voted themselves as the bona fide electors in Georgia \u8212\'20\'14 and then signed their names to a declaration to that effect that was sent to the National Archives.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with \uc2 Yahoo\uc2 ! News, Willis said she was also considering asking \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to testify before the grand jury investigating the plot.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 A colleague of Indiana doctor Caitlin Bernard, who provided the 10-year-old girl from Ohio with an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after her rape, has written {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/07/15/opinion/doctors-roe-v-wade-ohio-10-year-old.html?referringSource=articleShare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an op-ed in The New York Times}}}\uc2  about how the episode, and the downfall of Roe v. Wade, has affected reproductive health.\par \par \uc2 Tracey A. Wilkinson, an assistant professor of pediatrics at Indiana University School of Medicine, wrote:\par \par \uc2 Political attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers are, of course, nothing new. And that\u8217\'20\'19s not all that providers and their staff face: They have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/violence-against-abortion-clinics-like-planned-parenthood-hit-a-record-high-last-year-doctors-say-its-getting-worse/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 targeted}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2135360"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 harassed}}}\uc2  and in some cases even {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2015/11/29/us/30abortion-clinic-violence.html?mtrref=www.google.com&gwh=947E25DB2C424C4B851ECB420CCAE89B&gwt=regi&assetType=REGIWALL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 murdered}}}\uc2  for providing legal health care to their patients; some types of attacks against them recently have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/06/24/attacks-violence-abortion-provider-roe-bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased}}}\uc2 . This moment, post-Roe v. Wade, feels particularly frightening and is chilling to anyone who cares for patients, especially those providing reproductive health care.\par \par \uc2 This saga has had real-world repercussions for Dr. Bernard. The local police have been alerted to concerns for her physical safety.\par \par \uc2 My colleagues and I have watched all this in horror. We are worried that this could happen to us, too. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://law.justia.com/codes/indiana/2021/title-16/article-34/chapter-2/section-16-34-2-4-7/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A law}}}\uc2  that recently went into effect in Indiana mandates that doctors, hospitals and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics report to the state when a patient who has previously had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  presents {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.in.gov/health/files/Abortion-Complications-Reporting-Requirement-Guidance-12.14.21.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 any of dozens of physical or psychological conditions}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 including anxiety, depression, sleeping disorders and uterine perforation \u8212\'20\'14 because they could be complications of the previous \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Not doing so within 30 days can result in a misdemeanor for the physician who treated the patient, punishable with up to 180 days in jail and a $1,000 fine.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the story, which has become an example of the real consequences of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s landmark decision last month:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/14/man-charged-10-year-old-abortion-rightwing-media-indiana-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Man charged with rape of 10-year-old who had \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  after rightwing media called story \u8216\'20\'18not true\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://streaklinks.com/BH_LCI0z8104KyaIpQ0_FAlW/https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fus-news%2F2022%2Fjul%2F15%2Fdonald-trump-new-york-lawsuit-legal-trouble"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 depositions}}}\uc2  of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://streaklinks.com/BH_LCI0Gxs0FxlW3yQJbup-d/https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fus-news%2Fdonaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and two of his children planned for Friday will be delayed following the death of \uc2 Ivana Trump\uc2 , his first wife and the childrens\u8217\'20\'19 mother. \u8220\'20\'1CIn light of the passing of \uc2 Ivana Trump\uc2  yesterday, we received a request from counsel for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his children to adjourn all three depositions, which we have agreed to,\u8221\'20\'1D the New York Attorney General\u8217\'20\'19s Office said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a temporary delay and the depositions will be rescheduled as soon as possible,\u8221\'20\'1D the office also said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no other information about dates or otherwise to provide at this time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump and his two eldest children, Ivanka and Donald Jr., were scheduled to give sworn testimony in the office\u8217\'20\'19s three-year civil investigation into {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://streaklinks.com/BH_LCI4RUV9VRWzgQgHD0DuB/https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fus-news%2F2021%2Fjun%2F08%2Ftrump-legal-threat-investigations-courts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 potential misconduct }}}\uc2  surrounding property values. The office is probing whether the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  provided inaccurate valuation to secure loans at favorable rates, or improperly claim tax breaks.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney has reportedly indicated that the former president will invoke his constitutional right against self-incrimination and refuse to respond to questions. \uc2 The Trump Organization\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s longtime chief financial officer, Allen Weisselberg, is facing a tax fraud trial amid a parallel investigation by the Manhattan district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Democrats will today make a renewed push to pass legislation protecting the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide and the ability of Americans to cross state lines to seek the procedure. But the bills\u8217\'20\'19 chances of passing the Senate are slim due to opposition from Republicans.\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  just held an event with other Democrats prior to the vote, declaring, \u8220\'20\'1CAs we pass his landmark legislation today, Democrats will not stop ferociously defending freedom for women and for every American. And we want everybody to know, women out there who are concerned about their own personal reproductive freedom and what it means to their health, that... the message from the House Democrats in our groups here today is, we are not going back\u8221\'20\'1D, sparking a chant that was joined by the lawmakers assembled behind her.\par \par \uc2 You can watch the full speech below:\par \par \uc2 enltrJoin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/demwomenscaucus?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @DemWomensCaucus}}}\uc2  and me at the U.S. Capitol ahead of the passage of legislation to protect women's reproductive freedom and to stop Republicans from criminalizing women exercising their constitutional right to travel to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yHypmYBTR5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/yHypmYBTR5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (@SpeakerPelosi) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerPelosi/status/1547960887956230147?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lois-beckett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lois Beckett}}}\uc2  reports on an overlooked aspect of the bipartisan gun safety bill passed last month that will pay for efforts to reduce gun violence in neighborhoods across the country:\par \par \uc2 In 2013, a month after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2012/dec/14/newtown-shooting-gunman-kills-20-children"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 school shooting in Newtown, Connecticut}}}\uc2 , a group of Black pastors and other activists visited the Obama White House to press the administration to do more to prevent gun violence in communities of color.\par \par \uc2 Obama had just released his post-Newtown gun violence prevention plan, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/how-the-gun-control-debate-ignores-black-lives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did not include any funding}}}\uc2  for community violence prevention efforts, and which made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://obamawhitehouse.archives.gov/sites/default/files/docs/wh_now_is_the_time_full.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no mention}}}\uc2  of the disparate impact of gun violence on Black Americans.\par \par \uc2 When the clergy members expressed their frustration at the White House\u8217\'20\'19s lack of response, an Obama staffer told them that there was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/how-the-gun-control-debate-ignores-black-lives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no support nationally}}}\uc2  to address urban gun violence, and that Americans\u8217\'20\'19 political will was focused on \u8220\'20\'1Cthe issue of gun violence that affected suburban areas \u8211\'20\'13 schools where white kids were killed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Some of those same Black pastors who visited the White House in 2013 were invited back for a ceremony on the South Lawn earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/15/gun-violence-legislation-debate-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Groundswells of change\u8217\'20\'19: Black activists welcome evolution in gun violence debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 House committee announces hearing on new assault weapons ban\par \par \uc2 The House Judiciary Committee has announced it will hold a hearing on a new proposal to ban assault weapons in response to the recent spate of mass shootings across the United States.\par \par \uc2 The 20 July markup will see lawmakers debate the Assault Weapons Ban of 2021 proposed by Democrat \uc2 Dave Cicilline\uc2  of Rhode Island, which would restrict the sale and manufacture of several types of semi-automatic rifles and shotguns.\par \par \uc2 The United States had a ban affecting such weapons from 1994 to 2004, and Cicilline said in a statement the recent massacre in Uvalde, Texas as well as previous atrocities in Sandy Hook, Connecticut and Parkland, Florida demand a new measure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CResearchers estimate that if we still had a federal Assault Weapons Ban, we would see 70 percent fewer mass shooting deaths. How many more kids need to die in their schools before we finally crack down on these dangerous firearms which were designed for war?\u8221\'20\'1D, he said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The committee has further details of the proposal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://judiciary.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=4987"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2 , a former trade adviser to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , arrives for his arraignment on contempt of Congress charges for refusing to cooperate with the House committee investigating the Jan. 6 attack on the U.S. Capitol, at U.S. District Court in Washington on June 17, 2022. Photograph: Jonathan Ernst/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2 , a former top trade adviser to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who was indicted for failing to cooperate with the January 6 committee, today declined a plea deal, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Last month, Navarro pleaded not guilty to two charges of contempt of Congress over his refusal to provide documents or testify to the House committee investigating the attack. According to Reuters, the lead prosecutor in the case Elizabeth Aloi said Navarro has now refused a deal that would see him plead guilty to one of those charges, and \u8220\'20\'1Ccomply with the January 6 committee subpoena to the satisfaction of the Justice Department.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/03/peter-navarro-indicted-trump-adviser-capitol-attack-inquiry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ex-Trump adviser Peter Navarro indicted for defying Capitol attack panel}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service responded to the inspector general\u8217\'20\'19s report in a statement released later yesterday evening, which you can read in full {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.secretservice.gov/newsroom/releases/2022/07/statement-anthony-guglielmi-chief-communications-united-states-secret"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The meat of it is that the deletion of text messages wasn\u8217\'20\'19t intentional, but rather pre-planned and unrelated to the events of January 6:\par \par \uc2 The insinuation that the Secret Service maliciously deleted text messages following a request is false. In fact, the Secret Service has been fully cooperating with the Department of Homeland Security Office of Inspector General (DHS OIG) in every respect \u8211\'20\'13 whether it be interviews, documents, emails, or texts.\par \par \uc2 First, in January 2021, before any inspection was opened by OIG on this subject, the Secret Service began to reset its mobile phones to factory settings as part of a pre-planned, three-month system migration. In that process, data resident on some phones was lost.\par \par \uc2 DHS OIG requested electronic communications for the first time on Feb. 26, 2021, after the migration was well under way. The Secret Service notified DHS OIG of the loss of certain phones\u8217\'20\'19 data, but confirmed to OIG that none of the texts it was seeking had been lost in the migration.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reported that an inspector general found Secret Service agents erased text messages from when the US Capitol was attacked on January 6, and the day before:\par \par \uc2 Texts sent between US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/secret-service"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service}}}\uc2  agents on 5 and 6 January 2021 were erased after the agency\u8217\'20\'19s oversight body sought the communications in a review into the Capitol attack, according to a letter from the Department of Homeland Security\u8217\'20\'19s Office of Inspector General (OIG).\par \par \uc2 The disclosure in the letter, sent on Thursday to the House homeland security and Senate homeland security and government affairs committees, marked the latest failure for the Secret Service amid increasing scrutiny for their actions over the attack.\par \par \uc2 Appearing to rebuke the erasure of the messages, the inspector general, Joseph Cuffari, decried the move and noted that the destruction came only after the body sought the communications as part of an internal investigation into the agency\u8217\'20\'19s response to the January 6 events.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/14/us-secret-service-agents-texts-erased-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service agents\u8217\'20\'19 January 6 texts were erased after oversight request}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Manchin elaborates on opposition to climate, tax proposals\par \par \uc2 Senator Joe Manchin called in to West Virginia broadcaster {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wvmetronews.com/channel/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hoppy Kercheval\u8217\'20\'19s radio show}}}\uc2  and elaborated on his opposition to measures mulled by Democrats that are meant to fight climate change and increase taxes.\par \par \uc2 The senator added a caveat to reports that he was against those two provisions, saying he told Democratic Senate leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t commit to either until he saw what the inflation rate is for this month - which is due out on 10 August - and until after he sees the size of the interest rate hike agreed to by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  when it meets in the final days of July.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s wait until that comes out, so we know that we\u8217\'20\'19re going down a path that won\u8217\'20\'19t be inflammatory, to add more to inflation,\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin said. \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t make that decision... on taxes... and also on the energy and climate because it takes the taxes to pay for the investment into clean technology that I\u8217\'20\'19m in favor of. But I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to do something and overreach that causes more problem.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Manchin said he asked Schumer for more time, but the Democratic leader declined.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI said, Chuck, can we just wait until the inflation figures come out in July\u8221\'20\'1D and until after the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s decision on interest rates, Manchin said. \u8220\'20\'1CHow much more and how much damaging is that going to be? And then make a decision what we can do and how much we can do. He took that as a no I guess and came out with this big thing last night and I don\u8217\'20\'19t know why they did that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin cited inflation as one of the reasons why he won\u8217\'20\'19t back measures to fight climate change or raise taxes on the rich.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPolitical headlines are of no value to the millions of Americans struggling to afford groceries and gas as inflation soars to 9.1 percent,\u8221\'20\'1D his spokeswoman Sam Runyon said, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/us-policy/2022/07/14/manchin-climate-tax-bbb/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to The Washington Post}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CSenator Manchin believes it\u8217\'20\'19s time for leaders to put political agendas aside, reevaluate and adjust to the economic realities the country faces to avoid taking steps that add fuel to the inflation fire.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Inflation is indeed high in the United States, but there\u8217\'20\'19s evidence gas prices, one of the trend\u8217\'20\'19s major components, are on the decline. Patrick de Haan, head of petroleum analysis at GasBuddy, has been monitoring their movements:\par \par \uc2 enltr31 days straight! The national average fell 3.5c/gal to $4.567 per gallon, a 47 cent drop in the last 31 days, one of the largest monthly declines on record.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Patrick De Haan ???? (@GasBuddyGuy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GasBuddyGuy/status/1547933521779470336?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe US saw the *largest* single day decline in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gasprices?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gasprices}}}\uc2  yesterday since the 2008 recession: the national average fell 3.5c/gal. Americans today will spend $177 million less on gasoline than they did 31 days ago. Outside the 2008 recession, it was the largest daily decline EVER.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Patrick De Haan ???? (@GasBuddyGuy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GasBuddyGuy/status/1547933629929508865?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/adam-gabbatt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adam Gabbatt}}}\uc2  has more on what Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s decision means for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s agenda:\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin, the Democratic senator who has repeatedly thwarted his own party\u8217\'20\'19s legislation, refuses to support more funding for climate action and will also block tax raises for wealthy Americans, dealing a further stunning blow to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s agenda when the US president is struggling to notch up successes.\par \par \uc2 Manchin told \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate majority leader, late on Thursday that he will oppose an economic measure he has been negotiating with Democratic leaders if it includes climate or green energy provisions, or higher taxes on the rich and corporations, a Democrat briefed on the conversations said.\par \par \uc2 The decision by Manchin, a West Virginian whose coal business has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/31/joe-manchin-hold-climate-policy-hostage-to-benefit-his-financial-interests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earned him millions of dollars}}}\uc2  over the past three decades, is a new shock to Democrats, who had made the sweeping package a top priority as midterm elections approach.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-funding-tax-hikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Manchin refuses to back climate funding and tax hikes on rich Americans}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s take a trip down the long and frustrating road \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s marquee spending bill has journeyed over the past 14 months. Just over a year ago, Biden was fresh in the White House and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/28/joe-biden-budget-proposal-infrastructure-education-climate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed an expansive plan}}}\uc2  meant to fix many of the ills plaguing the United States: expensive housing costs, the lack of support for financially-strapped parents, dilapidated infrastructure, tax rates that favor the rich and, crucially for both the country and the world at large, climate change.\par \par \uc2 Months of talks ensued and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/06/joe-biden-infrastructure-bill-democrats-monumental-step-forward"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Congress managed to pass}}}\uc2  the provisions overhauling the nation\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure, but negotiations over tax reform, social services and steps to mitigate rising temperatures stalled, in part due to the opposition of Joe Manchin, West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/31/joe-manchin-hold-climate-policy-hostage-to-benefit-his-financial-interests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extensive ties to the fossil fuel industry}}}\uc2  and is a crucial swing vote in the chamber that requires the agreement of all 50 Democratic lawmakers if the legislation was to pass (since no Republicans support it). By the end of 2021, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/19/joe-manchin-biden-build-back-better-no-fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had rejected the legislation entirely}}}\uc2  - but Democrats weren\u8217\'20\'19t finished.\par \par \uc2 Quietly, they have spent this year attempting to craft a bill that would pass his muster. But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/us-policy/2022/07/14/manchin-climate-tax-bbb/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post reported last night}}}\uc2  that Manchin has now said he won\u8217\'20\'19t back any measures to combat America\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ucsusa.org/resources/each-countrys-share-co2-emissions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 substantial greenhouse gas emissions}}}\uc2 , nor any changes to the tax code, citing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/13/us-inflation-why-so-high-what-we-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the country\u8217\'20\'19s high rate of inflation}}}\uc2 . He would, however, vote for lowering prescription drug and health care costs.\par \par \uc2 Varshini Prakash, executive director of climate change activist group the Sunrise Movement, described Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s opposition as \u8220\'20\'1Cnothing short of a death sentence\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBiden must declare a climate emergency, and do everything in his executive power to stop the climate crisis immediately. That\u8217\'20\'19s the only way he can salvage his presidency and save our generation. And we must uproot this broken system and rebuild it to work for us,\u8221\'20\'1D Prakash said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Manchin deals death blow to Biden's climate aspirations\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. After a year of negotiations, Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 aspirations to pass major climate change aspirations died at the hands of one of their own: Senator Joe Manchin, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/us-policy/2022/07/14/manchin-climate-tax-bbb/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told party leaders yesterday he would not support any such legislation}}}\uc2 , nor the tax increases to pay for it. The United States is the world\u8217\'20\'19s second-largest emitter of greenhouse gasses, and the failure to address that will impact not just Americans, but the entire world.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 * President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is finishing up his visit to Israel and flying to Saudi Arabia, where the White House says he will meet with Crown Prince \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2  despite controversy over the murder of journalist Jamal Khashoggi.\par \par \uc2 * The Democratic-led House of Representatives will consider a bill to codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into law, and ensure people can travel across state lines to access the procedure.\par \par \uc2 * Former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , along with son Donald Jr and daughter Ivanka, appear for testimony in a civil suit brought by the New York attorney general, Letitia James, against their business.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220715ei7f0020a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
