\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Man charged with rape of 10-year-old who had  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  after rightwing media called story \u8216\'20\'18not true\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Adam Gabbatt and agencies \par \uc2 823 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 July 2022\par 09:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 29\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Police say Ohio man confessed to raping a girl who went to Indiana for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , following the right\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to discredit story\par \par \uc2 In a case that has become a flashpoint in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate after being highlighted by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and baselessly disputed by some rightwing media and politicians, an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2  man has been charged with raping a 10-year-old girl who later traveled to neighboring Indiana for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Gerson Fuentes, 27, who was arrested on Tuesday, appeared in Franklin county, Ohio, municipal court for an arraignment on Wednesday. A police investigator testified at the hearing that Fuentes had confessed to raping the girl at least twice.\par \par \uc2 The arrest came after rightwing media \u8211\'20\'13 and the Republican Ohio attorney general \u8211\'20\'13 had poured scorn on reports of the child\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , suggesting it was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot true\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo good to confirm\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The victim in the case underwent an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in neighboring Indiana on 30 June, the police officer testified at the Wednesday hearing.\par \par \uc2 A statewide ban on abortions in Ohio after the sixth week of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 before many women are aware they are pregnant \u8211\'20\'13 went into effect just hours after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that struck down Roe v Wade, the 1973 decision that had established a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The incident gained attention this month when the Indianapolis Star newspaper reported she had to travel to Indiana to secure an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because she was three days past Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s six-week limit, which does not include exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Abortions after six weeks remain legal in Indiana, though the Republican-controlled state legislature is expected to consider new restrictions later this month.\par \par \uc2 Biden spoke of the girl in remarks to reporters about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust imagine being that little girl \u8211\'20\'13 10 years old,\u8221\'20\'1D he said angrily at the White House on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s comments prompted a furious, unsavory response from rightwing media, including Fox News, Breitbart, and the Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , Fox News, most prominent host, said on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediamatters.org/media/3990856"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his show on Tuesday}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhy did the Biden administration, speaking of lying, just repeat a story about a 1o-year-old child who got pregnant, and then got an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or was not allowed to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , when it turns out the story was not true?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The New York Post ran an op-ed with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jeremymbarr/status/1547268525156442112"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 headline}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CActivist tale of a 10-year-old-rape victim\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  looks like a lie\u8221\'20\'1D, before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2022/07/12/activist-tale-of-a-10-year-old-rape-victims-abortion-looks-like-a-lie/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 changing}}}\uc2  the title, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediamatters.org/fox-news/these-media-figures-discredited-report-10-year-old-girl-needing-medical-abortion-there-was"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Media Matters reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 One America News, a rightwing cable news channel, covered the story above {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediamatters.org/media/3990859"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the chyron}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe lies and deceit of abortionists\u8221\'20\'1D, while Benny Johnson, from Turning Point USA, said \u8220\'20\'1Cthere is no proof\u8221\'20\'1D that the 10-year-old victim \u8220\'20\'1Cexists\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal, which, like Fox News and the New York Post, is owned by the Murdoch family, published {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/an-abortion-story-too-good-to-confirm-joe-biden-ten-year-old-girl-indiana-ohio-caitlin-bernard-11657648618"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an article from its editorial board}}}\uc2  with the headline: \u8220\'20\'1CAn \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Story Too Good to Confirm\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll kinds of fanciful tales travel far on social media these days, but you don\u8217\'20\'19t expect them to get a hearing at the White House,\u8221\'20\'1D the editorial began.\par \par \uc2 It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t just conservative media that claimed the incident did not happen.\par \par \uc2 Dave Yost\uc2 , the Republican Ohio attorney general, told Fox News on Monday that there was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a whisper\u8221\'20\'1D of evidence to support the story. In an interview with USA Today on Tuesday, Yost said the details were \u8220\'20\'1Cmore likely than not a fabrication\u8221\'20\'1D because there had been no arrest and no evidence uncovered, Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s Columbus Dispatch {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dispatch.com/story/news/2022/07/13/ohio-attorney-general-rejoices-arrest-child-rape-suspect/10048250002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a statement on Wednesday after the arrest, Yost, who defended the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week ban in state court after the supreme court decision, said: \u8220\'20\'1CMy heart aches for the pain suffered by this young child. I am grateful for the diligent work of the Columbus police department in securing a confession and getting a rapist off the street.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yost was not alone in doubting the story. \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , the governor of South Dakota, and Jim Jordan, a congressman from Ohio also claimed the story was untrue.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with CNN, Noem accused a journalist of attempting to \u8220\'20\'1Ctrap me\u8221\'20\'1D by asking about the case, Newsweek {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/every-conservative-who-called-story-10-year-old-girl-abortion-lie-1724485"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow it looks like the story was fake to begin with,\u8221\'20\'1D Noem tweeted on 8 July. \u8220\'20\'1CLiteral #FakeNews from the liberal media.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jim Jordan, in a tweet which was later deleted, wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CAnother lie. Anyone surprised?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fuentes is being held on $2m bond and is scheduled for a preliminary hearing on 22 July.\par \par \uc2 A court-appointed defense attorney for Fuentes did not immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 In all, 26 US states have either severely restricted abortions in the wake of the ruling or are expected to do so in the coming weeks and months.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220715ei7f0018i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\pi