\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republicans block bill on right to travel across state lines for abortions \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 5,293 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2022\par 20:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republican senator claims Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 proposal would encourage \u8216\'20\'18\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  tourism\u8217\'20\'19Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was feted in Israel, giving him a respite from the troubles awaiting him back home, which include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/13/biden-israel-middle-east-inflation-us-politics-live?page=with:block-62cef2aa8f0813fe76dde2fb#block-62cef2aa8f0813fe76dde2fb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismal approval ratings}}}\uc2 , states\u8217\'20\'19 moves to criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his aspirations in 2024.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of what happened today:\par \par \uc2 * Republicans blocked a bill to guarantee that people seeking abortions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/14/joe-biden-middle-east-israel-inflation-polling-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62d061638f08b970599b64a9#block-62d061638f08b970599b64a9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could travel across state lines}}}\uc2 , with one lawmaker decrying \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  tourism\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * Saudi Arabia and Israel{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/14/joe-biden-middle-east-israel-inflation-polling-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d05bbd8f08b970599b646d#block-62d05bbd8f08b970599b646d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could announce steps towards normalizing relations}}}\uc2 , which would give Biden a major win as he visits the region.\par \par \uc2 * Trump gave an interview to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/14/joe-biden-middle-east-israel-inflation-polling-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d03b608f08bee7e09c5e3a#block-62d03b608f08bee7e09c5e3a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Magazine}}}\uc2  in which he more or less said he was running in 2024, but was undecided on when to announce the campaign. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/14/joe-biden-middle-east-israel-inflation-polling-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d022978f086e8f9369614f#block-62d022978f086e8f9369614f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post reports}}}\uc2  that he\u8217\'20\'19s leaning towards announcing before the November midterm elections, though some Republicans don\u8217\'20\'19t think that is a good idea.\par \par \uc2 * In what is surely a healthy sign for American democracy, voters in a New York county are leaning towards {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/14/joe-biden-middle-east-israel-inflation-polling-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d024508f086e8f9369616f#block-62d024508f086e8f9369616f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 choosing a spider monster thing}}}\uc2  to represent their local elections.\par \par \uc2 * The attorney general in Indiana said it would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/14/joe-biden-middle-east-israel-inflation-polling-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d033e68f08bee7e09c5dd7#block-62d033e68f08bee7e09c5dd7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigate the doctor that provided an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  to a 10-year-old girl}}}\uc2  who was forced to travel from neighboring Ohio after being raped.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s first wife \uc2 Ivana Trump\uc2  has died in New York City, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 According to the AP:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am very saddened to inform all of those that loved her, of which there are many, that \uc2 Ivana Trump\uc2  has passed away at her home in New York City,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump posted on Truth Social. \u8220\'20\'1CShe was a wonderful, beautiful, and amazing woman, who led a great and inspirational life. Her pride and joy were her three children, Donald Jr., Ivanka, and Eric. She was so proud of them, as we were all so proud of her. Rest In Peace, Ivana!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Trump family also released a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is with deep sadness that we announce the passing of our beloved mother, \uc2 Ivana Trump\uc2 . Our mother was an incredible woman a force in business, a world-class athlete, a radiant beauty, and caring mother and friend. \uc2 Ivana Trump\uc2  was a survivor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe fled from communism and embraced this country,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement continued. \u8220\'20\'1CShe taught her children about grit and toughness, compassion and determination. She will be dearly missed by her mother, her three children and ten grandchildren.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tina Peters speaks to supporters at her election watch party in Sedalia, Colo., on June 28, 2022. Photograph: Thomas Peipert/AP\par \par \uc2 An arrest warrant has been issued for Tina Peters, the Colorado county clerk and 2020 election denier who recently lost her bid for a position overseeing voting in the state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usnews.com/news/politics/articles/2022-07-13/3rd-arrest-made-in-alleged-colorado-election-security-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Peters ran to be the Republican nominee for the position of Colorado secretary of state despite being indicted along with her deputy on charges related to tampering with election equipment. According to the AP, a judge issued the arrest warrant for Peters on Thursday after finding out she had left the state against his orders:\par \par \uc2 A judge revoked bond for Mesa County Clerk Tina Peters after District Attorney Dan Rubinstein said in the documents that he had learned she traveled to Nevada for a conference.\par \par \uc2 Rubinstein said he made the discovery after Peters sent a letter notarized in Las Vegas on Tuesday to Colorado Secretary of State \uc2 Jena Griswold\uc2 , according to court documents. The letter was released by the secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s office and requested a recount in her failed primary election bid for the GOP nomination in the state secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s race.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, Peters\u8217\'20\'19s election manager {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/13/biden-israel-middle-east-inflation-us-politics-live?page=with:block-62cf1b3c8f0813fe76dde4c6#block-62cf1b3c8f0813fe76dde4c6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turned herself in}}}\uc2  on charges similar to those facing the clerk, who is accused of allowing an unauthorized person to impersonate a county employee and access and copy information from the county\u8217\'20\'19s voting equipment.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/29/colorado-primary-result-tina-peters-republican"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Election denier Tina Peters loses Colorado primary for top poll official}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 prospects in the upcoming midterm elections are shaky, thanks in part to high inflation and President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s low approval ratings. But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/07/14/against-dire-headwinds-senate-dems-from-bennet-to-warnock-post-blockbuster-money-00045840"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2  that when it comes to the senate, the party\u8217\'20\'19s candidates have a clear edge in one area: fundraising.\par \par \uc2 Colorado Senator Michael Bennet has 10 times the funds of his Republican opponent Joe O\u8217\'20\'19Dea, while Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic Senator \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  raised more than double that of his Republican challenger in his most recent quarter. Democratic senators facing tough races in New Hampshire, Arizona and Nevada have also brought in big bucks.\par \par \uc2 From the story:\par \par \uc2 The race illustrates Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 circumstances throughout the country: While Bennet is slugging it out with O\u8217\'20\'19Dea in a state that President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won by 13 points, the party still sees a bright spot in candidates\u8217\'20\'19 fundraising as they hope to significantly outperform Biden\u8217\'20\'19s sagging approval ratings in November.\par \par \uc2 Candidates are posting \u8220\'20\'1Cblockbuster fundraising numbers,\u8221\'20\'1D as Democratic Senatorial Campaign Committee spokesperson David Bergstein put it \u8212\'20\'14 though, in some cases, they are spending cash just as fast as they take it in. Nonetheless, Democrats see it as a sign of momentum after the Supreme Court struck down Roe v. Wade last month and an uptick in their chances of keeping the Senate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt says enthusiasm, I think it says that people understand it\u8217\'20\'19s the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2  that confirms judges, particularly in light of what\u8217\'20\'19s happened,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sen. \uc2 Debbie Stabenow\uc2  (D-Mich.), the No. 4 party leader.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Texas is suing the Biden administration over its determination that federal law requires hospitals to offer abortions in cases of medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 After the supreme court overturned Roe v. Wade last month, health and human services secretary \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2  wrote a letter to healthcare providers saying the Emergency Medical Treatment and Active Labor Act protects providers from any purported state restrictions, should they be required to perform emergency abortions.\par \par \uc2 Texas is suing over that determination, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texasattorneygeneral.gov/news/releases/paxton-sues-biden-admin-over-its-efforts-force-abortions-texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying in a statement}}}\uc2  the Biden administration \u8220\'20\'1Cseeks to transform every emergency room in the country into a walk-in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis administration has a hard time following the law, and now they are trying to have their appointed bureaucrats mandate that hospitals and emergency medicine physicians perform abortions,\u8221\'20\'1D Texas attorney general \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  said in filing the lawsuit Thursday. \u8220\'20\'1CI will ensure that President Biden will be forced to comply with the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s important decision concerning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and I will not allow him to undermine and distort existing laws to fit his administration\u8217\'20\'19s unlawful agenda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/12/us-law-will-overrule-states-emergency-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US law overrules states on abortions in medical emergencies, health secretary says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Decrying '\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  tourism', Republicans block freedom-of-movement bill in Senate Republican Senator Steve Daines condemned a proposal to protect people\u8217\'20\'19s rights to travel for abortions as \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  tourism\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Republicans in the Senate have blocked a Democratic proposal to protect people\u8217\'20\'19s ability to cross state lines to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with one senator saying the proposal would encourage \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  tourism\u8221\'20\'1D and help \u8220\'20\'1Cfly-in abortionists.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cortezmasto.senate.gov/news/press-releases/cortez-masto-whitehouse-murray-gillibrand-introduce-legislation-to-protect-the-right-of-women-to-cross-state-lines-to-seek-abortion-care"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The bill}}}\uc2  from Nevada Senator \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  came in response to moves by Republican-led states to stop people from traveling to seek abortions, following the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling last month overturning the right to access the procedure nationwide. Democrats attempted to get the senate to pass the measure unanimously on Thursday, but Republicans refused to do so.\par \par \uc2 enltrSenate Republicans just blocked my bill to protect women who travel for reproductive care and those who help them. They want to allow state legislators to reach across state lines to punish and control women. It\u8217\'20\'19s absolutely outrageous. I won't stop fighting for women's freedom.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator \uc2 Cortez Masto\uc2  (@SenCortezMasto) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenCortezMasto/status/1547614222535733252?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Montana Republican Steve Daines was among those rejecting the measure, saying in a floor speech that it was \u8220\'20\'1Chastily put together\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cvery very extreme.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis bill would give fly-in abortionists free rein to commit abortions on demand up to the moment of birth,\u8221\'20\'1D Daines said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis bill also protects the greed, frankly, of woke corporations who see it\u8217\'20\'19s cheaper to pay for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  tourism, than maternity leave for their employees.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Might Saudi Arabia normalize relations with Israel during Biden\u8217\'20\'19s visit? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/07/14/saudi-israel-normalization-red-sea-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios reports that}}}\uc2  Israel\u8217\'20\'19s government has approved a deal that would resolve Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s claim to two strategic islands in the Red Sea, which has been a sticking point in getting the countries to establish diplomatic ties.\par \par \uc2 While it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if the deal will result in an agreement for Riyadh to fully recognize Israel, which it has never done before, Biden could seize on it as a win that would be comparable to what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  pulled off during his term. The Republican leader presided over deals that got the United Arab Emirates, Bahrain, Morocco and Sudan to recognize the country.\par \par \uc2 The potential deal involves the Tiran and Sanafir islands in the Red Sea, and the obligations of the two countries, as well as Egypt, under the 1979 Israel-Egypt peace agreement. According to Axios, \u8220\'20\'1CThe deal includes moving multilateral forces of observers currently on Tiran and Sanafir to new positions in the Egyptian Sinai Peninsula, as well as cameras to monitor activity on islands and the Strait of Tiran.\u8221\'20\'1D Saudi Arabia would pledge to allow ships to pass along the islands, while the United States would give Israel security commitments under that deal, the report said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  once pledged to turn Saudi Arabia into a pariah state but the day before his first visit to the country as president, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/14/joe-biden-defends-human-rights-record-ahead-of-saudi-visit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bethan McKernan}}}\uc2  reports he\u8217\'20\'19s downplaying his views on Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s rights record, including its murder of journalist Jamal Khashoggi:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has defended his imminent trip to Saudi Arabia, saying he will not avoid human rights issues on the final leg of his Middle East tour, despite refusing to commit to mentioning the murder of the dissident journalist Jamal Khashoggi when he meets the kingdom\u8217\'20\'19s crown prince.\par \par \uc2 Speaking during a news conference with the interim Israeli prime minister, \uc2 Yair Lapid\uc2 , in Jerusalem on Thursday, the US leader said his stance on Khashoggi\u8217\'20\'19s killing was \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely\u8221\'20\'1D clear.\par \par \uc2 US intelligence services concluded last year that Khashoggi\u8217\'20\'19s killing at the Saudi consulate in Istanbul was approved by the powerful heir to the throne, \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2 . On the campaign trail, the president vowed to turn the conservative Gulf kingdom into a \u8220\'20\'1Cpariah state\u8221\'20\'1D, but the turmoil in global oil markets unleashed by Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine has forced a U-turn.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/14/joe-biden-defends-human-rights-record-ahead-of-saudi-visit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden defends human rights record ahead of Saudi visit}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden, Lapid assert Iran must not get nuclear weapon - though US pressing diplomacy, Israel more bellicose\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Israeli Prime Minister \uc2 Yair Lapid\uc2  stood side-by-side in Jerusalem moments ago and declared they would not allow Iran to become a nuclear power.\par \par \uc2 They parted ways, though, on how to get there, the Associated Press writes.\par \par \uc2 The US president, in a joint news conference after a one-on-one meeting with the Israeli leader, said he still wants to give diplomacy a chance.\par \par \uc2 Seconds earlier, Lapid had insisted that words alone won\u8217\'20\'19t thwart Tehran\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear ambitions.\par \par \uc2 US President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (L), Israel\u8217\'20\'19s Prime Minister \uc2 Yair Lapid\uc2  (R) in Jerusalem today. Photograph: Anadolu Agency/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 While Biden suggested his patience with Iran was running low, he held out hope that Iran can be persuaded to rejoin a dormant deal intended to prevent it from building a nuclear weapon.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI continue to believe that diplomacy is the best way to achieve this outcome,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said on the second day of a four-day visit to Israel and Saudi\par \par \uc2 Arabia.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s his first trip to the Middle East as president. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s emphasis on a diplomatic solution contrasted with Lapid, who said Iran must face a real threat of force before it will agree to give up on its nuclear ambitions.\par \par \uc2 Words will not stop them, Mr President. Diplomacy will not stop them. The only thing that will stop Iran is knowing that if they continue to develop their nuclear program the free world will use force,\u8221\'20\'1D Lapid said.\par \par \uc2 Lapid suggested that he and Biden were in agreement, despite his tougher rhetoric toward Iran.\par \par \uc2 Resurrecting the Iran nuclear deal brokered by \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s administration and abandoned by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2018 was a key priority for Biden as he entered office.\par \par \uc2 But administration officials have become increasingly pessimistic about the chances of getting Tehran back into compliance.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  is expected to file an antitrust lawsuit against \uc2 Alphabet Inc\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Google\uc2  in weeks over its dominance in the online advertising market, Bloomberg News reported today, citing people familiar with the matter, Reuters writes.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department is likely to reject concessions offered by \uc2 Alphabet\uc2 , the report said.\par \par \uc2 DoJ did not immediately respond to Reuters requests for comment and \uc2 Google\uc2  declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the Wall Street Journal reported that \uc2 Google\uc2  has offered concessions to avoid a potential US antitrust lawsuit, including a proposal to spin off parts of its business that auctions and places ads on websites and apps into a separate company under \uc2 Alphabet\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, a \uc2 Google\uc2  spokesperson told Reuters on Friday that it was engaging with regulators to address their concerns, adding that it has no plans to sell or exit the ad-tech business.\par \par \uc2 The DoJ has been investigating \uc2 Google\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ad-tech practices since 2019 and expedited the inquiry into the advertising market in recent months under the supervision of antitrust division\u8217\'20\'19s official Doha Mekki, the report said.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2020/oct/20/us-justice-department-antitrust-lawsuit-against-google"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued Google}}}\uc2  in October 2020, accusing the company of illegally using its market muscle to hobble rivals, in the biggest challenge to the power and influence of \u8220\'20\'1CBig Tech\u8221\'20\'1D in decades.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Google\uc2  logo as seen in Brussels, Belgium. Photograph: Kenzo Tribouillard/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 A new US immigration enforcement directive issued today calls on federal officers to ask immigrants about their parental status during arrests, part of a broader effort by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to prioritize family unity and replacing more restrictive policies under former US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The directive, issued to all \uc2 US Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (Ice) employees, also calls for previously deported immigrants outside the United States to be allowed back into the country on a temporary basis for child custody hearings.\par \par \uc2 Democratic president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has promised a more humane and orderly approach to immigration than his Republican predecessor, but has faced large numbers of migrant arrests at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-mexico-border"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US-Mexico border}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The new Ice directive replaces Trump-era guidance issued in 2017 that did not explicitly require officers to inquire about and record parental status or guardianship.\par \par \uc2 In another departure from the Trump-era policy, the new guidance applies to parents or guardians of incapacitated adults as well as children.\par \par \uc2 Ice acting director Tae Johnson said in an email to staff that the agency is \u8220\'20\'1Ccommitted to safeguarding the integrity of our immigration system and preserving the parental and guardianship interests of noncitizen parents and legal guardians.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Federal courts have blocked separate Biden memos that sought to focus immigration enforcement efforts on individuals convicted of certain serious crimes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is being feted in Israel even as challenges mount at home. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a non-exhaustive list of them: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/13/biden-israel-middle-east-inflation-us-politics-live?page=with:block-62cef2aa8f0813fe76dde2fb#block-62cef2aa8f0813fe76dde2fb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismal approval ratings}}}\uc2 , states\u8217\'20\'19 moves to criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his aspirations in 2024.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s have a look at what happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 * Trump gave an interview to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/14/joe-biden-middle-east-israel-inflation-polling-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d03b608f08bee7e09c5e3a#block-62d03b608f08bee7e09c5e3a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Magazine}}}\uc2  in which he more or less said he was running in 2024, but was undecided on when to announce the campaign. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/14/joe-biden-middle-east-israel-inflation-polling-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d022978f086e8f9369614f#block-62d022978f086e8f9369614f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post reports}}}\uc2  that he\u8217\'20\'19s leaning towards announcing before the November midterm elections, which some Republicans don\u8217\'20\'19t think is a good idea.\par \par \uc2 * In what is surely a healthy sign for American democracy, voters in a New York county are leaning towards {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/14/joe-biden-middle-east-israel-inflation-polling-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d024508f086e8f9369616f#block-62d024508f086e8f9369616f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 choosing a spider monster thing}}}\uc2  to represent their local elections.\par \par \uc2 * The attorney general in Indiana said it would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/14/joe-biden-middle-east-israel-inflation-polling-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d033e68f08bee7e09c5dd7#block-62d033e68f08bee7e09c5dd7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigate the doctor that provided an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  to a 10-year-old girl}}}\uc2  who was forced to travel from neighboring Ohio after being raped.\par \par \uc2 * A Republican senator{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/14/joe-biden-middle-east-israel-inflation-polling-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d01c958f086e8f936960f3#block-62d01c958f086e8f936960f3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tested positive}}}\uc2  for Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 A leaked audio recording from top Trump advisor \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  shows just how gung-ho the president was when it came to declaring victory on election night in 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/adam-gabbatt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adam Gabbatt}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Days before the 2020 presidential election, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was already planning to declare victory on election night, even if there was no evidence he was winning, according to a leaked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/steve-bannon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steve Bannon}}}\uc2  conversation recorded before the vote.\par \par \uc2 In the audio, recorded three days before the election and published by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2022/07/leaked-audio-steve-bannon-trump-2020-election-declare-victory/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mother Jones}}}\uc2  on Wednesday, Bannon told a group of associates Trump already had a scheme in place for the 3 November vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat Trump\u8217\'20\'19s gonna do is just declare victory. Right? He\u8217\'20\'19s gonna declare victory. But that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean he\u8217\'20\'19s a winner,\u8221\'20\'1D Bannon, laughing, told the group, according to the audio.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/14/steve-bannon-audio-trump-declare-victory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Game over\u8217\'20\'19: Steve Bannon audio reveals Trump planned to claim early victory}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nymag.com/intelligencer/article/donald-trump-2024-decision.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Magazine snagged an interview with Donald Trump}}}\uc2 . The former president lives up to his reputation for loquaciousness in the piece, but the real question is what he\u8217\'20\'19s thinking when it comes to 2024.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he had to say about that:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLook,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, \u8220\'20\'1CI feel very confident that, if I decide to run, I\u8217\'20\'19ll win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 I fixated on If I decide. Trump is less a politician than a live-action mythological creature, and so punditry and all of the standard forms of analyses tend to fail. What would factor into such a decision for such an unusual person? \u8220\'20\'1CWell, in my own mind, I\u8217\'20\'19ve already made that decision, so nothing factors in anymore. In my own mind, I\u8217\'20\'19ve already made that decision,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t disclose what he\u8217\'20\'19d decided. Not at first. But then he couldn\u8217\'20\'19t help himself. \u8220\'20\'1CI would say my big decision will be whether I go before or after,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou understand what that means?\u8221\'20\'1D His tone was conspiratorial. Was he referring to the midterm elections? He repeated after me: \u8220\'20\'1C Midterms.\u8221\'20\'1D Suddenly, he relaxed, as though my speaking the word had somehow set it free for discussion. \u8220\'20\'1CDo I go before or after? That will be my big decision,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He was thinking aloud now. \u8220\'20\'1CI just think that there are certain assets to before,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CLet people know. I think a lot of people would not even run if I did that because, if you look at the polls, they don\u8217\'20\'19t even register. Most of these people. And I think that you would actually have a backlash against them if they ran. People want me to run.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican-led states are moving swiftly to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  outright or retaliate against patients seeking the care and the doctors providing it to them. But the message of a new Morning Consult/Politico poll of voters gauging support for these policies might be: not so fast.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://morningconsult.com/2022/07/13/state-abortion-restrictions-opposition-survey/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The survey found}}}\uc2  that of 13 state-level proposals, only two weren\u8217\'20\'19t opposed by a majority of voters. Banning all abortions without exception is the most disliked, with 73 percent opposing it, while criminalizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  seekers and people who travel out of state for care both came in with 70-percent disapproval. Proposals to fine or criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers also polled poorly, as did the idea to allow people to sue anyone involved in abortions.\par \par \uc2 The least disliked proposals were banning abortions after around 23 or 24 weeks of pregnancy, which only 38 percent of respondents opposed. Banning the procedure 15 weeks into pregnancy was opposed by 47 percent of those surveyed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general said he will investigate the doctor who provided the 10-year-old Ohio girl with an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  over whether she properly reported the child\u8217\'20\'19s rape.\par \par \uc2 Speaking on Fox News last night, Republican \uc2 Todd Rokita\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re gathering the evidence as we speak, and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to fight this to the end, including looking at her licensure if she failed to report. And in Indiana it\u8217\'20\'19s a crime \u8230\'20\'26 to intentionally not report.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked why it was so important that the child\u8217\'20\'19s rape be reported, Rokita replied: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a child, and there\u8217\'20\'19s a strong public interest in understanding if someone under the age of 16 or under the age of 18 or really any woman is having \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in our state. And then if a child is being sexually abused, of course parents need to know. Authorities need to know. Public policy experts need to know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/adam-gabbatt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adam Gabbatt}}}\uc2  reports, the story of a 10-year-old girl who had to travel from Ohio to Indiana to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after being raped has illustrated the real consequences of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling last month overturning Roe v. Wade:\par \par \uc2 In a case that has become a flashpoint in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate after being highlighted by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and baselessly disputed by some rightwing media and politicians, an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2  man has been charged with raping a 10-year-old girl who later traveled to neighboring Indiana for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Gerson Fuentes, 27, who was arrested on Tuesday, appeared in Franklin county, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2 , municipal court for an arraignment on Wednesday. A police investigator testified at the hearing that Fuentes had confessed to raping the girl at least twice.\par \par \uc2 The arrest came after rightwing media \u8211\'20\'13 and the Republican Ohio attorney general \u8211\'20\'13 had poured scorn on reports of the child\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , suggesting it was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot true\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo good to confirm\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/14/man-charged-10-year-old-abortion-rightwing-media-indiana-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Man charged with rape of 10-year-old who had \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  after rightwing media called story \u8216\'20\'18not true\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Spiders or not, voting correlates with better health outcomes, so much so that a top doctors group is looking to encourage the practice, as Simar Bajaj reports:\par \par \uc2 Access to voting is now considered a health issue, according to the country\u8217\'20\'19s largest physician group.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American Medical Association\uc2  (\uc2 AMA\uc2 ) House of Delegates adopted a resolution calling voting a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.who.int/health-topics/social-determinants-of-health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social determinant of health}}}\uc2 , a term used to describe non-medical factors that affect health and wellbeing. Co-sponsored by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nmanet.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 National Medical Association}}}\uc2 , the resolution also recognizes that gerrymandering limits access to care and leads to worse health outcomes.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 AMA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s move follows the 2020 election, in which Republican campaigns questioned election results, and a redistricting cycle where hyperpartisan districts were proposed in several states.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/14/voting-health-us-medical-association"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Voting is significant determinant of health, US medical association declares}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hudson Rowan\u8217\'20\'19s design for an \u8216\'20\'18I voted\u8217\'20\'19 sticker in Ulster County, New York. Photograph: Hudson Rowan/Ulster County Board of Elections\par \par \uc2 Speaking of elections, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  has looked into why that thing above may be the perfect visual encapsulation of the emotions around casting your ballot in America today:\par \par \uc2 One morning a few months ago, Ashley Dittus, a Democratic election commissioner in Ulster county, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2 , came into work and saw that someone had sent in the first submission in a countywide contest for an \u8220\'20\'1CI voted\u8221\'20\'1D sticker. She opened the email and was shocked. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a moment I\u8217\'20\'19ll never forget,\u8221\'20\'1D Dittus told me on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The design was a skull-like head with bloodshot eyes and multicolored teeth sitting atop turquoise spider legs. To the creature\u8217\'20\'19s right, the words \u8220\'20\'1CI voted\u8221\'20\'1D were scribbled in graffiti-like font. It was 4/20 so she wondered whether someone was playing a trick.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/14/ulster-county-voting-sticker-contest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why a \u8216\'20\'18spider crab\u8217\'20\'19 is crawling to the top of a US \u8216\'20\'18I voted\u8217\'20\'19 sticker contest | The fight to vote}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump considers announcing 2024 run before midterms \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 That former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is leaning towards another run for the White House is no secret. The question is: when will he announce it? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/07/14/trump-2024-announcement-fall/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post is reporting}}}\uc2  that Trump, despite the advice of some of his advisors, is considering making it official before the November midterm elections, perhaps as soon as September.\par \par \uc2 According to the report, Republicans are divided over the effect an early Trump campaign announcement would have:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Trump is going to run, the sooner he gets in and talks about winning the next election, the better,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sen. \uc2 Lindsey O. Graham\uc2  (R-S.C.), who recently golfed with Trump in New Jersey. \u8220\'20\'1CIt will refocus his attention \u8212\'20\'14 less grievance, more about the future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Graham has embraced an argument once dismissed inside much of the party, contending that Democrats are going to use Trump\u8217\'20\'19s unpopularity among some voter groups to try to drive turnout no matter what he does. If he gets in the race soon, they argue, he will be better positioned to drive turnout on the Republican side in the midterms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou might as well get the benefit if you\u8217\'20\'19re going to take the lashes too,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tony Fabrizio, a Trump pollster working for multiple Senate candidates this cycle. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you want to energize the base and get the base out, no one does it better than Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Others have argued that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s direct insertion into the midterm campaign will only play into Democratic plans to make the election a referendum on the extremism of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Great Again,\u8221\'20\'1D or MAGA, movement. Republicans believe they are on track for a banner midterm year, a result of massive dissatisfaction with inflation, President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s job performance and the direction of the country.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at a Republican summit in Nashville last month. Photograph: Harrison Mcclary/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican Senator \uc2 Ben Sasse\uc2  has tested positive for Covid-19, his office announced.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYesterday, after returning from the Ukrainian border, Senator Sasse tested positive for Covid. He\u8217\'20\'19s vaccinated and boosted, and is experiencing only mild symptoms. He\u8217\'20\'19ll isolate for the recommended five days \u8211\'20\'13 during that time, he\u8217\'20\'19ll be working remotely,\u8221\'20\'1D the Nebraska lawmaker\u8217\'20\'19s communications director James Wegmann said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Ben Sasse\uc2  on Capitol Hill in May. Photograph: Michael Reynolds/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  reports on why Biden probably won\u8217\'20\'19t be receiving any awards from the American public, at least not right now:\par \par \uc2 Another searing inflation report yesterday underscored the deep challenges facing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  ahead of this year\u8217\'20\'19s critical midterm elections, with widespread pessimism about the state of the US economy and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s stewardship of it.\par \par \uc2 Inflation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/cpi.nr0.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  soared 9.1% }}}\uc2  in June compared with the previous year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/13/high-us-gas-food-prices-june-led-to-largest-annual-increase-inflation-40-years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new 40-year high}}}\uc2 . The rising cost of gas, fuel and rent squeezes American households and puts pressure on the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  to raise interest rates further.\par \par \uc2 The sobering numbers, released as Biden arrived in Israel for a high-stakes trip to the Middle East, were driven largely by energy prices, an issue that will be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-07-12/biden-s-woes-at-home-loom-over-mideast-trip-that-s-all-about-oil?sref=fqqmZ8gi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 top of the agenda}}}\uc2  when he makes a controversial visit to oil-rich Saudi Arabia this week.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/13/joe-biden-middle-east-tour-inflation-approval-ratings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden, on Middle East tour, is battered by inflation and low approval ratings at home}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 First awarded in 2012, Israel\u8217\'20\'19s Presidential Medal of Honor has only been given to a handful of the world\u8217\'20\'19s most notable statesmen, including former US secretary of state \uc2 Henry Kissinger\uc2 , Germany\u8217\'20\'19s ex-chancellor \uc2 Angela Merkel\uc2 , author Elie Wiesel and former US president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , whom Biden served as vice president.\par \par \uc2 So why give it to Biden? Here\u8217\'20\'19s the reasoning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.il/en/departments/news/press-070722"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from the Israeli presidency}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Since the start of President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s rich career in public service in the 1970s, he has established himself as a person who loves Israel and is a true friend of the whole Jewish People.\par \par \uc2 For half a century, the President has stood by the State of Israel, has given his unconditional support to its right to exist, and has fought with determination to expand U.S. assistance to Israel.\par \par \uc2 In this, the President gives expression in word and deed to the importance of the alliance between Israel and the United States, to his commitment to deepen the cooperation between them, to his support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s security, and to his commitment to firmly confront antisemitism.\par \par \uc2 Biden and Israel\u8217\'20\'19s caretaker prime minister \uc2 Yair Lapid{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/07/14/the-jerusalem-u-s-israel-strategic-partnership-joint-declaration/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed a joint declaration earlier today}}}\uc2  that mostly reaffirms US policy on the country, including its right to defend itself.\par \par \uc2 One American president that didn\u8217\'20\'19t get the award was \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , even though he made major changes in Washington\u8217\'20\'19s policies towards Israel, the Palestinians and the country\u8217\'20\'19s relationship with the wider Middle East. Perhaps he would have been given the honor, had he won a second term.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/19/will-trumps-major-foreign-policy-legacy-be-israel-and-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Will Trump's major foreign policy legacy be Israel and Palestine?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Enjoy it while it lasts: Middle East trip offers Biden a respite from troubles at home\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics readers. Today is the second day of President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s visit to Israel, where the country\u8217\'20\'19s political leaders have hailed him as a true friend of the American ally and plan to award him the country\u8217\'20\'19s highest civilian honor. It must be nice, because the opinion of Biden back home is not as lofty. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/13/biden-israel-middle-east-inflation-us-politics-live?page=with:block-62cef2aa8f0813fe76dde2fb#block-62cef2aa8f0813fe76dde2fb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A poll released yesterday}}}\uc2  found that only a minority of Americans want him to run for a second term, a sign that his lengthy slump in public opinion polls could have dire consequences for his presidency.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we can expect from today:\par \par \uc2 * Israel is seven hours ahead of Washington so most of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s events will wrap up by the afternoon in the United States, but in the balance of the day, he is set to meet former prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , attend a ceremony where he\u8217\'20\'19ll receive Israel\u8217\'20\'19s President\u8217\'20\'19s Medal and watch the opening ceremony of the Maccabiah Games.\par \par \uc2 * Vice-PresidentKamala Harris is in Florida, where she will discuss reproductive rights with legislative leaders at 1:50 pm eastern time.\par \par \uc2 * The House judiciary committee holds a hearing titled \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://judiciary.house.gov/calendar/eventsingle.aspx?EventID=4978"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Whats Next: The Threat to Individual Freedoms in a Post-Roe World}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D beginning at 9am ET.\par \par \uc2 * The Senate homeland security committee is looking into {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hsgac.senate.gov/hearings/protecting-the-homeland-from-unmanned-aircraft-systems"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hsgac.senate.gov/hearings/protecting-the-homeland-from-unmanned-aircraft-systems"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Protecting the Homeland from Unmanned Aircraft Systems}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D starting at 10.15am ET.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220714ei7e001xm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
