\par\par \uc2 Books\par \b \uc2 Mark Haddon pledges all future US royalties to  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights groups\b0\par\par\uc2 Sarah Shaffi \par \uc2 551 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2022\par 16:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time author said his choice was \u8216\'20\'18pretty instant\u8217\'20\'19 after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 Author Mark Haddon is to donate all future royalties from US sales of his bestselling book The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time to the National Network of \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Funds.\par \par \uc2 Haddon made the announcement on his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mark_haddon/status/1547179043354775553"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Twitter}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/Cf82TBIruRg/?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Instagram}}}\uc2  accounts, saying that from now until the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Coverturning of Roe v Wade is reversed, or some equivalent action is taken\u8221\'20\'1D he would be donating all US royalties from the book.\par \par \uc2 The National Network of \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Funds is a network of grassroots organisations \u8220\'20\'1Cbuilding power to remove financial, logistical, cultural and political barriers to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Haddon told the Guardian that his decision to donate his royalties was \u8220\'20\'1Cpretty instant\u8221\'20\'1D, following the supreme court ruling taking away the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that he was keen to make a \u8220\'20\'1Cmore public statement\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He chose the National Network of \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Funds because the money \u8220\'20\'1Cgoes most directly\u8221\'20\'1D to the people who need support, and also because the word \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D was in the group\u8217\'20\'19s name, meaning both its intent and his was clear.\par \par \uc2 As the next payment of royalties from Curious Incident is not due for \u8220\'20\'1Ca while\u8221\'20\'1D, said Haddon on social media, he has made a $10,000 donation \u8220\'20\'1Cto get the ball rolling and as a statement of intent\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court ruled in June that there is no constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US, upending the landmark Roe v Wade decision of 1973. A number of states made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal within hours of Roe v Wade being overturned.\par \par \uc2 Critics of the decision worry that, as well as endangering lives, it will also lead to the court overturning rulings relating to other rights.\par \par \uc2 Haddon went on to say on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  that if the supreme court looked to \u8220\'20\'1Cturn its fire\u8221\'20\'1D on precedents regarding contraception, same-sex sexual activity and equal marriage rights for same-sex couples, he \u8220\'20\'1Cmay redirect some of the royalties to help people affected by those decisions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time was published in 2003 and won 17 literary prizes. It was adapted for the stage in 2012, and has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2019/may/04/mark-haddon-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sold more than 10m copies}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Haddon is not the only author to show his support to pro-choice organisations. Authors and creators including Neil Gaiman, Shannon Chakraborty, VE Schwab and Sabaa Tahir have donated books to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.32auctions.com/AuthorsForAbortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Authors for \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Access}}}\uc2 , an auction that will raise money for the National Network of \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Funds\u8217\'20\'19 collective power fund and Keep Our Clinics, a campaign that provides funding to independent clinics to cover expenses such as increased security, building repairs and legal fees in the face of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and restrictions.\par \par \uc2 The auction has been organised by authors Rebecca F Kuang and Vaishnavi Patel, and has already reached its $10,000 (\u163\'00\'A38,500) fundraising target.\par \par \uc2 The auction runs until July 26, and includes signed books, limited edition copies and boxed sets. Among the lots is a rare leather-bound Easton Press edition of Coraline by Gaiman, and a signed special edition of Schwab\u8217\'20\'19s The Invisible Life of Addie Larue.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220714ei7e00209\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
