\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 US law overrules states on abortions in medical emergencies, health secretary says\b0\par\par\uc2 Adam Gabbatt \par \uc2 578 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2022\par 00:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Biden administration says physicians must continue to offer procedure in such cases\par \par \uc2 Physicians must continue to offer abortions in cases of medical emergencies without exception, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration said on Monday, as it insisted federal law would overrule any total state bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hhs.gov/sites/default/files/emergency-medical-care-letter-to-health-care-providers.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a letter}}}\uc2  to healthcare providers, the president\u8217\'20\'19s health and human services secretary, \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2 , said the federal Emergency Medical Treatment and Active Labor Act (EMTALA) protects providers from any purported state restrictions should they be required to perform emergency abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnder the law, no matter where you live, women have the right to emergency care \u8211\'20\'13 including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care,\u8221\'20\'1D Becerra said. \u8220\'20\'1CToday, in no uncertain terms, we are reinforcing that we expect providers to continue offering these services, and that federal law preempts state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans when needed for emergency care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Becerra said medical emergencies include ectopic pregnancies, complications arising from miscarriages, and pre-eclampsia, NBC News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2022/07/11/roe-v-wade-hhs-says-physicians-must-provide-abortions-in-medical-emergencies-regardless-of-state-law.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A hospital found to have violated the federal law could be stripped of its Medicare provider status and subjected to \u8220\'20\'1Ccivil monetary penalties\u8221\'20\'1D, Becerra added.\par \par \uc2 The health secretary\u8217\'20\'19s intervention comes as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/08/joe-biden-to-sign-order-offering-protection-women-denied-right-to-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already taken effect}}}\uc2  in 13 states, with 13 more states expected to follow. The bans are taking effect after the supreme court last month overturned its landmark Roe v Wade decision that had granted federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights since 1973.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/08/joe-biden-to-sign-order-offering-protection-women-denied-right-to-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed}}}\uc2  an executive order which he said would protect access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and emergency contraception, and it aims to educate people on protecting their personal data to prevent \u8220\'20\'1Cextremist governors\u8221\'20\'1D from accessing confidential health data on phones.\par \par \uc2 As Democrats scramble to respond to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade, Senators Elizabeth Warren and Amy Klobuchar {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.klobuchar.senate.gov/public/_cache/files/d/f/dfbbacea-31dd-4f98-a74c-9ba1be7a1dd7/935CEA430B45C3FE9F9EBD598B0B37EE.letter-from-senators-klobuchar-and-warren-regarding-censoring-of-abortion-posts-7.7.2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  to the tech mogul \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2  regarding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/06/28/1108107718/instagram-and-facebook-begin-removing-posts-offering-abortion-pills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Instagram\uc2  are \u8220\'20\'1Ccensoring posts\u8221\'20\'1D that contain information about how to legally obtain \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services.\par \par \uc2 Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/06/28/1108107718/instagram-and-facebook-begin-removing-posts-offering-abortion-pills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  in June that, in the wake of the Roe v Wade decision, \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Instagram\uc2  had begun removing posts that offered \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to women who may not be able to access them\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In their letter, Warren and Klobuchar said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt is more important than ever that social media platforms not censor truthful posts about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly as people across the country turn to online communities to discuss and find information about reproductive rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats plan to hold votes this week on legislation that would preserve \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/07/11/us/politics/democrats-abortion-vote.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  on Tuesday, but with a divided Senate, any laws guaranteeing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are expected to fail.\par \par \uc2 Becerra said in his letter to medical providers: \u8220\'20\'1CIf a physician believes that a pregnant patient presenting at an emergency department, including certain labor and delivery departments, is experiencing an emergency medical condition as defined by EMTALA, and that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the stabilizing treatment necessary to resolve that condition, the physician must provide that treatment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd when a state law prohibits \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and does not include an exception for the life and health of the pregnant person \u8211\'20\'13 or draws the exception more narrowly than EMTALA\u8217\'20\'19s emergency medical condition definition \u8211\'20\'13 that state law is preempted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A majority of Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/alisondurkee/2022/06/24/how-americans-really-feel-about-abortion-the-sometimes-surprising-poll-results-as-supreme-court-reportedly-set-to-overturn-roe-v-wade/?sh=4c077ba2f3a6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 believe}}}\uc2  access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases, and last week a \uc2 Pew Research{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2022/07/06/majority-of-public-disapproves-of-supreme-courts-decision-to-overturn-roe-v-wade/?utm_source=AdaptiveMailer&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=22-7-6%20Abortion%20Attitudes%20Update_GEN%20DISTRO&org=982&lvl=100&ite=10196&lea=2141705&ctr=0&par=1&trk=a0D3j000011IIOAEA4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  found that 57% of Americans oppose the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s elimination of nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220712ei7c00231\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
