\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden in Israel as poll shows support for re-election bid at new low \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 5,600 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 July 2022\par 20:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Prices rise again as US inflation hits 40-year highJohn Bolton says he planned coups in other countries\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is in Israel, where he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/13/biden-israel-middle-east-inflation-us-politics-live?page=with:block-62cef5868f0813fe76dde337#block-62cef5868f0813fe76dde337"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reaffirmed Washington\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to one of its top allies}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, back home, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/13/biden-israel-middle-east-inflation-us-politics-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62cec0f98f08f97b5b5ce97f#block-62cec0f98f08f97b5b5ce97f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 another month of sky-high inflation data}}}\uc2  rocked the Democratic leadership and caused {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/13/biden-israel-middle-east-inflation-us-politics-live?page=with:block-62cedc058f086dba2eeb4a63#block-62cedc058f086dba2eeb4a63"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a key senator to warn}}}\uc2  he may not be on board for big spending bills as long as prices keep increasing.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 * Biden saw support for his re-election plummet {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/13/biden-israel-middle-east-inflation-us-politics-live?page=with:block-62cef2aa8f0813fe76dde2fb#block-62cef2aa8f0813fe76dde2fb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a poll}}}\uc2  that said a mere 18 percent of respondents would back him in 2024.\par \par \uc2 * A suspect was arrested in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/13/biden-israel-middle-east-inflation-us-politics-live?page=with:block-62cf1ece8f0885be5f581443#block-62cf1ece8f0885be5f581443"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 case of a girl who had to travel from Ohio to Indiana}}}\uc2  for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after being raped, refuting the doubts of Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s Republican attorney general.\par \par \uc2 * The main Senate candidates in Georgia brought in boatloads of money last quarter, though {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/13/biden-israel-middle-east-inflation-us-politics-live?page=with:block-62ceedcd8f0885be5f581227#block-62ceedcd8f0885be5f581227"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrat Raphael Warnock raised the most}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor moved to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/13/biden-israel-middle-east-inflation-us-politics-live?page=with:block-62cee8d88f0885be5f5811c1#block-62cee8d88f0885be5f5811c1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stop other states from trying to arrest people}}}\uc2  who travel there for abortions.\par \par \uc2 * The chair of the January 6 committee{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/13/biden-israel-middle-east-inflation-us-politics-live?page=with:block-62cf0ec68f086dba2eeb4cca#block-62cf0ec68f086dba2eeb4cca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dropped more hints}}}\uc2  of its cooperation with the department of justice, which could potentially charge former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with a crime.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Shortly after the supreme court overturned Roe v. Wade last month, the story of a 10-year-old girl who was forced to travel from Ohio to neighboring Indiana for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after being raped went viral.\par \par \uc2 Ohio was one of the states whose law greatly restricting access to abortions took effect after the court ruling, and news of the girl\u8217\'20\'19s ordeal sparked outrage over its consequences. However, the story had its doubters, chief among them the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican attorney general \uc2 Dave Yost\uc2 , whom the Columbus Dispatch reports gave interviews questioning whether the story happened at all.\par \par \uc2 It did indeed, the Dispatch reported today, with police arresting a 27-year-old man who confessed to twice raping the child. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dispatch.com/story/news/2022/07/13/columbus-man-charged-rape-10-year-old-led-abortion-in-indiana/10046625002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 From their story}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Gershon Fuentes, 27, whose last known address was an apartment on Columbus\u8217\'20\'19 Northwest Side, was arrested Tuesday after police say he confessed to raping the child on at least two occasions. He\u8217\'20\'19s since been charged with rape, a felony of the first degree in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 Columbus police were made aware of the girl\u8217\'20\'19s pregnancy through a referral by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dispatch.com/story/news/local/2022/02/03/columbus-police-investigating-after-15-month-old-abandoned-gas-station/6648554001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Franklin County Children Services}}}\uc2  that was made by her mother on June 22, Det. Jeffrey Huhn testified Wednesday morning at Fuentes\u8217\'20\'19 arraignment. On June 30, the girl underwent a medical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Indianapolis, Huhn said.\par \par \uc2 While Yost had plenty to say when the story first broke, the Dispatch reported he kept his comments following the arrest brief:\par \par \uc2 Ohio Attorney General \uc2 Dave Yost\uc2  questioned the validity of the account during an appearance on Fox News this week.\par \par \uc2 Yost, a Republican, told Fox News host Jesse Watters that his office had not heard \u8220\'20\'1Ca whisper\u8221\'20\'1D of a report being filed for the 10-year-old victim.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have regular contact with prosecutors and local police and sheriffs \u8212\'20\'14 not a whisper anywhere,\u8221\'20\'1D Yost said on the show.\par \par \uc2 Yost doubled down on that in an interview with the USA TODAY Network Ohio bureau on Tuesday, saying that the more time passed before confirmation made it \u8220\'20\'1Cmore likely that this is a fabrication.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know the cops and prosecutors in this state,\u8221\'20\'1D Yost said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s not one of them that wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be turning over every rock, looking for this guy and they would have charged him. They wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t leave him loose on the streets... I\u8217\'20\'19m not saying it could not have happened. What I\u8217\'20\'19m saying to you is there is not a damn scintilla of evidence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, once news of the arraignment of the Columbus man accused in the child\u8217\'20\'19s rape came, Yost issued a single sentence statement:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe rejoice anytime a child rapist is taken off the streets.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/03/ohio-indiana-abortion-rape-victim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10-year-old rape victim forced to travel from Ohio to Indiana for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports a third arrest has been made related to allegations officials mishandled election equipment in a Colorado county after the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 The case centers around Tina Peters, the clerk of Mesa county who last month lost her bid to be the Republican nominee for the position of top election official in Colorado. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-technology-arrests-colorado-voting-8ae3f1100f60463be87344d371e3f1e4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The AP reports}}}\uc2  that her election manager turned herself in earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the report:\par \par \uc2 Sandra Brown, who worked for Mesa County Clerk Tina Peters, turned herself in Monday in response to a warrant issued for her arrest on suspicion of conspiracy to commit criminal impersonation and attempting to influence a public servant, said Lt. Henry Stoffel of the Mesa County Sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s Office. The arrest was first reported by The Daily Sentinel newspaper.\par \par \uc2 Peters and her chief deputy, Belinda Knisley, are being prosecuted for allegedly allowing a copy of a hard drive to be made during an update of election equipment in May 2021. State election officials first became aware of a security breach last summer when a photo and video of confidential voting system passwords were posted on social media and a conservative website.\par \par \uc2 Peters, who has become a hero to election conspiracy theorists, following the lead of former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , lost her bid to become the GOP candidate for Colorado secretary of state last month.\par \par \uc2 Peters is charged with three counts of attempting to influence a public servant, criminal impersonation, two counts of conspiracy to commit criminal impersonation, one count of identity theft, first-degree official misconduct, violation of duty and failing to comply with the secretary of state.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  has previously covered the saga around Peters:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/29/colorado-primary-result-tina-peters-republican"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Election denier Tina Peters loses Colorado primary for top poll official}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden\u8217\'20\'19s questionable phrasing during a speech earlier this week has resulted in an apology from the first lady, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/erum-salam"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Erum Salam}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden has apologized for remarks in a speech to the civil rights and advocacy organization \uc2 UnidosUS\uc2  in which she likened the diversity of Latino Americans to breakfast tacos.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  on Monday, the first lady said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe diversity of this community \u8211\'20\'13 as distinct as the bodegas of the Bronx, as beautiful as the blossoms of Miami and as unique as the breakfast tacos here in San Antonio, is your strength.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amid condemnation of the statement, the National \uc2 Association of Hispanic Journalists{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NAHJ/status/1546646559529508865?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not tacos. Our heritage as Latinos is shaped by various diasporas, cultures and food traditions. Do not reduce us to stereotypes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary, Michael LaRosa, responded: \u8220\'20\'1CThe first lady apologizes that her words conveyed anything but pure admiration and love for the Latino community.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republicans, however, were quick to seize on the remarks.\par \par \uc2 The Texas governor, Greg Abbott, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GregAbbott_TX/status/1546895924353552385?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CBreakfast tacos? This is why Texas Hispanics are turning away from the Democratic party.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/13/jill-biden-criticized-latino-americans-remark"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We are not tacos\u8217\'20\'19: Jill Biden criticized over Latino Americans remark}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  has the latest on whether the January 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s hearings will lead to Trump facing a criminal prosecution:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is facing growing legal peril as the House January 6 committee lays out a case that appears increasingly geared to making a criminal prosecution all but inevitable.\par \par \uc2 The panel\u8217\'20\'19s seventh hearing on Tuesday argued that Trump instigated an attack on the US Capitol that was premeditated rather than spontaneous and that he cannot hide behind a defence of being \u8220\'20\'1Cwillfully blind\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The committee also sought to show an explosive convergence between Trump\u8217\'20\'19s interests and those of far-right extremist groups, although critics said the case fell short of direct collusion.\par \par \uc2 Even so, the late revelation that Trump had tried to contact a person talking to the committee about potential testimony \u8211\'20\'13 raising the prospect of witness tampering \u8211\'20\'13 was only likely to compound pressure on the Department of Justice to investigate the former president.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/13/trump-pressure-capitol-attack-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trouble for Trump as committee makes case Capitol attack was premeditated}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Chair of the January 6 committee \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  has revealed a bit more about the body\u8217\'20\'19s interactions with the justice department as it turns up more and more evidence of potentially criminal misconduct by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  around the time of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 At yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing, the House committee revealed that Trump had contacted a former witness who was working with the panel. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Thompson had to say about that:\par \par \uc2 enltrCNN's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @mkraju}}}\uc2  on Trump calling witnesses: "Is it your opinion that there's enough evidence to say that there was an attempt to intimidate these witnesses?"\par \par \uc2 1/6 Cmte Chair Thompson (D-MS): "It's highly unusual... that's why we...put that in the hands of the Justice Department." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hizi9wi4Wa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hizi9wi4Wa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1547272253926146050?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 He also talked about what of the committee\u8217\'20\'19s evidence the justice department was most interested in:\par \par \uc2 enltrBennie Thompson told us that DOJ is only interested in J6 panel's witness testimony over fake electors issue. He said they are in talks with DOJ over establishing a process for them to come in and review the records.\par \par \uc2 "That's right," he said when it was just about fake electors\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1547279939224961025?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says willing to use force on Iran as 'last resort', calls Democratic Israel foes 'wrong',\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is in Israel right now but in an interview with the country\u8217\'20\'19s Channel 12 broadcaster filed at the White House before his departure, he weighed in on the issues facing one of Washington\u8217\'20\'19s top allies in the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 The president kept the door open to using military force to stop Iran from getting a nuclear weapon, but said that would only be done as a \u8220\'20\'1Clast resort\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrEXCLUSIVE {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  interview with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/N12News?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @N12News}}}\uc2  : committed to keeping IRGC on the foreign terrorist organizations list even if it kills the deal; willing to use force \u8220\'20\'1Cas last resort\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jWjLO0SVQz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jWjLO0SVQz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Yonit Levi (@LeviYonit) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeviYonit/status/1547273246260723712?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 He also drew a line between himself and fellow Democrats who criticize aid to Israel and claim it\u8217\'20\'19s an apartheid state:\par \par \uc2 enltrMore from exclusive {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  interview with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/N12News?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @N12News}}}\uc2  : voices in the Democratic Party calling Israel an apartheid state are \u8220\'20\'1Cfew, and they are wrong\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CkX3XRkRSL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CkX3XRkRSL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Yonit Levi (@LeviYonit) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeviYonit/status/1547275658656718851?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden will on Friday travel to Saudi Arabia, but he made clear he does not expect that country to normalize relations with Israel anytime soon:\par \par \uc2 enltrNormalisation between Israel and Saudi Arabia \u8220\'20\'1Cwill take time\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/N12News?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @N12News}}}\uc2  : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4GBnv92B0A"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4GBnv92B0A}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Yonit Levi (@LeviYonit) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeviYonit/status/1547276631089287168?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , a former top advisor to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has tried again and again to delay his trial on contempt of Congress charges for ignoring a subpoena from the January 6 committee.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports that his latest bid has failed:\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: Former Trump strategist \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  makes new motion to delay his contempt of Congress trial date of July 18 \u8212\'20\'14 noting Jan. 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s mention of him at hearing yesterday. Judge Nichols though said he could seat jury and then assess if trial needed to be delayed.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1547257725649920001?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 A brief look at Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to stay out of the courtroom:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/11/steve-bannon-contempt-of-congress-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bannon suffers setback as judge rejects delaying contempt of Congress trial}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congress held two hearings today on the impact of last month\u8217\'20\'19s landmark supreme court decision overturning the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in which advocates for and against the procedure made their case to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oversight.house.gov/legislation/hearings/the-impact-of-the-supreme-court-s-dobbs-decision-on-abortion-rights-and-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.help.senate.gov/hearings/reproductive-care-in-a-post-roe-america-barriers-challenges-and-threats-to-womens-health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate}}}\uc2  lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 Here are some highlights:\par \par \uc2 A Missouri lawmaker worried the state\u8217\'20\'19s regulations would mean doctors and women alike would face jail for seeking out the procedure:\par \par \uc2 enltrMI State Sen. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MalloryMcMorrow?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @MalloryMcMorrow}}}\uc2  (D) on impact of Roe's reversal if a 1931 law making \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a felony "with no exception for age, rape, or incest" goes into effect:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNot only would doctors and medical professionals be sent to jail, but so too would countless women and girls.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/obFeJBkjLv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/obFeJBkjLv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1547233577557016576?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 And a Georgia state representative said the burden of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans would hit Black women and racial minorities the hardest:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1COur criminal legal system is really good at locking up Black and brown folks and... will likely believe Karen, but not believe Keisha when she says she had a miscarriage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Georgia State Rep. Shannon (D) on women who have miscarriages mistakenly being prosecuted for abortions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Wb7SlDKXbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Wb7SlDKXbi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1547244087086125056?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lawyer Erin Hawley, wife of Republican senator \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , batted away pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  talking points:\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s (R-MO) wife Erin Hawley, who worked with the state of Mississippi on Dobbs v. Jackson, asked how the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement is pro-women:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBabies can be female as well, so it\u8217\'20\'19s definitely pro-women in that sense.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4GPzNbvQUR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4GPzNbvQUR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1547238910748663809?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 As did Roger Marshall, Kansas\u8217\'20\'19s Republican Senator:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CMembers will imply today that carrying a baby to term is more dangerous than an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . So, using their logic, should we abort every baby? Should we stop all childbearing?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sen. Roger Marshall (R-KS) during hearing on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights following Roe v. Wade reversal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/R194o94XJo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/R194o94XJo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1547231048936857600?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Support for Biden's re-election bid plummets\par \par \uc2 More bad news for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on the polling front, where a mere 18% of respondents to a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ph.news.yahoo.com/poll-just-18-of-americans-say-biden-should-run-for-reelection-in-2024-a-new-low-140538311.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Yahoo News/YouGov poll}}}\uc2  said he should run for re-election in 2024 and 64% said he should step back in favour of another Democratic candidate.\par \par \uc2 Among Democrats, 41% said Biden should not run again, against 35% who still wanted him as president.\par \par \uc2 The result was worse than the same poll in May, when 25% of respondents said Biden should run for a second term. Among Democrats then, the figure was 49%.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s favourability rating remains stuck in the mid- to upper-30s \u8211\'20\'13 not good by any measure.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Yahoo\uc2 /YouGove poll also contained bad news for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , who was supported by just 19% of Democrats and Democratic-leaning independents to run in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s stead \u8211\'20\'13 behind doubty campaigners \u8220\'20\'1C someone else \u8221\'20\'1D (20%) and \u8220\'20\'1C not sure \u8221\'20\'1D (30%).\par \par \uc2 Biden has said he will run again but he is already the oldest president ever inaugurated and will turn 82 shortly after the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 He has also faced his fair share of crises in his short time in office, from the economic and physical effects of the coronavirus pandemic to the threat to democracy posed by his Republican opponents, and from the chaotic withdrawal from Afghanistan to Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine and its effects on gas prices, food supplies and more.\par \par \uc2 Such a roster of challenges would, it seems fair to say, challenge most non-Biden candidates the Democrats might be able to find.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Ross Barkan with more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jul/13/democrats-2024-biden-alternative"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden is deeply unpopular. But can Democrats find an alternative for 2024? | Ross Barkan}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  has said the US is committed to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  security, on arriving in Tel Aviv for the first leg of a three-day visit to the Middle East, a trip focused on deepening the majority Jewish state\u8217\'20\'19s ties with the Arab world as the region faces a common foe in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/iran"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iran}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The president was greeted by the Israeli president, \uc2 Isaac Herzog\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/20/israel-set-for-general-election-after-pm-announces-coalition-will-disband"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 caretaker prime minister, Yair Lapid}}}\uc2 , on Air Force One\u8217\'20\'19s arrival at Ben Gurion airport on Wednesday afternoon, fist-bumping rather than shaking hands with Israeli officials on the tarmac over what the White House said was concern over rising Covid cases.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s trip, senior Israeli officials briefed reporters that the two countries will issue a broad-ranging communique titled the \u8220\'20\'1CJerusalem Declaration\u8221\'20\'1D, which will take a tough stance on Iran\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear programme, and reaffirm Israel\u8217\'20\'19s right to defend itself.\par \par \uc2 In his opening remarks, Biden recalled that his first visit to the country had been as a young senator in 1973, just a few weeks before the Yom Kippur war with Egypt and Syria broke out. At that time, Israel and imperial Iran were still allies, and Egypt and Jordan were still hostile to the majority Jewish state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll continue to advance Israel\u8217\'20\'19s integration into the region and the relationship between the US and Israel is deeper and stronger in my view than it\u8217\'20\'19s ever been,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 Air Force One will make a first direct flight from Israel to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/saudiarabia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saudi Arabia}}}\uc2  amid efforts to build a relationship between the Jewish state and the conservative Gulf kingdom, which does not officially recognise Israel\u8217\'20\'19s existence.\par \par \uc2 Full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/13/biden-commits-to-israels-security-as-he-embarks-on-middle-east-tour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden commits to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s security as he embarks on Middle East tour}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Another sentence has been handed down against a January 6 rioter, in this case a Maryland man who pled guilty to charges related to striking a police officer with a lacrosse stick that had a Confederate battle flag attached.\par \par \uc2 He was ordered to serve five months in prison, according to the AP:\par \par \uc2 U.S. District Judge Christopher Cooper also sentenced David Alan Blair, to 18 months of supervised release after his prison term and ordered him to pay $2,000 in restitution, said William Miller, a spokesman for the U.S. Attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office for the District of Columbia.\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors recommended sentencing Blair to eight months in prison followed by three years of supervised release.\par \par \uc2 Blair\u8217\'20\'19s attorney, Terrell Roberts III, asked for a sentence of probation.\par \par \uc2 Blair, 27, left his home in Clarksburg, Maryland, and started driving to Washington, D.C., after the riot erupted at the Capitol on Jan. 6, 2021. Shortly before 6 p.m., Blair encountered a line of Metropolitan Police Department officers on the Capitol\u8217\'20\'19s West Lawn and refused to heed their commands to leave the area, prosecutors said.\par \par \uc2 A police officer\u8217\'20\'19s body camera captured Blair walking in front of the police line and yelling, \u8220\'20\'1CHell naw. Quit backing up. Don\u8217\'20\'19t be scared. We\u8217\'20\'19re Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Blair was arrested after he pushed his lacrosse stick against an officer\u8217\'20\'19s chest.\par \par \uc2 The officer responded to the push by striking Blair three times in the head with a baton, drawing blood and giving him a concussion, according to Blair\u8217\'20\'19s attorney.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 The race for the Senate seat in Georgia currently occupied by Democrat \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  is among those considered pivotal to deciding who controls the chamber following November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, and the incumbent seems to be prevailing, at least when it comes to money.\par \par \uc2 As the Associated Press reports, Warnock raised $17.2 million in the second quarter running from April through June, much more than the $6.2 million Republican \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  brought in.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-biden-entertainment-stacey-abrams-herschel-walker-81744050782976ddfab73f2a7a3fdf67"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 From the AP\u8217\'20\'19s report}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The dueling Senate campaign numbers underlined two truths. Georgia is again going to be one of the most expensive races to run for office in 2022, and Democrats are building a strong fundraising advantage.\par \par \uc2 Like Warnock, Democrat \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  heavily outraised incumbent Republican \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  in the race for governor, collecting almost $50 million compared to the $31 million Kemp has brought in over a longer period. Abrams and Warnock plan to run closely linked campaigns, echoing many of the same themes.\par \par \uc2 Warnock is one of several Democratic Senate incumbents in swing states who is trying to cling to their seat amid President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s deep unpopularity. Republicans had long dominated statewide races until Georgia helped elect Biden to the presidency and enabled Democrats to control the Senate by electing Warnock and fellow Democrat \uc2 Jon Ossoff\uc2  in a January 2021 runoff.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.michigan.gov/whitmer/news/press-releases/2022/07/13/whitmer-signs-executive-order-refusing-to-extradite-those-seeking-reproductive-freedom-in-michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed an executive order}}}\uc2  preventing women who travel to Michigan for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from being extradited to other states where seeking the procedure is illegal.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s how she described the order, which also protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in the state from extradition:\par \par \uc2 I will stand up for all women, even if their local and statewide leaders refuse to. Michigan must remain a place where a person\u8217\'20\'19s basic rights are preserved. In this existential moment for fundamental rights, it is incumbent on every elected official who believes that health\u8212\'20\'14not politics\u8212\'20\'14should guide medical decisions to take bold action.\par \par \uc2 Whitmer said the move was in response to attempts by Republican lawmakers to pass laws criminalizing out-of-state travel by women seeking abortions. Her order was similar to one made by Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Jared Polis\uc2 , who banned state agencies from cooperating with investigations into abortions by other states.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/07/colorado-governor-executive-order-protect-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Colorado governor issues executive order to protect \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican Senator \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  is a sponsor of legislation to keep transgender children out of sports, and at a hearing yesterday, one of his critics took the opportunity to tell him what she thought of his questions, as \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/adam-gabbatt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adam Gabbatt}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , a Republican senator from Missouri, was accused of being transphobic by a law professor on Tuesday, at a hearing on the consequences of the supreme court decision to overturn Roe v Wade, the ruling which guaranteed the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 During the judiciary committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/meetings/a-post-roe-america-the-legal-consequences-of-the-dobbs-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hearing}}}\uc2 , Hawley, who has previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lee.senate.gov/2021/2/sen-lee-leads-legislation-to-protect-women-s-sports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 co-sponsored a bill}}}\uc2  which would prevent transgender children from competing in sports, questioned Khiara Bridges, a professor at UC Berkeley School of Law who was invited to testify on reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ve referred to \u8216\'20\'18people with a capacity for pregnancy\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWould that be women?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/13/republican-josh-hawley-transphobia-berkeley-professor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican Josh Hawley accused of transphobia at Senate hearing}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in Congress, Punchbowl News has reported a strong comment from House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  during a meeting with Democrats this morning:\par \par \uc2 enltrPELOSI in closed House Dem caucus meeting this am: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Republicans are not capable of governing a democracy\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1547216949414871040?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 She also took a stab at forecasting when peak US inflation might be reached, a notoriously difficult thing to nail down:\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden told me this back in December. "I think it's the peak of the crisis.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/i64IjN8nlH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/i64IjN8nlH}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1547227243704975361?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator Joe Manchin, a crucial swing vote for Democrats hoping to get any major legislation through Congress before the end of the year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.manchin.senate.gov/newsroom/press-releases/manchin-statement-on-91-inflation-rate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has issued a statement}}}\uc2  warning against big spending plans at a time of high inflation.\par \par \uc2 It reads in part:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor more than a year, leaders in Washington have ignored the serious concerns raised by myself and others about the rising cost of inflation. While Washington seems to now understand this reality, it is time for us to work together to get unnecessary spending under control, produce more energy at home and take more active and serious steps to address this record inflation that now poses a clear and present danger to our economy. No matter what spending aspirations some in Congress may have, it is clear to anyone who visits a grocery store or a gas station that we cannot add any more fuel to this inflation fire.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Consider it something of a warning shot as Democrats look to pass a major spending package in what could be their final months controlling the House and Senate. Manchin cited his concerns about inflation last year when he torpedoed Build Back Better, a spending plan proposed by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to address a range of Democratic priorities, including fighting climate change, which ultimately collapsed after months of negotiations. In recent days, details have leaked out about a renewed effort to reach an agreement that can pass with only Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 votes via the reconciliation process. But with his statement, the West Virginia senator, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/31/joe-manchin-hold-climate-policy-hostage-to-benefit-his-financial-interests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who has a deep involvement in the coal industry}}}\uc2 , has reminded the party\u8217\'20\'19s leaders that he won\u8217\'20\'19t be an easy man to convince.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Planning a coup isn\u8217\'20\'19t for amateurs, ok? That was the argument Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former national security advisor \uc2 John Bolton\uc2  decided to make after yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s January 6 committee hearing, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 John Bolton\uc2 , a former national security adviser to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and before that ambassador to the United Nations under \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , said on Tuesday he helped plan coup attempts in other countries.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to CNN after the day\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/12/january-6-hearing-trump-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6 committee hearing}}}\uc2 , Bolton said it was wrong to describe Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to stay in power after the 2020 election as a coup.\par \par \uc2 Bolton with Trump, his former employer. Photograph: Justin Lane/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1CWhile nothing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did after the election, in connection with the lie about the election fraud, none of it is defensible, it\u8217\'20\'19s also a mistake as some people have said including on the committee, the commentators that somehow this was a carefully planned coup d\u8217\'20\'19etat to the constitution.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/13/john-bolton-planned-coups-donald-trump-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 John Bolton says he \u8216\'20\'18helped plan coups d\u8217\'20\'19etat\u8217\'20\'19 in other countries}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Details are trickling out about the January 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s next hearing, which \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports is set to take place Thursday of next week during the prime-time TV hour:\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: Sources tell me that the Jan. 6 committee is currently expected to do the final hearing of this \u8220\'20\'1Cseries\u8221\'20\'1D of hearings \u8212\'20\'14 how Trump did nothing during the 187mins of the Capitol attack \u8212\'20\'14 next week Thursday in prime time, confirming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alivitali?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @alivitali}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1546986475388018690?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 12, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Committee member \uc2 Stephanie Murphy\uc2  gave a hint of what to expect in an interview with MSNBC this morning:\par \par \uc2 enltr1/6 committee member \uc2 Stephanie Murphy\uc2  (D-FL) says the next hearing will focus on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s inaction during the 187-minute Capitol insurrection:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe next hearing will be about... what the president did, and, more importantly, what he didn\u8217\'20\'19t do.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KPqNbRCje8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/KPqNbRCje8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1547216749430439937?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Inflation numbers 'out-of-date', don't reflect price decreases, Biden says\par \par \uc2 The latest inflation figures are certainly bad, but President Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/07/13/president-biden-statement-on-cpi-inflation-in-june/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has just issued a statement}}}\uc2  arguing that the situation is better than it appears because gas prices have declined since the data was collected. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the meat of his argument:\par \par \uc2 While today\u8217\'20\'19s headline inflation reading is unacceptably high, it is also out-of-date. Energy alone comprised nearly half of the monthly increase in inflation. Today\u8217\'20\'19s data does not reflect the full impact of nearly 30 days of decreases in gas prices, that have reduced the price at the pump by about 40 cents since mid-June. Those savings are providing important breathing room for American families. And, other commodities like wheat have fallen sharply since this report.\par \par \uc2 Importantly, today\u8217\'20\'19s report shows that what economists call annual \u8220\'20\'1Ccore inflation\u8221\'20\'1D came down for the third month in a row, and is the first month since last year where the annual \u8220\'20\'1Ccore\u8221\'20\'1D inflation rate is below six percent.\par \par \uc2 Jason Furman\uc2 , a former top economic advisor to Democratic president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  might take issue with Biden\u8217\'20\'19s characterization of core inflation. He shared several thoughts about the latest report on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , which he described as \u8220\'20\'1Cbrutal\u8221\'20\'1D overall:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe 12-month core CPI fell from 6.0% in the year through May to 5.9% in the year through June. But don't get too excited--this is probably not telling you what you think it is.\par \par \uc2 All it says is that core inflation in the month of June-22 was slightly lower than it was in June-21.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jason Furman\uc2  (@jasonfurman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jasonfurman/status/1547215890067755008?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIt is more relevant to look at one month changes or, if you're worried about noise, three month changes. In June core CPI increased at a nearly 9% annual rate. Over the last three months it was about an 8% annual rate. Those are both up. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Ee9dwMRgsj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Ee9dwMRgsj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jason Furman\uc2  (@jasonfurman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jasonfurman/status/1547215895272951808?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 This may best sum up the damage done by the inflation wave to Americans:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe decline in real average hourly earnings at this point is terrible, the fastest pace of decline in 40 years. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/92rKJFtQRD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/92rKJFtQRD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jason Furman\uc2  (@jasonfurman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jasonfurman/status/1547205450046767105?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 If you missed it, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  has a look at what happened during yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing of the House committee investigating the January 6 attack, which painted a distressing picture of former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s willingness to resort to violence following his 2020 election loss:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe settle our differences at the ballot box.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , chairman of the congressional committee investigating the January 6 attack on the US Capitol, emphasised this article of faith in his opening remarks on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 But what followed was a three-hour story about how American democracy, like a rickety old house, creaked and bent and struggled to hold itself together during a thunderstorm of political violence.\par \par \uc2 There was the tale of an Oval Office meeting that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/12/january-6-hearings-testimony-cipollone-meeting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 almost ended in fisticuffs}}}\uc2 . There was testimony from a former true believer in the \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D who joined the rampage at the Capitol. There were predictions that if Trump runs again, no one will be safe.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/12/january-6-hearing-trump-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6 testimony tells chilling tale of democracy hanging by a thread}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biggest 12-month US inflation increase since 1981, data shows\par \par \uc2 Americans looking for relief from the country\u8217\'20\'19s inflation spike did not find it in June, the latest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/cpi.nr0.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data from the Labor Department}}}\uc2  confirmed.\par \par \uc2 The consumer price index rose 9.1% last month compared to June 2021, its biggest 12-month increase since the same period in November 1981. It even accelerated compared to May, rising 1.3% compared to that month\u8217\'20\'19s one percent increase.\par \par \uc2 Dig deeper into the numbers and you\u8217\'20\'19ll see a story of frustration and financial pain for people across the country. Grocery prices were up one percent compared to May and 10.4% over the prior 12 months. Gasoline prices have increased 59.9% over the past 12 months and 11.2% in June alone.\par \par \uc2 Washington\u8217\'20\'19s inflation fighter, the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 , may respond to this report with another big interest rate increase later in July to cut into the demand drivers of inflation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jun/15/interest-rate-us-latest-increase-federal-reserve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as they did at their meeting last month}}}\uc2 . Biden has already seen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/14/biden-approval-ratings-plunge-inflation-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 inflation wreck his approval rating}}}\uc2 , but can hope that if {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/02/biden-saudi-arabia-oil-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saudi Arabia agrees to bring more oil}}}\uc2  onto the market, the price of gasoline, an important contributor to inflation, will decline. Meanwhile, there\u8217\'20\'19s evidence the gas price surge is already receding:\par \par \uc2 enltr29 days straight of declining {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gasprices?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gasprices}}}\uc2  ! We\u8217\'20\'19re now down 40c/gal from the peak with Americans spending $150 million LESS on gasoline today alone vs June 14. National average $4.634/gal with over 10,000 stations at $3.99 or less. We will fall under $4.60 by the weekend.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Patrick De Haan ???? (@GasBuddyGuy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GasBuddyGuy/status/1547203544150851584?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden begins tough Middle East trip with US inflation as bad as ever\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics reader. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has just landed in Israel for the first visit to the Middle East of his presidency, but even there, he won\u8217\'20\'19t be able to escape the troubling state of the US economy. Inflation soared 9.1% in June compared to the same month last year, the government reported just minutes ago, and indeed, that problem will be on the agenda during his visit - convincing Saudi Arabia to raise oil production in a bid to lower gas prices in America is considered one of the president\u8217\'20\'19s priorities.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 * The Senate health committee will at 10 am eastern time be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.help.senate.gov/hearings/reproductive-care-in-a-post-roe-america-barriers-challenges-and-threats-to-womens-health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hearing from health care providers}}}\uc2  impacted by last month\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court ruling overturning the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/07/13/upshot/poll-2022-midterms-congress.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A new poll}}}\uc2  shows Democrats and Republicans are in a close race when it comes to which party voters would prefer controlling Congress.\par \par \uc2 * With Biden set to visit Saudi Arabia, Hanan Elatr Khashoggi, widow of murdered journalist Jamal Khashoggi, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsnationnow.com/world/khashoggis-widow-during-wh-visit-free-saudi-political-prisoners-stepson/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said she had met with White House advisors}}}\uc2  and called on the US president to press Riyadh\u8217\'20\'19s leadership for the release of political prisoners.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220713ei7d001xm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
