\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  urges voters to elect a \u8216\'20\'18pro-choice Congress\u8217\'20\'19 in midterms\b0\par\par\uc2 Oliver Laughland \par \uc2 612 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 July 2022\par 18:09 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Vice-president highlights that down-ballot contests at local level would also be central to restoring \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  renewed pleas to voters ahead of the midterm congressional races to elect pro-choice candidates, as the Biden administration continues to face criticism from progressives over a perceived lackluster response to the recent landmark supreme court decision striking down federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with CBS News on Sunday, Harris urged voters to elect a \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-choice Congress\u8221\'20\'1D in November and highlighted that down-ballot contests at the local level would also be central to restoring \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in certain parts of the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t have to advocate or believe that this is right for you or your family, but don\u8217\'20\'19t let the government make the decision for her family, whoever she may be,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said in a pre-recorded interview. \u8220\'20\'1CIt means state offices, governors, secretaries of state, attorneys general. It means local races, who\u8217\'20\'19s going to be your DA, who\u8217\'20\'19s going to be your sheriff, enforcing laws that are being passed to criminalize medical health providers, and maybe even the women who seek the service.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Friday, \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/08/joe-biden-to-sign-order-offering-protection-women-denied-right-to-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed a limited executive order}}}\uc2  designed to protect access to reproductive health services by expanding access to emergency contraception and bolstering legal services to support people who cross state lines to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But for many \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates and progressive Democrats, the president\u8217\'20\'19s measures do not go far enough. The administration has, for example, resisted calls to use federal land in anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  states to facilitate terminating pregnancies, or subsidizing travel to people forced to travel in order to access services.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/07/08/1110455155/abortion-rights-biden-executive-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 At least nine}}}\uc2  US states have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the wake of 6-3 supreme court ruling that overturned the Roe v Wade decision that had enshrined the procedure as a constitutional right since 1973. The ruling makes it likely that around half the country \u8211\'20\'13 26 states \u8211\'20\'13 will eventually outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in some way.\par \par \uc2 The decision followed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s installation of three rightwing justices to the supreme court, paving the way for a conservative super majority on the court.\par \par \uc2 Harris, then a US senator, voted against the former president\u8217\'20\'19s appointments of \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and Amy Coney Barrett. And she said on Sunday she had never believed assurances made in private and public by Gorsuch and Kavanaugh that they respected the precedence of the Roe decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI start from the point of experience of having served in the Senate,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CI never believed them. I didn\u8217\'20\'19t believe them. So I voted against.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked if the Democrats should have done more to enshrine the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  into federal law when the party controlled both chambers of Congress, Harris responded: \u8220\'20\'1CWe certainly believe that certain issues are just settled. Certain issues are just settled. And that\u8217\'20\'19s why I do believe that we are living, sadly, in real unsettled times.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats have faced criticism for fundraising drives off the back of the supreme court decision and recent polling indicates their party still faces a tough day at the ballot box in November, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval ratings plummeting}}}\uc2  and the party looking set to lose its majority in the House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, Harris sought to quell calls for Biden to serve just one term as president before allowing a new Democratic nominee to contest the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CListen to President Biden,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe intends to run. And if he does, I intend to run with him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220710ei7a0028l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
