\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Restoring US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  access won\u8217\'20\'19t be easy \u8211\'20\'13 but we need leaders who will try\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,104 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 July 2022\par 13:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democracy isn\u8217\'20\'19t just about turning up to the polls every couple of years, it\u8217\'20\'19s about constantly pushing your representatives and leaders to do better\par \par \uc2 Extra, extra, Democrats finally do something\par \par \uc2 After several weeks of twiddling their thumbs, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://slate.com/news-and-politics/2022/06/dobbs-decision-nancy-pelosi-poem-response.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reciting poems}}}\uc2 , and breaking out {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.independent.co.uk/tv/us-news/democrats-god-bless-america-roe-v-wade-b2109015.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 into song}}}\uc2 , the Democrats have finally done something halfway useful about the rightwing assault on reproductive rights. On Friday \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/08/joe-biden-to-sign-order-offering-protection-women-denied-right-to-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed an executive order}}}\uc2  safeguarding access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills and contraception. The executive order obviously doesn\u8217\'20\'19t restore the nationwide right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  (the president alone doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have the power to do that), but it does set out a plan of action. Of particular note is a provision that would seem to protect women who travel out of state to get the procedure done.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s great to see the White House finally do something tangible to try and protect reproductive rights, but why has it taken them this long? Roe was overturned two weeks ago. The draft opinion overruling Roe v Wade was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/first-edition-abortion-rights-leak-roe-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked more than two months ago. }}}\uc2  The Biden administration knew what was coming; they were gifted time to prepare and they squandered it. They should have been ready to spring into action the moment Roe was overturned \u8211\'20\'13 instead, it seemed like they were taken by surprise by the whole thing. There have been a lot of entreaties by Democrats over the last couple of weeks to \u8220\'20\'1Cvote!\u8221\'20\'1D but not much else.\par \par \uc2 Well, actually, that\u8217\'20\'19s not entirely true. Some top establishment Democrats, including \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , have been very busy throwing their weight behind {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msnbc.com/the-reidout/reidout-blog/henry-cuellar-nancy-pelosi-abortion-rcna34732"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Henry Cuellar}}}\uc2 , the last anti-choice House Democrat, in the primary for Texas\u8217\'20\'19s 28th congressional district. I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure exactly what makes the gun-loving, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -hating Cuellar a Democrat, because he seems to have basically all the same policy positions as a Republican, but he has a (D) next to his name. Even when they knew Roe was on the verge of being overturned, top House Democrats chose to help Cuellar \u8211\'20\'13 the incumbent \u8211\'20\'13 fend off a challenge from Jessica Cisneros, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jessicacisnerosforcongress.com/issues/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pro-choice}}}\uc2  progressive. In the end Cuellar won by just 289 votes. The Democrats have the gall to send out fundraising emails demanding people vote for them so they can safeguard our reproductive rights while simultaneously spending donor money to help prop up an anti-choice Democrat. It truly beggars belief. As \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1529303844030754816?s=20&t=KpIIOpYrz9Rhndie6iBPDg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stated on Twitter}}}\uc2 , Democrats rallying for \u8220\'20\'1Ca pro-NRA, anti-choice incumbent \u8230\'20\'26 was an utter failure of leadership\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Ocasio-Cortez gets a lot of flak for calling out members of her own party. Progressives, in general, are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jacobin.com/2020/08/joe-biden-rahm-emanuel-democratic-party-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 frequently told to shut up}}}\uc2  and fall in line if they don\u8217\'20\'19t want to imperil the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 chance of success at the next election. But do you think Biden would have signed an executive order on Friday if the Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/07/08/biden-abortion-executive-order-00044647"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hadn\u8217\'20\'19t been facing a lot of criticism}}}\uc2  for doing nothing? Of course not. Democracy isn\u8217\'20\'19t just about turning up to the polls every couple of years, it\u8217\'20\'19s about constantly pushing your representatives and leaders to do better; it\u8217\'20\'19s about constantly holding them to account.\par \par \uc2 AOC is not perfect by any means, but she is one of the few Democrats to actually show the leadership we need for this political and cultural moment. We are in a crisis and we need fighters\u8211\'20\'13 we need people with energy and ideas. After Roe was overturned, Ocasio-Cortez was one of the only Democrats who actually spoke up with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1541111717140234241?s=20&t=Ujnk4ro8OtCLfbKJ0NQV_w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 concrete ideas}}}\uc2  about what to do next. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can at least TRY,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1541111717140234241?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1541111717140234241%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.newsweek.com%2Fseven-ways-democrats-can-fight-back-against-roe-v-wade-being-overturned-aoc-1719398"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she tweeted}}}\uc2 . And that, I think, is the key point here. We are well aware that restoring nationwide access to abortions is not going to be easy but we need leaders who will at least TRY.\par \par \uc2 Women accused of illegal abortions in the UK after miscarriages and stillbirths\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re in the UK and looking on at what is happening in the US with horror, it\u8217\'20\'19s worth remembering that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights aren\u8217\'20\'19t set in stone in the UK either; \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  still technically hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been decriminalised in England and Wales. Indeed, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/02/women-accused-of-abortions-in-england-and-wales-after-miscarriages-and-stillbirths"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dozens of investigations}}}\uc2  into illegal abortions have been launched by the police during the past decade into suspected breaches of an 1861 law, which says is unlawful to procure a miscarriage using \u8220\'20\'1Cpoison\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Can instrument\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cother means whatsoever.\u8221\'20\'1D In one case, a 15-year-old girl who had an unexplained stillbirth was subjected to a year-long criminal investigation before the coroner concluded the pregnancy ended because of natural causes.\par \par \uc2 A male demographer wants to tax the childfree\par \par \uc2 The UK should {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jul/04/population-crisis-britain-paul-morland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fix its declining birth rates}}}\uc2  by introducing \u8220\'20\'1Ca \u8216\'20\'18negative child benefit\u8217\'20\'19 tax for those who do not have offspring,\u8221\'20\'1D an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffingtonpost.co.uk/entry/sunday-times-article-tax-childless_uk_62c2a896e4b00a9334ea7083"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oxford academic recently opined}}}\uc2 . This did not go down well for obvious reasons.\par \par \uc2 Antigua ban on same-sex acts ruled unconstitutional\par \par \uc2 There are hopes that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.com/news/world-latin-america-62068589"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 high court ruling}}}\uc2  could spur change in neighbouring islands.\par \par \uc2 Steakhouse defends Kavanaugh\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18right to eat dinner\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday supreme court justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  enjoyed dinner (and, one imagines, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.buzzfeednews.com/article/skbaer/brett-kavanaugh-likes-beer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 few beers}}}\uc2  ) at Morton\u8217\'20\'19s Steakhouse in DC Protesters gathered outside forcing Kavanaugh \u8211\'20\'13 you\u8217\'20\'19re never going to believe how awful this is \u8211\'20\'13 to exit through a backdoor. I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure how he will ever recover from the trauma of this but at least he\u8217\'20\'19s got Morton\u8217\'20\'19s to help him through it. The steakhouse {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/regulation/court-battles/3549907-mortons-condemns-abortion-rights-protestors-for-disrupting-kavanaughs-freedom-to-eat-dinner/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued a statement}}}\uc2  saying that politics \u8220\'20\'1Cshould not trample the freedom at play of the right to congregate and eat dinner.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Upside-down bikinis are a trend now, apparently\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/fashion/2022/jul/08/upside-down-bikinis-the-trend-made-popular-by-love-island-and-the-kardashians"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Searches for the style}}}\uc2  rose 203% within the last month.\par \par \uc2 How police reforms improved the way officers treat women in India\par \par \uc2 About four women in ten in India experience intimate-partner violence \u8211\'20\'13 and the police are often less than helpful thanks to institutional misogyny. However, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-022-01857-y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new analysis of criminal justice reforms}}}\uc2  found that putting dedicated women\u8217\'20\'19s help desks in police stations results in the police taking violence against women more seriously.\par \par \uc2 The week in penguinarchy\par \par \uc2 Inflation is hurting everyone, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/penguins-japan-aquarium-refuse-cheaper-fish-1722984"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 even penguins}}}\uc2 . A zoo in Japan has started feeding its penguins budget fish because the fancy mackerel they were previously fed has gone up by 30%. The animals are not impressed and are quite literally turning their noses up at it. I had no idea penguins had such so-fish-ticated palates.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arwa Mahdawi\u8217\'20\'19s new book, Strong Female Lead, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://linktr.ee/ARWAMAHDAWI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 available for order}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220709ei79001jm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
