\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  signs executive order protecting access to  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith Washington bureau chief \par \uc2 913 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 July 2022\par 21:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 34\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Move by president signals start of White House fightback after supreme court struck down Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has signed an executive order offering protections to millions of American women denied the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The move signals the start of a White House fightback after the supreme court last month {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , its landmark ruling that for half a century had legalised \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 In a White House address on Friday, the president condemned the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision as \u8220\'20\'1Cterrible, extreme and I think so totally wrong-headed\u8221\'20\'1D and not a constitutional judgment but \u8220\'20\'1Can exercise in raw political power\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 With multiple states already imposing harsh restrictions, Biden outlined an executive order that will safeguard access to reproductive healthcare services, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and contraception. This includes access to medication abortions, also known as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plannedparenthood.org/learn/abortion/the-abortion-pill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills}}}\uc2 , approved by the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Among the provisions is a plan for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/merrick-garland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Merrick Garland}}}\uc2 , the attorney general, and \uc2 Dana Remus\uc2 , the White House counsel, to convene private pro bono lawyers, bar associations and public interest organisations to encourage \u8220\'20\'1Crobust legal representation of patients, providers and third parties lawfully seeking or offering reproductive health care services throughout the country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Such representation could include protecting the right to travel out of state to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Biden and Garland have vowed to oppose any state or local official who attempts to interfere with women exercising that right.\par \par \uc2 In addition, the executive order is designed to promote \u8220\'20\'1Cthe safety and security of patients, providers and clinics\u8221\'20\'1D. A how-to guide for consumers will explain steps to ensure they are protecting their personal data on mobile apps amid fears that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/02/abortion-tech-companies-data-police-privacy?curator=MediaREDEF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state officials could try to track}}}\uc2  and prosecute them.\par \par \uc2 Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s an increasing concern that extremist governors and others will try to get that data off of your phone which is out there in the ether to find what you\u8217\'20\'19re seeking, where you\u8217\'20\'19re going and what you\u8217\'20\'19re doing with regard to your healthcare. Talk about no privacy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis executive order asks the FTC [\uc2 Federal Trade Commission\uc2 ] to crackdown on data brokers that sell private information to extreme groups.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An interagency taskforce will coordinate federal government efforts to protect reproductive rights. Garland will provide technical assistance to states affording legal protection to out-of-state patients as well as providers who offer legal reproductive health care.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade two weeks ago was a seismic shock to the political system that left elected officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/jun/26/us-supreme-court-abortion-ruling-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scrambling to respond}}}\uc2 . The president noted that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans have taken effect in 13 states with 12 additional states likely to following in the coming weeks. They will disproportionately affect women of colour, low-income women and rural women.\par \par \uc2 Flanked by vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and health secretary \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2 , Biden warned: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19re witnessing is a giant step backwards in much of our country \u8230\'20\'26 Some of these states don\u8217\'20\'19t allow for exceptions for rape or incest. This isn\u8217\'20\'19t some imagined horror. It\u8217\'20\'19s already happening.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president became visibly angry as he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/03/ohio-indiana-abortion-rape-victim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted recent media reports}}}\uc2  that a 10-year-old rape victim in Ohio who was six weeks pregnant and ineligible for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in her own state was forced to travel to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/indiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Indiana}}}\uc2  for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA 10-year old girl should be forced to give birth to a rapist\u8217\'20\'19s child? I can tell you what I know. I can\u8217\'20\'19t think of anything that\u8217\'20\'19s much more extreme. The court\u8217\'20\'19s decision has already been received by Republicans in Congress as a green light to go further and pass a national ban \u8230\'20\'26 That would mean the right to choose will be illegal nationwide if, in fact they succeed. Let me tell you something. As long as I\u8217\'20\'19m president, it won\u8217\'20\'19t happen because I\u8217\'20\'19ll veto it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Louisiana on Friday, a New Orleans judge let dissolve a 27 June order temporarily blocking the enforcement of laws banning virtually all abortions in the state after the reversal of Roe.\par \par \uc2 Biden has been criticised for failing to push back hard enough to defend \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Friday\u8217\'20\'19s executive order might buy him some time, but is necessarily limited in scope. He acknowledged as much in his remarks as he urged Congress to codify Roe as federal law \u8211\'20\'13 which in turns depends on November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, in which Democrats are widely expected to perform poorly.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe court now practically dares the women of America to go to the ballot box and restore the very rights they\u8217\'20\'19ve just taken away,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think the court or, for that matter, Republicans who for decades have pushed the extreme agenda have a clue about the power of American women. But they\u8217\'20\'19re about to find out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2022/07/06/majority-of-public-disapproves-of-supreme-courts-decision-to-overturn-roe-v-wade/?utm_source=AdaptiveMailer&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=22-7-6%20Abortion%20Attitudes%20Update_GEN%20DISTRO&org=982&lvl=100&ite=10196&lea=2141705&ctr=0&par=1&trk=a0D3j000011IIOAEA4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pew Research Center survey}}}\uc2  published this week found that 57% of adults disapprove of the court\u8217\'20\'19s sweeping decision, while 41% approve. Public support for legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains largely unchanged {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/2022/05/06/americas-abortion-quandary/?utm_source=AdaptiveMailer&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=22-7-6%20Abortion%20Attitudes%20Update_GEN%20DISTRO&org=982&lvl=100&ite=10196&lea=2141705&ctr=0&par=1&trk=a0D3j000011IIOAEA4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 since before the decision}}}\uc2 , with 62% saying it should be legal in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 Biden concluded: \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot allow an out-of-control supreme court, working in conjunction with extremist elements of the Republican party, to take away freedoms and our personal autonomy. The choice we face as a nation is between the mainstream and the extreme.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220708ei78001h1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
