\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden signs executive order to protect US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  access and urges Americans to \u8216\'20\'18vote, vote, vote\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 3,397 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 July 2022\par 20:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US president says electing senators who would help codify Roe v Wade is the \u8216\'20\'18fastest route\u8217\'20\'19 to solidifying federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rightsSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today! Here\u8217\'20\'19s a wrap up of everything that happened, US politics-wise:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to signed an executive order to protect access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reproductive healthcare services after the rollback of Roe v wade, urging Americans to elect pro-choice senators during the midterm elections this November.\par \par \uc2 * Biden spoke critically of the conservative-leaning Supreme court, accusing the justices who voted to overturn Roe v wade of \u8220\'20\'1Cplaying fast and loose with the facts\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * Democrats generally applauded Biden\u8217\'20\'19s order, but urged him to do more amid nationwide rollbacks of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 * US politicians published statements of condolences after the assassination of former Japanese prime minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2 , including Biden, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The US job market added over 300,000 jobs in June, a sign of economic resilience amid slowed growth.\par \par \uc2 Thank you for reading!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 In other news, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/useconomy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy}}}\uc2  added 372,000 jobs in June, an sign of economic resilience despite signs of slowed economic growth.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19re more information from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwardhelmore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edward Helmore}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/useconomy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy}}}\uc2  added 372,000 jobs in June, an indicator of resilience despite signs of slowing economic growth.\par \par \uc2 The jobs reports is seen as a key indicator on whether high inflation \u8211\'20\'13 and central bank efforts to tame it with interest rates rises \u8211\'20\'13 is beginning to bite down on the wider American economy.\par \par \uc2 The US unemployment rate held steady at 3.6%, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jun/03/job-growth-us-may-unemployment-rate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the same as month earlier}}}\uc2 , the labor department said on Friday. Job growth far exceeded the projections of economists, who expected the US to add roughly 278,000 jobs last month, according to consensus estimates.\par \par \uc2 The figures may ease some fears of a looming recession, but also show that the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  has more room to raise interest rates, cooling consumer demand, in its fight against historically high inflation.\par \par \uc2 Read the full article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/08/us-jobs-report-june-unemployment-rate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/08/us-jobs-report-june-unemployment-rate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US adds 372,000 jobs in June as growth exceeds expectations}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Several Democrats have responded to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s executive order, calling the order a good first step but urging Biden to do more to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights federally, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/minutes/congress/07-8-2022/pushing-for-more/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports Politico}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 From Massachusetts senator Elizabeth Warren:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  ' executive order will help Americans receive the reproductive health care they need. I urged the Biden administration to expand access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , protect patient privacy, and safeguard interstate travel for care. Today's actions are important first steps.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Elizabeth Warren (@SenWarren) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWarren/status/1545448006946029574?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Administration should continue to explore every available option to protect access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care. The overwhelming majority of Americans oppose this extremist Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v. Wade, and we must use every tool possible to address this emergency.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Elizabeth Warren (@SenWarren) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWarren/status/1545448009248415745?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 From US representative \uc2 Adam Smith\uc2  of Washington:\par \par \uc2 enltrToday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  announced actions he's taking to protect access to reproductive health care in the wake of the Supreme Court's dangerous decision to overturn Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Adam Smith\uc2  (@RepAdamSmith) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepAdamSmith/status/1545465464410853376?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Executive Order will also protect consumer privacy, personal data, and sensitive health information and importantly will advance the safety of providers and clinics who are courageously providing essential reproductive health care services in the face of heightened risk.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Adam Smith\uc2  (@RepAdamSmith) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepAdamSmith/status/1545465467103584257?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThese actions are a step in the right direction, but they are not enough on their own. We must codify Roe v. Wade into law, and to do so, we must be willing to scrap the filibuster - our freedoms are so much more important than Senate procedure.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Adam Smith\uc2  (@RepAdamSmith) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepAdamSmith/status/1545465468567306242?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 On the same day that Biden signed an executive order safeguarding access to abortions, Louisiana is now able to enforce a near-total ban of abortions in the state under a judge\u8217\'20\'19s order issued on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a piece from the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s health reporter Jessica Glenza on the issue:\par \par \uc2 Louisiana is fighting to become a leader in the race to criminalize doctors who allegedly provide abortions, since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ended federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections.\par \par \uc2 In doing so, the state may also become an example of how \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans could worsen maternal health in America, as criminal penalties across the US redefine where and how doctors are willing to practice.\par \par \uc2 In turn, that is likely to worsen a leading reason some states are more dangerous places to give birth \u8211\'20\'13 lack of hospitals, birthing centers and obstetricians.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt should be no surprise that in a lot of the states where there\u8217\'20\'19s a [trigger ban], there\u8217\'20\'19s a strong correlation [with maternity care deserts],\u8221\'20\'1D said Stacey Stewart, president and chief executive of the March of Dimes, an organization that advocates for maternal and infant health and is strictly neutral on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Read the rest of the piece {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/08/abortion-roe-v-wade-maternal-care-deserts-louisiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/08/abortion-roe-v-wade-maternal-care-deserts-louisiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pregnant women face increasingly dangerous risks as doctors flee punitive US states}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 With \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access threatened across the country, those seeking out \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services and other reproductive healthcare options will be forced to travel if their states do not provide it.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/alvin-chang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alvin Chang}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/andrew-witherspoon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Witherspoon}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/jessica-glenza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jessica Glenza}}}\uc2  have explored how the creation of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cdeserts\u8221\'20\'1D throughout the country will change who can access care \u8211\'20\'13 and how far they will be forced to travel.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/abortion-laws-by-state-map-clinics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  deserts: America\u8217\'20\'19s new geography of access to care \u8211\'20\'13 mapped}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 During the briefing, White house press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  got into a back and forth discussion with a reporter on whether or not people can peacefully protest against Supreme court justices, even in settings like restaurants.\par \par \uc2 The question was prompted after Justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  reportedly had to leave a steakhouse when protestors confronted him for voting to overturn Roe v wade.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre replied to a question on if protestors could confront justices at a restaurant they\u8217\'20\'19re eating at, saying that the Biden administration is against the intimidation of Supreme court justices and using violence against them.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre also cited recent legislation passed to protect the safety of justices.\par \par \uc2 Later on in her response, Jean-Pierre clarified, saying the Biden administration supports the right to peaceful protest, even outside of a restaurant.\par \par \uc2 Here is more information on the bill expanding security for Supreme court justices that passed:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/14/us-house-expand-supreme-court-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US House passes bill to expand supreme court security to justices\u8217\'20\'19 families}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White house press briefing is happening right now, with questions largely focused on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s executive order meant to safeguard access to abortions and other reproductive healthcare services.\par \par \uc2 Questions were answered by White House Gender Policy Council director Jen Klein, who clarified actions that will be taken under the executive order.\par \par \uc2 A link to watch the briefings is available below:\par \par \uc2 enltrWhite House Press Briefing with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PressSec}}}\uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JKlein46?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JKlein46}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 LIVE online here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/a3vT0sqXcw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/a3vT0sqXcw}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YxLsmvhHhQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YxLsmvhHhQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1545452590791622657?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s additional context on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks from the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s health reporter Jessica Glenza:\par \par \uc2 In a speech to mark an executive order to on reproductive rights, President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  emphatically called on the American people to \u8220\'20\'1Cvote, vote, vote, vote,\u8221\'20\'1D in the upcoming election, describing it as the fastest way to regain \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US.\par \par \uc2 Both the speech and executive order, which directs federal agencies to enhance coordination and regulation, \u8220\'20\'1Cjust like in the Civil Rights era,\u8221\'20\'1D comes amid mounting criticism of the administration\u8217\'20\'19s response to the end of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights ended nearly two weeks ago when the supreme court, controlled by a conservative supermajority, overturned Roe v Wade. The landmark 1973 case had prevented states hostile to the procedure from banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, the president\u8217\'20\'19s emphasis on voting also underscores the limitations on the federal government. While the executive order calls on agencies to protect access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, patient privacy, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in states where it remains legal and interstate travel, intervention from Congress is necessary to restore the rights of people who can become pregnant in state that have already banned the procedure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe choice is clear: if you want to change the circumstances for women and even little girls in this country please go out and vote,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden.\par \par \uc2 He also emphasized the stakes of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, citing the case of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/03/ohio-indiana-abortion-rape-victim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10-year-old sexual abuse victim}}}\uc2  from Ohio who was allegedly forced to travel to Indiana to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C10 years old, 10 years old!\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden. \u8220\'20\'1CRaped, six weeks pregnant, already traumatized, was forced to travel to another state\u8230\'20\'26 Does anyone believe that it is Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s majority view that should not be able to be dealt with? A 10-year-old girl should be forced to give birth to a rapist\u8217\'20\'19s child?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/jun/28/tracking-where-abortion-laws-stand-in-every-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tracking where \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  laws stand in every state}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 During his remarks, Biden also pledged to veto any further \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions that could come across his desk if Republicans gain control of Congress during the midterm elections in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs long as I\u8217\'20\'19m president it won\u8217\'20\'19t happen, because I\u8217\'20\'19ll veto it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden during his speech today, shortly before he signed an executive order safeguarding access to abortions and other reproductive healthcare services.\par \par \uc2 From the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Lauren Gambino:\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden warns that Republicans would seek a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if they take control of Congress in November.\par \par \uc2 As long as I'm president, he said, "I'll veto it."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1545442691269492738?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrcc {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/amandalitman?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @amandalitman}}}\uc2  who told me last week that voters so far hadn't heard Biden say clearly that he would veto any new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions sent to him by a potential Republican-controlled Congress. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Z8ngEYyZVm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Z8ngEYyZVm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1545443333685886983?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden signs executive order protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s official; Biden has formally signed an executive order protecting access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other reproductive healthcare services.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  signs an executive order on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access during an event in the Roosevelt Room of the White House, Friday, July 8, 2022, in Washington. Photograph: Evan Vucci/AP\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/08/biden-abortion-executive-order-access-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-62c83cd08f081211720cd6f1#block-62c83cd08f081211720cd6f1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here}}}\uc2  is a previous post detailing what is in the executive order.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden also brought up the story of a 10-year-old girl in Ohio who was raped and forced to travel to Indiana to receive an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA 10-year-old girl should be forced to given birth to rapist\u8217\'20\'19s child?\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden of the Ohio case, calling it an example of Republican extremism.\par \par \uc2 Biden added: \u8220\'20\'1CDoes anyone believe it\u8217\'20\'19s Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s majority view that that should not be able to be dealt with?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s coverage of the case by Ed Helmore {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwardhelmore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/03/ohio-indiana-abortion-rape-victim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10-year-old rape victim forced to travel from Ohio to Indiana for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says supreme court conservatives 'playing fast and loose with the facts'\par \par \uc2 Biden is currently speaking on the rollback of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections, two weeks after the supreme court voted to overturn Roe v Wade, the landmark case that protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was not a decision driven by the constitution. This was not a decision driven by history,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden of the supreme court overturning Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Discussing the conservative majority in the court, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court majority is playing fast and loose with the facts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Later on in his remarks, Biden called on Americans to use their electoral power to elect senators who would help codify Roe v Wade, saying that it was the \u8220\'20\'1Cfastest route\u8221\'20\'1D to solidifying federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Biden in the Roosevelt Room of the White House on Friday. Photograph: Yuri Gripas/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYour votes can make that a reality,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden, acknowledging the frustration his administration has received amid urging people to vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou, the women of America, can determine the outcome of this issue,\u8221\'20\'1D adding the courts do not have a \u8220\'20\'1Cclue about the power of American women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor God\u8217\'20\'19s sakes, there\u8217\'20\'19s an election in November. Vote, vote, vote,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks come on the same day that he is signing an executive order protecting access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other reproductive healthcare nationwide.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ahead of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech, US politicians are sharing reproductive rights resources that are currently available, modest steps the Biden administration have taken prior to the executive order expected today.\par \par \uc2 From US House representative \uc2 Zoe Lofgren\uc2 , a Democrat from California:\par \par \uc2 ICYMI: in response to the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s assault on reproductive health care, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HHSGov/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @HHSGov}}}\uc2  created a guide for women about their reproductive rights. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  & other reproductive care remains safe & legal in California.\par \par \uc2 enltrICYMI: in response to the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s assault on reproductive health care, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HHSGov?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @HHSGov}}}\uc2  created a guide for women about their reproductive rights.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  & other reproductive care remains safe & legal in California. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/b9UaitzI74"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/b9UaitzI74}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Zoe Lofgren\uc2  (@RepZoeLofgren) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepZoeLofgren/status/1545432870394728451?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 At 11.30am, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will give remarks from the White House on protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Biden will likely speak on an executive order he is expected to sign today that would safeguard access to abortions and other reproductive healthcare services.\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned to hear highlights from his remarks and watch the live speech {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vsS3RMW6Chg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Other US politicians have shared statements of condolence following the assassination of \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  called Abe \u8220\'20\'1Ca close friend of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D writing that the country stands \u8220\'20\'1Cwith our Japanese friends in honoring him and condemning this horrific act of violence\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrDoug and I send our deepest condolences to the family of former Prime Minister \uc2 Abe Shinzo\uc2  and the Japanese people. He was a close friend of the United States and on this tragic day, we stand with our Japanese friends in honoring him and condemning this horrific act of violence.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@VP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP/status/1545409769971777539?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Former US president \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  released a statement today on Abe\u8217\'20\'19s death, writing:\par \par \uc2 I am deeply saddened to learn of the senseless assassination of former Japanese Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2 . I had the privilege of getting to know him during his first time as Prime Minister in 2006 and found him to be a decent and caring man. \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2  was a patriot of his country who wanted to continue serving it. Laura and I send our heartfelt condolences to Akie Abe, their family, and the people of Japan during this difficult time.\par \par \uc2 In a series of tweets published today, \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  wrote:\par \par \uc2 I am shocked and saddened by the assassination of my friend and longtime partner \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2  in Japan. Former Prime Minister Abe was devoted to both the country he served and the extraordinary alliance between the United States and Japan.\par \par \uc2 enltrI am shocked and saddened by the assassination of my friend and longtime partner \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2  in Japan. Former Prime Minister Abe was devoted to both the country he served and the extraordinary alliance between the United States and Japan.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Barack Obama (@BarackObama) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BarackObama/status/1545388676242456576?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 In other news, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has publicized a statement following the shooting death of former Japanese prime minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Abe was assassinated yesterday while giving a campaign speech in the south-central Japanese city of Nara.\par \par \uc2 In a statement shared on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , Biden said:\par \par \uc2 I am stunned, outraged, and deeply saddened by the news that my friend \uc2 Abe Shinzo\uc2 , former Prime Minister of Japan, was shot and killed.\par \par \uc2 He was a champion of the friendship between our people. The United States stands with Japan in this moment of grief.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, with the addition of 372,000 new jobs in June, our private sector has recovered all of the jobs lost during the pandemic \u8211\'20\'13 and added jobs on top of that.\par \par \uc2 We have more work to do. But no country is better positioned than America to face global economic challenges.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1545409897948499980?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are more specifics on what Biden\u8217\'20\'19s executive order protecting access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will entail.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/07/08/fact-sheet-president-biden-to-sign-executive-order-protecting-access-to-reproductive-health-care-services/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to a fact sheet from the White house}}}\uc2 , the executive order will direct the secretary of Health and Human Services (\uc2 HHS\uc2 ) to take steps in a number of areas concerning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and report back in 30 days.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 HHS\uc2  secretary will take steps to:\par \par \uc2 * Protect access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also known as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills\par \par \uc2 * Ensure emergency medical care for pregnant people and anyone experiencing pregnancy loss\par \par \uc2 * Launch education and public outreach efforts\par \par \uc2 * Convene volunteer lawyers to represent patients who seek out care\par \par \uc2 The executive order will also seek to protect patient privacy and ensure the safety of patients, providers, and clinics who provide reproductive healthcare services.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s executive order comes at a time when frustration is mounting against his administration for not doing enough to protect federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Progressive politicians and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates have been public about their disappointment with the Biden administration, asking Biden and other Democrats to do more to protect reproductive rights following the overturning of Roe v Wade two weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 US House representative \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , a Democrat of New York, urged Democrats to push back harder against the rollback of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1542504295559442432"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeting last week}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CUse the bully pulpit. We need more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrNow we\u8217\'20\'19re talking! Time for people to see a real, forceful push for it. Use the bully pulpit. We need more. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dZ1qhdu8iM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/dZ1qhdu8iM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  (@AOC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1542504295559442432?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 30, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 A group of more than 20 Black Democratic congresswomen signed a letter last week, urging Biden to declare a public health emergency following the rollback of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn this unprecedented moment, we must act urgently as if lives depend on it because they do,\u8221\'20\'1D the legislators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pressley.house.gov/media/press-releases/pressley-leads-black-congresswomen-urging-biden-declare-public-health-emergency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/02/biden-democrats-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden urged to do more to defend \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights: \u8216\'20\'18This is a five-alarm fire\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to sign executive order to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access\par \par \uc2 Good morning! It\u8217\'20\'19s Gloria from the New York office. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what is happening today:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is signing an executive order to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access for millions, two weeks after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, a landmark ruling that ensured federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections for the past 50 years.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights protesters participate in nationwide demonstrations, in Atlanta, Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Photograph: Alyssa Pointer/Reuters\par \par \uc2 According to a fact sheet, the executive order will protect access to several reproductive healthcare services, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and contraception.\par \par \uc2 The order also safeguards access to medication abortions, also known as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plannedparenthood.org/learn/abortion/the-abortion-pill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills}}}\uc2 , approved by the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 The executive order comes as many have been critical of the Biden administration for failing to do more to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, including codifying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access amid ongoing attacks on reproductive rights nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Biden is expected to speak on the executive order and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights generally at 11:30am eastern time.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/08/joe-biden-to-sign-order-offering-protection-women-denied-right-to-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden to sign executive order protecting access to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220708ei780020h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
