\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Tinder owner halts political donations after support for anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  group\b0\par\par\uc2 Coral Murphy Marcos \par \uc2 297 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 July 2022\par 19:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Revelation that \uc2 Match Group\uc2  donated to Republican Attorneys General Association prompts decision to cut all funding\par \par \uc2 Match Group\uc2 , the company behind dating apps including Tinder and Hinge, has broken up with political lobbying after coming under fire for supporting a Republican group that works to undermine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The company\u8217\'20\'19s chief executive, \uc2 Bernard Kim\uc2 , said the company has stopped funding the Republican Attorneys General Association after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://popular.info/p/the-hypocrisy-of-abortion-as-a-corporate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Popular Information}}}\uc2  revealed that it had made a $137,000 donation to the group.\par \par \uc2 It said it was also ceasing donations to the Democratic equivalent, the Democratic Attorneys General Association.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s my responsibility to understand how these donations fit into our larger lobbying activity, and determine what we will do moving forward,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kim in an internal memo to company employees obtained by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/07/07/business/match-group-donations-dobbs-roe.html?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times}}}\uc2  on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Match Group\uc2  has been a vocal advocate of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, especially after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling in June. The company announced on Tuesday that it would add a \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-choice\u8221\'20\'1D badge to users\u8217\'20\'19 profile options. \uc2 Match Group\uc2  also supports Planned Parenthood and Bansoff.org through in-app promotions.\par \par \uc2 In September, when Texas passed a bill to ban abortions after six weeks, the company announced it would provide reproductive care coverage, which covers travel and lodging costs for full and part-time employees, contractors and their eligible dependents, plus a companion, who need to travel out of state to receive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 After the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ended nearly 50 years of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, numerous companies pledged to cover travel costs for employees who live in states where the procedure is now illegal so they can terminate pregnancies, including \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , \uc2 Disney\uc2  and \uc2 Apple\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220708ei78002xl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
