\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US gunmakers summoned to Congress to justify soaring profits from gun violence \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 4,373 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 July 2022\par 20:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Top Democrats \u8216\'20\'18deeply troubled that gun manufacturers continue to profit from the sale of weapons of war\u8217\'20\'19Fears over Trump loyalists\u8217\'20\'19 \u8216\'20\'18sham\u8217\'20\'19 integrity drive\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/07/biden-democrats-climate-crisis-manchin-presidential-medal-freedom-latest?page=with:block-62c732558f08ea322519f3d2#block-62c732558f08ea322519f3d2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 honored notable Americans}}}\uc2  with the country\u8217\'20\'19s highest civilian honor, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/07/biden-democrats-climate-crisis-manchin-presidential-medal-freedom-latest?page=with:block-62c71ed38f08599e90423c7e#block-62c71ed38f08599e90423c7e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 details emerged}}}\uc2  of the January 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s plans for its next - and potentially last - hearings.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 * American women\u8217\'20\'19s basketball star Brittney Griner{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/07/biden-democrats-climate-crisis-manchin-presidential-medal-freedom-latest?page=with:block-62c6f66e8f081211720ccaf2#block-62c6f66e8f081211720ccaf2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded guilty to drug charges in Russia}}}\uc2 , the latest development in a case that has captured the attention of the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 * Another Democratic senator said she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/07/biden-democrats-climate-crisis-manchin-presidential-medal-freedom-latest?page=with:block-62c738278f08ea322519f405#block-62c738278f08ea322519f405"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would support creating an exemption to the filibuster}}}\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights legislation. Meanwhile, lawmakers in South Carolina began debate on a bill to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/07/biden-democrats-climate-crisis-manchin-presidential-medal-freedom-latest?page=with:block-62c72ef18f08ea322519f3bc#block-62c72ef18f08ea322519f3bc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 almost completely ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Details are trickling out about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/07/biden-democrats-climate-crisis-manchin-presidential-medal-freedom-latest?page=with:block-62c6da708f081211720cc97b#block-62c6da708f081211720cc97b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new effort}}}\uc2  by Democrats to pass a big spending bill in what could be their final months controlling both houses of Congress.\par \par \uc2 * The CEOs of firearms manufacturers{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/07/biden-democrats-climate-crisis-manchin-presidential-medal-freedom-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62c6f1578f081211720cca95#block-62c6f1578f081211720cca95"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have been summoned}}}\uc2  by a congressional committee investigating the gun industry.\par \par \uc2 * Illinois police will investigate the father of the man who opened fire at an Independence Day parade on Monday for his involvement in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/07/biden-democrats-climate-crisis-manchin-presidential-medal-freedom-latest?page=with:block-62c6e7558f081211720cca1c#block-62c6e7558f081211720cca1c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his son\u8217\'20\'19s purchase of a firearm}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Sacha Baron Cohen, the comedian best known for portraying Borat, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/07/biden-democrats-climate-crisis-manchin-presidential-medal-freedom-latest?page=with:block-62c705148f08599e90423b1c#block-62c705148f08599e90423b1c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fended off a lawsuit}}}\uc2  from a former Republican Senate candidate in Alabama.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2  has come out in support of creating an exception to the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s filibuster rules in order to pass legislation protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide.\par \par \uc2 enltrLet me be clear: If it comes down to protecting the filibuster or protecting a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose, there should be no question that I will vote to protect a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rpHANTjyqn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rpHANTjyqn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2  (@SenFeinstein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenFeinstein/status/1545130481414438914?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights activists are pressuring Democrats to pass a law protecting access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide after the supreme court last month {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade}}}\uc2 . But the filibuster, which allows the Republican minority to stop legislation in the Senate that does not win at least 10 of their party\u8217\'20\'19s votes, has stood in the way of that, and until now, Feinstein {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfchronicle.com/politics/joegarofoli/article/Dianne-Feinstein-supports-abortion-rights-but-17288854.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hasn\u8217\'20\'19t said if she would support modifying it}}}\uc2  to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law passed.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/30/filibuster-abortion-vote-exception-joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden backs exception to Senate filibuster to protect \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has handed out the Presidential Medal of Freedom, the United States\u8217\'20\'19s highest civilian honor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/07/01/president-biden-announces-recipients-of-the-presidential-medal-of-freedom/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to 17 people}}}\uc2 , including Olympic gymnast Simone Biles.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  presents the medal to Simone Biles at the White House. Photograph: Alex Wong/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from when Biles received the award:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Simone_Biles?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Simone_Biles}}}\uc2  receives the Presidential Medal of Freedom. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5MPnIzDWTW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5MPnIzDWTW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1545121626261528577?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Former congresswoman and gun control advocate \uc2 Gabrielle Giffords\uc2  was also honored:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GabbyGiffords?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GabbyGiffords}}}\uc2  receives the Presidential Medal of Freedom. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vzE1IdrhdD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vzE1IdrhdD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1545122084627570698?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 As was soccer star Megan Rapinoe :\par \par \uc2 enltrMegan Rapinoe ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mPinoe?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @mpinoe}}}\uc2  ) receives the Presidential Medal of Freedom {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GGc4JGwJxg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GGc4JGwJxg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1545124392245641217?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Three people were given the award posthumously: \uc2 Apple\uc2  co-founder \uc2 Steve Jobs\uc2 , president of the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  trade union federation \uc2 Richard Trumka\uc2  and senator \uc2 John McCain\uc2 . His wife \uc2 Cindy McCain\uc2  accepted on his behalf:\par \par \uc2 enltr"John McCain was a giant among Americans from a family of patriots." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cindymccain?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @cindymccain}}}\uc2  accepts the Presidetial Medal of Freedom on behalf of her late husband, Sen. \uc2 John McCain\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7ejuKszzWe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/7ejuKszzWe}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1545124018415697920?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden, a longtime Democratic senator, remarked on his relationship with McCain, a Republican.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden on \uc2 John McCain\uc2 : "I never stopped admiring John. I never said a negative thing about him in my life because I knew his honor, his courage and his commitment. That was \uc2 John McCain\uc2 ." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DSJD9scTAv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DSJD9scTAv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1545121571882369024?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Actor Denzel Washington was also due to get the award, but could not attend the White House ceremony due to a positive Covid-19 test, according to a White House official:\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden on Denzel Washington: "He's couldn't be with us here today. I'll be giving him this award at a later date when he's able to get here." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/N15bEG3gxv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/N15bEG3gxv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1545118055033933825?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 South Carolina lawmakers have begun considering a bill to ban nearly all abortions in the state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/government/south-carolina-lawmakers-consider-banning-almost-all-abortions-2022-07-07/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The proposal would \u8220\'20\'1Cban all abortions from conception, except to save the life of the mother, and would make performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a felony punishable by up to 25 years in prison,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the report.\par \par \uc2 The measure would be more stringent than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/abortion-ban-south-carolina-court-rules-law-can-go-into-effect/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a law that a federal judge allowed to go into effect last month}}}\uc2  which outlaws the procedure after about six weeks of pregnancy. The court ruling followed the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision overturning Roe v. Wade and allowing states to ban abortions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee has for the past month held carefully choreographed hearings that are meant to be attention-grabbing to a degree rarely seen in Congress, but a poll released today found they aren\u8217\'20\'19t doing much to sway Americans\u8217\'20\'19 beliefs about what happened that day.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.monmouth.edu/polling-institute/reports/monmouthpoll_us_070722/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The survey from Monmouth University}}}\uc2  found only six percent of Americans say the hearings have changed their mind about January 6, in part due to the relatively few Republicans who are following the testimony. Only 10 percent of GOP supporters are turning in, versus 45 percent of Democrats and 16 percent of independents.\par \par \uc2 For Republicans who did watch the hearings, only five percent said it changed their minds, with some telling Monmouth, \u8220\'20\'1Cthey learned about the pressure Trump was exerting or that election fraud claims were spurious.\u8221\'20\'1D The poll said that other respondents \u8220\'20\'1Cclaim they have \u8216\'20\'18learned\u8217\'20\'19 that \u8216\'20\'18police officers were not killed in that protest,\u8217\'20\'19 or that \u8216\'20\'18the Democrats were highly involved as well as the F.B.I.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The poll also documents a decline in Americans\u8217\'20\'19 faith in their government. Only 36 percent of respondents told Monmouth that the American system of government is basically sound, a decline from February 2020, when it was 55 percent.\par \par \uc2 In the words of Patrick Murray, director of the independent Monmouth University Polling Institute:\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s more than just partisanship at work in declining faith in the institutional framework of American democracy. Yes, electoral outcomes play a role. Yes, the current economic crisis plays a role. But attacks on our fundamental democratic processes \u8211\'20\'13 and the lack of universal condemnation of those attacks by political leaders from both sides of the aisle \u8211\'20\'13 have taken a toll.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 The head of the \uc2 IRS\uc2  has asked for an investigation into a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/07/biden-democrats-climate-crisis-manchin-presidential-medal-freedom-latest?page=with:block-62c6fe8d8f08599e90423ad0#block-62c6fe8d8f08599e90423ad0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  that former \uc2 FBI\uc2  director \uc2 James Comey\uc2  and his deputy \uc2 Andrew McCabe\uc2 , both of whom clashed with ex-president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , were subject to rare, intrusive audits, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/irs-asks-treasury-watchdog-to-probe-comey-mccabe-audits/2022/07/07/8961ec30-fe1f-11ec-b39d-71309168014b_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IRS\uc2  commissioner has asked the Treasury Department\u8217\'20\'19s inspector general to immediately review the circumstances surrounding intensive tax audits that targeted ex-\uc2 FBI\uc2  Director \uc2 James Comey\uc2  and ex-Deputy Director \uc2 Andrew McCabe\uc2 , both frequent targets of President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s anger.\par \par \uc2 IRS\uc2  spokesperson Jodie Reynolds said Thursday that IRS Commissioner \uc2 Charles Rettig\uc2  had personally reached out to the Treasury Inspector General for Tax Administration. Reynolds said the agency has officially referred the matter to the inspector general.\par \par \uc2 But Reynolds insisted it is \u8220\'20\'1Cludicrous and untrue to suggest that senior \uc2 IRS\uc2  officials somehow targeted specific individuals for National Research Program audits.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/07/06/us/politics/comey-mccabe-irs-audits.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  the original \uc2 New York Times\uc2  article that led to the investigation.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell has more detail about what we can expect from next week\u8217\'20\'19s two January 6 committee meetings - one of which will shine more light on what was happening inside the White House as the Capitol was being attacked:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Jan. 6 committee members \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2  and \uc2 Stephanie Murphy\uc2  will lead Tuesday hearing on Trump sending extremist groups to DC and pinpointing the 6th, and \uc2 Elaine Luria\uc2  and \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  will lead expected Thursday primetime hearing on inside the WH during the Capitol attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1545088930655117313?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTentative schedule is tentative, per sources familiar with the tentative schedule. But the Thursday prime time hearing is expected to be the final one held by the Jan. 6 committee \u8212\'20\'14 for now.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1545089590029082624?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has weighed in on the resignation of British prime minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 , though the White House statement makes no mention of his name:\par \par \uc2 enltrJUST IN: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  Biden statement on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BorisJohnson?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BorisJohnson}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s resignation: \u8220\'20\'1Cthe special relationship between our people remains strong and enduring. I look forward to continuing our close cooperation with the \uc2 government of the United Kingdom\uc2 , as well as our Allies and partners\u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/sk4X6vWOxb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/sk4X6vWOxb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ed O'Keefe (@edokeefe) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/edokeefe/status/1545084730156146688?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 For the latest developments in the political upheaval across the pond, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  is here for you:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2022/jul/07/boris-johnson-latest-resignations-today-conservatives-uk-politics-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Boris Johnson resigns and says no new policies until next prime minister announced \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will soon hold a ceremony at the White House to give the medal of freedom to a group of recipients, including some of the country\u8217\'20\'19s best known politicians, actors and athletes.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps the biggest names are two-time Academy Award winner Denzel Washington and Simone Biles, the most decorated American gymnast ever. Women\u8217\'20\'19s soccer star Megan Rapinoe will also be honored, as well as former congresswoman \uc2 Gabrielle Giffords\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2014/feb/11/gabby-giffords-gun-control-book-newtown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who was badly injured during a mass shooting in 2010}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Apple\uc2  co-founder \uc2 Steve Jobs\uc2  and Republican senator \uc2 John McCain\uc2  will receive the award posthumously in the event vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and her husband will also attend.\par \par \uc2 The White House has a full rundown {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/07/01/president-biden-announces-recipients-of-the-presidential-medal-of-freedom/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/01/simone-biles-megan-rapinoe-presidential-medal-of-freedom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Simone Biles and nurse who received first Covid vaccine to get top US honor}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 DeSantis appoints elections police chief\par \par \uc2 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  caused shock when he announced the creation of the Office of Election Crimes and Security in the state, to keep an eye on election fraud: a crime for which there is usually very little evidence that it exists.\par \par \uc2 Now, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.clickorlando.com/news/2022/07/07/desantis-taps-former-prosecutor-pete-antonacci-to-lead-elections-security-office/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  CBS station in Orlando reports}}}\uc2 , we know the identity of the man who will head up that unit: Pete Antonacci, a former prosecutor and onetime supervisor of elections.\par \par \uc2 CBS{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.clickorlando.com/news/2022/07/07/desantis-taps-former-prosecutor-pete-antonacci-to-lead-elections-security-office/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CAntonacci, 73, has a long history of being called upon by state leaders as a fix-it man of sorts. His career includes stints as executive director of the South Florida Water Management District, president of the state business-recruitment agency Enterprise Florida and state attorney in Palm Beach County.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But in a sign that may ease - a few - fears about voter suppression in the state, it seems some Democrats welcome the appointment.\par \par \uc2 CBS{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.clickorlando.com/news/2022/07/07/desantis-taps-former-prosecutor-pete-antonacci-to-lead-elections-security-office/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThis elections police thing is terrible. However, Antonacci is a pretty no-nonsense administrator. Even us Dems praised his work in Broward. He is by far the best that could be hoped for. So much so I could see DeSantis growing to hate him if he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t go on witch hunts,\u8221\'20\'1D Matt Isbell, a Tallahassee-based consultant for Democrats, tweeted Wednesday.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 committee plans Thursday prime-time hearing\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee will hold a hearing on Thursday of next week that will be broadcast at the prime-time TV hour, Punchbowl News reports.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Jan. 6 committee is scheduled to hold hearings Tuesday AND Thursday next week, sources tell me.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1545083834672324609?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThursday night is slated to be another primetime hearing, sources tell me {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WWlpehZj9P"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/WWlpehZj9P}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1545084365201350657?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The House committee investigating the insurrection had earlier this week announced it will hold its next hearing on Tuesday, 12 July, which is expected to focus on the links between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and extremist groups.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/07/next-jan-6-hearing-trump-far-right-militias"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s possible ties to far-right militias examined by January 6 committee}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Congress is on recess, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/07/biden-democrats-climate-crisis-manchin-presidential-medal-freedom-latest?page=with:block-62c6da708f081211720cc97b#block-62c6da708f081211720cc97b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 details are slowly emerging}}}\uc2  about Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 plans for a spending bill to be revealed perhaps in the coming weeks, while the party has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/07/biden-democrats-climate-crisis-manchin-presidential-medal-freedom-latest?page=with:block-62c6f1578f081211720cca95#block-62c6f1578f081211720cca95"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced a hearing}}}\uc2  to take firearms manufacturers to task over gun violence.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what has happened today:\par \par \uc2 * American women\u8217\'20\'19s basketball star Brittney Griner{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/07/biden-democrats-climate-crisis-manchin-presidential-medal-freedom-latest?page=with:block-62c6f66e8f081211720ccaf2#block-62c6f66e8f081211720ccaf2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded guilty to drug charges in Russia}}}\uc2 , the latest development in a case that has captured the attention of the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 * Illinois police will investigate the father of the man who opened fire at an Independence Day parade on Monday for his involvement in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/07/biden-democrats-climate-crisis-manchin-presidential-medal-freedom-latest?page=with:block-62c6e7558f081211720cca1c#block-62c6e7558f081211720cca1c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his son\u8217\'20\'19s purchase of a firearm}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Sacha Baron Cohen, the comedian best known for portraying Borat, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/07/biden-democrats-climate-crisis-manchin-presidential-medal-freedom-latest?page=with:block-62c705148f08599e90423b1c#block-62c705148f08599e90423b1c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fended off a lawsuit}}}\uc2  from a former Republican Senate candidate in Alabama.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 A winner has been declared in the showdown between comedian Sacha Baron Cohen and former judge and failed Senate candidate \uc2 Roy Moore\uc2 , at least for now.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/litigation/sacha-baron-cohen-beats-ex-judge-roy-moores-defamation-appeal-2022-07-07/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters reports }}}\uc2  that Cohen, who is perhaps best known for portraying the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2020/oct/21/borat-subsequent-moviefilm-review-sacha-baron-cohen-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Borat}}}\uc2  character, has fended off a defamation lawsuit by Moore over an interview broadcast on his show, \u8220\'20\'1CWho Is America?\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 In a 3-0 vote, the 2nd U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals in Manhattan said the interview was constitutionally protected speech, agreeing with a lower court judge that it was \u8220\'20\'1Cclearly comedy and that no reasonable viewer would conclude otherwise.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The court also said Moore waived his right to pursue his $95 million lawsuit by signing a standard consent agreement before the interview, which he knew would be televised. It also dismissed related claims by Moore\u8217\'20\'19s wife Kayla.\par \par \uc2 Larry Klayman, the Moores\u8217\'20\'19 lawyer, called the decision a \u8220\'20\'1Ctravesty,\u8221\'20\'1D saying the consent agreement was ambiguous because Judge Moore crossed out a provision waiving claims related to alleged sexually oriented behavior and questioning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis should not have been taken away from the jury,\u8221\'20\'1D Klayman said in an interview. The Moores will ask the entire 2nd Circuit to review the case.\par \par \uc2 Accusation of sexual misconduct swirled around Moore when he stood as a Republican to represent Alabama in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  in 2017, a race he lost to Democrat \uc2 Doug Jones\uc2  despite the state being among the most conservative in the country.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2017/dec/12/roy-moore-loses-alabama-senate-race-doug-jones-wins"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alabama election: Democrats triumph over Roy Moore in major blow to Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Could \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have had the \uc2 IRS\uc2  carry out its most stringent audit on two of his political foes? That\u8217\'20\'19s the question posed by a story {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/07/06/us/politics/comey-mccabe-irs-audits.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published yesterday}}}\uc2  in \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  that says former \uc2 FBI\uc2  director \uc2 James Comey\uc2  and his deputy \uc2 Andrew McCabe\uc2  were both selected for random audits by the tax authority, which is run by an appointee of the former president.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for Trump denied knowing anything about the matter, and experts quoted in the story wondered whether it was even possible for a president to order the \uc2 IRS\uc2  to carry out such an action. The coincidence is nonetheless abnormal. Here\u8217\'20\'19s how one former \uc2 IRS\uc2  official put it to the Times:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLightning strikes, and that\u8217\'20\'19s unusual, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what it\u8217\'20\'19s like being picked for one of these audits,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 John A. Koskinen\uc2 , the I.R.S. commissioner from 2013 to 2017. \u8220\'20\'1CThe question is: Does lightning then strike again in the same area? Does it happen? Some people may see that in their lives, but most will not \u8212\'20\'14 so you don\u8217\'20\'19t need to be an anti-Trumper to look at this and think it\u8217\'20\'19s suspicious.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump fired Comey in 2017, one of his many controversial moves early in his term, while McCabe was dismissed the next year. As recently as this year, the former president was continuing to feud with his one-time \uc2 FBI\uc2  head, naming him in a lawsuit over the investigation into Russia interference in the 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/24/trump-hillary-clinton-russia-lawsuit-2016-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Trump sues Hillary Clinton, alleging \u8216\'20\'18plot\u8217\'20\'19 to rig 2016 election against him}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking of news in other countries: With a declaration of \u8220\'20\'1CThem\u8217\'20\'19s the breaks,\u8221\'20\'1D Britain\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  has resigned as leader of the Conservatives, though he intends to stay on until his party chooses a new prime minister.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has a live blog chronicling all the latest developments in Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s downfall, which came after a revolt by his cabinet and a wave of scandals.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2022/jul/07/boris-johnson-latest-resignations-today-conservatives-uk-politics-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Boris Johnson resigns as John Major warns he must not stay as caretaker prime minister \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Basketball star Brittney Griner pleads guilty to drug charges in Russia\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been repeatedly asked what his administration is doing to win the release of Brittney Griner, an American women\u8217\'20\'19s basketball star detained in Russia. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/pjotr-sauer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pjotr Sauer}}}\uc2  reports that she has now pled guilty to the drug charges against her:\par \par \uc2 The jailed US basketball star Brittney Griner has pleaded guilty to drug possession and smuggling charges during her trial in Moscow, Russian news agencies reported on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Griner\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/01/brittney-griner-russia-trial-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trial began last week}}}\uc2  amid a growing chorus of calls for Washington to do more to secure her freedom nearly five months after her arrest.\par \par \uc2 The athlete {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/mar/05/brittney-griner-reportedly-detained-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was detained in February at Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s Sheremetyevo airport}}}\uc2  after vape canisters with cannabis oil were allegedly found in her luggage. She faces up to 10 years in prison if convicted of large-scale transportation of drugs.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/07/basketball-brittney-griner-returns-russian-court-drug-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Basketball star Brittney Griner pleads guilty to drug charges in Russia}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Gunmakers summoned to Congress to testify on gun violence\par \par \uc2 Democrats in Congress are summoning the CEOs of firearm manufacturers to testify at a hearing later this month on gun violence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am deeply troubled that gun manufacturers continue to profit from the sale of weapons of war, including AR-15-style assault rifles that were used by a white supremacist to murder ten people in Buffalo, New York, and in the massacre of 19 children and two teachers in Uvalde, Texas,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Carolyn Maloney\uc2 , the Democratic chair of the House Oversight Committee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oversight.house.gov/news/press-releases/following-fourth-of-july-shooting-in-highland-park-chairwoman-maloney-invites"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote in letters}}}\uc2  to the leaders of \uc2 Daniel Defense\uc2 , \uc2 Smith & Wesson\uc2 , and Ruger, which make AR-15 style rifles.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProducts sold by your company have been used for decades to carry out homicides and even mass murders, yet your company has continued to market assault weapons to civilians.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Under her leadership, the committee began investigating gun manufacturers last May. The following month, it held a hearing featuring {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/08/us-house-hearing-gun-violence-survivors-testify-miah-cerrillo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gut-wrenching testimony}}}\uc2  from survivors of the school shooting in Uvalde, Texas.\par \par \uc2 The latest hearing is set for July 20.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 The gun violence on July 4 could have been much worse. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/07/richmond-virginia-mass-shooting-fourth-of-july-tip-police"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coral Murphy Marcos}}}\uc2  reports that police in Richmond, Virginia say another mass shooting was planned in the city that day:\par \par \uc2 Police in Richmond, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Virginia}}}\uc2 , said a tip-off from an anonymous informant helped them to stop another planned mass shooting at an amphitheater on the Fourth of July.\par \par \uc2 The caller informed them of a planned mass shooting at the Dogwood Dell Amphitheater during the holiday celebration, the police chief, Gerald Smith, said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The tip sparked an investigation that led to the arrest of two men in possession of assault rifles and more than 200 rounds of ammunition. Police said the men were planning to attack the arena, which seats about 2,400 people.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/07/richmond-virginia-mass-shooting-fourth-of-july-tip-police"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anonymous tip helped Virginia police block planned Fourth of July shooting}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 The father of the man who opened fire Monday at an Independence Day parade and killed seven in a Chicago suburb will be facing a criminal investigation, local media reports.\par \par \uc2 enltrIllinois State Police announced that there will be criminal investigations into the culpability of the father after he signed off on his son\u8217\'20\'19s, the accused Highland Park shooter, FOID affidavit.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Danielle Ellis (@Danielle__Ellis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Danielle__Ellis/status/1545039376564064256?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Robert Crimo Jr had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abc7chicago.com/highland-park-shooting-parade-robert-crimo-father/12026458/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously told ABC News}}}\uc2  he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t concerned about a potential investigation into his involvement in his son\u8217\'20\'19s purchase of a gun, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CI filled out the consent form to allow my son to go through the process that the Illinois State Police have in place for an individual to obtain a FOID card. They do background checks. Whatever that entails, I\u8217\'20\'19m not exactly sure. And either you\u8217\'20\'19re approved or denied, and he was approved.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 In other news concerning the former president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/peter-stone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peter Stone}}}\uc2  reports on a campaign to train election observers by allies of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 A conservative group called the America Project that boasts \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  loyalists and \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D pushers \uc2 Roger Stone\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/michael-flynn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michael Flynn}}}\uc2  as key advisers, has begun a self-styled \u8220\'20\'1Celection integrity\u8221\'20\'1D drive to train activists in election canvassing and poll-watching, sparking fears from voting rights watchdogs about voter intimidation.\par \par \uc2 Patrick Byrne, the multimillionaire co-founder of the America Project, has said he has donated almost $3m to launch the drive, dubbed \u8220\'20\'1COperation Eagles Wings\u8221\'20\'1D, with a focus on eight states including Arizona, Michigan and Pennsylvania, which Trump lost, plus Texas and Florida, which he won.\par \par \uc2 The drive was unveiled in late February at a press event where Byrne touted plans to educate \u8220\'20\'1Celection reform activists\u8221\'20\'1D to handle election canvassing, grassroots work and fundraising \u8220\'20\'1Cto expose shenanigans at the ballot box\u8221\'20\'1D in what has echoes of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false claims that the 2020 election was rigged, and could become a sequel to those charges.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/07/sham-fears-over-trump-loyalists-election-integrity-drive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s a sham\u8217\'20\'19: fears over Trump loyalists\u8217\'20\'19 \u8216\'20\'18election integrity\u8217\'20\'19 drive}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congress\u8217\'20\'19s return means the January 6 committee will air new evidence, and \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  has a look at what to expect from its next hearing set for Tuesday:\par \par \uc2 Towards the end of her testimony to the House January 6 select committee, former Trump aide Cassidy Hutchinson raised for the first time the prospect that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  might have had a line of communication to the leaders of the extremist groups that stormed the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 The potential connection from the former US president to the extremist right-wing groups came through {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/29/january-6-donald-trump-mark-meadows-rudy-giuliani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her account of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s order}}}\uc2  to his White House chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  to call \uc2 Roger Stone\uc2  and \uc2 Mike Flynn\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which Meadows did \u8211\'20\'13 the evening before the Capitol attack.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s order to Meadows, even though Hutchinson said she did not know what was discussed, is significant because it shows the former president seeking to have a channel to two figures with close ties to the leaders of the far-right Proud Boys and Oath Keepers groups.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/07/next-jan-6-hearing-trump-far-right-militias"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s possible ties to far right militias examined by January 6 committee}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 When they were negotiating Build Back Better last year, president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Democratic leaders made proposals, and then tried to get all their lawmakers in Congress on board. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/08/build-back-better-democrats-midterms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The effort ended up failing}}}\uc2 , and now it appears they are trying a different strategy as they work on a new spending bill that could be announced in the weeks after Congress returns from recess.\par \par \uc2 Negotiators appear to be focusing on writing legislation that will contain proposals all of its lawmakers will support - particularly in the Senate, where every Democrat\u8217\'20\'19s vote will be needed to overcome a filibuster and pass the bill through the reconciliation procedure.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/06/biden-economy-labor-unions-ohio-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-62c5a9c38f088ba9fc80d8d2#block-62c5a9c38f088ba9fc80d8d2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reported}}}\uc2  that lawmakers had reached an agreement on provisions to lower prescription drug costs, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/climate-environment/2022/07/07/climate-reconciliation-bill-manchin/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post\u8217\'20\'19s report today}}}\uc2  signals that they\u8217\'20\'19re trying to find consensus around measures to fight climate change - particularly those that would pass muster from \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , the West Virginia senator whose resistance doomed Build Back Better last year.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/22/joe-biden-build-back-better-climate-crisis-consequences"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why the collapse of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Build Back Better would be a major blow to the climate fight}}}\par \par \uc2 Republicans are looking for ways to stop the effort. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/06/biden-economy-labor-unions-ohio-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-62c5aa9f8f088ba9fc80d8db#block-62c5aa9f8f088ba9fc80d8db"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate GOP leader Mitch McConnell has threatened}}}\uc2  to torpedo a bipartisan bill meant to fund American technological competitiveness if Democrats move forward with their unilateral proposal.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats bargain over climate with a familiar obstacle: \uc2 Joe Manchin\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Democrats are using what may be their limited time left controlling Congress to build a new spending package that will pay for many of the party\u8217\'20\'19s priorities \u8211\'20\'13 such as fighting climate change. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/climate-environment/2022/07/07/climate-reconciliation-bill-manchin/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post reported today}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , the West Virginia centrist who scuttled a previous spending effort last year, remains a sticking point in reaching a climate agreement, though talks are continuing.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 * President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will present the Presidential Medal of Freedom to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/07/01/president-biden-announces-recipients-of-the-presidential-medal-of-freedom/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 17 people}}}\uc2  in a ceremony at 2pm, including the gymnast Simone Biles, the actor Denzel Washington and, posthumously, \uc2 Apple\uc2  co-founder \uc2 Steve Jobs\uc2  and senator \uc2 John McCain\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * American airports will get {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/pete-buttigieg-federal-aviation-administration-government-and-politics-6f1100197862bcca7c0f5246625b418a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1bn for upgrades}}}\uc2  from the federal government, paid for by the infrastructure bill enacted last year.\par \par \uc2 * The fallout from the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision overturning Roe v Wade continues, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coloradosun.com/2022/07/06/colorado-abortion-investigations-polis-executive-order/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s governor moving to protect people seeking abortions}}}\uc2 , and a Louisiana court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theadvocate.com/baton_rouge/news/courts/article_46246d52-fd85-11ec-a465-cf68f1d929a6.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stopping the state from outlawing the procedure, for now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220707ei77001s1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
