\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Colorado governor issues executive order to protect  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  access\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 402 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 July 2022\par 15:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 34\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Jared Polis\uc2  pledges that his state will not assist other states in criminal or civil investigations into abortions\par \par \uc2 The Democratic governor of Colorado has mandated that his state will not cooperate with any investigations into abortions led by other states.\par \par \uc2 Jared Polis\uc2  signed an executive order on Wednesday pledging that the western US state will not assist other states in criminal or civil investigations used to prevent people from accessing abortions.\par \par \uc2 The executive order adds protections for individuals and organizations that provide abortions, as well as for individuals obtaining an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including people who have traveled from other states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are taking needed action to protect and defend individual freedom and protect the privacy of Coloradans,\u8221\'20\'1D said Polis in a statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coloradosun.com/2022/07/06/colorado-abortion-investigations-polis-executive-order/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtained by the Colorado Sun}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis important step will ensure that Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s thriving economy and workforce are not impacted based on personal health decisions that are wrongly being criminalized in other states.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/24/overturning-roe-story-is-women-unfreedom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nearly two weeks after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , dissolving a nearly 50-year precedent of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections, states have taken measures to protect reproductive rights for those living in the state or those traveling for reproductive healthcare services.\par \par \uc2 In North Carolina, the Democratic governor, Roy Cooper, signed an executive order on Wednesday protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights within the state. The order protects those who receive an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or medical providers who perform them from any penalties for providing, seeking or inquiring about reproductive healthcare, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/north-carolina-governor-signs-executive-order-protect-abortion/story?id=86330488"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported ABC News}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, other states have taken steps to further criminalize and limit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access following the supreme court decision.\par \par \uc2 In Mississippi, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/06/mississippi-abortion-clinic-closing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a state law taking effect on Thursday}}}\uc2  will ban most abortions throughout the state after a judge rejected an emergency request to block the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  trigger law.\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, closed on Wednesday following the ruling.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Ohio will remain in place after the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court refused to halt the ban while the court reviews lawsuit to overturn it, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cincinnati.com/story/news/politics/elections/2022/07/01/ohio-supreme-court-abortion-access/7776834001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported the Cincinnati Enquirer}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COhioans are suffering in real time, and we have not yet seen the worst of this healthcare crisis,\u8221\'20\'1D said a group of Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CAll people deserve autonomy over their bodies and the power to make their own healthcare decisions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220707ei770023a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
