\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: UK PM \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  to quit after extraordinary cabinet mutiny\b0\par\par\uc2 Mattha Busby \par \uc2 1,482 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 July 2022\par 10:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Johnson to resign as party leader but push to stay on as PM until autumn. Plus, Biden planned to nominate an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lawyerDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 The UK prime minister, \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2022/jul/07/boris-johnson-to-resign-as-conservative-leader"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been forced to resign}}}\uc2  as Conservative leader after an unprecedented standoff with his own cabinet that triggered dozens of resignations following criticism over his government\u8217\'20\'19s handling of a series of scandals, the latest surrounding alleged sexual misconduct by a deputy chief whip.\par \par \uc2 A delegation of senior cabinet ministers, including the new chancellor, \uc2 Nadhim Zahawi\uc2 , the home secretary, \uc2 Priti Patel\uc2 , and the transport secretary, \uc2 Grant Shapps\uc2 , personally urged him to resign. After the Northern Ireland secretary, the minister for tech and the recently appointed education secretary were among the latest to quit on Thursday, he relented.\par \par \uc2 Downing Street\uc2  issued a statement saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThe prime minister will make a statement to the country today.\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson is expected to deliver it from No 10 before lunchtime in the UK and reportedly wants to stay on as PM until a new Tory leader is chosen.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The pound was trading higher on the news of Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s resignation \u8211\'20\'13 up 0.6% at 1.198 US dollars after it fell to a two-year low against the dollar amid instability as the PM attempted to cling on.\par \par \uc2 Biden planned to nominate anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lawyer to judgeship\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  intended {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/06/biden-anti-abortion-lawyer-plan-emails"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to nominate a conservative lawyer}}}\uc2  who has previously defended anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation, Chad Meredith, to a federal judgeship.\par \par \uc2 The office of Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , has shared emails confirming the plans that were part of a reported deal with the Senate Republican leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , to avoid holding up the US president\u8217\'20\'19s other judicial nominations.\par \par \uc2 But after the supreme court released its decision to overturn Roe v Wade, ending the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, the nomination was not announced. Biden had already faced criticism over not defending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights strongly enough.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18If the president makes that nomination, it is indefensible.\u8217\'20\'19 Meredith has not yet been nominated to the federal bench, and it is likely doing so would set off a brutal internal battle within the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Outrage after latest mass shooting suspect obtained weapon despite record\par \par \uc2 The weaknesses of US gun control laws are in the spotlight again following the Highland Park mass shooting on the Fourth of July in which the alleged gunman was allowed to legally buy weapons despite multiple alarming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/06/highland-park-shooting-gun-law-loopholes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prior encounters with law enforcement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Local authorities in September 2019 declared Robert Crimo a \u8220\'20\'1Cclear and present danger\u8221\'20\'1D to the Illinois state police after he threatened to kill his family. Police briefly confiscated weapons from his house, yet three months later he successfully applied for a gun license at the age of 19. An emergency call was also reportedly made in April 2019 after the gunman had attempted suicide.\par \par \uc2 Before the massacre, Highland Park already had relatively strict gun laws by US standards. But the tragedy shows they still fell well short.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US mass shootings are getting deadlier and more common, analysis shows. The last five years have seen more mass shootings than any other comparable time span dating back to 1966, with 31 massacres from 2017 through 2021, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/06/us-mass-shootings-deadlier-more-common"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 compared with 24 from 2012 through 2016}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DoJ sues Arizona over voting law requiring citizenship proof\par \par \uc2 A new Arizona law that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/06/arizona-voting-law-doj-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 requires voters to provide proof of citizenship}}}\uc2  for presidential elections, among other new restrictions in the red state, is being challenged by the Department of Justice, which says the measure is a \u8220\'20\'1Ctextbook violation\u8221\'20\'1D of a federal law meant to protect voters.\par \par \uc2 The challenged measure was signed into law by the Republican governor, \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2 , in March. It requires anyone who wants to vote in a presidential election, or vote by mail in any election, to provide proof of citizenship.\par \par \uc2 This is in opposition to a 2013 supreme court ruling but some see the law as an attempt to get the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to reconsider its 2013 decision. The court has become significantly more conservative since then.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general gears up for a fight. \uc2 Mark Brnovich\uc2  has vowed that he would continue to defend the law. \u8220\'20\'1CPlease be assured I will defend this law to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  if necessary and defeat the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to interfere with our state\u8217\'20\'19s election safeguards.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The world\u8217\'20\'19s wealthiest man, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , fathered two children in 2021 with Shivon Zilis, an executive at his artificial intelligence company \uc2 Neuralink\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/jul/06/elon-musk-twins-children-shivon-zilis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new court documents show}}}\uc2 . Zilis reportedly gave birth weeks before Musk and singer Claire Boucher had their second child through a surrogate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A rural Georgia monument that some conservative Christians have criticized as satanic and that others have\par \par \uc2 called \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica\u8217\'20\'19s Stonehenge\u8221\'20\'1D was bombed before dawn yesterday\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/06/georgia-monument-guidestones-americas-stonehenge-bombed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in an attack}}}\uc2  reducing one of its granite panels to rubble.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Brazil\u8217\'20\'19s meat plants could be putting pregnant workers at risk, health experts have said. Rates of maternal disorders appear higher than in any other employment sector, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jul/07/brazils-meat-plants-could-be-putting-pregnant-workers-at-risk-say-health-experts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with thousands of women suffering}}}\uc2  as meat exports hit record highs.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United States Soccer Federation\uc2  has confirmed it has suspended the coaching\par \par \uc2 license\par \par \uc2 of Brad Evans after a Guardian investigation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jul/07/brad-evans-suspended-guardian-investigation-sexual-misconduct"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 into alleged sexual misconduct}}}\uc2  by the former \uc2 University of Toledo\uc2  head coach.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: US water likely contains more \u8216\'20\'18forever chemicals\u8217\'20\'19 than \uc2 EPA\uc2  tests show\par \par \uc2 A Guardian analysis of water samples from around the US shows that the type of water testing relied on by the \uc2 US Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) \uc2 is so limited in scope that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/06/us-drinking-water-pfas-toxic-forever-chemicals-epa-tests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it is probably missing significant levels of PFAS pollutants}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The undercount leaves regulators with an incomplete picture of the extent of PFAS contamination and reveals how millions of people may be facing an unknown health risk in their drinking water.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  found that seven of the nine samples collected showed higher levels of PFAS in water using the test that identifies markers for PFAS, than levels found when the water was tested using the \uc2 EPA\uc2  method \u8211\'20\'13 and at concentrations as much as 24 times greater, Tom Perkins writes.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: psychologists find hunger and emotions link\par \par \uc2 In one of the first studies to explore how hunger affects emotions as people go about their daily lives, psychologists have confirmed widespread suspicions in a finding that goes some way to confirming that the more hungry people feel, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2022/jul/06/being-hangry-is-a-real-thing-psychologists-find-link-between-hunger-and-emotions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the more angry \u8211\'20\'13 or hangry \u8211\'20\'13 they become}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Writing in the journal Plos One, the psychologists describe how hunger was associated with stronger feelings of anger and irritability and lower levels of pleasure. \u8220\'20\'1CIt turns out that being hangry is a real thing,\u8221\'20\'1D said the study lead, Prof Viren Swami, a social psychologist at \uc2 Anglia Ruskin University\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Climate check: why US may be headed for a summer of mega-fire\par \par \uc2 Fire activity is expected to increase in several US states over the coming months, according to a newly released outlook from the National Interagency Fire Center (NIFC), with parts of the Pacific north-west, northern California, Texas, Hawaii and Alaska {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/06/us-west-wildfire-summer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 forecast to be among those hardest hit}}}\uc2  by fire conditions in the months ahead.\par \par \uc2 It comes after an explosive spring that unleashed major wildfires from the US south-west to Alaska. The amount of acreage burned by this point in the year has eclipsed previous years, standing at roughly 220% higher than the 10-year average. In New Mexico in April, a blaze that started as a controlled burn escaped containment before it spread quickly and burned for months, consuming swaths of land and hundreds of homes and other buildings, Gabrielle Canon reports.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: inside the secret world of tennis umpires\par \par \uc2 There have been a string of acrimonious, high-profile incidents this year in which players have openly criticised officials, sometimes with obscenities. Tennis umpires, like officials in other sports, are not allowed to explain their decisions in press conferences or on social media. But journalist William Ralston was granted exceptional access {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jul/07/tennis-umpires-secret-world-you-cant-be-the-players-friend"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to many of the profession\u8217\'20\'19s most experienced officials}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mohamed Lahyani, a Swede who is one of the longest-serving umpires on the ATP tour, told him that criticism of umpires is becoming more intense and personal \u8211\'20\'13 even as technology reduces the margin for error in tight calls. The challenge is how to be strong and passive at moments like this. \u8220\'20\'1CIf the player comes to you and says, \u8216\'20\'18What the fuck are you doing,\u8217\'20\'19 we can\u8217\'20\'19t say, \u8216\'20\'18I am just doing my fucking job,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D said the Brazilian umpire Carlos Bernardes.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220707ei770018j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
