\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s White House counsel \uc2 Pat Cipollone\uc2  agrees to testify to January 6 panel \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 5,889 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 July 2022\par 20:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lawyer was subpoenaed last month by the House committee investigating the 2021 assault on the CapitolTrump White House counsel to cooperate with January 6 committeeSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/06/biden-economy-labor-unions-ohio-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-62c5e2868f089a79171d3fd5#block-62c5e2868f089a79171d3fd5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pitched his economic agenda to union workers in Ohio}}}\uc2  today, while there were further developments in the January 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s investigation as well as jostling within states ahead of November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Here are the highlights:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s White House counsel Pat Cipollone{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/06/january-6-trump-white-house-counsel-pat-cipollone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has agreed to speak}}}\uc2  to the January 6 committee, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/06/biden-economy-labor-unions-ohio-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-62c58c918f086c618d4b5655#block-62c58c918f086c618d4b5655"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced its next hearing}}}\uc2  for Tuesday 12 July.\par \par \uc2 * South Carolina senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  said he will fight a subpoena from a Georgia grand jury {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/06/biden-economy-labor-unions-ohio-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-62c5a12e8f089dd60ac4ea69#block-62c5a12e8f089dd60ac4ea69"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 looking into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts}}}\uc2  to subvert the 2020 election result in the state.\par \par \uc2 * Senate Democrats have agreed on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/06/biden-economy-labor-unions-ohio-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-62c5a9c38f088ba9fc80d8d2#block-62c5a9c38f088ba9fc80d8d2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposal to lower prescription drug costs}}}\uc2  via a reconciliation bill. However Senate Republican leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/06/biden-economy-labor-unions-ohio-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-62c5aa9f8f088ba9fc80d8db#block-62c5aa9f8f088ba9fc80d8db"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trying to stop Democrats from passing the legislation}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/06/biden-economy-labor-unions-ohio-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-62c58f7e8f084595044be62c#block-62c58f7e8f084595044be62c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will close}}}\uc2  after the supreme court overturned Roe v. Wade and the state banned the procedure.\par \par \uc2 * A group of Republicans in Pennsylvania {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/06/biden-economy-labor-unions-ohio-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-62c59aa58f084595044be6e2#block-62c59aa58f084595044be6e2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have endorsed the Democrat running for governor}}}\uc2  against a 2020 election denier.\par \par \uc2 * Democrats in Kentucky are unhappy with president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/06/biden-anti-abortion-lawyer-plan-emails"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 apparent plan to nominate an anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  judge}}}\uc2  to a federal court position, in what appears to be a bid to get Senate Republican leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  to stop blocking the president\u8217\'20\'19s nominees.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 The president finished up his speech in Cleveland by drawing a contrast between his administration and the Republicans who are waiting in the wings, hoping to take over the House of Representatives and Senate following the November midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Remarking on Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 previous efforts to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/08/obamacare-senator-ron-johnson-republican-affordable-care-act"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturn the Affordable Care Act}}}\uc2  and accusing them of wanting to privatize social security, Biden told unionized workers, \u8220\'20\'1CFolks, this is a different world where they live.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cfighting like hell\u8221\'20\'1D to try to lower costs for Americans, and accused Republicans of obstructing his efforts, including his proposal to lower taxes on gasoline - though several Democrats are also lukewarm towards that idea.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m asking Congress to eliminate the federal gas tax for... however long this crisis goes on, lower food prices lower health care costs, hopefully soon, lower your prescription drug costs,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, eluding to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/06/biden-economy-labor-unions-ohio-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-62c5a9c38f088ba9fc80d8d2#block-62c5a9c38f088ba9fc80d8d2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a recent proposal from Democratic senators}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden is telling union workers about his efforts to get the Butch Lewis Act passed, which allowed the Treasury to assist unions\u8217\'20\'19 pension plans that were financially struggling, and was included in the America Rescue Plan Biden enacted in March 2021.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s also attacking former president Trump, saying the economy was in shambles when he left office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CY\u8217\'20\'19all remember what the economy was like when I was elected? A country in a pandemic, with no real plans how to get out of it. Millions of people out of their jobs. Families and cars, remember, backed up for literally miles, to wait for a box of food to be put in their trunk,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe previous administration lost more jobs in his watch than any administration since \uc2 Herbert Hoover\uc2 . That\u8217\'20\'19s a fact. All based on failed trickle-down economics that benefit the wealthiest Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe came in with a fundamentally different economic vision, an economy that grows from the bottom up in the middle out. It\u8217\'20\'19s good for everyone because when the middle class does well the poor have a ladder up in the wealthy still do very well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 U.S. President Biden speaks about his economic agenda, in Cleveland, Ohio. Photograph: Kevin Lamarque/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Biden has started his speech to union workers in Cleveland, and while the address is mostly about the economy, he began with brief remarks about the police shooting of Jayland Walker in nearby Akron.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C The justice department\u8217\'20\'19s civil rights division, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and the local US attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office are closely viewing what happened,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf the evidence reveals potential violations of federal criminal statutes, the justice department will take the appropriate action.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Walker, who is Black, sustained more than 60 wounds after multiple officers opened fire at him following a car chase.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/04/jayland-walker-shooting-body-cam-video-outrage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Outrage after video of police fatally shooting Jayland Walker released}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden has arrived in Cleveland and is expected to shortly begin giving remarks on the economy, focused on the American Rescue Plan spending bill he won passage of near the beginning of his term last year.\par \par \uc2 Also speaking at the event are Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2 , and two of the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic House representatives, \uc2 Marcy Kaptur\uc2  and Shontel Brown. However, two notable Democrats won\u8217\'20\'19t be in attendance: \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2 , the party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination for \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , and \uc2 Nan Whaley\uc2 , its nominee in the governor\u8217\'20\'19s race.\par \par \uc2 enltrPlenty of mounting questions from fellow Dems on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s ability to lead after \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling, mass shootings and inflation. Today he\u8217\'20\'19s in Cleveland to talk \u8220\'20\'1CJobs, unions, retirement security.\u8221\'20\'1D Notably, the two Democrats running for statewide office in the state aren\u8217\'20\'19t there. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/02098n1SK5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/02098n1SK5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kevin Liptak (@Kevinliptakcnn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Kevinliptakcnn/status/1544750065499136000?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 With \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  so unpopular, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ensnarled in investigations centering on the January 6 insurrection and his efforts to overturn the 2020 election, the question must be asked: is it possible that neither man will be on the ballot in 2024?\par \par \uc2 There would be many contenders to fill the vacuum created if neither man stands in the next presidential election, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/07/06/newsom-desantis-election-2024-00044128"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico has a look}}}\uc2  at one possible matchup: California\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  against Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 The governors for California and Florida have hurled insults about each other\u8217\'20\'19s leadership and policies during most of the Covid-19 pandemic. But now Newsom has ratcheted up the conflict by taking almost daily pot-shots at his Republican foils such as DeSantis and Texas Attorney General \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 . Most recently, Newsom dropped more than $100,000 on a new ad airing on Fox News that tweaked DeSantis in his home state. On Tuesday, he started fundraising off the ad and conflict with DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 Fox-watching Floridians won\u8217\'20\'19t likely switch their voter registration or move to California after seeing a TV spot in which Newsom warned them \u8220\'20\'1Cfreedom is under attack in your state.\u8221\'20\'1D But the ad is producing a frenzy of national coverage that boosts Newsom\u8217\'20\'19s profile while allowing DeSantis to sharpen his attacks on Democrats ahead of a possible 2024 White House bid.\par \par \uc2 The fight highlights how two young governors have captured the attention of their respective parties: On one side is Newsom, a progressive and telegenic leader who survived an attempted recall. On the other is DeSantis, who is often heralded as a more disciplined \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  but who also has a penchant for populism and a refusal to back down from a fight.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMost politicians operate best when they have somebody or something to contrast against, and there\u8217\'20\'19s no bigger contrast to \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  and California right now than Florida and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jim Ross, a Democratic consultant who ran Newsom\u8217\'20\'19s first mayoral campaign.\par \par \uc2 Newsom has in fact just put out a statement to supporters explaining why he purchased ads in Florida:\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GavinNewsom?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GavinNewsom}}}\uc2  emails supporters to explain why he spent $100,000 to run a TV spot in Florida: to reclaim the word "Freedom," declaring that "The DeSantis vision of freedom is a fraud." Here's what Newsom says freedom should really mean: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Vf7s5pLcJS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Vf7s5pLcJS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Doug Sovern (@SovernNation) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SovernNation/status/1544751470234390529?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/04/gavin-newsom-florida-ad-fox-news-ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Newsom airs Florida ad urging people to fight for freedom \u8211\'20\'13 or move to California}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona was one of the states where Trump attempted unsuccessfully to convince officials to work with him to overturn the results of the 2020 elections. As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  reports, its elections are under scrutiny again, this time by Biden\u8217\'20\'19s justice department:\par \par \uc2 The Department of Justice is challenging a new Arizona law that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/30/arizona-voting-rights-citizenship-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 requires voters to provide proof of citizenship}}}\uc2  for presidential elections, among other new restrictions, saying the measure was a \u8220\'20\'1Ctextbook violation\u8221\'20\'1D of a federal law meant to protect voters.\par \par \uc2 The challenged {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2  measure, HB 2492, was signed into law by the Republican governor, \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2 , in March, requires anyone who wants to vote in a presidential election, or vote by mail in any election, to provide proof of citizenship.\par \par \uc2 The law was among several pushed by the Arizona legislature following the 2020 election in a state where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies have spread baseless claims of fraud. Voting by mail is widely used in Arizona, a key battleground state, and Republicans in the state have made numerous attempts to make it harder to cast a ballot that way.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/06/arizona-voting-law-doj-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DoJ sues Arizona over voting law that requires proof of citizenship}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  has more details about what to expect from Trump White House counsel \uc2 Pat Cipollone\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s testimony to the January 6 committee:\par \par \uc2 The former Trump White House counsel \uc2 Pat Cipollone\uc2  is expected to testify to the House January 6 select committee on Friday after reaching an agreement over the scope of his cooperation with a subpoena compelling his testimony, according to a source familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The testimony from Cipollone is expected to be a transcribed interview and recorded on camera, the source said, and the former top White House lawyer is expected to only answer questions on a narrow subset of topics and conversations with the former president.\par \par \uc2 Among the topics Cipollone could discuss include how he told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  that pressuring \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , the vice-president, to refuse to certify \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election win was unlawful, and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plot to coerce the justice department into falsely saying the 2020 election was corrupt.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/06/january-6-trump-white-house-counsel-pat-cipollone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump White House counsel to cooperate with January 6 committee}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The dispute over USICA and the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 potential reconciliation bill has now spilled on to \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It began when \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2 , a Republican senator from Texas, criticized Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 move to pass a spending package unilaterally via the reconciliation procedure, accusing them of giving up on the USICA technological competitiveness bill:\par \par \uc2 enltrLooks like Schumer giving up on USICA, including shoring up the vulnerable supply chain for high end semiconductors. Major chip makers will likely abandon their plans to build manufacturing facilities in the US. Body blow to US national security, economy, and well paying jobs. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KwV7mUR4iF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/KwV7mUR4iF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  (@JohnCornyn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JohnCornyn/status/1544624445368803328?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  did not take kindly to his accusation:\par \par \uc2 enltrCornyn is joining McConnell to hold hostage a bipartisan bill that would make more in America, in order to protect pharmaceutical companies\u8217\'20\'19 profits.\par \par \uc2 We need to do BOTH: increase American manufacturing and strengthen our competitive edge against China, AND lower Rx drug costs. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VewJih7c59"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/VewJih7c59}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  (@PressSec) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec/status/1544724102300110848?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Prompting this retort from Cornyn:\par \par \uc2 enltrYou people in the Biden administration are very confused {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yXaIT7K4JY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/yXaIT7K4JY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  (@JohnCornyn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JohnCornyn/status/1544740072712327168?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Whether on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  or in Congress, expect the broader dispute to play out in the months to come.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s top Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has given Democrats an ultimatum: if they proceed with their reconciliation package, his lawmakers won\u8217\'20\'19t support a bill to enhance US industries\u8217\'20\'19 technological competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 enltrLet me be perfectly clear: there will be no bipartisan USICA as long as Democrats are pursuing a partisan reconciliation bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Leader McConnell (@LeaderMcConnell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeaderMcConnell/status/1542600738823618564?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 30, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/senate-bill/1260"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 United States Innovation and Competition Act}}}\uc2 , known as USICA, has been bargained over in Congress for months. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/archive/7-6-22-punchbowl-news-am/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to Punchbowl}}}\uc2 , the prospects for the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s democratic majority pulling off both the reconciliation package and USICA are not good:\par \par \uc2 There are 1,015 outstanding items in the USICA package and GOP sources tell us that party leaders have only come to agreement or agreed to drop 127 of them. That means nearly nine-tenths of the bill is open and unresolved.\par \par \uc2 Democrats take issue with this characterization. They say the two sides have actually closed out many more issues, but Republicans have withheld final confirmation on several hundred items until bigger-picture topics have been resolved.\par \par \uc2 In negotiations like this, it\u8217\'20\'19s often difficult to totally discern where talks stand because both sides have incentive to show that the other is slow walking the talks or otherwise acting in a capricious manner.\par \par \uc2 But let\u8217\'20\'19s put it this way: Any way you slice it, the two sides can\u8217\'20\'19t even agree on which phase of the negotiation they\u8217\'20\'19re in.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Politico has details of Senate Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to find agreement on a major piece of legislation that they can pass, likely without Republican support.\par \par \uc2 The negotiations come after the collapse of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Build Back Better proposal last year, which was meant to spend potentially trillions of dollars on fighting climate change, expanding social services and other Democratic priorities, but collapsed amid infighting in the party, particularly with senators \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  and \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Democrats have been quietly trying to come up with a new proposal that could make it through the chamber using its reconciliation procedure, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/huddle/2022/07/06/recess-reconciliation-move-schumer-submits-some-text-00044194"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports that they\u8217\'20\'19ve reached an agreement on a measure to lower prescription drug costs}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (D-N.Y.) will submit text today to the Senate parliamentarian on a 50-Democrat agreement (yes, that includes Sen. \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  (D-W.Va.)) to allow the federal government to negotiate prescription drug costs for Medicare, according to two sources familiar. That will kick off the so-called \u8220\'20\'1CByrd Bath\u8221\'20\'1D where the parliamentarian reviews the proposed text to make sure it abides by the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s reconciliation rules. The bath is supposed to purge extraneous provisions that don\u8217\'20\'19t align with the reconciliation instructions.\par \par \uc2 But drug price negotiation is just one piece of the puzzle. The rest of the party-line package is still in flux and isn\u8217\'20\'19t ready for its Byrd Bath. Schumer and Manchin have been meeting regularly about what might make it into the bill, talking about tax reform and climate provisions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden holds call with the wife of Brittney Griner\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , joined by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , spoke today with Cherelle Griner, the wife of Brittney Griner, the US basket ball star detained in Russia. Griner was detained by \uc2 Russian Federal Customs Service\uc2  in February after they said they found vape cartridges that contained hashish oil in her luggage at an airport near Moscow.\par \par \uc2 In a readout of the call, the White House said: \u8220\'20\'1C The President called Cherelle to reassure her that he is working to secure Brittney\u8217\'20\'19s release as soon as possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe President directed his national security team to remain in regular contact with Cherelle and Brittney\u8217\'20\'19s family, and with other families of Americans held hostage or wrongfully detained abroad, to keep them updated on efforts to secure the release of their loved ones as quickly as possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Brittney Griner recently wrote a letter to Biden appealing for his assistance in getting her released from prison.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Congress may be in recess but there\u8217\'20\'19s been plenty of political news this morning, from the ongoing work of the January 6 committee to jostling within states ahead of November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what has happened so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s White House counsel Pat Cipollone{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/06/biden-economy-labor-unions-ohio-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-62c59e6c8f086c618d4b5761#block-62c59e6c8f086c618d4b5761"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has agreed to speak}}}\uc2  to the January 6 committee, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/06/biden-economy-labor-unions-ohio-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-62c58c918f086c618d4b5655#block-62c58c918f086c618d4b5655"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced its next hearing}}}\uc2  for Tuesday 12 July.\par \par \uc2 * South Carolina senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  said he will fight a subpoena from a Georgia grand jury {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/06/biden-economy-labor-unions-ohio-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-62c5a12e8f089dd60ac4ea69#block-62c5a12e8f089dd60ac4ea69"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 looking into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts}}}\uc2  to subvert the 2020 election result in the state.\par \par \uc2 * Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/06/biden-economy-labor-unions-ohio-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-62c58f7e8f084595044be62c#block-62c58f7e8f084595044be62c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will close}}}\uc2  after the supreme court overturned Roe v. Wade and the state banned the procedure.\par \par \uc2 * A group of Republicans in Pennsylvania {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/06/biden-economy-labor-unions-ohio-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-62c59aa58f084595044be6e2#block-62c59aa58f084595044be6e2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have endorsed the Democrat running for governor}}}\uc2  against a 2020 election denier.\par \par \uc2 * Democrats in Kentucky are unhappy with president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/06/biden-economy-labor-unions-ohio-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-62c5a7338f089dd60ac4eacc#block-62c5a7338f089dd60ac4eacc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 apparent plan to nominate an anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  judge}}}\uc2  to a federal court position, in what appears to be a bid to get Senate Republican leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  to stop blocking the president\u8217\'20\'19s nominees.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking together in Britain, the heads of the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and MI5 have issued a joint warning about China\u8217\'20\'19s behavior, saying Beijing is stealing western technology and studying from the war in Ukraine, particularly when it comes to evading sanctions.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: The heads of MI5 and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FBI?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FBI}}}\uc2  have used an unprecedented joint speech to warn that China is their biggest \u8220\'20\'1Cgame-changing challenge\u8221\'20\'1D, with the UK doubling efforts to combat Chinese "activity of concern". 1/\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Deborah Haynes (@haynesdeborah) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/haynesdeborah/status/1544713873957294081?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrChristopher Wray, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, said Beijing is drawing lessons from Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Talking about the Chinese threat against Taiwan, he said the Chinese government was looking for ways to protect its economy against any potential, future sanctions. 2/\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Deborah Haynes (@haynesdeborah) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/haynesdeborah/status/1544714345359331328?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CIn our world, we call that kind of behaviour a clue,\u8221\'20\'1D Mr Wray said, sharing a platform with Ken McCallum on a visit to MI5\u8217\'20\'19s headquarters in London. Western allies used sweeping sanctions to punish Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  over his invasion of Ukraine. 3/\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Deborah Haynes (@haynesdeborah) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/haynesdeborah/status/1544714569356087297?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe 2 chiefs focused on the Chinese Communist Party & its covert operations.\par \par \uc2 They accused Beijing of a vast, enduring effort to steal western advances in technology, research & other sectors as well as use the West\u8217\'20\'19s democratic, media & legal systems to their own advantage. 4/\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Deborah Haynes (@haynesdeborah) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/haynesdeborah/status/1544715221339619333?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CThe most game-changing challenge we face comes from the Chinese Communist Party,\u8221\'20\'1D Mr McCallum said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s covertly applying pressure across the globe. This might feel abstract. But it\u8217\'20\'19s real and it\u8217\'20\'19s pressing. We need to talk about it. We need to act.\u8221\'20\'1D 5/\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Deborah Haynes (@haynesdeborah) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/haynesdeborah/status/1544715344765501440?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Illinois parade shooter confesses, says planned second attack\par \par \uc2 The shooter at an Independence Day parade in a Chicago suburb has admitted to the attack and told police he contemplated opening fire at a second Fourth of July gathering, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/gun-violence-chicago-shootings-lake-michigan-9fd3e23a6396aa5e008943fbb260551b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The man charged with killing seven people at an Independence Day parade confessed to police that he unleashed a hail of bullets from a rooftop in suburban Chicago and then fled to the Madison, Wisconsin, area, where he contemplated shooting up an event there, authorities said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Robert Crimo III turned back to Illinois, where he was later arrested after deciding he was not prepared to pull off a shooting in Wisconsin, Lake County Major Crime Task Force spokesman Christopher Covelli said.\par \par \uc2 An Illinois judge ordered Crimo to be held without bail. Police found the shells of 83 bullets and three ammunition magazines on the rooftop that he fired from, Lake County Assistant State\u8217\'20\'19s Attorney Ben Dillon said in court.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sen. \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  speaks during a visit to the Mack Gaston Community Center in Dalton, Ga. on Wednesday, June 29, 2022. Photograph: Matt Hamilton/AP\par \par \uc2 The Georgia Senate race is another closely watched election this year, where the Democratic incumbent \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  will face off against Republican challenger \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Walker has had multiple complaints leveled against him of breaking rules governing electioneering, but Politico is reporting that Warnock also may have violated campaign finance laws:\par \par \uc2 Sen. \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  (D-Ga.) used campaign money to cover legal expenses for a lawsuit relating to his time as a church minister \u8212\'20\'14 transactions that raise questions about whether the spending runs afoul of federal rules governing personal use of campaign funds.\par \par \uc2 The case, first filed in 2019 by Atlanta resident Melvin Robertson, involved baffling and seemingly baseless allegations against Warnock that date back to 2005 when he was a pastor. It was dismissed by a federal district court judge in Georgia without any of the defendants being served.\par \par \uc2 But Robertson refiled a similar lawsuit in April 2021, outlining the same allegations against Warnock while also suing Ebenezer Baptist Church, where he has long served as senior pastor, and other public figures.\par \par \uc2 This time, Warnock was serving in the Senate. And he enlisted his campaign attorneys from Elias Law Group to represent him in the case, along with an Atlanta firm, Krevolin & Horst, which assisted ELG.\par \par \uc2 The issue for Warnock is whether this was a proper use of campaign funds.\par \par \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2  guidance states that campaign money can be used on \u8220\'20\'1Clitigation expenses where the candidate/officeholder was the defendant and the litigation arose directly from campaign activity or the candidate\u8217\'20\'19s status as a candidate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Warnock was one of two Democrats elected to represent Georgia in the Senate last year, giving the party control of the chamber by a one-vote margin. Walker, meanwhile, is a rare Black Republican politician, and looking to reclaim a seat held by the GOP for the past 15 years.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/22/herschel-walker-senate-republican-primary-georgia-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Herschel Walker: the ex-football star running for Senate in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s shadow}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 A feud appears to be brewing between Biden and the top Democrats in Kentucky, including its governo r \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It began last week when the Courier-Journal reported that Biden intended to nominate an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  judge to a federal district court, in an apparent deal with \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senator who leads the party in Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber. Now, the Courier-Journal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courier-journal.com/story/news/politics/mitch-mcconnell/2022/07/05/beshear-turns-over-privileged-emails-chad-meredith-nomination/7816042001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has managed to obtain emails}}}\uc2  between the White House and Beshear\u8217\'20\'19s office that elaborate on the deal, which the Biden administration has declined to talk about.\par \par \uc2 The governor\u8217\'20\'19s office also turned over a follow-up email from a White House official sent June 29 \u8212\'20\'14 five hours before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courier-journal.com/story/news/politics/mitch-mcconnell/2022/06/29/biden-backs-anti-abortion-judge-candidate-apparent-mcconnell-deal/7767539001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Courier Journal first broke the story}}}\uc2  on the pending nomination of attorney Chad Meredith \u8212\'20\'14 clarifying that the original email was \u8220\'20\'1Cpre-decisional and privileged information.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 White House aide Kathleen M. Marshall, a former lieutenant governor in Nevada who joined the White House in August as senior adviser to governors in the Office of Intergovernmental Affairs, sent the June 23 email that stated: \u8220\'20\'1CTo be nominated tomorrow: \u8230\'20\'26 Stephen Chad Meredith: candidate for the United States District Court for the Eastern District of Kentucky.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The email, with a subject line of \u8220\'20\'1CClose hold,\u8221\'20\'1D was sent to Coulter Minix, a Beshear staffer in the governor\u8217\'20\'19s D.C. office, who immediately replied: \u8220\'20\'1CThanks, Kate. I\u8217\'20\'19ll share the info and appreciate the heads up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Beshear and \uc2 John Yarmuth\uc2 , a prominent Democratic House representative from the state, have both objected to the nomination, particularly after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade last month. The Courier-Journal has reported that the White House is looking for ways to stop McConnell from blocking the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s nominations for Senate-confirmed posts.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania is the site of one of the more high-profile governorship races this year, with the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic attorney general Josh Shapiro facing off against state senator \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , a promoter of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s false claims that the 2020 election was stolen.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.post-gazette.com/news/politics-state/2022/07/06/republican-endorsement-pennsylvania-governor-race-democrat-josh-shapiro-doug-mastriano-candidates/stories/202207050085"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Pittsburgh Post-Gazette reports}}}\uc2  that several state Republicans have taken the unusual step in the swing state of defecting from their party and backing Shapiro for the governorship:\par \par \uc2 Mr. Shapiro, the sitting attorney general, will roll out the endorsements of 10 Republicans on Wednesday as part of a continued effort to label his candidacy a reach-across-the-aisle aficionado who will unify the parties to get things done.\par \par \uc2 The list includes two former U.S. representatives, Charlie Dent and Jim Greenwood; former state House Speaker Denny O\u8217\'20\'19Brien; former Lt. Gov. and longtime state Sen. Robert Jubelirer; and former state Supreme Court Justice Sandra Schultz Newman.\par \par \uc2 The endorsements aren\u8217\'20\'19t just vague odes to bipartisanship in a divided country; they serve as a direct hit against state Sen. \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , the Republican candidate for governor, and it\u8217\'20\'19s reminiscent of the effort before the GOP primary among Republican insiders to coalesce support around an alternative. That effort failed, but Mr. Shapiro\u8217\'20\'19s camp and allies are hoping this lends credence to his argument that Mr. Mastriano is on the fringe of his own party.\par \par \uc2 Mastriano was involved in an effort to swing Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s vote from Biden to Trump following the 2020 election, and has been subpoenaed by the January 6 committee.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/20/doug-mastriano-pennsylvania-republican-governor-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Trump loyalist who could be a major threat to US democracy}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 South Carolina senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  has vowed to fight a subpoena issued to him by a Georgia grand jury looking into efforts to subvert that state\u8217\'20\'19s election result in 2020.\par \par \uc2 enltrU.S. Sen. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  has lawyered up as a Georgia grand jury investigates possible interference in the 2020 presidential election. The SC Republican\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys have released a statement saying Graham is neither a subject nor a target even after being subpoenaed in the probe. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3ESeXDQSZ8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3ESeXDQSZ8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Avery G. Wilks (@AveryGWilks) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AveryGWilks/status/1544690659692630018?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Other targets of the subpoenas reported yesterday include \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyer \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  and conservative attorneys John Eastman, Cleta Mitchell, Kenneth Chesebro and Jenna Ellis. Eastman has been repeatedly mentioned by witnesses before the January 6 committee as playing a major role in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/05/georgia-grand-jury-subpoenas-trump-legal-advisers-2020-election-effort"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia grand jury subpoenas Trump lawyers over effort to overturn election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump White House counsel to speak to January 6 committee\par \par \uc2 Pat Cipollone\uc2 , the White House counsel for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has agreed to testify to the January 6 committee, \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS: Deal for Cipollone to testify on Friday in transcribed interview, per person briefed on the matter.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Maggie Haberman (@maggieNYT) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maggieNYT/status/1544690546287038465?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrCipollone is appearing under subpoena for a transcribed interview with the House select committee.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Maggie Haberman (@maggieNYT) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maggieNYT/status/1544690713094397955?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe appearance is not going to be in public, according to the person briefed on the matter.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Maggie Haberman (@maggieNYT) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maggieNYT/status/1544692397594087430?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The committee investigating the attack had last month subpoenaed Cipollone, who \u8220\'20\'1Crepeatedly raised legal and other concerns about President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s activities on January 6 and in the days that preceded\u8221\'20\'1D, the committee\u8217\'20\'19s chairman, \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/29/january-6-committee-subpoena-pat-cipollone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6 committee subpoenas former White House counsel Pat Cipollone}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 committee announces July 12 hearing\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee has announced it will resume its hearings on Tuesday of next week, when Congress returns from recess.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEXT HEARING: Tuesday, July 12th at 10:00am ET\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 January 6th Committee (@January6thCmte) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/January6thCmte/status/1544428991272161280?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The House lawmakers\u8217\'20\'19 most recent hearing featured major revelations about the actions of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his inner circle before and during the insurrection.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/28/january-6-committee-session-new-evidence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ex-White House aide delivers explosive public testimony to January 6 panel}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling curbing the \uc2 US government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ability to regulate greenhouse gasses has repercussions worldwide, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/oliver-milman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oliver Milman}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election triggered a global surge in optimism that the climate crisis would, finally, be decisively confronted. But the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision last week to curtail America\u8217\'20\'19s ability to cut planet-heating emissions has proved the latest blow to a faltering effort by Biden on climate that is now in danger of becoming largely moribund.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/30/us-supreme-court-ruling-restricts-federal-power-greenhouse-gas-emissions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling}}}\uc2  that the \uc2 US government\uc2  could not use its existing powers to phase out coal-fired power generation without \u8220\'20\'1Cclear congressional authorization\u8221\'20\'1D quickly ricocheted around the world among those now accustomed to looking on in dismay at America\u8217\'20\'19s seemingly endless stumbles in addressing global heating.\par \par \uc2 The decision \u8220\'20\'1Cflies in the face of established science and will set back the US\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to keep global temperature below 1.5C\u8221\'20\'1D, said Saleemul Huq, director of the International Centre for Climate Change and Development in Bangladesh, in reference to the internationally agreed goal to limit global heating before it becomes truly catastrophic, manifesting in more severe heatwaves, floods, droughts and societal unrest.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jul/06/supreme-court-epa-ruling-biden-climate-policy-global-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Global dismay as supreme court ruling leaves Biden\u8217\'20\'19s climate policy in tatters}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic that was at the center of the supreme court decision overturning Roe v Wade, will close, the Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 The clinic had sued to stop the enforcement of state law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but lost in court yesterday. According to the AP:\par \par \uc2 As attorneys argued about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws across the south on Tuesday, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mississippi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi}}}\uc2  judge rejected a request by the state\u8217\'20\'19s only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic to temporarily block a law that would ban most abortions.\par \par \uc2 Without other developments in the Mississippi lawsuit, the clinic will close at the end of business on Wednesday and the state law will take effect on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 One of the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys, \uc2 Hillary Schneller\uc2  of the Center for Reproductive Rights, said the judge should have blocked the law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople in Mississippi who need abortions right now are in a state of panic, trying to get into the clinic before it\u8217\'20\'19s too late,\u8221\'20\'1D Schneller said. \u8220\'20\'1CNo one should be forced to live in fear like that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/06/mississippi-abortion-clinic-closing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s only \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  clinic to close after judge leaves state law in force}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 If it seems like mass shootings in America are getting worse, it\u8217\'20\'19s because they are, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.themarshallproject.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Marshall Project}}}\uc2  has concluded, based on data from the tragedies:\par \par \uc2 On the morning of 4 July, President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  hailed the day as one to \u8220\'20\'1Ccelebrate the goodness of our nation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Less than an hour after his 9.25am EST tweet, a gunman on a rooftop opened fire into a crowd of spectators who gathered to enjoy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://chicago.suntimes.com/2022/7/4/23194354/highland-park-fourth-july-parade-gunfire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Fourth of July parade in a Chicago suburb}}}\uc2 . He killed seven people and injured dozens.\par \par \uc2 Monday\u8217\'20\'19s mass shooting in Highland Park, Illinois, brought fresh anguish to a nation already shaken this year by the murders of schoolchildren in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://chicago.suntimes.com/2022/7/4/23194354/highland-park-fourth-july-parade-gunfire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Uvalde}}}\uc2 , Texas, and Black shoppers in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/15/nyregion/buffalo-shooting-hate-crime-charges.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Buffalo}}}\uc2 , New York.\par \par \uc2 If it feels like mass shootings have become more frequent, that intuition is correct, according to data analysis by the Marshall Project.\par \par \uc2 Under one of the most conservative definitions of \u8220\'20\'1Cmass shootings\u8221\'20\'1D, in which a gunman slaughters four or more strangers in a public place, the number of these crimes has indeed been climbing in the last few years \u8211\'20\'13 and they have higher death tolls, as well.\par \par \uc2 Mass shootings account for just a fraction of the daily toll of firearm deaths in the US, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/violenceprevention/firearms/fastfact.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 124 people die}}}\uc2  every day in other acts of gun violence.\par \par \uc2 Our analysis is based on data from the Violence Project, a nonprofit research group that uses a narrow definition of mass shootings adopted from the congressional research service, which advises federal lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 Thirty-one of these massacres occurred from 2017 through 2021, compared with 24 from 2012 through 2016, according to the Violence Project data. We compared five-year periods so we could measure trends over time, rather than focus on the dip to two incidents in 2020, which researchers attributed to the Covid-19 lockdown, or the spike caused by the 2017 mass shooting in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lasvegassun.com/news/2021/oct/01/in-our-memories-forever-las-vegas-marks-4th-annive/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Las Vegas}}}\uc2  that left 58 dead. The last five years have seen more mass shootings than any other comparable time span dating back to 1966.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/06/us-mass-shootings-deadlier-more-common"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US mass shootings are getting deadlier and more common, analysis shows}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 A reminder of the setbacks and tragedies that Biden has had to contend with in the past few weeks.\par \par \uc2 First the supreme court overturned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, expanded gun access and curbed the government\u8217\'20\'19s ability to regulate greenhouses gasses. Then the Independence Day weekend was rocked by gun violence, including a mass shooting at a July 4 parade in Illinois that killed seven people and wounded more than 40.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/07/05/biden-democrats-newsom-pritzker/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 string}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/07/06/biden-gun-bill-highland-park-shooting-00044166?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 of}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/07/05/politics/democrats-frustrated-biden-lack-of-urgency-supreme-court-setbacks/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent}}}\uc2  news reports suggest that even some of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s allies are questioning his approach to these challenges. Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/05/highland-park-shooting-chicago-philadelphia-gun-violence-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62c459058f088c74bb93b98e#block-62c459058f088c74bb93b98e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a poll released yesterday}}}\uc2  showed that his approval rating is suffering badly, and voters are still most worried about inflation and the economy, rather than gun rights and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , two issues that Democrats hoped to could rally their base ahead of the midterms.\par \par \uc2 In Ohio today, Biden will highlight the continued benefits of the American Rescue Plan, a massive spending bill passed last year at the cost of $1.9 trillion that was intended to revitalize the economy after the downturn caused by Covid-19. The audience will be union workers at a high school in Cleveland, but whether his message reaches voters remains to be seen.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden searches for reset after supreme court, shootings hamper agenda\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Repeatedly in the past few weeks, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has had to reassure voters that everything is going to be OK after upheavals at the supreme court, or gun violence in the streets. But from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/05/highland-park-shooting-chicago-philadelphia-gun-violence-latest?page=with:block-62c459058f088c74bb93b98e#block-62c459058f088c74bb93b98e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brutal polls}}}\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/07/05/politics/democrats-frustrated-biden-lack-of-urgency-supreme-court-setbacks/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 skeptical news articles}}}\uc2 , evidence has mounted that voters aren\u8217\'20\'19t convinced he\u8217\'20\'19s the man to tackle these challenges. Biden will get a chance today to dispel these doubts during a trip to Ohio, where he\u8217\'20\'19s set to make a speech on the economy.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 * The House and Senate are in recess but senators are working on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/newsletter/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reconciliation bill}}}\uc2  full of Democratic priorities.\par \par \uc2 * Political analysis doyen \uc2 Larry Sabato\uc2  will hold forth about the state of play {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?521469-5/washington-journal-larry-sabato-discusses-campaign-2022-political-news-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on C-Span this morning}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Wrangling over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access continues as conservative state governments attempt to outlaw the procedure following last month\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court ruling, with courts yesterday weighing in on bans in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wdrb.com/news/kentucky-supreme-court-denies-ags-request-to-reinstate-abortion-ban/article_dac6abf6-fcd5-11ec-9f30-ff89a597b9b2.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kentucky}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/05/florida-abortion-ban-restored-15-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220706ei76001xk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
