\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden backs exception to Senate filibuster to protect  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  access\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly and agencies \par \uc2 606 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 July 2022\par 12:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President in Madrid says he supports \u8216\'20\'18exception to the filibuster for this action to deal with the supreme court decision\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said on Thursday he would support an exception to the Senate filibuster to protect access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/29/roe-v-wade-dobbs-abortion-ruling-states-power-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned the right}}}\uc2  in a historic ruling this month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the filibuster gets in the way, it\u8217\'20\'19s like voting rights,\u8220\'20\'1C Biden said during a press conference at the Nato summit in Madrid, adding that there should be an \u8220\'20\'1Cexception to the filibuster for this action to deal with the supreme court decision\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The term filibuster refers to the 60-seat super-majority needed for most legislation to pass the Senate without being blocked by any single senator.\par \par \uc2 The rule is meant to help the Senate act as a less volatile chamber than the House, which works on simple majority votes, and to protect the rights of the minority.\par \par \uc2 But many on the left charge Republicans and some centrist Democrats with using the rule more in the archaic, Spanish-derived sense of the word \u8220\'20\'1Cfilibuster\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.senate.gov/reference/Index/Filibuster.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as pirates or raiders}}}\uc2 , ransacking the political process to their own advantage.\par \par \uc2 Biden was a senator from 1973 until 2009. An institutionalist to the core, he has been reluctant to support changes to the filibuster \u8211\'20\'13 even \u8220\'20\'1Ccarve-outs\u8221\'20\'1D for key legislation.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, Biden endorsed a carve-out on the issue of voting rights. The move was meant to answer Republican attacks on those likely to vote Democratic, prominently African Americans, but two Democrats, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/2022/1/19/22881837/senate-filibuster-vote-voting-rights-joe-manchin-kyrsten-sinema"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Manchin of West Virginia}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/01/13/us/politics/sinema-voting-rights-bill.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema of Arizona}}}\uc2 , stood in the way of their party.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s latest comments made clear he is willing to support a carve-out to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Manchin and Sinema would in all likelihood block the move once again.\par \par \uc2 With the Senate split 50-50 and controlled by the vote of the vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 legislative options are limited.\par \par \uc2 Biden is therefore under pressure to take executive action to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Although his options are few, in Madrid he said he would meet governors on Friday to talk about the issue and would \u8220\'20\'1Chave announcements to make then\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2022/jun/24/overturning-roe-a-sad-day-for-the-court-and-for-the-country-says-joe-biden-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeated}}}\uc2  harsh criticism of the decision to overturn Roe v Wade, the 1973 ruling which guaranteed the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and reiterated his warning that other constitutional protections could be at risk from a supreme court tilted right by three justices appointed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1COne thing that has been destabilising is the outrageous behavior of the supreme court of the United States in overruling not only Roe v Wade but essentially challenging the right to privacy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , the senior conservative on the court, has written that other privacy-based rights, to contraception, gay sex and same sex marriage, should be examined.\par \par \uc2 Thomas did not say another such right, to interracial marriage, was in question. He is Black. His wife, the far-right activist Ginni Thomas, is white.\par \par \uc2 As a devout Catholic, Biden has long seen many US left {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/jun/13/joe-biden-2006-video-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 question his bona fides}}}\uc2  as a supporter of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. In such quarters, the president\u8217\'20\'19s remarks in Spain met with rather weary responses.\par \par \uc2 Elie Mystal, justice correspondent of the Nation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ElieNYC/status/1542505166645039111"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1COh look, Biden said he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t open to changing the filibuster to pass a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, people loudly complained, and now he\u8217\'20\'19s changed his mind. FUNNY HOW THAT WORKS!\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s almost like telling elected officials what we want them to DO makes them more likely to DO IT.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220706ei76002q7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
