\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Police may be at your hospital bed\u8217\'20\'19: an  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights activist on post-Roe criminalization\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levin in Los Angeles \par \uc2 1,736 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 July 2022\par 12:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Renee Bracey Sherman argues that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and police support cannot go hand-in-hand\par \par \uc2 On the day {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  was overturned, longtime reproductive justice activist Renee Bracey Sherman joined thousands of demonstrators in front of the supreme court as they processed the news.\par \par \uc2 The mood was one of profound sadness, shock and disbelief, she said. Even though pro-choice activists had known this day was coming, it marked a stunning moment of loss for organizers who had spent decades fighting for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The day before the decision, Bracey Sherman, the founder of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wetestify.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 We Testify}}}\uc2 , an organization that shares stories of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , argued in a column in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thenation.com/article/society/abortion-police/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Nation}}}\uc2  that police and law enforcement have long hampered the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights movement \u8211\'20\'13 and that they would have a dramatically expanded role in a post-Roe world where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely criminalized.\par \par \uc2 Citing police abuse of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights demonstrators at rallies, officers failing to stop the harassment of patients by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists, instances of mistreatment of pregnant people in custody and the surveillance and prosecutions of people who have experienced pregnancy loss, she wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CWhere \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a crime, state officials will be responsible for enforcing the law, and that duty will fall primarily to the police \u8211\'20\'13 the very police who now support and foster anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  harassment of patients.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  spoke to Bracey Sherman on Monday about the protests, and why she believes \u8220\'20\'1Cyou can\u8217\'20\'19t support Roe v Wade and then turn around and say we need to give the police more money\u8221\'20\'1D. This conversation has been edited and condensed for clarity.\par \par \uc2 You wrote in The Nation about the chaos at anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protests in New York earlier this month. What was it like at the supreme court on Friday?\par \par \uc2 People were upset and angry. They were crying. It did feel beautiful to be around so many people who care. It felt like this swirling of grief and sadness, but also love from being with our people, and hope seeing people rise up. But it was scary.\par \par \uc2 One anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protester followed me around and filmed me. There were a lot of young white men, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protesters, harassing and taunting us. One man saw my \u8220\'20\'1CI had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D shirt and told his young son, \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s a murderer.\u8221\'20\'1D When I told the son, \u8220\'20\'1CYour dad\u8217\'20\'19s a white supremacist,\u8221\'20\'1D the dad said, \u8220\'20\'1CDid you see how she ratcheted this up? Do you see how they respond? Did you see how angry they get?\u8221\'20\'1D As I walked away, he taunted me more. It was a reminder of how much hate, violence and denigration of Black and brown people is taught from a father to a son.\par \par \uc2 Then there were the police who came out with their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1540362945921785856"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 riot gear}}}\uc2  in full force. It was violent and intimidating. You look up and there were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jbendery/status/1540352994482348033"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 snipers}}}\uc2  at the top of the supreme court with guns pointed at us. The police were not standing between us and the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protesters who were taunting us, and they weren\u8217\'20\'19t making sure the counterprotesters weren\u8217\'20\'19t harming us. Police were standing with their backs to the court, because they were there to protect the court.\par \par \uc2 Of course, then came the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/28/peaceful-pro-choice-protests-violence-attacks-police"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 videos}}}\uc2  about police {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/news/local/phoenix-breaking/2022/06/25/law-enforcement-deploys-tear-gas-phoenix-abortion-rights-protesters/7732759001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arresting}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2022-06-25/lapd-treatment-of-journalists-denounced-again-after-abortion-rights-protest-downtown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 beating}}}\uc2  protesters over the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.greenvilleonline.com/story/news/2022/06/27/greenville-sc-abortion-protest-arrest-investigate-use-force/7745350001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weekend}}}\uc2 . I\u8217\'20\'19m Black, this is nothing new to me. I\u8217\'20\'19m used to police going from zero to sixty. At these protests, every little thing you do can be misconstrued or used as an excuse to incite violence toward you as a protester. Seeing those videos made me think, \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the history of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Can you tell me more about what you mean when you say \u8220\'20\'1Cthis is the history of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D?\par \par \uc2 When \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a crime, police and prosecutors investigate people. In the 1920s, 30s and 40s, when authorities were doing a lot of clinic raids, they had people who had abortions on their deathbeds in the hospitals and said \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re dying. I need you to tell me what happened. Tell me who this was.\u8221\'20\'1D Prosecutors basically held threats of jail against them if they didn\u8217\'20\'19t testify against their providers. Our nation has also always allowed incarcerated people to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jan/24/shackled-pregnant-women-prisoners-birth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shackled while giving birth}}}\uc2 . That feels really symbolic about what\u8217\'20\'19s next. That police will be at the bedside, not of everyone, but of the people who are most marginalized.\par \par \uc2 The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement today claims it is only targeting providers. They say, \u8220\'20\'1CWe never want to prosecute the women who have abortions.\u8221\'20\'1D But it\u8217\'20\'19s bullshit. People have been prosecuted for years. Just in April, a woman was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/09/texas-woman-26-charged-murder-self-induced-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested}}}\uc2  in Texas and charged with murder for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 even though that murder statute did not allow it. People have been arrested for allegations and self-managing their abortions back in 2014 and 2015. Don\u8217\'20\'19t forget, we are the providers when we self-manage our abortions.\par \par \uc2 With Roe overturned, how will we see law enforcement\u8217\'20\'19s reach expanding?\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m really worried for people who may suffer some sort of stillbirth, miscarriage or self-manage their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They go to the hospital. The clinician, nurse, counselor, whoever\u8217\'20\'19s taking care of them, asks, \u8220\'20\'1CWhat did you take?\u8221\'20\'1D The patients will answer, trying to just be honest with their doctor, because they think it\u8217\'20\'19s covered by the provider-patient confidentiality. Well, then, maybe that provider turns around and decides to tell a police officer because they don\u8217\'20\'19t believe in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 We have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/27/roe-v-wade-overturned-maternal-mortality-rate-will-rise"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 horrific maternal health outcomes}}}\uc2  in this country, particularly for Black and brown people, and pregnancies can go wrong at any moment. Let\u8217\'20\'19s say someone is at the hospital and is internalizing the stigma or grief and says, \u8220\'20\'1CThis is my fault.\u8221\'20\'1D It will be police\u8217\'20\'19s job to be suspicious and investigate. Is that really a miscarriage? And now you\u8217\'20\'19re facing murder charges.\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19ve also made the argument that because of the history of police and prosecutors in criminalizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates today should break up with the police. Can you explain that?\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19ve been times when large national reproductive rights organizations have welcomed police at their events, thanking them for protecting them. There have been large national reproductive rights organizations that have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rewirenewsgroup.com/article/2017/05/24/planned-parenthood-opens-new-memphis-clinic-better-serve-latino-residents-next-ice-office/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opened}}}\uc2  new clinics near to the offices of \uc2 US Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (Ice), hoping to reach more undocumented folks and Black and brown folks that way.\par \par \uc2 Such decisions tell me that those organizations don\u8217\'20\'19t understand how violent police and the military can be towards Black and brown or undocumented people. For years, Ice used to hang outside of free family planning clinics, because they knew that\u8217\'20\'19s where undocumented people would go to get birth control, pap smears and wellness checkups. And so they were hanging out there, hoping that they could round people up.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, I know some clinics have chosen to work with police to protect their staff. And I don\u8217\'20\'19t pretend to know what it is like to go work inside of a clinic and be an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, with threats on your life every single day. But it makes me wonder how we create a health care system where people who need abortions, and who may have been stopped or harassed by a police officer the day before, don\u8217\'20\'19t have to see what might be an off duty police officer when they walk up to the clinic.\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19ve argued for a link between your battle for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and the ideas of the defund the police movement.\par \par \uc2 Yes, for all of those reasons, I think that the reality is we shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t trust the police to \u8220\'20\'1Ckeep us safe\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 There are a lot of people within the pro-choice movement that turn away when the Democratic party continues to give untold sums of money to police. When \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in his State of the Union did not say the word \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D but did say \u8220\'20\'1Cfund the police\u8221\'20\'1D three times, he sent a message. You can\u8217\'20\'19t say you believe in Roe v Wade and then turn around and say we need to give the police more money. We could take money from police budgets and invest it in schools, sex education, clinics, healthcare, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds \u8211\'20\'13 and also free baby formula, diapers, free lunches, housing for children, all of these basic needs that should be a \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D priority.\par \par \uc2 White liberals love to argue what a bad slogan \u8220\'20\'1Cdefund the police\u8221\'20\'1D is, but I wish they\u8217\'20\'19d stop complaining about the words that we use, and actually focus on the thing that we\u8217\'20\'19re telling you is happening. Do those people understand that with Roe overturned, the police \u8211\'20\'13 the ones that you have given tanks to, that you have given more rifles to, that you have given free rein to beat people \u8211\'20\'13 will be the ones who arrest and surveil people for their pregnancies?\par \par \uc2 White women in the reproductive rights movement have fantasized about heading to The Handmaid\u8217\'20\'19s Tale land and \uc2 Gilead\uc2  for so long, that they\u8217\'20\'19ve forgotten that in the story, there were white women at the helm who helped and supported the increased militarization because it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t happening to them. White women have looked away as more and more money was given to police to surveil and corral Black and brown communities. People really have to take a hard look in the mirror about where our society is going. Stop fantasizing about The Handmaid\u8217\'20\'19s Tale, and actually look around to what is happening to your neighbors, and to the people on the other side of your communities.\par \par \uc2 The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement is just the political arm of the white supremacist movement \u8211\'20\'13 it grew out of the backlash to the civil rights movement. A congresswoman this week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/26/illinois-mary-miller-roe-wade-abortion-verdict-victory-for-white-life-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the overturning of Roe was a \u8220\'20\'1Cvictory for white life\u8221\'20\'1D. White supremacist groups openly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/think/opinion/patriot-front-s-anti-abortion-advocacy-march-life-sends-clear-ncna1287952"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 marched}}}\uc2  at the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  March for Life. It\u8217\'20\'19s just going to get worse from here. In the National Right to Life\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/06/27/politics/national-right-to-life-convention-medication-abortion/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 model legislation}}}\uc2 , they want to criminalize people who explain how to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They want people prosecuted for crossing state lines to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And some are calling for a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220706ei76002qg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
