\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18No one can be neutral\u8217\'20\'19: \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 942 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 July 2022\par 17:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , the president and CEO of the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, outlines the three goals she has to get women the access they need\par \par \uc2 In the time after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  rescinded the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in America and thereby allowed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/jun/28/tracking-where-abortion-laws-stand-in-every-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly a dozen states}}}\uc2  to outlaw the procedure, the president and CEO of the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , has worked feverishly with three goals in mind.\par \par \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2  wants to get women where they need to be to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whether that means helping patients {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/09/texas-abortion-ban-cross-state-lines-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cross state lines}}}\uc2  or flying doctors to states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal.\par \par \uc2 Then, she wants to win in state courts. \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2  (CRR) and the \uc2 American Civil Liberties Union (ACLU) \uc2 have filed 11 lawsuits seeking to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/27/louisiana-judge-abortion-ban-roe-v-wade-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delay \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans}}}\uc2  or, perhaps optimistically, strike them down entirely.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we can see, essentially, is just a lot of chaos, a lot of confusion and a lot of concern for patients on the ground being able to get the care they need,\u8221\'20\'1D McGill Johnson told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19ve also seen is a significant amount of rage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That will power her third goal \u8211\'20\'13 to win at the ballot box.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur work right now is to maximize the care that we can in the states that we can, and also take this moment as an opportunity to maximize mobilization.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is already either illegal or largely inaccessible in half a dozen states, as bans and ensuing court battles play out. And all of this will get harder as many more states join their ranks in the coming days, weeks and months, until an expected {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/05/abortion-deserts-clinics-access-closed-map"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26 states ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  altogether}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is suddenly out of reach for more and more women, and there will be more and more pressure on the resources that remain, probably delaying appointments even in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is protected.\par \par \uc2 The reality is there\u8217\'20\'19s no world in which 24 states can absorb the nation\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care\par \par \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe reality is there\u8217\'20\'19s no world in which 24 states can absorb the nation\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care,\u8221\'20\'1D said McGill Johnson. \u8220\'20\'1CThe intent \u8230\'20\'26 of the opposition has been to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/jul/01/anti-abortion-movement-roe-reversal-what-next"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 end access to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 To combat this, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  is fortifying \u8220\'20\'1Clogistics centers\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cprovider corps\u8221\'20\'1D of doctors, so there is capacity at \u8220\'20\'1Csurge sites\u8221\'20\'1D to take care of patients in states that protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Patient \u8220\'20\'1Cnavigators\u8221\'20\'1D will connect women to charities to help pay for both abortions and the costs of a long journey: gas, airfare and hotel stays. McGill Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s hope is, eventually, to help build out a kind of online {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/feb/19/the-abortion-travel-agents-some-women-know-what-they-need-others-just-say-help-europe-margaret-atwood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 travel agency to access \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 To sustain this, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  also plans to combat the next expected line of attack on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access: the right to travel out of state. Organizations hostile to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have already suggested state lawmakers ban patients from crossing state lines to obtain abortions, and perhaps extradite providers.\par \par \uc2 Even with the vast logistical operation McGill Johnson has in mind, she acknowledges tens of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/27/roe-v-wade-overturned-maternal-mortality-rate-will-rise"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thousands of women a year}}}\uc2  will never reach these resources, and be forced to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/27/roe-wade-forced-birth-america-abortion-ban-misogyny"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bear unwanted children}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery day a clinic can stay open changes lives,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Nancy Northup\uc2 , president and CEO of CRR, said in a press call with McGill Johnson on Friday. They have succeeded in delaying bans in Florida, Kentucky and Utah.\par \par \uc2 However, it\u8217\'20\'19s the third leg of this stool that shows the long-term and sweeping effects of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision. Even though about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/1576/abortion.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 85% of Americans}}}\uc2  believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in at least some circumstances, more than half of states will probably ban it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe reason we are here is because many of the statehouses \u8230\'20\'26 where we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing these restrictions have been so {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/09/republicans-keep-passing-extreme-anti-abortion-bans-without-popular-support"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extremely gerrymandered}}}\uc2  that we are at a structural disadvantage in shaping the policy fights there,\u8221\'20\'1D McGill Johnson said.\par \par \uc2 In effect, partisan redistricting or \u8220\'20\'1Cgerrymandering\u8221\'20\'1D has made elections less responsive to voters\u8217\'20\'19 will. Following the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, and short of congressional action, the only way to restore legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is through the state ballot box. That reality is reflected by \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plan to spend $150m up and down the ballot. The political spending is jointly supported by Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List, which supports Democratic women for elected office, and NARAL, a reproductive rights advocacy group.\par \par \uc2 Even so, restoring legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in deep red states like Texas or Arizona where 13.5 million women of reproductive age live, presently looks like a distant future.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur job now is making sure all of these politicians who are completely out of step \u8211\'20\'13 that people understand where every single state [representative] stands on this issue so they can start to build power in the state,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to make every candidate \u8211\'20\'13 whether they\u8217\'20\'19re applying for school board or state supreme court, or governor \u8211\'20\'13 reflect on where they are on this decision.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Outside of legislatures, direct democracy will make up new battlegrounds. An anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kcur.org/news/2022-05-26/with-roe-doomed-the-kansas-fight-over-abortion-takes-on-a-new-urgency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas}}}\uc2  will ask voters to affirm there is no right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 But crucially, voters in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/health-legislature-reproductive-rights-constitutions-vermont-42b7fd8364b444a1c151fc9c4ea5c363"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vermont}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://calmatters.org/newsletters/whatmatters/2022/06/california-abortion-constitutional-amendment/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/28/abortion-rights-michigan-roe-wade-ballot-initiative"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 purple Michigan}}}\uc2  will cast ballots on whether to affirm a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  alongside other reproductive rights, such as contraception.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo one can be neutral in this moment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 5 July 2022 to clarify that the $150m ad buy figure refers to \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List and NARAL, and not just \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , as we originally said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220706ei76001uz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
