\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden planned to nominate anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  lawyer to federal judgeship, emails show\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan E Greve in Washington \par \uc2 736 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 July 2022\par 17:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 White House planned to submit Chad Meredith\u8217\'20\'19s nomination as part of deal with \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  to avoid holding up Biden\u8217\'20\'19s other nominations\par \par \uc2 The office of Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , has shared emails confirming that Joe Biden intended to nominate Chad Meredith, a conservative lawyer who has previously defended anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation, to a federal judgeship.\par \par \uc2 Reports of Meredith\u8217\'20\'19s potential nomination have sparked outrage among progressives and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates, even as the White House has dodged questions about the matter. Biden is already seen by some as not taking a strong enough lead on defending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Beshear, a Democrat, shared the emails with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2022/07/05/biden-emails-chad-meredith-nomination/7817264001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Louisville Courier-Journal}}}\uc2 , which broke the news of Meredith\u8217\'20\'19s expected nomination last week.\par \par \uc2 In a 23 June email to one of Beshear\u8217\'20\'19s advisers in DC, the White House aide Kathleen M Marshall said, \u8220\'20\'1CTo be nominated tomorrow: \u8230\'20\'26 Stephen Chad Meredith: candidate for the United States district court for the eastern district of Kentucky.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Meredith\u8217\'20\'19s nomination was not announced the following day, 24 June, when the supreme court released its decision to overturn Roe v Wade, ending the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Instead, Marshall sent a follow-up email on 29 June, telling Beshear\u8217\'20\'19s aide, \u8220\'20\'1CSorry for not including this in the original e-mail, but I wanted to clarify that the e-mail I sent was pre-decisional and privileged information.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked about Meredith on Tuesday, the White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , emphasized that no formal nomination had yet been submitted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe make it a point here to not comment on any vacancy, whether it is on the executive branch or the judicial branch, especially those that the nomination has not been made yet,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said.\par \par \uc2 But the emails released by Beshear\u8217\'20\'19s office confirm that the White House had planned to soon submit Meredith\u8217\'20\'19s nomination. According to reports, the nomination was part of a deal with the Senate Republican leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , to avoid holding up Biden\u8217\'20\'19s other judicial nominations.\par \par \uc2 That explanation failed to appease Meredith\u8217\'20\'19s critics, who warned that he would use his post as a federal judge to further attack \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. They noted that, as the chief deputy general counsel for former governor \uc2 Matt Bevin\uc2 , Meredith defended a Kentucky law requiring doctors to perform an ultrasound and describe the image to patients before performing abortions.\par \par \uc2 Meredith also served as an adviser to Bevin as the then governor issued {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2019/12/13/787952251/outgoing-kentucky-gov-matt-bevin-issues-428-pardons-many-which-are-controversial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hundreds of pardons}}}\uc2 , many of them for violent crimes, during his final days in office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy understanding right now is it has not been submitted, which I hope means at the very least means it\u8217\'20\'19s on pause,\u8221\'20\'1D Beshear said of Meredith\u8217\'20\'19s nomination on Thursday. \u8220\'20\'1CIf the president makes that nomination, it is indefensible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Charles Booker, a progressive running against the Republican senator \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2  in Kentucky, said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CThe president is making a deal with the devil and once again, the people of Kentucky are crushed in the process. At a time when we are fighting to protect human rights, this is a complete slap in the face. This is some bullshit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The President is making a deal with the devil and once again, the people of Kentucky are crushed in the process.\par \par \uc2 At a time when we are fighting to protect human rights, this is a complete slap in the face.\par \par \uc2 This is some bullshit. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/A4LV6PxSeK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/A4LV6PxSeK}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Charles Booker (@Booker4KY) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Booker4KY/status/1542274756958994434?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 29, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 For some progressives, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s willingness to nominate Meredith exemplified his failure thus far to meet the moment and use every tool at his disposal to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the wake of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 Brian Fallon, the executive director of the progressive group Demand Justice, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/brianefallon/status/1542274628193771522"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said on Thursday}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CTo recap last 48 hours, Biden: 1. Wont yet support gutting the filibuster to codify Roe 2. Is skeptical about using federal land in red states for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services 3. Has ruled out Court reform 4. Is reportedly set to nominate an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  GOP lawyer for a federal judgeship.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As of now, Meredith has not been nominated to the federal bench. If he is, Biden will probably set off a brutal battle between his administration and members of his own party.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220706ei76002gy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
