\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Highland Park shooting death toll rises to seven with 46 injured \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 4,815 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 July 2022\par 21:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Suspect pre-planned Fourth of July parade attack and wore \u8216\'20\'18women\u8217\'20\'19s clothing\u8217\'20\'19, police saySign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Americans grappled with another wave of gun violence that left seven people dead after a shooting in a Chicago suburb while two new polls paint a grim picture of Americans\u8217\'20\'19 views of President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2 , his handling of the economy, and the country\u8217\'20\'19s institutions in general.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a rundown of what\u8217\'20\'19s happened today:\par \par \uc2 * A Chicago Sun-Times journalist wrote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/05/highland-park-shooting-chicago-philadelphia-gun-violence-latest?page=with:block-62c44cf78f0824967a54c6c5#block-62c44cf78f0824967a54c6c5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a harrowing account}}}\uc2  of the mass shooting in Highland Park, Illinois, that killed seven during an Independence Day parade.\par \par \uc2 * Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/05/highland-park-shooting-chicago-philadelphia-gun-violence-latest?page=with:block-62c450088f088c74bb93b902#block-62c450088f088c74bb93b902"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 awarded the Medal of Honor}}}\uc2  to four army veterans who fought in Vietnam.\par \par \uc2 * The head of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  talked to the Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/05/highland-park-shooting-chicago-philadelphia-gun-violence-latest?page=with:block-62c43ccb8f0824967a54c5d1#block-62c43ccb8f0824967a54c5d1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about how the group}}}\uc2  will continue working to help women get abortions.\par \par \uc2 * Inflation and the overall cost of living remains Americans\u8217\'20\'19 top concern, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/05/highland-park-shooting-chicago-philadelphia-gun-violence-latest?page=with:block-62c459058f088c74bb93b98e#block-62c459058f088c74bb93b98e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a poll released today}}}\uc2  that casts doubt on Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 hopes that concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gun access will reverse Biden\u8217\'20\'19s poor approval ratings.\par \par \uc2 * But if Biden is unpopular, he\u8217\'20\'19s not alone. Americans\u8217\'20\'19 confidence in almost all of their institutions has declined compared with last year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/05/highland-park-shooting-chicago-philadelphia-gun-violence-latest?page=with:block-62c45f0e8f088c74bb93ba03#block-62c45f0e8f088c74bb93ba03"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a different poll}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Local authorities also announced the names of three more victims which had not been known yet. The identity of the seventh \u8211\'20\'13 and so far last \u8211\'20\'13 victim has not been released.\par \par \uc2 The three new names are:\par \par \uc2 Katherine Goldstein, 88\par \par \uc2 Irina McCarthy, 35\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy, 37\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 At a press conference police have detailed two previous incidents involving the alleged shooter Robert Crimo.\par \par \uc2 The first happened in April, 2019 when police got a report from Crimo\u8217\'20\'19s family that he had attempted suicide. The second occurred in September, 2019 when there was a report that Crimo had been making threats that he wanted to \u8220\'20\'1Ckill everyone\u8221\'20\'1D and had a collection of knives.\par \par \uc2 Police visited where Crimo was living and confiscated a collection of 16 knives, a dagger and a sword.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  has some heartbreaking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2022/07/05/us/highland-park-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 details}}}\uc2  on the third victim to be identified. The paper {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2022/07/05/us/highland-park-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Steve Straus, 88\par \par \uc2 A father of two, grandfather of four and a financial adviser who, at 88, still took the train every day from his Highland Park home to his office at a brokerage firm in Chicago, Steve Straus \u8220\'20\'1Cshould not have had to die this way,\u8221\'20\'1D his niece, Cynthia Straus, said in a phone interview.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe was an honorable man who worked his whole life and looked out for his family and gave everyone the best he had,\u8221\'20\'1D Ms Straus said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe was kind and gentle and had huge intelligence and humor and wit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He was devoted to his wife, she said, and intensely close with his brother, and extremely health conscious: \u8220\'20\'1CHe exercised as if he were 50.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden has no plans yet to visit Highland Park, Illinois, site of Monday\u8217\'20\'19s mass shooting that killed seven people, his press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  told reporters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C We don\u8217\'20\'19t have any plans right now to go to Chicago\u8221\'20\'1D, the city of which Highland Park is a suburb, Jean-Pierre said. However vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is scheduled to be in the city later today to to address the \uc2 National Education Association\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cand she will speak to the devastation that we that we all saw with our own eyes yesterday in Highland Park\u8221\'20\'1D, according to Jean-Pierre.\par \par \uc2 Biden will travel to Cleveland, Ohio on Wednesday for a speech regarding the economy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  is holding the daily press briefing, and reiterated the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to get \uc2 WNBA\uc2  star Brittney Griner released from prison in Russia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe she was wrongfully detained. We believe she needs to come home, she should be home,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said, adding that Griner\u8217\'20\'19s wife spoke with national security advisor Jake Sullivan over the weekend, their second phone call in the past 10 days.\par \par \uc2 Griner wrote a letter to Biden asking him to push for her release, which Jean-Pierre said the president had read. \u8220\'20\'1CHe takes this to heart, he takes this job very seriously, especially when it comes to bringing home US nationals who are wrongfully detained,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said.\par \par \uc2 This post has been updated to clarify that Griner\u8217\'20\'19s wife, not Griner herself, spoke to Jake Sullivan.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jul/05/brittney-griner-letter-joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8217\'20\'19I\u8217\'20\'19m terrified I might be here forever\u8217\'20\'19: Brittney Griner appeals to Biden in letter}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 President Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/presidential-actions/2022/07/05/proclamation-on-honoring-the-victims-of-the-tragedy-in-highland-park-illinois/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has ordered flags flown at half-staff}}}\uc2  across the United States and its embassies abroad until the end of the day on July 9 in memory of the people killed at the mass shooting in Highland Park.\par \par \uc2 Biden had previously ordered flags flown at half-staff in May after the shooting at an elementary school in Uvalde, Texas that killed 19 children and two teachers.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Death toll in Illinois mass shooting rises to seven\par \par \uc2 A seventh person has died following the July 4 shooting at an Independence Day parade in Highland Park, Illinois, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcchicago.com/news/local/7th-person-dies-day-after-highland-park-parade-mass-shooting/2873971/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC Chicago reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The death brings the toll of wounded in the shooting to 46, according to the broadcaster. Police have said the man suspected of carrying out the attack {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/05/highland-park-shooting-chicago-philadelphia-gun-violence-latest?page=with:block-62c46da08f084f4c6fce78c4#block-62c46da08f084f4c6fce78c4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 planned it for weeks and dressed as a woman in order to conceal his identity.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  were at the center of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling last month overturning Roe v. Wade}}}\uc2 , but the litigation isn\u8217\'20\'19t finished in the state.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/mississippi-abortion-law-ruling-6d95ff3116c33f1202561d8da3315061"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Associated Press reports}}}\uc2  that Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, the plaintiff in the supreme court case, is suing to stop a law that would ban almost all abortions in the state:\par \par \uc2 The law \u8212\'20\'14 which state lawmakers passed before the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  overturned the 1973 ruling that allowed abortions nationwide \u8212\'20\'14 is set to take effect Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization sought a temporary restraining order that would allow it to remain open, at least while the lawsuit remains in court.\par \par \uc2 The closely watched lawsuit is part of a flurry of activity that has occurred nationwide since the Supreme Court ruled. Conservative states have moved to halt or limit abortions while others have sought to ensure \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, all as some women try to obtain the medical procedure against the changing legal landscape.\par \par \uc2 If Chancery Judge Debbra K. Halford grants the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s request to block the new Mississippi law from taking effect, the decision could be quickly appealed to the state Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 Twenty-six states are expected to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  entirely following the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://states.guttmacher.org/policies/south-dakota/abortion-policies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2 , six states have already done so.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Maryland\u8217\'20\'19s governor announced today that his state will change its requirements for licensing concealed weapons in response to last month\u8217\'20\'19s ruling by the supreme court expanding Americans\u8217\'20\'19 ability to possess a gun outside their homes.\par \par \uc2 enltrIn light of a recent Supreme Court ruling and to ensure compliance with the Constitution, I am directing the Maryland State Police to suspend utilization of the \u8216\'20\'18good and substantial reason\u8217\'20\'19 standard when reviewing applications for Wear and Carry Permits.\par \par \uc2 My full statement: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0wi1dzD8Aw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/0wi1dzD8Aw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Governor \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2  (@GovLarryHogan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovLarryHogan/status/1544322879327596545?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 As its term came to a close in June, the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority overturned a New York law that had placed strict limits on carrying a firearm outside the home, which affected states with similar laws on their books, including Maryland.\par \par \uc2 New York\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.governor.ny.gov/news/governor-hochul-signs-landmark-legislation-strengthen-gun-laws-and-bolster-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last week signed legislation}}}\uc2  designed to counter the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling by prohibiting the carrying of weapons in certain locations such as bars and restaurants that serve alcohol, schools, government buildings and airports, as well as requiring owners to consent to people carrying guns on their property.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/23/us-supreme-court-new-york-law-gun-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court overturns New York handgun law in bitter blow to gun-control push}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 In other January 6 news, \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , one of only two Republicans sitting on the House committee investigating the insurrection, has released a compilation of threatening and profane phone calls his office has received.\par \par \uc2 enltrThreats of violence over politics has increased heavily in the last few years. But the darkness has reached new lows. My new interns made this compilation of recent calls they\u8217\'20\'19ve received while serving in my DC office.\par \par \uc2 WARNING: this video contains foul & graphic language. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yQJvvAHBVV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/yQJvvAHBVV}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  (@RepKinzinger) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepKinzinger/status/1544327335830327301?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Last year, Kinzinger announced he would retire from Congress, where he\u8217\'20\'19s served since 2011.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Georgia grand jury investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempts to subvert the 2020 election result in the state has issued subpoenas to a number of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys and allies, including senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The special grand jury empaneled in Fulton county, where the capital and largest city Atlanta lies, issued the subpoenas today, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/fulton-grand-jury-subpoenas-giuliani-graham-trump-confidantes/POUNSTTUXZDGDB3D5LKA7TIQQM/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Atlanta Journal-Constitution}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 In addition to Giuliani, among those being summoned are John Eastman, Cleta Mitchell, Kenneth Chesbro and Jenna Ellis, all of whom advised Trump on strategies for overturning Democrat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s wins in Georgia and other swing states.\par \par \uc2 The grand jury also subpoenaed South Carolina U.S. Sen. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s top allies in the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2 , and attorney and podcast host Jacki Pick Deason.\par \par \uc2 The subpoenas, were filed July 5 and signed off by Fulton Superior Court Judge Robert McBurney, who is overseeing the special grand jury. Unlike subpoenas issued to Georgians, the summons were required to receive McBurney\u8217\'20\'19s blessing since they are for people who reside outside the state.\par \par \uc2 Viewers of the January 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s hearings will remember Eastman, the lawyer who, according to testimony from witnesses before the lawmakers, worked with Trump on his plot to undermine the results of the 2020 election. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/16/trump-lawyer-john-eastman-presidential-pardon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Eastman is among those who asked Trump for a pardon before he left office.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 At the press conference, investigators said the suspect Robert E Crimo III, 21, had legally bought the rifle allegedly used in the shootings and recovered at the scene \u8211\'20\'13 a high-powered rifle styled after an AR-15 \u8211\'20\'13 along with at least one more, as well as some pistols.\par \par \uc2 The attack had evidently been planned for weeks, said Covelli, though investigators had not been tipped off to the social media videos posted by the suspect before the shooting.\par \par \uc2 Authorities have still not said what charges Crimo faces, though another press conference is scheduled for later today.\par \par \uc2 All six people killed were adults, Covelli said, and more than 30 others went to hospitals with bullet wounds.\par \par \uc2 Covelli said there is no indication targets were picked out based on race, religion or any other federally protected status.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Suspect pre-planned Highland Park attack and wore 'women's clothing' \u8211\'20\'13 police\par \par \uc2 The suspect in the 4 July shootings in Highland Park pre-planned the attack for several weeks, according to officials, and wore \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen\u8217\'20\'19s clothing\u8221\'20\'1D in what investigators said they believed was an effort to conceal his identity.\par \par \uc2 According to Chris Covelli, the leader of a police taskforce investigating major crimes in the Illinois county that includes Highland Park, local officers recognized the suspect in surveillance footage they reviewed after the shooting, which helped them track him down. The suspect has prominent facial tattoos.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Details continue to emerge about the mass shooting in a Chicago suburb yesterday, while two new polls paint a grim picture of Americans\u8217\'20\'19 views of President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , his handling of the economy, and the country\u8217\'20\'19s institutions in general.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a rundown of what\u8217\'20\'19s happened so far today:\par \par \uc2 * A Chicago Sun-Times journalist wrote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/05/highland-park-shooting-chicago-philadelphia-gun-violence-latest?page=with:block-62c44cf78f0824967a54c6c5#block-62c44cf78f0824967a54c6c5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a harrowing account}}}\uc2  of the mass shooting in Highland Park, Illinois, that killed six during an Independence Day parade.\par \par \uc2 * Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/05/highland-park-shooting-chicago-philadelphia-gun-violence-latest?page=with:block-62c450088f088c74bb93b902#block-62c450088f088c74bb93b902"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 awarded the Medal of Honor}}}\uc2  to four army veterans who fought in Vietnam.\par \par \uc2 * The head of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  talked to the Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/05/highland-park-shooting-chicago-philadelphia-gun-violence-latest?page=with:block-62c43ccb8f0824967a54c5d1#block-62c43ccb8f0824967a54c5d1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about how the group}}}\uc2  will continue working to help women get abortions.\par \par \uc2 * Inflation and the overall cost of living remains Americans\u8217\'20\'19 top concern, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/05/highland-park-shooting-chicago-philadelphia-gun-violence-latest?page=with:block-62c459058f088c74bb93b98e#block-62c459058f088c74bb93b98e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a poll released today}}}\uc2  that casts doubt on Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 hopes that concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gun access will reverse Biden\u8217\'20\'19s poor approval ratings.\par \par \uc2 * But if Biden is unpopular, he\u8217\'20\'19s not alone. Americans\u8217\'20\'19 confidence in almost all of their institutions has declined compared with last year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/05/highland-park-shooting-chicago-philadelphia-gun-violence-latest?page=with:block-62c45f0e8f088c74bb93ba03#block-62c45f0e8f088c74bb93ba03"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a different poll}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 High inflation is just one reason why economists are worrying that the United States is poised to enter a recession.\par \par \uc2 But if the economy does contract, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/recession-economy-unemployment-jobs-11656947596"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Wall Street Journal reports}}}\uc2  that it may not look like more recent downturns such as at the start of the Covid-19 pandemic or the global financial crisis. One key difference is that waves of layoffs that accompanied those downturns may not occur.\par \par \uc2 From their article exploring the \u8220\'20\'1Cvery strange\u8221\'20\'1D situation the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest economy finds itself in:\par \par \uc2 Today, something highly unusual is happening. Economic output fell in the first quarter and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/inflation-consumer-spending-personal-income-may-2022-11656531317?mod=hp_lead_pos2&mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signs suggest}}}\uc2  it did so again in the second. Yet the job market showed little sign of faltering during the first half of the year. The jobless rate fell from 4% last December {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/may-jobs-report-unemployment-rate-2022-11654195243?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to 3.6%}}}\uc2  in May.\par \par \uc2 It is the latest strange twist in the odd trajectory of the pandemic economy, and a riddle for those contemplating a recession. If the U.S. is in or near one, it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t yet look like any other on record.\par \par \uc2 Analysts sometimes talked about \u8220\'20\'1Cjobless recoveries\u8221\'20\'1D after past recessions, in which economic output rose but employers kept shedding workers. The first half of 2022 was the mirror image\u8212\'20\'14a \u8220\'20\'1Cjobful\u8221\'20\'1D downturn, in which output fell and companies kept hiring. Whether it will spiral into a fuller and deeper recession isn\u8217\'20\'19t known, though a growing number of economists believe it will.\par \par \uc2 Some companies, especially in the tech sector, have given indications that they\u8217\'20\'19re {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/more-companies-start-to-rescind-job-offers-11655865283/?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pulling back on hiring}}}\uc2 , though across the broad economy the job market has rarely looked stronger.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Also unpopular with Americans: the country\u8217\'20\'19s institutions.\par \par \uc2 Gallup has today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/394283/confidence-institutions-down-average-new-low.aspx?utm_source=twitter&utm_term=gallupnews&utm_content=98a3d355-7a03-4603-910b-038af74c7e05&utm_campaign=gallup_news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released a poll}}}\uc2  showing a decline in confidence for most of the 16 institutions they track, in particular the supreme court and the presidency.\par \par \uc2 enltrAmericans\u8217\'20\'19 confidence in major U.S. institutions has dropped to the lowest point in Gallup\u8217\'20\'19s more than 40-year trend. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/G2frb7HXxk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/G2frb7HXxk}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OyWfUwXmjp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/OyWfUwXmjp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 GallupNews (@GallupNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GallupNews/status/1544294942000009217?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 In the yearly survey, confidence in the supreme court dropped 11 percentage points from 2021 to 25 percent, while the presidency suffered a 15 point decline to 23 percent. The least popular institution was Congress, in which only seven percent of respondent had confidence, down five points from last year. Just above them was television news, in which only 11 percent of Americans had confidence.\par \par \uc2 Small businesses were the most popular institution of those surveyed, with 68 percent confidence, a decline of only two percentage points from last year. The military was up next with 64 percent confidence, followed by the police, with 45 percent confidence.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden still unpopular, inflation still Americans' top concern in new poll\par \par \uc2 A new poll from \uc2 Monmouth University\uc2  has found that President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  remains unpopular, but for Democrats, that\u8217\'20\'19s not its most troubling finding. The Biden administration has hoped that the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s recent rulings curtailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and expanding concealed weapons possession would fire up Democrats ahead of the midterm elections, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.monmouth.edu/polling-institute/reports/MonmouthPoll_US_070522/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the poll instead shows}}}\uc2  that voters\u8217\'20\'19 biggest issue remains the nation\u8217\'20\'19s high rate of inflation - a trend that Biden has had little success in reversing.\par \par \uc2 First the bad news about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating, which Monmouth reports actually worsened last month:\par \par \uc2 enltrNATIONAL POLL: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JoeBiden}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s job rating:\par \par \uc2 36% approve (38% in May)\par \par \uc2 58% disapprove (57%)\par \par \uc2 APPROVE by PARTY:\par \par \uc2 DEM \u8211\'20\'13 74%\par \par \uc2 IND \u8211\'20\'13 29%\par \par \uc2 REP \u8211\'20\'13 3% {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/icoqYkvs7M"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/icoqYkvs7M}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TbzntDlSEE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/TbzntDlSEE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MonmouthPoll (@MonmouthPoll) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MonmouthPoll/status/1544335407978106885?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Now for what voters care most about. In response to the question \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat is the biggest concern facing your family right now?,\u8221\'20\'1D 33 percent of the 978 adults surveyed said inflation, 15 percent gas prices, nine percent said the economy and six percent said everyday bills and groceries. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reproductive rights was the top concern for only five percent of respondents, while guns and gun ownership was cited by a mere three percent.\par \par \uc2 The poll was conducted from June 23 to 27, while the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision overturning Roe v. Wade came out on June 24.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 President Biden is today awarding the Medal of Honor, the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest military decoration, to four Army veterans who fought in the Vietnam War.\par \par \uc2 Staff Sergeant Edward N. Kaneshiro, Specialist Five Dwight W. Birdwell, Specialist Five Dennis M. Fujii and Major John J. Duffy are set to receive the award in a White House ceremony beginning at 11:15 am eastern time.\par \par \uc2 Kaneshiro perished in 1967 in Vietnam, but Birdwell, Fujii and Duffy are still alive and presumably will attend. The White House has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/06/27/president-biden-to-award-medal-of-honor/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a rundown of the actions they are being awarded for}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 You can watch the ceremony live {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?521467-1/president-biden-awards-medal-honor-vietnam-war-soldiers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Empty chairs sit along the sidewalk after parade-goers fled Highland Park\u8217\'20\'19s Fourth of July parade after shots were fired, Monday, July 4, 2022 in Highland Park, Ill. (Lynn Sweet/Chicago Sun-Times via AP) Photograph: Lynn Sweet/AP\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know why I\u8217\'20\'19m writing this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 So begins a first-hand account of yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s mass shooting by Lynn Sweet, Washington bureau chief of the Chicago Sun-Times, who was there when a gunman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/05/highland-park-shooting-alleged-attacker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opened fire from a rooftop and killed six}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She continues:\par \par \uc2 I saw, frozen in time, what people left when they fled. So many baby carriages. Folding chairs. Backpacks. Water bottles. Towels. Blankets. Police were asking people to leave the active shooting scene.\par \par \uc2 As I approached Port Clinton Square, by the reviewing stand, I saw a woman down. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know if she was dead or alive. Two people were leaning over her. I saw another woman on the ground.\par \par \uc2 Then, near a bench in the square, I came upon a pool of blood, ruby red blood. There was so much blood, that the blood puddle was lumpy because so much already coagulated. The shape of the blood \u8212\'20\'14 was this a twisted Rorschach test? \u8212\'20\'14 looked like a handgun to me.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m going into this gruesome detail because this is what gun violence from a rapid-fire weapon with an apparent high capacity magazine looks like. My sister, Neesa, on Central near the railroad tracks, heard two sequences of rapid fire. The pause is likely when the shooter switched out magazines.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://chicago.suntimes.com/2022/7/5/23194659/highland-park-mass-shooting-fourth-july-parade-lynn-sweet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The full piece is worth a read.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 When it comes to his relationship with Saudi Arabia, oil production and jailed relatives aren\u8217\'20\'19t the only issues Biden has to deal with. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/stephanie-kirchgaessner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stephanie Kirchgaessner}}}\uc2  reports that his administration is facing a deadline to give its opinion in a lawsuit brought against Riyadh by the fiancee of a murdered journalist:\par \par \uc2 A US judge has asked the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration}}}\uc2  to weigh in on whether \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2 , the crown prince of Saudi Arabia, should be granted sovereign immunity in a civil case brought against him in the US by Hatice Cengiz, the fiancee of Jamal Khashoggi, the journalist who was killed by Saudi agents in 2018.\par \par \uc2 John Bates, a district court judge, gave the \uc2 US government\uc2  until 1 August to declare its interests in the civil case or give the court notice that it has no view on the matter.\par \par \uc2 The administration\u8217\'20\'19s decision could have a profound effect on the civil case and comes as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is facing criticism for abandoning a campaign promise to turn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/saudiarabia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saudi Arabia}}}\uc2  into a \u8220\'20\'1Cpariah\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/03/judge-puts-biden-on-the-spot-over-immunity-for-saudi-prince-jamal-khashoggi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judge puts Biden on the spot over immunity for Saudi crown prince}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 President Biden will next week go to the Middle East, including a controversial stop in Saudi Arabia, which is seen as an attempt to reset relations with a top oil producer. Ahead of the trip, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/stephanie-kirchgaessner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stephanie Kirchgaessner}}}\uc2  reports that families of Americans detained in the country are worried the White House is ignoring their plight:\par \par \uc2 Family members of several US nationals who are being held in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/saudiarabia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saudi Arabia}}}\uc2  and Egypt were not invited to attend a recent call with \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , the secretary of state, in a move that was called \u8220\'20\'1Cinfuriating and discriminatory\u8221\'20\'1D by one critic.\par \par \uc2 The apparent decision to exclude the families from a June 22 call between Blinken and relatives of US nationals who are hostages or otherwise wrongfully detained in Russia, Venezuela, Rwanda, and other countries, was made just weeks before \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s controversial trip to the Middle East and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/14/joe-biden-middle-east-trip-saudi-arabia-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an expected rapprochement}}}\uc2  between the US president and Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s de facto ruler, \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2 , the crown prince.\par \par \uc2 Biden is due to visit Israel and Saudi Arabia later this month as part of a summit where oil production is likely to be high on the agenda, as well as a focus on improved relations between Saudi Arabia and Israel.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/05/us-detainees-middle-east-antony-blinken-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anger as families of US detainees in Middle East left off Blinken call }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee won\u8217\'20\'19t be holding any hearings this week because the House of Representatives is in recess, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwardhelmore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edward Helmore}}}\uc2  reports that one of its top lawmakers says the committee is gathering more and more evidence about what happened that day - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/28/january-6-committee-session-new-evidence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 especially since the testimony}}}\uc2  of an aide to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff:\par \par \uc2 Republican congressman \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  has said that bombshell testimony given by Cassidy Hutchinson to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jan-6-hearings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6 hearings}}}\uc2  last week has inspired more witnesses to come forward and the committee is getting more new evidence by the day.\par \par \uc2 The panel is investigating the events surrounding the 2021 attack on the US Capitol by a mob of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  supporters. Kinzinger is one of two Republicans serving on the panel which has publicized explosive testimony about the insurrection and an apparent plot to subvert the 2020 election, which \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won.\par \par \uc2 Last week Hutchinson, a former top aide to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff, \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , gave sworn testimony that painted the former president as a violent and unstable figure desperately seeking to cling to power.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/04/jan-6-witnesses-cassidy-hutchinson-kinzinger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6 panel getting more new evidence by the day, says Kinzinger}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Americans are continuing to grapple with the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling last month allowing states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  - including the founder of the country\u8217\'20\'19s largest provider of the procedure. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/jessica-glenza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jessica Glenza}}}\uc2  spoke to \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , president and CEO of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , about how the group plans to help women continue accessing abortions:\par \par \uc2 In the time after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  rescinded the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in America and thereby allowed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/jun/28/tracking-where-abortion-laws-stand-in-every-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly a dozen states}}}\uc2  to outlaw the procedure, the president and CEO of the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , has worked feverishly with three goals in mind.\par \par \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2  wants to get women where they need to be to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whether that means helping patients {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/09/texas-abortion-ban-cross-state-lines-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cross state lines}}}\uc2  or flying doctors to states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal.\par \par \uc2 Then, she wants to win in state courts. \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2  (CRR) and the \uc2 American Civil Liberties Union (ACLU) \uc2 have filed 11 lawsuits seeking to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/27/louisiana-judge-abortion-ban-roe-v-wade-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delay \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans}}}\uc2  or, perhaps optimistically, strike them down entirely.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we can see, essentially, is just a lot of chaos, a lot of confusion and a lot of concern for patients on the ground being able to get the care they need,\u8221\'20\'1D McGill Johnson told \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19ve also seen is a significant amount of rage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That will power her third goal \u8211\'20\'13 to win at the ballot box.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur work right now is to maximize the care that we can in the states that we can, and also take this moment as an opportunity to maximize mobilization.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/05/planned-parenthood-abortion-rights-ceo-alexis-mcgill-johnson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  \u8216\'20\'18No one can be neutral\u8217\'20\'19: Planned Parenthood\u8217\'20\'19s chief on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s shooting in a Chicago suburb has already spurred calls for more action to tackle gun violence, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/erum-salam"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Erum Salam}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/coral-murphy-marcos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coral Murphy Marcos}}}\uc2  report:\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/04/chicago-shooting-fourth-of-july-parade-police"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shooting at a Fourth of July parade in Highland Park}}}\uc2  that left at least six dead and 24 wounded has rocked the small, well-off community in suburban Chicago, and shocked the US as a whole.\par \par \uc2 It is the latest in a slew of mass killings that have recently included a shooting at a school in Texas and the racist massacre of Black shoppers at a supermarket in Buffalo, New York.\par \par \uc2 But this latest mass murder has struck a particularly symbolic note as the shooter targeted a flag-waving parade celebrating the country\u8217\'20\'19s national day and \u8211\'20\'13 once again \u8211\'20\'13 forced Americans to wrestle with how and why their nation is so often struck by such bloody attacks.\par \par \uc2 Highland Park\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, Nancy Rotering, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis morning at 10.14, our community was terrorized by an act of violence that has shaken us to our core. Our hearts go out to the victims at this devastating time. On a day that we came together to celebrate community and freedom, we are instead mourning the tragic loss of life and struggling with the terror that was brought upon us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/04/highland-park-shooting-chicago-suburb-parade-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This isn\u8217\'20\'19t freedom\u8217\'20\'19: Fourth of July shooting rocks Chicago and shocks US}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Less than two weeks ago, Democrats and Republicans managed to bridge the yawning gap between them on the issue of gun control to pass a measure that tightened down domestic abusers\u8217\'20\'19 access to weapons, and allocated money towards mental health programs and schools.\par \par \uc2 The bill\u8217\'20\'19s catalysts were the mass shooting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/15/buffalo-shooting-suspect-charged-federal-hate-crimes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at a grocery store in Buffalo, New York}}}\uc2  and, 10 days later, an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/28/texas-shooting-uvalde-survivors-stories"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elementary school in Uvalde, Texas}}}\uc2 . While it was the most significant piece of legislation targeting gun violence in decades, it won the support of only a minority of Republicans, and Democrats acknowledged they would have passed much stronger legislation, if they had the votes.\par \par \uc2 The law was only days old when the latest high-profile mass shooting, at an Independence Day celebration in Highland Park, Illinois, occurred. Congress is in recess this week, and many lawmakers are back in their districts, where they may face calls to do more to stop the massacres - or to ensure continued access to guns.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Gun violence rattles America again, this time during Independence Day celebrations\par \par \uc2 Good morning US politics live blog readers. The ink has only just dried on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/25/joe-biden-signs-gun-control-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 compromise legislation Congress passed last month}}}\uc2  to curb mass shootings across the country, but on Monday, violence interrupted Americans\u8217\'20\'19 celebrations of the United States\u8217\'20\'19 246th birthday. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/04/highland-park-shooting-fourth-of-july-arrest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A gunman killed six people}}}\uc2  in a Chicago suburb, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2022/jul/05/two-police-officers-shot-at-philadelphia-fourth-of-july-celebration-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crowds fled an Independence Day celebration in Philadelphia}}}\uc2  after another shooting injured two police officers.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 * Politico has obtained{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/07/05/trailer-trump-documentary-january-6-committee-holder-00043960"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new trailer}}}\uc2  for an upcoming documentary on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s final days of the White House, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/02/alex-holder-trump-filmmaker-january-6-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which has drawn the interest of the January 6 committee}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 WNBA\uc2  star Brittney Griner{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jul/05/brittney-griner-letter-joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has appealed to president Joe Biden}}}\uc2  to seek her release from prison in Russia.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/07/05/us/politics/abortion-roe-midterm-elections-moderate-women.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats are pouncing}}}\uc2  on last month\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court ruling overturning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to try to win back moderate voters who have drifted away.\par \par \uc2 * Flight delays at American airports {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/travel-holidays-transportation-7756251927ba023f3b60bb301a0ed2cc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seem to be easing}}}\uc2  after waves of cancelations disrupted travel during the July 4 weekend.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220705ei75001xo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
