\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Florida restores state  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban beyond 15 weeks after temporary halt\b0\par\par\uc2 Coral Murphy Marcos \par \uc2 455 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 July 2022\par 19:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 A judge had ruled that the ban violated the privacy protections in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution, pausing the restrictive measure\par \par \uc2 After a judge in Florida temporarily halted a state law banning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abortions}}}\uc2  beyond 15 weeks of pregnancy, a state appeal restored the ban on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Judge John C Cooper of an appellate court in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s capital of Tallahassee ruled that the ban in question \u8211\'20\'13 enshrined in a bill that Republican lawmakers approved in April \u8211\'20\'13 violates privacy protections in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Cooper\u8217\'20\'19s decision temporarily halted the ban, though it had no effect on a ban prohibiting abortions beyond 24 weeks of pregnancy. But the state\u8217\'20\'19s appeal automatically ensured a stay on the temporary blocking of the more restrictive measure, meaning that ban still applies as the case continues playing out.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Florida constitution does not include \u8211\'20\'13 and has never included \u8211\'20\'13 a right to kill an innocent unborn child,\u8221\'20\'1D said a spokesperson for Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , last week.\par \par \uc2 The move is the latest in a series of conflicting state court rulings after the federal supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s recent decision to overturn its landmark Roe v Wade ruling, which since 1973 had granted nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now banned in at least eight states, with more bans expected to follow in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 Other states are expected to follow procedures similar to those in Florida. In late June, a Kentucky judge temporarily halted an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that was triggered by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision. Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s law sought a near total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In southern states that had passed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in anticipation of Roe\u8217\'20\'19s reversal, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates sued to at least delay bans on terminating pregnancies after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ruling.\par \par \uc2 There were more than 79,000 abortions in Florida during the past year, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ahca.myflorida.com/mchq/central_services/training_support/docs/TrimesterByReason_2021.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  from the state\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare agency. About 94% of those cases happened in the first trimester, which lasts through the 11th week of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFlorida politicians have turned their backs on women and people who can become pregnant, forcing us into a second-class status by denying us the right to make decisions about our bodies, our healthcare, and our futures,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  wrote in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ACLU/status/1544362362869874690"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweet}}}\uc2  on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican leaders are expected to pursue further \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions. The Republican representative Anthony Sabatini said in late June that he was pushing for a special session for the legislature to pass a more stringent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe must pass the heartbeat bill & other strong \u8230\'20\'26 measures to protect Florida\u8217\'20\'19s unborn children,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220705ei7500362\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
