\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 This terrifying backslide on LGBTQ rights is a threat to women\u8217\'20\'19s rights too\b0\par\par\uc2 Owen Jones \par \uc2 992 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 July 2022\par 11:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s no surprise that people opposing the rights of this minority are also anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Unless we unite, patriarchy will come for us all\par \par \uc2 Is Pride a protest, a party or a corporate jamboree? London\u8217\'20\'19s annual {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/jul/02/it-feels-amazing-revellers-young-and-old-celebrate-pride-in-london"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pride}}}\uc2  took place this Saturday \u8211\'20\'13 the first since 2019, due to Covid \u8211\'20\'13 and, while the banks marched and the capital\u8217\'20\'19s LGBTQ citizens revelled, a shadow loomed over the parade. All minorities must at some point confront a cruel truth: complacency bred by the illusion that history is a story of perpetual progress is an unwise error. After Britain\u8217\'20\'19s anti-gay laws were repealed and unapologetic homophobia lost its vice-like grip over public opinion, Pride became depoliticised. The important battles had been won. Now we simply celebrate past victories in a mass piss-up, allowing some companies with questionable records to wrap themselves in the feelgood rainbow flag.\par \par \uc2 Well, bad news: history isn\u8217\'20\'19t a merry tale of humanity skipping into an ever-more enlightened sunny upland. London Pride took the correct decision this year to ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/jun/30/uniformed-police-not-welcome-at-pride-in-london-say-organisers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 uniformed police officers from marching}}}\uc2 , re-imposing a ban lifted in 2003. It was a nod to this reality: families of the victims of the murderer Stephen Port denounced the Metropolitan police for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/dec/10/police-homophobia-stephen-port-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 institutional homophobia}}}\uc2  after a disastrously bungled investigation into the so-called \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Grindr\uc2  killer\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a reminder that, no, the authorities are not your friend.\par \par \uc2 Across the Atlantic, the reversal on LGBTQ rights is stark. It was unsurprising but gruesome when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  banned trans Americans from serving in the US military, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jun/12/trump-transgender-lgbt-healthcare-protections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminated civil rights protections}}}\uc2  for trans people in healthcare. Despite Democratic rule at federal level, this backslide is continuing. The so-called \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/04/florida-dont-say-gay-bill-children-mental-health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 don\u8217\'20\'19t say gay}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D law in Florida, which bans schools from discussing sexual orientation or gender identity between Kindergarten and third grade, is one striking example. Even more terrifying is Texas\u8217\'20\'19s banning of gender-affirming healthcare for young trans people, with their parents now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/01/lawsuit-aims-to-block-texas-investigating-parents-seeking-care-trans-children"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legally defined as child abusers}}}\uc2  if they seek it. Republicans across the US are seeking to introduce so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cbathroom bills\u8221\'20\'1D, banning trans people using toilets corresponding to their transitioned gender.\par \par \uc2 In this deteriorating climate, it\u8217\'20\'19s unsurprising that reported {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abc7ny.com/hate-crime-lgbtq-new-york-city-pride-month/11958809/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-LGBTQ}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://prismreports.org/2022/04/20/hate-crimes-rise-anti-lgbtq-legislation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hate crimes}}}\uc2  are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/asian-america/anti-black-gay-asian-bias-fuel-california-hate-crime-surge-rcna35895"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 soaring}}}\uc2  across the US. The same here, too: reported homophobic and transphobic hate crimes have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/03/recorded-homophobic-hate-crimes-soared-in-pandemic-figures-show"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surged in the UK}}}\uc2 . In January, the \uc2 Council of Europe\uc2  placed the UK in the same category as Hungary, Poland, Russia and Turkey for its position on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://inews.co.uk/news/world/council-of-europe-condemns-virulent-attacks-on-lgbt-rights-uk-1423399"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LGBTQ rights}}}\uc2 , while for the third year running the UK has been relegated in the annual ranking of LGBTQ rights {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/12/uk-falls-down-europes-lgbtq-rights-ranking-for-third-year-running"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 across Europe}}}\uc2 . The overriding reason is the anti-trans moral panic that grips British society, fostered by an overwhelmingly hostile media and a government that is using trans people as a prop in a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/apr/13/local-elections-tories-culture-war-trans-rights-conversion-practices"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 culture war}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D (just as \uc2 Margaret Thatcher\uc2  used gay people in the 1980s), and has refused to ban trans conversion practices.\par \par \uc2 There is a common culprit here: and it\u8217\'20\'19s the P-word \u8211\'20\'13 patriarchy. It is no coincidence that attacks on gay and trans rights in the US have been accompanied by the onslaught against reproductive rights \u8211\'20\'13 or indeed that the same politicians are leading the charge against each. Historically, it has ever been thus: it was natural that the Russian revolution legalised both homosexuality and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while Joseph Stalin re-criminalised both over a decade later. \uc2 Progress\uc2  and regression were interlinked. More recently, Hungary\u8217\'20\'19s far-right government has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20210707-hungary-s-controversial-anti-lgbt-law-goes-into-effect-despite-eu-warnings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned}}}\uc2  the teaching of young people about LGBTQ issues, ended legal recognition for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrw.org/news/2020/05/21/hungary-ends-legal-recognition-transgender-and-intersex-people"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trans and intersex}}}\uc2  people and toughened its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://balkaninsight.com/2020/11/19/activists-fear-abortion-at-risk-in-hungary-from-orbans-family-first-crusade/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  stance. The same applies in the opposite direction. Thanks entirely to grassroots struggle in the face of a reluctant political elite, Ireland has loosened its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, introduced equal marriage and made it easier for trans people to transition. This understanding of common struggle is reflected by Ireland\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Rights Campaign, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.abortionrightscampaign.ie/2021/11/20/transphobia-has-no-place-in-paper-of-record-says-abortion-rights-campaign/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 boycotted}}}\uc2  the Irish Times because of its negative stance on trans issues.\par \par \uc2 The past and the present offer an obvious truth: the fate of women \u8211\'20\'13 of all sexualities \u8211\'20\'13 and LGBTQ people are bound together. While women are the principal targets of patriarchy (that is, a society rigged in favour of men), this system also punishes those seen to deviate from rigid gender norms. Improving the position of women will probably be accompanied by progress for LGBTQ people; likewise, rolling back women\u8217\'20\'19s rights will also mean those of LGBTQ people deteriorate in tandem.\par \par \uc2 This underlines why it is wrongheaded to claim that trans rights and women\u8217\'20\'19s rights are on a collision course. Is it a coincidence that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jolyonmaugham/status/1274566296512987136"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawyer}}}\uc2  who was instructed to act against the Tavistock Clinic \u8211\'20\'13 which provides gender-affirming healthcare for young trans people \u8211\'20\'13 previously worked on cases involving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and a challenge to legalising the homosexual {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.stonewall.org.uk/our-work/campaigns/love-wins-age-consent-equalised-gay-and-bi-men"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 age of consent}}}\uc2  ? Is it really a coincidence that the rightwing Tory MP \uc2 David Davies\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who called claims to introduce equal marriage \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2012/dec/21/david-davies-gay-marriage-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 barking mad}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and consistently voted against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wheredotheystand.org.uk/t/monmouth/david-davies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 would so gladly support {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.transgendertrend.com/transgender-law-concerns/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 groups}}}\uc2  that are opposing trans rights?\par \par \uc2 For LGBTQ people on both sides of the Atlantic, the reversal of progress is bewildering and frightening. But it isn\u8217\'20\'19t happening in isolation. After suffering historic defeats, patriarchy is roaring back, and it\u8217\'20\'19s angry. Our rights and freedoms are bound together: we rise together, and unless we\u8217\'20\'19re united, patriarchy will come for us all.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Owen Jones is a Guardian columnist\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://membership.theguardian.com/event/the-making-of-heartstopper-350418580407"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The making of Heartstopper}}}\uc2  : join the author, Alice Oseman, and actor Joe Locke in conversation with Owen Jones on Tuesday 5 July 2022 from 8pm to 9pm BST\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Do you have an opinion on the issues raised in this article? If you would like to submit a letter of up to 300 words to be considered for publication, email it to us at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:guardian.letters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guardian.letters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220705ei75001e3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
