\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Man in custody after six shot dead at Fourth of July parade\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,598 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 July 2022\par 10:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Witnesses speak of their terror after at least six killed and 30 injured at public event in Highland Park, Chicago. Plus, US drag queens stand their ground\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 A person of interest in the mass killing that targeted a Fourth of July parade in the Chicago suburb of Highland Park {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/04/highland-park-shooting-fourth-of-july-arrest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been taken into custody}}}\uc2 , the Highland Park police chief said yesterday evening.\par \par \uc2 More than 100 law enforcement officers had scoured the suburb and surrounding areas after at least six people were killed when a lone gunman rained down bullets on the town\u8217\'20\'19s independence celebrations yesterday morning.\par \par \uc2 Thirty people were injured in the attack, with ages ranging from eight to 85, said Dr Brigham Temple, medical director of emergency preparedness at \uc2 NorthShore University\uc2  health center, where 26 of the injured were treated. At least four of the injured are believed to be children.\par \par \uc2 On Monday afternoon, the police chief, Lou Jogmen, identified 22-year-old Robert E Crimo III as a person of interest in the shooting, and cautioned that the man should be considered armed and dangerous.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Is Crimo the person in custody? Police are still investigating Crimo\u8217\'20\'19s connection to the shooting and declined to immediately identify him as a suspect. But they said identifying him as a person of interest and sharing his name and other information publicly was a serious step.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Who were the victims? Among the victims was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/04/chicago-shooting-fourth-july-parade-highland-park"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nicolas Toledo, a 76-year-old grandfather who was identified by his family}}}\uc2 . He was watching the parade from his wheelchair when gunshots rang out. The other victims have yet to be named.\par \par \uc2 After Roe, are Republicans willing to expand the social safety net?\par \par \uc2 Republicans across the US cast the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision last month that allowed states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a victory for \u8220\'20\'1Clife\u8221\'20\'1D. Left unsaid was the quality of life that families and mothers set to be left dealing with unplanned pregnancies might have.\par \par \uc2 For years, the Republican party has pushed to ban a procedure that is mostly sought out by people who are poor, while showing much less enthusiasm for efforts to permanently expand the country\u8217\'20\'19s social safety net. Critics have labeled the party\u8217\'20\'19s stance as caring a lot politically about unborn fetuses, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/05/roe-v-wade-abortion-republicans-social-safety-net"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 losing interest in them when they are born as American citizens}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Twenty-six states are expected to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  entirely following the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, and following November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, Republicans could gain control of one or both houses of Congress, and make gains in state legislatures.\par \par \uc2 That dynamic could give many more Americans a close-up look at what the party\u8217\'20\'19s policies mean for women and families dealing with any wave of unplanned pregnancies, and there are signs Republicans are worried about what they will see.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What has\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief said about the fight for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights since the\par \par \uc2 supreme\par \par \uc2 court ruling? \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , the president and CEO of the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/05/planned-parenthood-abortion-rights-ceo-alexis-mcgill-johnson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outlines the three goals she has to get women the access they need}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump 2024 run could upend midterms \u8211\'20\'13 and deflect risk of prosecution\par \par \uc2 Speculation is swirling in the US media that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/05/trump-2024-run-us-elections-prosecution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 considering announcing a 2024 presidential run}}}\uc2  as early as this summer and in the face of ever more damaging revelations from a congressional investigation of his role in the 6 Januaryattack on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Irrespective of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chances of winning a second term, another presidential campaign under consideration \u8211\'20\'13 as reported by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , \uc2 CBS\uc2  and other US outlets \u8211\'20\'13 could give the former president a multi-year shield to deflect the attention of prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 The reports have come after committee hearings into the 6 January 2021 Capitol riot that could lead to the congressional panel itself recommending Trump face criminal charges for his role in an attempt to thwart the certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s electoral win. Or the justice department could charge Trump via its own investigation of the scheme.\par \par \uc2 In testimony to the panel last week, Cassidy Hutchinson, a former aide to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , strengthened a potential criminal case when she alleged that Trump knew his supporters were armed when he encouraged them to march on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What would happen if Trump were to run for a second stint in the White House? Most experts believe it would \u8211\'20\'13 at the very least \u8211\'20\'13 complicate any decision to criminally charge him. It would also be likely to bolster his support in the Republican party, which has begun to ebb slightly in the wake of the 6 January revelations.\par \par \uc2 Special event: What will the end of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in America mean for the world?\par \par \uc2 The supreme court decision overturning Roe v Wade reverses a historic victory of the global women\u8217\'20\'19s movement. What comes next? Will we see increased criminalization of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US? Will other rights, such as marriage equality and IVF access, be targeted next? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://membership.theguardian.com/event/what-will-the-end-of-abortion-rights-in-america-mean-for-the-world-358372139717"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Our panel}}}\uc2 , moderated by Guardian columnist Arwa Mahdawi, will discuss what the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision means for the future in a live discussion on Wednesday, 6 July, 3pm-4pm ET. Book tickets for this virtual event {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://membership.theguardian.com/event/what-will-the-end-of-abortion-rights-in-america-mean-for-the-world-358372139717"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The detained \uc2 WNBA\uc2  star Brittney Griner made a direct appeal to US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for her freedom in a handwritten letter that was delivered to the White House yesterday morning. Griner, one of America\u8217\'20\'19s most decorated women\u8217\'20\'19s basketball players, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jul/05/brittney-griner-letter-joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 detained in Russia in February}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  of California has aired a commercial in Florida over the Fourth of July holiday weekend urging residents there to fight for freedom, or move to his state\par \par \uc2 to find it. The ad \u8211\'20\'13 which pits blue state California against currently red state Florida \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/04/gavin-newsom-florida-ad-fox-news-ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exemplified the growing divides in the US}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s demolition of Brazil\u8217\'20\'19s Indigenous and environmental protection services and \u8220\'20\'1Csurrender of the Amazon to crooks\u8221\'20\'1D played a direct role in the murders of Dom Phillips and Bruno Pereira, the politician leading a congressional inquiry into the crime {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/04/bolsonaro-surrender-of-amazon-to-crooks-played-role-in-murders-of-dom-phillips-bruno-pereira"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has claimed}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Family members of several US nationals who are being held in Saudi Arabia and Egypt were not invited to attend a recent call with \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , the secretary of state, in a move that was called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/05/us-detainees-middle-east-antony-blinken-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cinfuriating and discriminatory\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  by one critic. The apparent decision to exclude the families was made weeks before \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s controversial trip to the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma is planning to execute a prisoner on death row nearly every month starting in August through 2024 in a move\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/04/oklahoma-death-row-prisoners-executions-plans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 likely to cause outrage among opponents of the death penalty}}}\uc2 . The Oklahoma court of criminal appeals set the execution dates on Friday for six inmates, who have all exhausted their appeals.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: Ukraine lays out $750bn \u8216\'20\'18recovery plan\u8217\'20\'19 for postwar future\par \par \uc2 The eventual restoration of Ukraine through a $750bn (\u163\'00\'A3620bn) recovery plan is the common task of the entire democratic world, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/04/ukraine-zelenskiy-lays-out-750bn-recovery-plan-for-postwar-future"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Ukrainian president said yesterday}}}\uc2  at the first detailed event to map out a physical future for the country in the event it survives as a western-facing nation after the Russian invasion. Speaking by video link to a high-level conference in Lugano, Switzerland, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  admitted the task ahead was colossal, claiming the war was a battle of outlooks in which Russia was determined to destroy his country\u8217\'20\'19s physical and moral fabric.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: US drag queens stand their ground amid intimidation by the far right\par \par \uc2 The drag queens were out in force across New York\u8217\'20\'19s recent Pride parade triggering cheers and waves with their flamboyant and extravagant costumes. But this year, the world of American drag has been marred by fears of violence and intimidation as they have been specifically targeted by conservatives and extremist far-right and militia groups amid a general rise in anti-LGBTQ hate. Drag queens themselves, however, are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/04/drag-queens-targeted-us-far-right"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 standing their ground}}}\uc2 , writes Edward Helmore.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 Or this: Public lands are Americans\u8217\'20\'19 birthright. It\u8217\'20\'19s our duty to defend them against new landgrabs\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is your land we are talking about,\u8221\'20\'1D the firebrand historian and conservationist Bernard DeVoto wrote in 1947, paraphrasing Woody Guthrie\u8217\'20\'19s fresh folk classic. Bernard and his stylish, sharp-witted wife, Avis DeVoto, had returned from an epic road trip across the Lewis and Clark trail. On the road, they discovered a plot \u8211\'20\'13 birthed by the Nevada senator Pat McCarran \u8211\'20\'13 to sell away nearly all of it. This is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jul/05/bernard-avis-devoto-public-lands-protect"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the story of how one couple helped save vast areas of wilderness}}}\uc2  in the 1940s \u8211\'20\'13 and provided a map for protecting them today.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Methane much more sensitive to global heating than previously thought \u8211\'20\'13 study\par \par \uc2 Methane is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jul/05/global-heating-causes-methane-growth-four-times-faster-than-thought-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 four times more sensitive to global warming than previously thought}}}\uc2 , a study shows. The result helps to explain the rapid growth in methane in recent years and suggests that, if left unchecked, methane related warming will escalate in the decades to come. The growth of this greenhouse gas \u8211\'20\'13 which over a 20-year timespan is more than 80 times as potent than carbon dioxide \u8211\'20\'13 had been slowing since the turn of the millennium but since 2007 has undergone a rapid rise.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220705ei75001gx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
