\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Fox and friends face billion-dollar US lawsuits\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,413 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 July 2022\par 10:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Rightwing networks Fox News, OAN and \uc2 Newsmax\uc2  could be found liable over election fraud claims. Plus, the amazing fates of Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s greatest dresses\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 In the months after the 2020 US presidential election, rightwing TV news in America was a wild west, an apparently lawless free-for-all where conspiracy theories about voting machines, ballot-stuffed suitcases and dead Venezuelan leaders were repeated to viewers around the clock.\par \par \uc2 There seemed to be little consequence for peddling the most outrageous ideas on primetime.\par \par \uc2 But now, unfortunately for Fox News, One America News Network (OAN) and \uc2 Newsmax\uc2 , it turns out that this brave new world was not free from legal jurisdiction \u8211\'20\'13 with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2022/jul/04/fox-oan-newsmax-lawsuits-election-fraud-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the three networks now facing billion-dollar lawsuits }}}\uc2  as a result of their baseless accusations.\par \par \uc2 In June, \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  , which provided voting machines to 28 states, was given the go-ahead to sue \uc2 Fox Corp\uc2  , the parent company of Fox News, in a case that could draw \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2  and his son Lachlan into the spotlight.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What does Dominion say \uc2 Fox Corp\uc2  did? In the $1.6bn lawsuit, Dominion accuses \uc2 Fox Corp\uc2  , and the Murdochs specifically, of allowing Fox News to amplify false claims that the voting company had rigged the election for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Should Fox News be worried? Ciara Torres-Spelliscy, a legal expert, thinks Dominion has a good case. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s particularly bad for \uc2 Fox\uc2  is [that] Dominion asked them to stop and correct the record in real time, and Fox persisted in spreading misrepresentations about the voting machine company,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers fear violence after Roe overturned\par \par \uc2 Boulder, Colorado, has for decades made its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers feel welcome. The city council passed one of the country\u8217\'20\'19s first laws regulating how close demonstrators could get to patients seeking reproductive care, and residents took to the streets in protest when it became clear that the supreme court was ready to overturn the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as it did last month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBoulder is probably the most pro-choice community in the country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Warren Hern, the director of Boulder \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic. \u8220\'20\'1CBut there are people in the community who want me dead.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 From targeted killings of doctors to vandalism of clinics and intimidation of staff, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/03/abortion-providers-violence-danger-roe-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 danger is a daily reality }}}\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in the US. With states now empowered to ban the procedure after the supreme court overturned federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, reproductive health experts fear a new wave of violence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  violence is more common when you have these moments of uncertainty and upheaval, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what we have now,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Ziegler, a legal historian at Florida State University College of Law who studies \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else is the\par \par \uc2 supreme court set to tear up? The ideologically driven conservative majority is likely to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/03/voting-rights-us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 further weaken key civil rights legislation }}}\uc2  after a term of radical rulings.\par \par \uc2 Leaders gather to work out \u8216\'20\'18Marshall\par \par \uc2 plan\u8217\'20\'19 to rebuild Ukraine\par \par \uc2 Leaders from dozens of countries, international organisations and the private sector will gather in Switzerland on Monday to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/jul/04/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-marshall-plan-volodymyr-zelenskiy-putin-russian-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62c25e358f084d8ff381aa1f#block-62c25e358f084d8ff381aa1f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hash out a \u8220\'20\'1CMarshall plan\u8221\'20\'1D to rebuild war-ravaged Ukraine }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  , who will take part virtually, earlier warned that the work ahead in just the areas that have been liberated was \u8220\'20\'1Creally colossal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd we will have to free over 2,000 villages and towns in the east and south of Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 It is estimated more than 120,000 homes in Ukraine have been destroyed during the Russian invasion, creating the need for billions in income to restore the country economically and make it a Europe-faced economy.\par \par \uc2 Lingering concerns about widespread corruption in Ukraine mean far-reaching reforms remain in focus and will be a condition for any recovery plan.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How much of Ukraine has been damaged? It is estimated that at least 45m sq meters of housing, 256 enterprises, 656 medical institutions and 1,177 educational institutions have been damaged, destroyed or seized, while Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s economy has already lost up to $600bn.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How much will it cost to rebuild Ukraine? It is expected to cost hundreds of billions of dollars. Kyiv School of Economics (KSE) has estimated the damage done so far to buildings and infrastructure at nearly $104bn.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else is happening? Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/04/russia-ukraine-war-what-we-know-on-day-131-of-the-invasion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what we know on day 131 }}}\uc2  of the invasion.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The last remaining Medal of Honor recipient from the second world war will lie in state at the US Capitol,\par \par \uc2 the West Virginia senator Joe Manchin announced at a memorial on Sunday where Hershel W \u8220\'20\'1CWoody\u8221\'20\'1D Williams was remembered for his courage, humility and selflessness.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Danish police believe a shooting at a shopping mall in Copenhagen that left three people dead and four others seriously wounded was not terror-related. They said on Monday that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/04/copenhagen-shooting-denmark-police-say-no-indication-of-terrorism-motive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the gunman acted alone }}}\uc2  and appeared to have selected his victims at random.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Hong Kong legislator who appeared in a group photo with \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  during his visit to the territory has said he has tested positive for Covid, as Macau kicks off a new round of citywide coronavirus testing. In his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/04/xi-jinping-in-covid-scare-during-hong-kong-handover-trip-china"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  first trip outside mainland China since the pandemic began }}}\uc2 , the Chinese president met only people who had undergone quarantine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The search for survivors of a glacier collapse in which at least six people have died has resumed in Italy\u8217\'20\'19s Dolomites region. Authorities believe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/03/deaths-glacier-breaks-marmolada-mountain-italy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as many as 15 people may still be missing }}}\uc2  after a large chunk of glacier broke loose on Sunday afternoon and caused ice and rock to fall on hikers.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: US consumer prices increased 8.6% from May 2021 to May 2022, the biggest increase since 1981\par \par \uc2 Inflation is hitting Americans hard. US consumer prices increased 8.6% from May 2021 to May 2022, the biggest increase since 1981, outpacing overall annual wage growth at 5.2% in May 2022. Food prices have increased more than 10% over the year. A gallon of gas is more than 50% more expensive than a year ago. The median monthly rent in the US hit an all-time high of $2,002 a month in May 2022. Workers at big chains are struggling to make ends meet as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/03/fast-food-workers-inflation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prices increase but their wages do not }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this:\par \par \uc2 stuffed into a shoebox, seized by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  : the amazing fates of Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s greatest dresses\par \par \uc2 Kim Kardashian is no stranger to a fleeting moment becoming a viral news story. But her recent appearance at the Met Gala wearing the dress that Marilyn Monroe wore to sing Happy Birthday to President John Kennedy in 1962 proved particularly divisive. Whatever your feelings about Galagate, the furore does make you wonder about the fate of other coveted \u8211\'20\'13 and increasingly valuable \u8211\'20\'13 garments from Hollywood history. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/costume-and-culture/2022/jul/04/kim-kardashian-marilyn-monroe-hollywood-dresses-fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What happened to those other magnificent outfits }}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and why did no one realise their eye-popping value?\par \par \uc2 Climate check:\par \par \uc2 grunion run has fascinated scientists, but their future is threatened by the climate crisis\par \par \uc2 On certain nights on a quiet California beach, thousands of small, silvery fish gather in the moonlight to perform a unique mating ritual. Known as the \u8220\'20\'1Cgrunion run\u8221\'20\'1D, the spectacle is one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/02/california-fish-beach-sex-rare-climate-crisis-danger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lesser known natural wonders of the US west coast }}}\uc2 . Grunion are a rare fish species that come ashore to spawn. The grunion run has fascinated scientists and local people for decades. But its future could be imperiled by the climate crisis \u8211\'20\'13 including warmer land and water temperatures and increasingly acidic oceans \u8211\'20\'13 as well as human activities such as fishing.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing:\par \par \uc2 newly identified water lily species is world\u8217\'20\'19s largest\par \par \uc2 A giant waterlily grown at Kew Gardens has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jul/04/third-species-of-giant-waterlily-discovered-at-kew-gardens"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 named as new to science }}}\uc2 , in the first discovery of its type in more than a century. Scientists at the south-west London garden suspected for decades there could be a third species of giant waterlily and worked with researchers in its native home in Bolivia to see if their thesis was correct. With leaves growing up to 3 meters in the wild, it is also the largest giant waterlily on the planet. The striking lily has flowers that turn from white to pink, and bears spiny petioles.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220704ei740018m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
