\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Monday briefing:  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  is safe, supported, and available in the UK. Why is the law so complicated?\b0\par\par\uc2 Archie Bland \par \uc2 2,106 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 July 2022\par 05:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In today\u8217\'20\'19s newsletter: After Roe v Wade fell in America, this is the state of reproductive rights in the UK \u8226\'20\'22 Sign up here for our daily newsletter, First Edition\par \par \uc2 Good morning. The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision to overturn Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  ten days ago was vastly consequential for the millions of American women who will now be denied the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 but it also reverberated around the world.\par \par \uc2 In the UK, one consequence has been a renewed focus on a legal picture here that is extremely confusing. For most women, most of the time, access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the UK is unfettered and uncontroversial, with widespread public support. And yet the blunt fact remains that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still, technically, a criminal offence \u8211\'20\'13 and persistent exceptions and complications can be a real barrier for the women who need help the most.\par \par \uc2 For today\u8217\'20\'19s newsletter, I spoke to Kaye Wellings, a professor of sexual and reproductive health research at the \uc2 London School of Hygiene & Tropical Medicine\uc2 , who \u8211\'20\'13 at a moment of heightened anxiety - gave an incredibly helpful guide to how all of this plays out in principle and in practice. That\u8217\'20\'19s right after the headlines.\par \par \uc2 Five big stories\par \par \uc2 Conservatives\par \par \uc2 | \uc2 Boris Johnson{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/03/johnson-faces-backlash-for-failure-to-act-over-chris-pincher-warnings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is facing a backlash}}}\uc2  over the promotion of his ally Chris Pincher, who resigned as deputy chief whip over allegations that he groped two men. A group of party staffers accused the prime minister of a \u8220\'20\'1Cfailure to act on warnings\u8221\'20\'1D of sexual misconduct by his MPs.\par \par \uc2 Cost of living\par \par \uc2 | Half of children in lone-parent families {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/04/half-of-all-children-in-lone-parent-families-are-in-relative-poverty"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are now living in relative poverty}}}\uc2 , exclusive research shared with the Guardian said. Relative poverty for children in lone-parent families has risen at a significantly faster rate than other households.\par \par \uc2 Denmark\par \par \uc2 | {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/03/several-wounded-in-shooting-at-copenhagen-shopping-centre-say-police"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Three people were shot dead}}}\uc2  and one suspect has been arrested and charged with manslaughter after gunfire at a busy Copenhagen shopping centre, with emergency services rushing to the scene on Sunday evening.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\par \par \uc2 | Russia has said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/03/russias-claim-it-has-won-effective-control-of-luhansk-rejected-by-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it is in control of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s eastern Luhansk region}}}\uc2  after taking over the last Ukrainian-controlled city there. Russian defence minister \uc2 Sergei Shoigu\uc2  said \u8220\'20\'1Cfull control\u8221\'20\'1D had been established over Lysychansk.\par \par \uc2 Theatre\par \par \uc2 | The groundbreaking British director Peter Brook, whose huge influence reached around the world, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/stage/2022/jul/03/peter-brook-influential-theatre-visionary-dies-aged-97"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has died at the age of 97}}}\uc2 . The actor Ben Kingsley told the Guardian: \u8220\'20\'1CHis genius continues to guide us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In depth: The theory and reality of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the UK\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Dominic Raab\uc2  was asked to include the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the forthcoming UK bill of rights last week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2022/jun/29/dominic-raab-says-right-to-abortion-does-not-need-to-be-in-bill-of-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he insisted}}}\uc2  the matter was already \u8220\'20\'1Csettled in UK law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But at least 17 women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nationalworld.com/news/crime/abortion-uk-police-investigate-women-illegal-abortions-england-wales-us-states-bans-3749526"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have been investigated}}}\uc2  over illegal abortions since 2014; \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wetrustwomen.org.uk/5-reasons-to-decriminalise-abortion/#:~:text=Data%20from%20the%20Medicines%20and,Ireland%20in%20a%20recent%20crackdown."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have been seized}}}\uc2  on their way to women across the UK; women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://time.com/6192022/northern-ireland-abortion-access/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 still have limited access}}}\uc2  in Northern Ireland; some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/22/abortion-hierarchy-uk-lack-of-services-scotland-northern-ireland-england-terminate-pregnancy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are being forced to travel hundreds of miles}}}\uc2  for treatment.\par \par \uc2 99 MPs voted against decriminalisation in Northern Ireland. And a woman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oxfordmail.co.uk/news/20083264.woman-24-court-accused-procuring-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is due to go on trial in Oxford next week}}}\uc2  for unlawfully procuring her own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs. None of this appears to support the image of benevolent clarity that Raab seeks to present.\par \par \uc2 Kaye Wellings has as broad a view of the state of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care as anyone: at LSHTM, she runs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lshtm.ac.uk/research/centres-projects-groups/sacha"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the SACHA study}}}\uc2 , the biggest ever UK research project on the subject, with the support of the National Institute for Health and Care Research. She says it\u8217\'20\'19s important to start by saying clearly that the overall picture is good for supporters of reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been working in this field for 30 years, and it\u8217\'20\'19s striking to me just how satisfactory most services are most of the time,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. But that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean there aren\u8217\'20\'19t real issues.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 What does the law say on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 In the UK, apart from Northern Ireland, the law is \u8230\'20\'26 extremely weird. The basis for the provision of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/1967/87"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 1967 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Act}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which does not declare that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal, but instead sets out circumstances under which women and healthcare professionals will not be prosecuted. If an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not meet those criteria, it is a crime.\par \par \uc2 The language of the act might seem pretty onerous. It says that after 24 weeks, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only legal if there is a grave risk to the health or life of the pregnant woman, or if there is a serious risk of severe fetal abnormalities. Before that point, the standard is a risk to physical or mental health that exceeds the risk of a termination. Two doctors have to sign off on any such decision.\par \par \uc2 In practice, the law should not stop women getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if they want one before 24 weeks. (The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.uk/government/statistics/abortion-statistics-for-england-and-wales-2021/abortion-statistics-england-and-wales-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2021 statistics show}}}\uc2  that 90% of abortions take place before 10 weeks, against 1% after 20 weeks and 0.1% after 24 weeks in very unusual circumstances.)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe criteria are viewed flexibly and leniently,\u8221\'20\'1D said Wellings. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd taking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills [which now account for 87% of abortions] is safer than childbirth, so the framework is almost redundant.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, though the agreement of two doctors may sound intimidating, it is not required that they see the patient before agreeing, and can rely on information provided by other members of their team.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Are there other obstacles to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access?\par \par \uc2 Yes:\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 The fact that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains a taboo in some communities, which is only exacerbated when women hear that it has not been decriminalised. \u8220\'20\'1CWomen are shocked to think they could be doing something which could be seen as a crime,\u8221\'20\'1D said Wellings, whose work is heavily informed by interviews with women who have had abortions. \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of them were terrified that they wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t get through the gatekeeping system.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That fear is sometimes more of an obstacle than the practice. \u8220\'20\'1CIn general women seeking abortions are of the view that they\u8217\'20\'19ve been supported, sympathised with, that there\u8217\'20\'19s been no frowning or judgmental attitudes,\u8221\'20\'1D Wellings said.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 The personal views of some doctors. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are practitioners in this country who don\u8217\'20\'19t believe in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Wellings. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is a risk that they won\u8217\'20\'19t then quickly refer a woman to another GP. But most women are very savvy whatever their educational level. They told us, my GP seemed a bit hesitant so I went online.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Other doctors feeling that they are unable to provide proper care. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not the law that makes them resistant,\u8221\'20\'1D said Wellings. \u8220\'20\'1CThe question that seems to worry them is resources \u8211\'20\'13 payment for the service \u8211\'20\'13 and time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 The intimidation of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protesters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-62009477"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outside clinics}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 although this is much less widespread an issue than in the US, and \u8220\'20\'1Cbuffer zones\u8221\'20\'1D around clinics are increasingly common as a way of limiting this effect.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Living in Northern Ireland, where the law is ahead of the rest of the UK after \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was fully decriminalised in 2019 \u8211\'20\'13 but practice has not caught up. The region\u8217\'20\'19s health minister \uc2 Robin Swann\uc2  is against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and has refused to publish information about it on the department of health website, the i newspaper {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://inews.co.uk/news/northern-ireland-abortion-advice-virtually-impossible-1697938"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently reported}}}\uc2 . Some women in Northern Ireland are still being forced to cross the Irish Sea, though many fewer than a few years ago.\par \par \uc2 Against these concerns, there has been one piece of progress recently: rules brought in during the pandemic allowing both \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to be taken at home have been extended {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/extension-of-temporary-approval-of-home-use-for-both-stages-of-early-medical-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least until the end of August}}}\uc2  in England, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gov.wales/written-statement-arrangements-early-medical-abortion-home"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indefinitely in Wales}}}\uc2 . That is good news, Wellings said: \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lshtm.ac.uk/newsevents/news/2022/without-doubt-way-forward-new-study-shows-women-who-accessed-abortion-during"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Women we spoke to}}}\uc2  love having control over their own procedure, and in terms of convenience.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 So what needs to change?\par \par \uc2 While the awkward legal basis for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the UK is far from ideal, there are some risks attached to fixing it, says Wellings, who points to the intensity of the right to life movement in response to a consultation over extending the coronavirus rules: \u8220\'20\'1CThey got mobilised, they got thousands of signatures. There is a risk in waking sleeping dogs up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, advocates and MPs pursuing reform are seeking a worthwhile goal, she argues, so long as they are vigilant and ready to make their case. \u8220\'20\'1CIt would stop \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  being a special case and it would put it on a par with other health issues,\u8221\'20\'1D Wellings said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are many areas of medical practice that cope perfectly well without a law, using the very good systems of medical governance. But a strong theme of our work is that decriminalisation is not enough. There\u8217\'20\'19s still a great deal of work to be done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 What else we\u8217\'20\'19ve been reading\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Saturday magazine\u8217\'20\'19s history of protest photography, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/01/we-wont-stay-silent-any-longer-the-protest-photographs-that-changed-britain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the UK}}}\uc2  and around {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/02/it-felt-like-history-itself-48-protest-photographs-that-changed-the-world"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  the world}}}\uc2 , is absorbing, moving, and occasionally electrifying. \u8220\'20\'1CI still find it tragic that we don\u8217\'20\'19t see as many images of these events in the media any more,\u8221\'20\'1D writes Don McCullin. \u8220\'20\'1CI worry we are being denied the truth.\u8221\'20\'1D Archie\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 With Labour expected to say that it will never strike a deal with the SNP to enter government, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jul/03/talk-to-the-snp-keir-starmer-tory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Neal Lawson writes}}}\uc2  that the decision is \u8220\'20\'1Cmorally dubious and tactically inept\u8221\'20\'1D. He adds: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat it won\u8217\'20\'19t do is stop the charge from the Tories that voting Labour means a coalition of chaos\u8221\'20\'1D. Archie\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Smartphones have been linked to a range of society\u8217\'20\'19s ills in the last decade. The most recent of those worries is how technology is impacting our memory: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global/2022/jul/03/is-your-smartphone-ruining-your-memory-the-rise-of-digital-amenesia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rebecca Seal talks to experts about how concerned they are about digital amnesia}}}\uc2 . Nimo\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Stamps are getting a digital barcode, and enthusiasts aren\u8217\'20\'19t happy. Simon Usborne {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2022/jul/04/eventually-it-will-just-be-a-barcode-wont-it-why-britains-new-stamps-are-causing-outrage-and-upset"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 encourages a bit of mild sedition}}}\uc2 , and sets out a rich history that may be entering its final chapter. Archie\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sarah Butler identifies the wider trends behind the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jun/05/missguided-went-badly-off-course-could-this-become-a-trend?utm_term=Autofeed&CMP=twt_gu&utm_medium&utm_source=Twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fall of fast fashion titan}}}\uc2 Missguided, asking what\u8217\'20\'19s next for the other online fast-fashion retailers. Nimo\par \par \uc2 Sport\par \par \uc2 Tennis\par \par \uc2 | Cameron Norrie {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jul/03/britains-cameron-norrie-rises-to-the-occasion-by-overpowering-tommy-paul"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reached his first grand slam quarter-final}}}\uc2  with a 6-4, 7-5, 6-4 win over Tommy Paul at Wimbledon. Heather Watson\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jul/03/bruised-heather-watson-outplayed-by-jule-niemeier-in-last-16-of-wimbledon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 excellent run ended}}}\uc2  with a straight sets defeat by Jule Niemeier. Novak Djokovic eased into the last eight after beating Van Rijthoven 6-2, 4-6, 6-1, 6-2.\par \par \uc2 Cricket\par \par \uc2 | Jonny Bairstow scored another remarkable century for England but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jul/03/england-india-fifth-test-day-three-match-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 India appeared to be ahead}}}\uc2  at the end of the third day at Edgbaston, with a lead of 257 and seven wickets still in hand.\par \par \uc2 Formula One\par \par \uc2 | Ferrari\u8217\'20\'19s Carlos Sainz {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jul/03/ferraris-carlos-sainz-claims-first-win-ahead-of-perez-in-thrilling-british-f1-gp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took his first victory}}}\uc2  in a classic British Grand Prix which Lewis Hamilton described as \u8220\'20\'1CFormula One at its best\u8221\'20\'1D. Hamilton secured an impressive third for Mercedes behind the Red Bull of Sergio P\u233\'00\'E9rez in second.\par \par \uc2 The front pages\par \par \uc2 Several papers lead with fallout over \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s promotion of Chris Pincher. The Telegraph has \u8220\'20\'1CPM facing Cabinet backlash over Pincher\u8221\'20\'1D while the Times reports \u8220\'20\'1CSex scandal revitalises rebel plot to topple PM\u8221\'20\'1D. The i newspaper says \u8220\'20\'1CPoll blow to Johnson as new Pincher claims made\u8221\'20\'1D. The Mirror\u8217\'20\'19s headline reads \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t know what decent is\u8221\'20\'1D and says Labour demands an explanation from Johnson over the situation.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  leads with \u8220\'20\'1CRevealed: children of lone parents hardest hit by Tory austerity\u8221\'20\'1D while the Mail reports \u8220\'20\'1CPolice let 22,000 suspects roam free\u8221\'20\'1D. The Sun\u8217\'20\'19s splash reads \u8220\'20\'1CTowie stars\u8217\'20\'19 death smash\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Today in Focus\par \par \uc2 Surviving Britain\u8217\'20\'19s homelessness crisis\par \par \uc2 Reporter Daniel Lavelle {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2022/jul/04/surviving-britains-homelessness-crisis-daniel-lavelle-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on his experience of homelessness}}}\uc2  and what it taught him about the impact of government cuts.\par \par \uc2 Cartoon of the day | Nicola Jennings\par \par \uc2 The Upside\par \par \uc2 A bit of good news to remind you that the world\u8217\'20\'19s not all bad\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/jul/02/it-feels-amazing-revellers-young-and-old-celebrate-pride-in-london"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 50th anniversary of pride in London }}}\uc2  has come and gone. Visitors and locals alike celebrated after a two-year-long pause because of the pandemic. All kinds of people - young and old, of different ethnic backgrounds, genders and sexualities - came together to party and protest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt feels bigger,\u8221\'20\'1D said one attendee, \u8220\'20\'1CIt feels like everyone who\u8217\'20\'19s here is enjoying it and has missed it \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s nice to be back.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m trying to focus on enjoying it, and seeing it as a coming together of the community where you can be who you want to be,\u8221\'20\'1D another said.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/feb/12/the-upside-sign-up-for-our-weekly-email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up here}}}\uc2  for a weekly roundup of The Upside, sent to you every Sunday\par \par \uc2 Bored at work?\par \par \uc2 And finally, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s crosswords to keep you entertained throughout the day \u8211\'20\'13 with plenty more on the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Puzzles app for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.apple.com/app/id1487780661?mt=8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 iOS}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=uk.co.guardian.puzzles&hl=en_GB&gl=US"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Android}}}\uc2 . Until tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/crosswords/quick/16273"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Quick crossword}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/crosswords/cryptic/28800"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptic crossword}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220704ei74000jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
