\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18People want me dead\u8217\'20\'19:  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  providers fear violence after Roe overturned\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington DC \par \uc2 1,194 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 July 2022\par 18:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Danger is a daily reality for the health workers, and moments of upheaval raise the risk, expert says\par \par \uc2 Boulder, Colorado, has for decades made its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers feel welcome. The city council passed one of the country\u8217\'20\'19s first laws regulating how close demonstrators could get to patients seeking reproductive care, and residents took to the streets in protest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/us-supreme-court-abortion-protesters-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when it became clear}}}\uc2  that the supreme court was ready to overturn the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as it did last month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBoulder is probably the most pro-choice community in the country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Warren Hern, director of the Boulder \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Clinic. \u8220\'20\'1CBut there are people in the community who want me dead.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 From targeted killings of doctors to vandalism of clinics and intimidation of staff, danger is a reality of life for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in the US. With states now empowered to ban the procedure after the supreme court overturned federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, reproductive health experts fear a new wave of violence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  violence is more common when you have these moments of uncertainty and upheaval, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what we have now,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Ziegler, a legal historian at Florida State University College of Law who studies \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That would add to the nervousness \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers feel in states where the procedure remains legal, but where a change in the party controlling the state legislature could upend their ability to provide care.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo woman\u8217\'20\'19s life and health should be at the mercy of the next election, or zip code, or \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  or Donald Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D Hern said, referring to the Republican Senate leader and the former president.\par \par \uc2 The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement has always found its greatest success in courtrooms and statehouses, passing laws that curbed access to clinics and encouraging Republicans to appoint supreme court justices who would vote to overturn the 1973 Roe v Wade ruling, which until last month protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/abortion-rulings-history-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Yet by the 1990s}}}\uc2 , extremists with the movement came to conclude that more needed to be done. Since then, four \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors have been assassinated and clinic staffers and bystanders have also lost their lives in shootings and bombings targeting facilities, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2015/nov/27/colorado-springs-shooting-planned-parenthood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the last deadly incident occurring in 2015}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Such violent attacks have \u8220\'20\'1Cbeen successful insofar as it\u8217\'20\'19s made people less interested in going to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics and less interested in going to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers,\u8221\'20\'1D Ziegler said.\par \par \uc2 They have also transformed life for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, who have taken to wearing bulletproof vests in public and outfitting their clinics with security doors and bullet-resistant glass.\par \par \uc2 But Ziegler said the attacks were often counterproductive because they swayed public opinion against anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups and reminded Americans of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/08/anti-abortion-movement-radicalized"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the links between the anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  movement and white supremacists}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople in the United States thought more negatively of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement as being a kind of misogynist white supremacist movement. Being a violent movement makes a lot of people reluctant to associate with you,\u8221\'20\'1D Ziegler said.\par \par \uc2 When insurrectionists attacked the US Capitol on 6 January 2021, \u8220\'20\'1Ca lot of our providers recognized people. They are people who have been outside their clinics,\u8221\'20\'1D said Melissa Fowler, chief program officer at the \uc2 National \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Federation\uc2 , which monitors violence against clinics.\par \par \uc2 Its data, which encompasses the US, Canada, Mexico City and Colombia, shows an increase in violence and harassment towards \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers. Every type of incident {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://prochoice.org/national-abortion-federation-releases-2021-violence-disruption-report/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the organization tracks in its annual report}}}\uc2  rose last year compared with 2020, including stalking of clinic staff, which in the US jumped 200% from the year prior, with 12 incidents reported.\par \par \uc2 Fowler said the latest surge dated back to 2015, when anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups released {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2015/aug/04/planned-parenthood-fifth-video-center-for-medical-progress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 misleading videos}}}\uc2  about Planned Parenthood, while the following year\u8217\'20\'19s election further raised tensions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve seen in the last few years people being more out and more bold with their hate,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think that also contributes to an environment when people might be more bold and more aggressive outside of clinics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In 1993, David Gunn became the first \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctor to be assassinated, and not long after, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.splcenter.org/fighting-hate/intelligence-report/2015/signers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a group of activists}}}\uc2  signed a petition saying \u8220\'20\'1Cthe use of force\u8221\'20\'1D was warranted to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Extremists killed two more doctors that decade, including Barnett Slepian, who was shot through a window in his home by an extremist with a high-powered rifle.\par \par \uc2 In 2009 came the assassination of George Tiller at his church in Wichita, Kansas. Hern considered him a friend.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe was a very fine person and a friend of mine and helped a lot of women, and that was why he was killed,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hern.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAny doctor that does \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in this country is the target of assassination, as well as anyone who helps them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Much of the violence in the past coincided with political losses, Fowler said. Gunn\u8217\'20\'19s murder came a year after the supreme court generally upheld \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in Planned Parenthood v Casey, and shortly after Bill Clinton took office. Tiller\u8217\'20\'19s assassination wasn\u8217\'20\'19t far into Barack Obama\u8217\'20\'19s time in the White House, while a 2015 mass shooting in Colorado Springs was near the end of his term.\par \par \uc2 Prominent anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  organizations have repudiated violence. Following Tiller\u8217\'20\'19s assassination, the executive director of National Right to Life, David N O\u8217\'20\'19Steen, said the group \u8220\'20\'1Cunequivocally condemns any such acts of violence regardless of motivation. The pro-life movement works to protect the right to life and increase respect for human life. The unlawful use of violence is directly contrary to that goal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yet for many providers, the threat of violence is rarely far from their minds.\par \par \uc2 In her decades of work with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers across the United States, Julie Burkhart can\u8217\'20\'19t think of a single facility that hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been picketed by demonstrators or vandalized. She\u8217\'20\'19s worked in clinics where windows were broken with bricks or shot out with bullets. At one clinic, someone cut open the roof and used a hose to flood the building.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, protesters greeted her as she worked to open what would be the only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Wyoming\u8217\'20\'19s second-largest city, Casper. Weeks before she was going to start operations, and days after the leak of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s opinion overturning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, an arsonist torched the building.\par \par \uc2 Now she\u8217\'20\'19s gutting the flame-and-smoke-damaged interior with an eye to reopening in November, even though {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wyofile.com/supreme-court-ruling-to-trigger-wyoming-abortion-ban/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wyoming is among the states moving to ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a time I hoped I would never see, that we would collectively never see,\u8221\'20\'1D Burkhart said.\par \par \uc2 But one person who saw the court\u8217\'20\'19s reversal coming was Tiller, her mentor whom she had worked alongside in Wichita for eight years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe did feel that ultimately Roe would be overturned. That was without a question in his mind. And I, at that time when he expressed that, I still didn\u8217\'20\'19t feel like I could see that same writing on the wall that he did,\u8221\'20\'1D Burkhart said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sad that what he thought came true.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220703ei73000gq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
