\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 10-year-old rape victim forced to travel from Ohio to Indiana for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Edward Helmore \par \uc2 648 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 July 2022\par 18:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 19\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Case places prominent anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures in position of balancing rights of women and girls while defending restrictions\par \par \uc2 The case of a 10-year-old child rape victim in Ohio who was six weeks pregnant, ineligible for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in her own state, and forced to travel to Indiana for the procedure has spotlighted the shocking impact of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ruling on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The story of the girl came to light three days after the court overturned a nationwide right to terminate pregnancy, and Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger ban\u8221\'20\'1D came into effect.\par \par \uc2 Dr Caitlin Bernard, an Indianapolis obstetrician-gynecologist, said she had received a call from a colleague doctor in Ohio who treats child abuse victims and asked for help. Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s lawmakers have not yet banned or restricted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but they are likely to do so when a special session of the state assembly convenes later this month.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers like Bernard say they are receiving a sharp increase in the number of patients coming to their clinics for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the neighboring states where such procedures are now restricted or banned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s hard to imagine that in just a few short weeks we will have no ability to provide that care,\u8221\'20\'1D Bernard {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dispatch.com/story/news/2022/07/01/ohio-girl-10-among-patients-going-indiana-abortion/7788415001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Columbus Dispatch.}}}\par \par \uc2 But the case of the 10-year-old girl has placed prominent anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  political figures in the position of balancing the rights of women and girls \u8211\'20\'13 including abuse victims \u8211\'20\'13 while defending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Republican governor \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  of South Dakota, mentioned as a potential running mate to Donald Trump in 2024, told CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union on Sunday that she found it to be \u8220\'20\'1Cincredible\u8221\'20\'1D that \u8220\'20\'1Cnobody\u8217\'20\'19s talking about the pervert, horrible and deranged individual that raped a 10-year-old\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Abortions are now criminal acts in South Dakota \u8220\'20\'1Cunless there is appropriate and reasonable medical judgment that performance of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is necessary to preserve the life of the pregnant female\u8221\'20\'1D. Cases of incest and rape are not an exception under South Dakota\u8217\'20\'19s law as it stands.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the state also banned medical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by telemedicine and increased the penalty for the unlicensed practice of medicine when performing abortions.\par \par \uc2 Dana Bash\uc2 , CNN\u8217\'20\'19S State of the Union host, pressed Noem on whether it was right for a 10-year-old rape victim who was pregnant to have to cross state lines for a legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Seeming to try to deflect, Noem said the rape of children is \u8220\'20\'1Can issue that the supreme court has weighed \u8230\'20\'26 as well\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that the public should also be \u8220\'20\'1Caddressing those sick individuals [who] do this to our children\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Asked if she would seek to have the law changed if a similar case occurred in her state, Noem replied: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t believe a tragic situation should be perpetuated by another tragedy. There\u8217\'20\'19s more that we have got to do to make sure that we really are living a life that says every life is precious, especially innocent lives that have been shattered, like that 10-year-old girl.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked if the girl should have to have the baby, Noem responded that \u8220\'20\'1Cevery single life \u8211\'20\'13 every single life is precious. This tragedy is horrific. But, in South Dakota, the law today is that the abortions are illegal, except to save the life of the mother.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But asked if allowing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be be performed on a 10-year-old would be considered as protecting the life of the mother, Noem did not rule out that interpretation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYes, that situation, the doctor, the family, the individuals closest to that will make the decisions there for that family,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, returning to the issue that for many Republicans is the central focus of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220703ei73001up\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
