\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden urged to do more to defend  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights: \u8216\'20\'18This is a five-alarm fire\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Washington \par \uc2 1,255 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 July 2022\par 13:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Furious Americans have taken to the streets, but many Democrats believe Biden has failed to capture the urgency and anger\par \par \uc2 High above America\u8217\'20\'19s capital, pro-choice activists scaled a construction crane, inching across its latticed steel arm, to affix a banner with a message for the president to see. It read: \u8220\'20\'1CBIDEN PROTECT \b \highlight22\uc2 ABORTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the days since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade, eliminating the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , legions of furious Americans have taken to the streets to protest a decision that was once unimaginable. But as a new reality takes shape, many are demanding the president and Democratic leaders do more to defend reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIs it that they can\u8217\'20\'19t, or they won\u8217\'20\'19t, go as far as they need to to stem the tide of the radical Republican agenda?\u8221\'20\'1D said Aimee Allison, founder of She the People, a progressive advocacy group that works to mobilize women of color.\par \par \uc2 For many Democrats, the president has failed to capture the urgency and fear they feel as conservative states and courts rush to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIs this a five-alarm fire? Yes, absolutely,\u8221\'20\'1D Allison said, adding that Democrats must show voters they are prepared to \u8220\'20\'1Cfight like hell\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In the week since the ruling was issued, Biden stepped up his rhetoric. During a meeting with Democratic governors, Biden said he \u8220\'20\'1Cshare[d] public outrage of this extremist court that\u8217\'20\'19s committed to moving America backward.\u8221\'20\'1D He also endorsed a change to the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s filibuster rule that would create an exception for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other privacy rights potentially under threat by the conservative court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow we\u8217\'20\'19re talking!\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1542504295559442432"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  Congresswoman \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , a Democrat of New York, who has pushed Democrats to deliver a more aggressive response. \u8220\'20\'1CUse the bully pulpit. We need more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With narrow majorities in Congress, Biden is under pressure to use the full force of his executive authority to protect reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 More than 20 Black Democratic congresswomen sent a letter to Biden asking him to immediately declare a public health emergency. \u8220\'20\'1CIn this unprecedented moment, we must act urgently as if lives depend on it because they do,\u8221\'20\'1D the lawmakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pressley.house.gov/media/press-releases/pressley-leads-black-congresswomen-urging-biden-declare-public-health-emergency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Other proposals include expanding access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication, covering expenses for federal employees who have to travel out of state, ensuring women serving in the military can receive care regardless of where they are stationed and using federal lands to perform abortions in states where it is banned.\par \par \uc2 Warning of potentially \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous ramifications,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House has so far resisted calls to open federal lands for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , led by Democratic senator Elizabeth Warren of Massachusetts and echoed on Friday by the governors of New York and New Mexico.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo it anyway,\u8221\'20\'1D said Amanda Litman, co-founder of Run for Something, a progressive organisation that helps young people run for local and state office. \u8220\'20\'1CShow me you are willing to put some skin in the game.\par \par \uc2 Democrats need to give voters concrete plans, she said. When Biden warns voters Republicans would ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide if they win control of Congress, they also need to hear him say he will not sign any restrictions they send to his desk, she added.\par \par \uc2 In recent days, the justice department has said it would seek to protect any woman who travels out of state for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  while the health department said it is working to expand access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden has promised additional actions but has repeatedly said the only way to \u8220\'20\'1Ctruly\u8221\'20\'1D protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is to elect enough Democrats to codify Roe v Wade into federal law. \u8220\'20\'1CVote, vote, vote. That\u8217\'20\'19s how we\u8217\'20\'19ll change it,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said during a press conference in Madrid.\par \par \uc2 But Democrats face a historically difficult election environment in the midterms this November, with inflation at a four-decade high and fears of a recession weighing down Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating.\par \par \uc2 Yet there are early signs that the court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the potential threat it poses to other rights such as same-sex marriage and contraception, is energizing Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 demoralized base.\par \par \uc2 The number of Americans who identified \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as top concern more than doubled since December, particularly among Democrats, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-biden-nancy-pelosi-womens-rights-government-and-politics-c410dbe9a8321b35a4e779b2fb226de5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new poll }}}\uc2  by the Associated Press-Norc Center for Public Affairs Research found. Meanwhile, public opinion polls show a shift toward Democrats in the wake of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, which drew thousands of people to the streets.\par \par \uc2 To successfully galvanize voters around the issue, Democrats must \u8220\'20\'1Cconnect the dots\u8221\'20\'1D by showing them that Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 end goal is a total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Molly Murphy, a Democratic pollster who has surveyed voters\u8217\'20\'19 views on the issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBeing against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is potentially for some voters not an indictment,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut wanting to make it illegal and trying to make it illegal is \u8211\'20\'13 and that\u8217\'20\'19s where the debate needs to go.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This week, House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  sent a letter to Democrats outlining potential votes the caucus could take. They include protecting personal data stored on reproductive health apps from \u8220\'20\'1Csinister\u8221\'20\'1D prosecutors who might use it to target women who have abortions; ensuring the right to travel between states; and enshrining the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  into federal law, a version of which has already passed the House but has no path forward in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Much of the fight has now shifted to the state and local level, where Democrats are vowing to use their power to expand access or, where they can, block new restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Across the country, Democratic governors and attorneys generals are vowing to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Governors in states like California and Illinois want to become havens for women seeking abortions in states where it\u8217\'20\'19s banned.\par \par \uc2 Progressive\uc2  local prosecutors and officials in conservative states say they will not enforce strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws against patients or providers. Some liberal-run cities are considering plans to set up funds for women who have to go out of state for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, activists have declared a \u8220\'20\'1Csummer of rage\u8221\'20\'1D, vowing to keep marching and resisting until a national right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is restored.\par \par \uc2 But cracks are also in display in the party.\par \par \uc2 Many progressives remain furious with party leaders for backing Texas congressman \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2 , the lone House Democrat to oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , over his progressive, pro-choice challenger, Jessica Cisneros. Cuellar won the primary by fewer than 300 votes.They are also mobilizing to stop Biden from nominating an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Republican attorney for federal judgeship in Kentucky, which was reported by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courier-journal.com/restricted/?return=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.courier-journal.com%2Fstory%2Fnews%2Fpolitics%2Fmitch-mcconnell%2F2022%2F06%2F29%2Fbiden-backs-anti-abortion-judge-candidate-apparent-mcconnell-deal%2F7767539001%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Courier Journal.}}}\par \par \uc2 Democrats increasingly believe the problem is the supreme court itself. A number of Democratic lawmakers have backed efforts to expand the number of justices on the court or impose term limits. Some lawmakers are calling for Congress to investigate \u8211\'20\'13 or even impeach\u8211\'20\'13 justices who signaled during their Senate confirmation hearings they would respect precedent but then voted to overturn Roe.\par \par \uc2 Biden has mostly resisted those calls. But as long as there remains a 6-3 conservative majority of justices on the court, little else will change, said Christopher Kang, cofounder and general counsel of Demand Justice, a liberal group that advocates for expanding the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHaving spent 50 years wresting a supermajority of power on the court, they\u8217\'20\'19re not likely to give that away,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CUnless you have a balanced supreme court, none of these other reforms will get a fair shot.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220702ei72001gw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
