\par\par \uc2 Australia news\par \b \uc2 South Australian Liberal leader and state MPs to \u8216\'20\'18mentor\u8217\'20\'19 young people at anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  event\b0\par\par\uc2 Tory Shepherd \par \uc2 903 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 June 2022\par 23:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Days before new SA \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws start, \uc2 David Speirs\uc2 , three of his colleagues and Labor minister Clare Scriven will feature in training dayFollow our Australia news live blog for the latest updatesGet our free news app, morning email briefing and daily news podcast\par \par \uc2 A week after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/26/the-guardian-view-on-overturning-roe-v-wade-anti-abortionists-reign-supreme"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade was overturned}}}\uc2  in the US, and just days before new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws come into force in South Australia, parliamentarians are set to \u8220\'20\'1Cmentor\u8221\'20\'1D young people at an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  event.\par \par \uc2 The Liberal leader, \uc2 David Speirs\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 along with three others from his shadow ministry, the Labor minister Clare Scriven and other political leaders \u8211\'20\'13 will feature in a training day aimed at activating \u8220\'20\'1Ca new generation to rise up and fight for the human rights of the unborn\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Greens MLC Tammy Franks said the move showed women could never take \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights for granted and was \u8220\'20\'1Cchilling for anyone who believes in bodily autonomy\u8221\'20\'1D, while Speirs said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot an activist\u8221\'20\'1D for change.\par \par \uc2 The deputy premier, Labor\u8217\'20\'19s Susan Close, said the \u8220\'20\'1Cmajority of the SA community and parliamentarians support safe, legal terminations of pregnancy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo one could want the US experience of division and heartbreak over this issue to come to our shores.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Enid Lyons List event is on Saturday, and coincides with the state byelection in Bragg, which was held by the former attorney general \uc2 Vickie Chapman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Chapman, one of the most senior members of the moderate Liberal faction under the former premier \uc2 Steven Marshall\uc2 , ushered in the new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws. From 7 July, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be decriminalised in SA. Women will be able to access medical abortions through telehealth at up to nine weeks gestation, and surgical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to 22 weeks and six days. After that two doctors will need to approve the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Opponents claimed the availability of late-term abortions was akin to \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  [up] to birth\u8221\'20\'1D. Chapman told Guardian Australia she rejected that idea: \u8220\'20\'1CThe parliament has decided this matter is best dealt with as a health issue and not the criminal sanction model.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTerminations are a medical procedure that remains highly regulated. Accordingly, I reject the claim that this provides \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to birth as promoted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Chapman stood down on the day Speirs was elected leader, after two investigations into her conduct. Weeks later {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.abc.net.au/news/2022-05-03/sa-ombudsman-report-into-vickie-chapman-kangaroo-island-decision/101034536"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she was cleared of any wrongdoing}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Labor candidate Alice Rolls is challenging the Liberal party\u8217\'20\'19s Jack Batty for the blue-ribbon, eastern suburbs Adelaide seat on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/guardian-australia-morning-mail/2014/jun/24/-sp-guardian-australias-morning-mail-subscribe-by-email?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up to receive an email with the top stories from Guardian Australia every morning}}}\par \par \uc2 Speirs said his views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  were on the public record and he had \u8220\'20\'1Cno intention\u8221\'20\'1D of trying to overturn the new laws, although his position would remain the same if the legislation came back to the parliament.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI very clearly see a place for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in society, but I always think there should be appropriate restrictions on late-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI see that as a reasonably pragmatic position.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COf course, if legislation were to be represented to parliament again, I of course would, on the late-term stuff, I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t change my position. But I have no intention to see the regulations disallowed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Speirs and his Liberal colleagues Nicola Centofanti (the leader in the legislative council), Heidi Girolamo (the shadow finance minister) and Dennis Hood (shadow cabinet secretary) are all listed as speaking at the event.\par \par \uc2 Scriven, Labor\u8217\'20\'19s primary industries minister, is also listed, as is SA Best MLC Frank Pangallo. All those who were in parliament at the time voted against the law change.\par \par \uc2 Family First representatives Tom Kenyon and Deepa Mathew, who are not in parliament, will also speak.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople should be rightly concerned that such high-profile Liberal members of the supposedly new, fresh leadership are pulling out all stops to reverse reproductive rights in this state,\u8221\'20\'1D Franks said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think many Liberal supporters would be shocked \u8230\'20\'26 the week the termination laws come into play, [they\u8217\'20\'19re] actively white-anting that work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 SA\u8217\'20\'19s laws were passed more than a year ago, after lengthy debate, a series of amendments, and a conscience vote.\par \par \uc2 Enid Lyons was married to Joseph Lyons when he became prime minister in 1932. After he died, she ran herself for the Tasmanian seat that is now Braddon and became the first female member of the House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 The Australian Dictionary of Biography notes that \u8220\'20\'1Cshe disapproved of early sex education, deplored homosexuality and promiscuity, opposed divorce, and in 1973 came out fighting against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. Her name has since become associated with a range of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPlease join Enid Lyons List and other key pro-life leaders as we discuss and seek solutions to the critical issues and challenges that confront us as we face the most pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in Australia\u8217\'20\'19s history,\u8221\'20\'1D the event invitation spruiking the parliamentarians reads.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to activate a new generation to rise up and fight for the human rights of the unborn and for greater support and proper health care for their mothers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned 50 years of protection for women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive freedoms, Australian experts said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/27/explainer-abortion-laws-australia-is-it-legal-illegal-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Australia was travelling well}}}\uc2 , but that these are hard fought rights that are easily lost.\par \par \uc2 Guardian Australia has contacted Labor and Enid Lyons List for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220630ei6u002k7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
