\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Europeans are overwhelmingly pro-choice, but that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean women\u8217\'20\'19s rights are safe\b0\par\par\uc2 Anna Grzymala-Busse \par \uc2 981 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 June 2022\par 09:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Roe v Wade was overturned in the US by a court, not by voters. The same happened in Poland \u8211\'20\'13 and it could happen again\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is about to be severely curtailed or cut off for millions of women in the United States following the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision}}}\uc2  to abolish the constitutional protections for the termination of pregnancy established by the landmark Roe v Wade case 50 years ago.\par \par \uc2 The decision allows state legislatures to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and half {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/10/26-states-are-certain-or-likely-ban-abortion-without-roe-heres-which-ones-and-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  are now likely to limit access}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Despite the condemnation from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.eu/article/europe-leaders-decry-us-restriction-abortion-rights-supreme-court/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many European leaders}}}\uc2 , not all EU states have decriminalised \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Malta retains {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2022/jun/22/us-woman-left-traumatised-after-malta-hospital-refuses-life-saving-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a total ban}}}\uc2 . And in Poland, an already restrictive law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/monkey-cage/wp/2016/04/18/why-would-poland-make-its-already-strict-abortion-law-draconian/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was made draconian}}}\uc2  in 2020. Medical personnel now face lengthy prison sentences for providing or procuring an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/world-europe-59206683"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 women have died}}}\uc2  as a result.\par \par \uc2 It should be remembered, however, that in both the US and Poland, courts of law, not democratic majorities, made the decisions. What has happened in the US is the culmination of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/06/21/1106363363/meet-the-man-who-helped-build-the-court-that-may-overturn-roe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 years of efforts}}}\uc2  by US activists to see more socially conservative judges appointed.\par \par \uc2 In Poland, the seismic change in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law also came after a court ruling. The conservative Law and Justice government had in 2016 attempted to push through legislation, but backed down in the face of massive street protests. Instead, it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/us-eu-poland-chronology/chronology-poland-clashes-with-eu-over-judicial-reforms-rule-of-law-idUSKBN1JU25U"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 packed the constitutional tribunal}}}\uc2  and other courts with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/monkey-cage/wp/2018/07/10/poland-may-be-forcibly-retiring-dozens-of-supreme-court-justices/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 its appointees}}}\uc2 . In 2020, the tribunal duly ruled that foetal defects were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/oct/22/poland-rules-abortion-due-to-foetal-defects-unconstitutional"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no longer a justification}}}\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , limiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access to cases of verified rape and incest.\par \par \uc2 This judicial activism is no accident. Democratic majorities in most countries support the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Independent judicial courts are not accountable to majorities, however. As a result, it is the judiciary that can often enact the restrictions that conservatives seek.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/2018/10/29/eastern-and-western-europeans-differ-on-importance-of-religion-views-of-minorities-and-key-social-issues/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Majorities across Europe}}}\uc2  favour \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. This is also the case in the US, where recent polls show more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/fact-sheet/public-opinion-on-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 60% of respondents}}}\uc2  stating that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in most cases. In Poland, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oko.press/66-proc-za-prawem-do-aborcji/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 66% of respondents}}}\uc2  in 2020 said they favoured legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first trimester. Only {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/12/world/europe/poland-abortion-ban.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one in 10 Poles}}}\uc2  backs the 2020 restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Men and women support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2018/12/14/in-the-u-s-and-europe-women-are-about-as-likely-as-men-to-favor-legal-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at very similar rates}}}\uc2 . In the US, support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cuts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/244709/pro-choice-pro-life-2018-demographic-tables.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 across race and income}}}\uc2 . Not surprisingly, younger people are more likely to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  than older voters, and liberal voters are more likely to do so than conservative voters. Religious beliefs play less of role than we might think: the exception being white evangelical Protestants in the US, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/2022/05/06/americas-abortion-quandary/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overwhelmingly oppose}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but only since a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfchronicle.com/opinion/openforum/article/Supreme-Court-Justice-Alito-thinks-the-U-S-has-17162437.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 political shift}}}\uc2  within the Republican party in the 1980s.\par \par \uc2 Voters support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 and so democratic processes, such as parliamentary votes and referendums, generally tend to extend access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In most countries where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal, it is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2022/06/24/global-abortion-laws-roe-wade-courts/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thanks to laws}}}\uc2  passed by democratic parliamentary majorities. In almost all European countries, democratically elected parliaments have gradually established legal support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access with a broad societal consensus. Germany only last week abolished a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/germany-scraps-nazi-era-abortion-law-that-criminalises-doctors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nazi-era \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\uc2  that criminalised doctors after a majority of the Bundestag supported the reform.\par \par \uc2 Referendums have also widened access. In the famous 2018 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum in Ireland, more than 66% of voters supported the repeal of a constitutional \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, with one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thejournal.ie/yes-ireland-votes-to-repeal-eighth-amendment-4034416-May2018/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highest voter turnouts}}}\uc2  recorded in the country. Recent referendums in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/26/san-marino-votes-in-referendum-on-lifting-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 San Marino}}}\uc2  and in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/world-europe-57606228"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gibraltar}}}\uc2  have also increased access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Indeed, it is authoritarian leaders, whether in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2021/07/turkey-takes-centre-stage-in-the-fight-for-womens-rights/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Turkey}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/dec/21/hungary-female-politicians-viktor-orban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hungary}}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/aug/16/decriminalisation-of-domestic-violence-in-russia-leads-to-fall-in-reported-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2 , who have pushed to restrict women\u8217\'20\'19s rights and gender equality.\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups pay close attention to the public mood. This is why they tend to steer the conversation away from majority views or democratic legitimation. They argue that public support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ordoiuris.pl/ochrona-zycia/sztuczne-kreowanie-proaborcyjnych-postaw-opinii-publicznej"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 artificially created}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and have vociferously opposed popular referendums. In 1990s Poland, the Roman Catholic church was already so worried about the result of a referendum that it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://press.princeton.edu/books/hardcover/9780691164755/nations-under-god"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accepted a \u8220\'20\'1Ccompromise\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  solution that made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal in some cases.\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaigners have also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oneofus.eu/about-us/initiative-explanation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 begun using new EU citizens\u8217\'20\'19 rights mechanisms}}}\uc2  to challenge the bloc\u8217\'20\'19s funding of what they call \u8220\'20\'1Clife-destroying\u8221\'20\'1D science and research programmes, rather than pursuing changes in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, which would not fall within the EU\u8217\'20\'19s remit.\par \par \uc2 This is not surprising, since \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents face even more of an uphill climb in Europe than in the US. They command {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/why-abortion-doesnt-resonate-in-european-politics-1490283010"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lower levels of political support}}}\uc2  and have fewer people turning out at their marches. Religious observance in Europe is less common than in the US, and so fewer people anchor their views about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in faith or belief. Most populist parties that have otherwise challenged the mainstream political consensus have left the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not simply available \u8220\'20\'1Con demand\u8221\'20\'1D in most European countries, and access is more limited after the first trimester. These strictures make it more difficult to polarise public opinion, or convincingly argue that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  consists of \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.focusonthefamily.com/pro-life/is-abortion-murder/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 murdering babies}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usccb.org/issues-and-action/human-life-and-dignity/abortion/partial-birth-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismembering children}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D as anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  forces have done in the US. Indeed, the self-proclaimed \u8220\'20\'1Clargest international pro-life\u8221\'20\'1D group in Europe, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hli.eu/about.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Human Life International}}}\uc2 , is based in the US.\par \par \uc2 So how does this bode for opponents of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Europe? Judging by these patterns, they can rely on non-democratic means, whether court challenges or autocratic leaders. But they cannot depend on popular backing or democratic legislative processes. Yet, as the US and Poland both show, determined minorities can still get their way.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Anna Grzymala-Busse is a professor of political science at \uc2 Stanford University\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Do you have an opinion on the issues raised in this article? If you would like to submit a letter of up to 300 words to be considered for publication, email it to us at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:guardian.letters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guardian.letters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220630ei6u001bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
