\par\par \uc2 Global development\par \b \uc2 US woman left traumatised after Malta hospital refuses life-saving  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Megan Clement and Weronika Strzyzynska \par \uc2 858 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2022\par 18:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Desperate\u8217\'20\'19 tourist who fell foul of country\u8217\'20\'19s total ban fears for her life if complications set in while she waits for transfer to UK\par \par \uc2 Doctors have denied an American woman on holiday in Malta a potentially life-saving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite saying her baby had a \u8220\'20\'1Czero chance\u8221\'20\'1D of survival after she was admitted to hospital with severe bleeding in her 16th week of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Despite an \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme risk\u8221\'20\'1D of haemorrhage and infection, doctors at the Mater Dei hospital in Msida told Andrea Prudente that they would not perform a termination because of the country\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/19/the-fight-for-abortion-in-malta"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 total ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Prudente and her husband are seeking a medical transfer from Malta to the UK, which the couple say is their only option due to the risk to her life. They claim medical staff were uncooperative in their attempts to leave and in sharing medical records with the couple\u8217\'20\'19s insurance company.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI just want to get out of here alive,\u8221\'20\'1D Prudente told the Guardian from her hospital room in Malta\u8217\'20\'19s capital, Valletta. \u8220\'20\'1CI couldn\u8217\'20\'19t in my wildest dreams have thought up a nightmare like this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Activists in Malta say the case has alarming echoes of the treatment of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/may/23/ireland-abortion-referendum-savita-father-galway"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Savita Halappanavar, who died of sepsis in an Irish hospital}}}\uc2  in 2012 after doctors refused a request to terminate her pregnancy when she began to miscarry at 17 weeks, due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that was in place in Ireland then.\par \par \uc2 Malta is the only country in the EU to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under any circumstances. The only options for those seeking to end a pregnancy on the island nation are to buy illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication online or seek a termination overseas.\par \par \uc2 Prudente, 38, was on holiday with her partner, Jay Weeldreyer, 45, on the island of Gozo on 12 June when she began bleeding heavily in the night.\par \par \uc2 Doctors in Gozo prescribed her a drug to protect against miscarriage, but two days later when they were back on Malta, the main island, Prudente\u8217\'20\'19s waters broke and she was admitted to St Thomas hospital, where she was told that her placenta had become partially detached.\par \par \uc2 A follow-up ultrasound 48 hours later found there was no amniotic fluid left in her womb, and the couple were told the baby could not survive. They were also told that because of Malta\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, there was nothing doctors could do to end the pregnancy as long as the foetus had a heartbeat.\par \par \uc2 Prudente was transferred to Mater Dei hospital, where she was additionally diagnosed with a ruptured membrane and an umbilical cord that was protruding from her cervix, putting her at even greater risk of haemorrhage and infection. She also tested positive for Covid-19. She is being kept in Covid isolation and receiving antibiotics to ward off infection.\par \par \uc2 Weeldreyer said medical staff came to check for a foetal heartbeat every day.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s an inconceivable form of emotional and psychological torture,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CPart of me still celebrates hearing the heartbeat \u8230\'20\'26 and at the same time, I don\u8217\'20\'19t want that heartbeat there because this is just leading to more suffering for this woman that I love.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lara Dimitrijevic, founder of Malta\u8217\'20\'19s Women\u8217\'20\'19s Rights Foundation and the lawyer representing Prudente, said the hospital only provided medical records after she intervened, which has delayed a transfer to the UK.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt took a day for Andrea to receive her file and we are dealing with an emergency situation,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CEvery minute could lend itself to putting Andrea\u8217\'20\'19s life in danger.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mater Dei hospital confirmed that it had given Prudente access to her file, but did not comment further on the case. No comment was forthcoming from the government or the ministry for health.\par \par \uc2 Prudente said the current advice from Maltese medical staff was for her to leave the hospital and wait at the couple\u8217\'20\'19s hotel for the foetus\u8217\'20\'19s heartbeat to stop or for Prudente to develop an infection, after which they could intervene.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel like I\u8217\'20\'19m being actively traumatised,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The Women\u8217\'20\'19s Rights Foundation filed a judicial protest last week on behalf of 188 women, claiming the Maltese government\u8217\'20\'19s blanket ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  breached their right to health, privacy and equality. The foundation is now preparing to launch a case challenging the constitutional ban.\par \par \uc2 Weeldreyer said the couple had no idea that Malta had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban when they booked the holiday, intended to be a \u8220\'20\'1Cbabymoon\u8221\'20\'1D, where they could spend time on a Mediterranean island before the birth of their first child together.\par \par \uc2 Prudente said she was \u8220\'20\'1Cdesperate\u8221\'20\'1D to get off the island and receive appropriate medical care, but also wanted to raise awareness of the situation in Malta to prevent others suffering in the way that she had.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t want this to happen to more people,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was updated on 29 June 2022 to make clear that no comment on Andrea Prudente\u8217\'20\'19s case was issued by the ministry for health or the government.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220622ei6m001xk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
