\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas sheriff says he \u8216\'20\'18will not persecute\u8217\'20\'19 those seeking an  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Erum Salam \par \uc2 339 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2022\par 20:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 31\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Javier Salazar posted on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  that he would not use his power to \u8216\'20\'18impose the morals\u8217\'20\'19 of others on those \u8216\'20\'18exercising a right\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 A Texas sheriff, whose beat largely includes the city of San Antonio, has declared he would not be pursuing those in his jurisdiction who choose to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the supreme court scrapping of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 In a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post he shared on Tuesday, Bexar county sheriff Javier Salazar wrote of his \u8220\'20\'1Ctwo beautiful and intelligent\u8221\'20\'1D daughters, who he said had a right to choose what to do with their own bodies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs their Dad, I have no control over their adult bodies. As their sheriff, it is absolutely none of my business. I will not persecute Texas women or anyone else pursuing those same rights,\u8221\'20\'1D Salazar stated.\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CShame on the supreme court and the bureaucrats in Washington DC and Austin who are attempting to impose their own supposed morals on others. They will not use my badge or the color of my office to do so. My job is chasing predators, rapists, and human traffickers, not someone exercising a right.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf it\u8217\'20\'19s religion those career politicians would like to enforce, then they should remember that there are many other commandments in scripture that they themselves have very publicly chosen to ignore.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Texas attorney general \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  was quick to react to last week\u8217\'20\'19s ruling to overturn Roe v Wade, which gave people the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The prominent Republican invoked his state\u8217\'20\'19s trigger law, which immediately reverted Texas to outright banning abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnder these pre-Roe statutes, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers could be criminally liable for providing abortions starting today,\u8221\'20\'1D Paxton said.\par \par \uc2 Salazar had one final message for the state\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Ccareer politicians\u8221\'20\'1D in a state that has also borne witness to a terrible recent school shooting. \u8220\'20\'1CIf it\u8217\'20\'19s truly about protecting children, how about starting with the ones in our schools?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220629ei6t001ba\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
