\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Giuliani associate \uc2 Lev Parnas\uc2  handed 20 months in prison for campaign finance fraud \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Adam Gabbatt in New York \par \uc2 3,583 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2022\par 20:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lawyers had sought leniency as Parnas had helped inquiryMixed results for Trump-backed candidates in primariesSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from us today, thanks for reading. Here\u8217\'20\'19s how the day unfolded in Washington:\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 \uc2 Lev Parnas\uc2 , an associate of \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  and a key figure in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s first impeachment investigation, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/29/supreme-court-decisions-epa-trump-immigration-primary-elections-latest#:~:text=From%202h%20ago-,13.41,-Giuliani%20associate%20sentenced"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sentenced}}}\uc2  to a year and eight months in prison for fraud and campaign finance crimes. Parnas used the riches of a wealthy Russian to make illegal donations to politicians who might aid the launch of a legal recreational-marijuana business.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Trump-backed candidates had a mixed Tuesday in Republican primary elections around the country. Colorado voters largely rejected most Trump-supporting candidates in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s GOP primaries, although \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2 , the extremist Colorado Republican congresswoman, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/29/republican-lauren-boebert-wins-colorado-primary-church-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won}}}\uc2  her bid for re-election. Moderate Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/29/supreme-court-decisions-epa-trump-immigration-primary-elections-latest?page=with:block-62bc5f0e8f08918da77e7ed1#block-62bc5f0e8f08918da77e7ed1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held off }}}\uc2  challenges from more extreme challengers in Utah, Mississippi and Oklahoma, but two Trump-endorsed officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcchicago.com/news/local/chicago-politics/illinois-primary-election-results-republican-darren-bailey-to-face-jb-pritzker-in-race-for-illinois-governor-in-november/2869100/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 triumphed}}}\uc2  in Illinois.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22The Supreme Court will issue two key decisions tomorrow which could impact both the climate crisis and immigration. The court has been weighing how much power the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  should have to regulate greenhouse gas emissions from power plants, and is also considering whether {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  can end Remain in Mexico, the controversial Trump-era policy which sends asylum seekers to Mexico while they wait for their immigration cases to be heard.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2 , the Supreme Court justice, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/29/supreme-court-decisions-epa-trump-immigration-primary-elections-latest?page=with:block-62bc7b2e8f0898ef443a4504#block-62bc7b2e8f0898ef443a4504"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 formally announced}}}\uc2  his retirement from the court, effective Thursday. Breyer, had announced earlier this year that he would retire and will be replaced by \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2 , who was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/07/ketanji-brown-jackson-confirmation-us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed}}}\uc2  to the Supreme Court in April. Brown Jackson will be sworn in as a Supreme Court justice on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , the Texas Attorney General, said he would be \u8220\'20\'1Cwilling and able\u8221\'20\'1D to defend a law which banned sodomy, in the wake of the Supreme Court overturning Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsnationnow.com/on-balance-with-leland-vittert/texas-ag-vows-to-enforce-abortion-laws-with-roe-overturned/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with News Nation}}}\uc2 , Paxton was asked about Lawrence v Texas, a 2003 Supreme Court ruling that overturned a state anti-sodomy law and made all such laws invalid nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Last week \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , in a concurring opinion following the Supreme Court overturning the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.yahoo.com/entertainment/justice-thomas-says-supreme-court-143557082.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  that the court should also \u8220\'20\'1Creconsider\u8221\'20\'1D the Lawrence v Texas ruling.\par \par \uc2 In the News Nation Paxton was asked if he would \u8220\'20\'1Cfeel comfortable defending a law that once again outlawed sodomy,\u8221\'20\'1D as well as gay marriage and birth control.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI mean, there\u8217\'20\'19s all kinds of issues here, but certainly, the Supreme Court has stepped into issues that I don\u8217\'20\'19t think there was any constitutional issues dealing with, they were legislative issues,\u8221\'20\'1D Paxton said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis [\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] is one of those issues, and there may be more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The News Nation host then asked Paxton how he would act if Texas passed a law banning sodomy.\par \par \uc2 Paxton said: \u8220\'20\'1CMy job is to defend state law and I\u8217\'20\'19ll continue to do that. That is my job under the Constitution and I\u8217\'20\'19m certainly willing and able to do that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has announced that the US will increase its military forces across Europe with more land, sea and air deployments, as he gathered with \uc2 Nato\uc2  leaders for a two-day summit in response to Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Arriving at the meeting in Madrid, the US president announced the stationing of a brigade of 3,000 combat troops in Romania, two squadrons of F-35 fighters in the UK and two navy destroyers in Spain.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe US and its allies are going to step up. We\u8217\'20\'19re stepping up. We\u8217\'20\'19re proving that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/nato"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nato}}}\uc2  is more needed now than it ever has been,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a short statement he read out before the first summit meeting began.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s announcement is expected to be followed by further commitments by \uc2 Nato\uc2  members to a strengthening of forces on the alliance\u8217\'20\'19s eastern flank, which was being discussed by \uc2 Nato\uc2  leaders on Wednesday morning.\par \par \uc2 The US president also said the US fifth army corps would establish a permanent base in Poland, extra troops would be committed to the Baltic states and extra air defence systems would be stationed in Germany and Italy.\par \par \uc2 It was, Biden said, a response to Russian aggression, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CTogether with our allies, we are going make sure \uc2 Nato\uc2  is ready to meet threats across every domain, land, air and in the sea\u8221\'20\'1D, which came \u8220\'20\'1Cat a moment when Putin has shattered peace in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/europe-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Europe}}}\uc2  and the very tenets of rules-based order\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The US sent a further 20,000 troops to Europe earlier this year, taking the total based across the continent to over 100,000. Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s announcements come on top of that and Biden said the US would \u8220\'20\'1Ccontinue to our adjust our posture\u8221\'20\'1D if necessary.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 A lawyer for Ginni Thomas, the wife of the supreme court justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/clarence-thomas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clarence Thomas}}}\uc2 , has dimmed prospects for a quick appearance before congressional investigators probing the January 6 Capitol riot, after the attorney asked for more information on her requested appearance.\par \par \uc2 Ginni Thomas on June 16 expressed eagerness to speak with the House of Representatives panel investigating the 2021 assault, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dailycaller.com/2022/06/16/ginni-thomas-talk-testify-january-6-committee-clear-up-thompson-eastman/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 telling the Daily Caller}}}\uc2  she \u8220\'20\'1Ccan\u8217\'20\'19t wait to clear up misconceptions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The committee sent an invitation that day.\par \par \uc2 Ginni Thomas, with her husband, \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 . Photograph: Erin Scott/Reuters\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, however, Thomas\u8217\'20\'19 lawyer, Mark R. Paoletta, wrote to the committee that he did not \u8220\'20\'1Cunderstand the need to speak with Mrs Thomas\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBefore I can recommend that she meet with you, I am asking the Committee to provide a better justification for why Mrs Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s testimony is relevant to the Committee\u8217\'20\'19s legislative purpose,\u8221\'20\'1D Paoletta wrote.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month the \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2022/06/10/ginni-thomas-election-arizona-lawmakers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that Thomas emailed 29 Arizona lawmakers in a bid to help overturn Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election defeat.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Giuliani associate sentenced to prison over campaign finance fraud\par \par \uc2 Lev Parnas\uc2 , an associate of \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  who was a figure in President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s first impeachment investigation, was sentenced Wednesday to a year and eight months in prison for fraud and campaign finance crimes.\par \par \uc2 Parnas, who had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jan/16/lev-parnas-who-is-he-trump-ukraine-rudy-giuliani-aid-scandal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 helped Giuliani connect with Ukrainian figures}}}\uc2  as part of a campaign to dig up dirt on President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s son, had sought leniency on the grounds that he\u8217\'20\'19d helped the Congressional probe, Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 But prosecutors said the Soviet-born businessman\u8217\'20\'19s aid was in response to a subpoena and deserved little credit.\par \par \uc2 Instead, they asked the judge to focus on a jury\u8217\'20\'19s finding that Parnas used the riches of a wealthy Russian to make illegal donations to politicians who might aid the launch of a legal recreational-marijuana business.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors had asked that Parnas be sentenced to more than six years.\par \par \uc2 An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/22/lev-parnas-former-associate-rudy-giuliani-convicted-illegal-campaign-contributions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October conviction}}}\uc2  also supported a finding that he made illegal donations in 2018 to jump-start a new energy company.\par \par \uc2 Lev Parnas\uc2  outside court on Wednesday. Photograph: Yuki Iwamura/AP\par \par \uc2 In March, Parnas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/lev-parnas-an-ex-giuliani-associate-plead-guilty-conspiracy-charge-2022-03-10/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded guilty}}}\uc2  to conspiring to commit wire fraud, admitting that between 2012 and 2019 he conspired with another person to give investors false information about a Florida-based business, Fraud Guarantee.\par \par \uc2 Fraud Guarantee was promoted as a company that could protect investors against fraud. Giuliani accepted $500,000 from the company to act as a consultant, but was not accused of wrongdoing or charged with any crimes.\par \par \uc2 The criminal case against Parnas was not directly related to his work acting as a fixer for Giuliani as the former New York City mayor tried to get Ukrainian officials to investigate Biden\u8217\'20\'19s son, Hunter, before he was elected president.\par \par \uc2 Giuliani, who was working at the time as a personal lawyer for then-President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has said he knew nothing about the crimes of Parnas and others.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 It was a mixed Tuesday for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 -backed candidates in Republican primary elections around the country. Colorado voters largely rejected most Trump-supporting candidates in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s GOP primaries, although \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2 , the extremist Colorado Republican congresswoman, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/29/republican-lauren-boebert-wins-colorado-primary-church-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won}}}\uc2  her bid for relection.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 In Illinois, Mary Miller, who had been criticized after she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/06/26/mary-miller-white-life-trump-rally/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared}}}\uc2  the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision as a \u8220\'20\'1Cvictory for white life\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a spokesman said she had mixed up her words \u8211\'20\'13 won in after she was backed by Trump. Darren Bailey, who was also endorsed by Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcchicago.com/news/local/chicago-politics/illinois-primary-election-results-republican-darren-bailey-to-face-jb-pritzker-in-race-for-illinois-governor-in-november/2869100/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won }}}\uc2  the Republican gubernatorial primary in the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Elsewhere John Curtis, and Blake Moore, Republican congressional candidates in Utah, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ksltv.com/497566/ap-all-4-utah-house-incumbents-win-gop-primaries/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defeated more extreme challengers}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Stephanie Bice\uc2 , a congresswoman from Oklahoma who \u8211\'20\'13 like Moore and Curtis \u8211\'20\'13 voted to form the January 6 commission, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/huddle/2022/06/29/trio-of-incumbents-toppled-00043101"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won her primary bid}}}\uc2 , as did Michael Guest, in Mississippi.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 The supreme court is now due to issue two key decisions, on the climate and immigration, on Thursday. The court has been weighing how much power the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  should have to regulate greenhouse gas emissions from power plants, and is also considering whether \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  can end Remain in Mexico, the controversial Trump-era policy which sends asylum seekers to Mexico while they wait for their immigration cases to be heard.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2 , the Supreme Court justice, has formally announced his retirement from the Court, effective Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2 . Photograph: Reuters\par \par \uc2 Breyer, who announced earlier this year that he would retire \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2  has already been chosen to replace him \u8211\'20\'13 wrote to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to confirm he would step down tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis past January, I wrote to inform you of my intent to retire from regular active service as an Associate Justice of the \uc2 Supreme Court of the United States\uc2 , upon the Court rising for its summer recess,\u8221\'20\'1D Breyer wrote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Court has announced that tomorrow, beginning at 10 am, it will hand down all remaining opinions ready during this Term. Accordingly, my retirement from active service under the provisions of 28 U.S.C. \u167\'00\'A7 371(b) will be effective on Thursday, June 30, 2022, at noon.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt has been my great honor to participate as a judge in the effort to maintain our Constitution and the Rule of Law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/07/ketanj-brown-jackson-confirmation-vote-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18So much joy\u8217\'20\'19: Ketanji Brown Jackson\u8217\'20\'19s confirmation lauded as ray of hope}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 The extremist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/colorado"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Colorado}}}\uc2  Republican congresswoman \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  won her primary on Tuesday night, shortly after attacking the separation of church and state under the US constitution.\par \par \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2 . Photograph: \uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m tired of this separation of church and state junk,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 A dedicated controversialist first elected in 2020, backed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2022-election/lauren-boebert-wins-colorado-primary-rcna35574"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 described by NBC News}}}\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1CMaga lightning rod\u8221\'20\'1D, Boebert convincingly beat Don Coram, a state senator, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/27/lauren-boebert-extreme-rightwing-colorado-reelect-primary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for the nomination}}}\uc2  to contest the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 At one event recently Coram, 74, told voters: \u8220\'20\'1CMy politics are very similar to my driving. To the chagrin of both my wife and my Republican colleagues, I tend to crowd the center line and sometimes I veer over a bit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In contrast, Boebert has heckled \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  during the state of the union address; made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/27/ilhan-omar-lauren-boebert-bigotry-republicans-trump-pelosi-mccarthy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 racist attacks}}}\uc2  on \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2 , a Democrat from Minnesota; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/05/republican-lauren-boebert-gun-congress-washington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vowed}}}\uc2  to carry a gun {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cpr.org/2021/01/12/boebert-clashes-with-capitol-police-after-setting-off-metal-detectors/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on to the House floor}}}\uc2  ; and voted to object to results in swing states in the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Boebert {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/06/28/us/elections/results-colorado-us-house-district-3.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 beat Coram}}}\uc2  by 31 points.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/29/republican-lauren-boebert-wins-colorado-primary-church-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican Lauren Boebert wins in Colorado after denouncing separation of church and state}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fox News Channel is airing the January 6 committee hearings when they occur in daytime hours \u8211\'20\'13 and a striking number of the network\u8217\'20\'19s viewers have made clear they\u8217\'20\'19d rather be doing something else, according to Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 During two daytime hearings last week, Fox averaged 727,000 viewers, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nielsen.com/us/en/solutions/measurement/television/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nielsen company}}}\uc2  said. That compares to the 3.09 million who watched the hearings on MSNBC and the 2.21 million tuned in to CNN.\par \par \uc2 It completely flips the typical viewing pattern for the news networks. During weekdays when the hearings are not taking place, Fox News routinely has more viewers than the other two networks combined, Nielsen said.\par \par \uc2 Last Thursday, Fox had 1.33 million viewers for the 2 pm Eastern hour before the hearing started \u8211\'20\'13 slightly below its second quarter average, but on par for early summer, when fewer people are watching TV.\par \par \uc2 After the hearing started, Fox\u8217\'20\'19s audience\u8217\'20\'19s sank to 747,000 for the 3 pm Eastern hour and even lower, to 718,000, at 4 pm. Fox cut away from the hearing at 5 pm to show its popular panel program, \u8220\'20\'1CThe Five,\u8221\'20\'1D and fans immediately rewarded them: viewership shot up to 2.76 million people, Nielsen said.\par \par \uc2 The apparent lack of interest explains why the Trump-friendly network {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2022/jun/09/us-capitol-attack-hearings-fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stuck with its regular lineup during the committee\u8217\'20\'19s only prime-time hearing}}}\uc2 , while ABC, \uc2 CBS\uc2 , NBC, CNN and MSNBC all showed the Washington proceedings.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Presidential historian Michael Beschloss made a joke at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s expense, in the aftermath of Cassidy Hutchinson \u8217\'20\'19s explosive testimony before the January 6 committee yesterday.\par \par \uc2 This morning, Beschloss shared a photo to \uc2 Twitter\uc2  of the last meal that Richard Nixon ate at the White House before he resigned as president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNixon\u8217\'20\'19s last lunch at White House, 1974,\u8221\'20\'1D Beschloss said of the photo. \u8220\'20\'1CRecord shows that although he was leaving Presidency against his will, he did not throw this plate at the wall.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrNixon\u8217\'20\'19s last lunch at White House, 1974. Record shows that although he was leaving Presidency against his will, he did not throw this plate at the wall. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/joCuuCsTcg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/joCuuCsTcg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Michael Beschloss (@BeschlossDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BeschlossDC/status/1542162552171515905?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 29, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 That appeared to be a tongue-in-cheek reference to Hutchinson\u8217\'20\'19s claim that Trump had a habit of throwing food when he was angry.\par \par \uc2 That habit reared its head in December 2020, when the AP published an interview with then-attorney general \uc2 William Barr\uc2 , who said there was no evidence of widespread fraud in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 According to Hutchinson, she walked into the White House dining room that day to see a valet cleaning up a dirty tablecloth. She noticed ketchup dripping down the wall where a television was mounted, and a porcelain plate lay shattered on the floor.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether Trump often engaged in such behavior, Hutchinson said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere were several times throughout my tenure with the chief of staff that I was aware of him either throwing dishes or flipping the tablecloth to let all the contents of the table go onto the floor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York City is suing five companies it says are involved in the sale of illegal, largely untraceable \u8220\'20\'1Cghost guns\u8221\'20\'1D flowing into the city, Reuters reports:\par \par \uc2 In a complaint filed in Manhattan federal court on Wednesday, New York attorneys said the companies have created a public nuisance by selling \u8220\'20\'1Cunfinished\u8221\'20\'1D firearms components that purchasers can build into guns, without undergoing background checks.\par \par \uc2 The result is \u8220\'20\'1Ca proliferation of unserialized, untraceable, unlawful ghost guns in the city\u8217\'20\'19s streets and homes, making the City more dangerous for both the public and for law enforcement, causing a quintessential public nuisance,\u8221\'20\'1D the complaint said.\par \par \uc2 Arm or Ally LLC, Rainier Arms LLC, 80P Builder, Rock Slide USA LLC and Indie Guns LLC were named as defendants The companies did not immediately respond to requests from Reuters for comment.\par \par \uc2 New York City wants the defendants to stop selling ghost gun components and provide records of sales into the city over the last five years. City officials said this month that gun arrests are at a 28-year high.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican primaries\par \par \uc2 Colorado voters rejected most Trump-supporting candidates in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s GOP primaries, and they weren\u8217\'20\'19t the only ones.\par \par \uc2 In Utah Blake Moore, a first-term US congressman who voted for an independent commission to investigate the January 6 insurrection, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ksltv.com/497566/ap-all-4-utah-house-incumbents-win-gop-primaries/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defeated his more extreme challengers}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 John Curtis, a moderate Republican, also defeated a primary opponent from the right.\par \par \uc2 Stephanie Bice\uc2 , a congresswoman Oklahoma from who \u8211\'20\'13 like Moore and Curtis \u8211\'20\'13 voted to form the January 6 commission, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/huddle/2022/06/29/trio-of-incumbents-toppled-00043101"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won her primary bid}}}\uc2 , as did Michael Guest, in Mississippi.\par \par \uc2 Tina Peters, who became nationally known after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.denverpost.com/2022/03/09/tina-peters-grand-jury-indictment-election-breach-allegations-belinda-knisley/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 being indicted}}}\uc2  for her role in a break-in of her own county election system, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterms-colorado-secretary-state-269974d305ef9565af38009cb4237d4a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost her bid}}}\uc2  for the GOP nomination for Colorado secretary of state.\par \par \uc2 Still, there were some victories for Trump.\par \par \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2 , the extremist Colorado Republican congresswoman, who has been backed by Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/29/republican-lauren-boebert-wins-colorado-primary-church-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won}}}\uc2  her bid for relection, days after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.denverpost.com/2022/06/27/lauren-boebert-church-state-colorado/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denouncing}}}\uc2  separation of church and state.\par \par \uc2 Mary Miller, who had been criticized after she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/06/26/mary-miller-white-life-trump-rally/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared}}}\uc2  the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision as a \u8220\'20\'1Cvictory for white life\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a spokesman said she had mixed up her words \u8211\'20\'13 won in Illinois after she was backed by Trump. Darren Bailey, who was also endorsed by Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcchicago.com/news/local/chicago-politics/illinois-primary-election-results-republican-darren-bailey-to-face-jb-pritzker-in-race-for-illinois-governor-in-november/2869100/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won }}}\uc2  the Republican gubernatorial primary in the state.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Andrew Giuliani\uc2 , the anti-vax, Trumpite son of \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , lost his bid to be governor of New York on Tuesday night.\par \par \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2 , a US congressman who, like the younger Giuliani, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/06/28/zeldin-gop-primary-new-york-governor-00043015"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supported Donald Trump}}}\uc2 , defeated his opponent by 19 points, bringing to an end a chaotic, firebrand campaign by Giuliani that failed to catch on with New Yorkers.\par \par \uc2 One of Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s final campaign events was marked by his father {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/realrudygiuliani/videos/360709459467389"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claiming}}}\uc2  a supermarket employee had assaulted him during a campaign event.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/rudy-giuliani-says-supermarket-employee-accused-slapping-prosecuted-rcna35438"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Video footage}}}\uc2  showed a man patting \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  on the back. Giuliani Sr said he could have been killed. Eric Adams, New York City\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, has suggested Giuliani, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s on-again, off-again friend/lawyer/advisor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/28/nyregion/rudy-giuliani-eric-adams-investigation-ny.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 should be prosecuted}}}\uc2  for falsely reporting a crime.\par \par \uc2 enltrWhat \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  says happened at ShopRite vs. what actually happened {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZQ1Qwi1HC0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZQ1Qwi1HC0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1541441207448096768?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Colorado rejected two prominent candidates whose political profiles were centered on election falsehoods, in a fresh reminder that fealty to former President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/hub/donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  lies about mass voter fraud is no guarantee of success with conservative voters, Associated Press reports:\par \par \uc2 Tina Peters, the Mesa County clerk who became nationally known after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.denverpost.com/2022/03/09/tina-peters-grand-jury-indictment-election-breach-allegations-belinda-knisley/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 being indicted}}}\uc2  for her role in a break-in of her own county election system, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterms-colorado-secretary-state-269974d305ef9565af38009cb4237d4a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost her bid}}}\uc2  for the GOP nomination for Colorado secretary of state. Instead, Republicans selected Pam Anderson, a critic of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election lies and a former clerk in suburban Denver who is well-regarded among election professionals. She is now positioned to challenge Democratic Secretary of State \uc2 Jena Griswold\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will continue my fight for restoring the confidence of Colorado voters against lies and the politicians or interest groups that seek to weaponize elections administration for political advantage,\u8221\'20\'1D Anderson said after her victory.\par \par \uc2 One of Peters\u8217\'20\'19 top Colorado allies, state Rep Ron Hanks, lost his bid for the party\u8217\'20\'19s Senate nomination to Joe O\u8217\'20\'19Dea, a businessman who has repeatedly acknowledged that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  legitimately won the 2020 election. That was a sharp contrast with Hanks, who attended the January 6 rally in Washington, doesn\u8217\'20\'19t believe Biden is a legitimate president and says he discovered a new, animating purpose fighting election fraud after 2020.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Hello and welcome to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s live coverage of the day\u8217\'20\'19s political news. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19re monitoring today:\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22The Supreme Court is expected to give decisions today which could have lasting effects on how the US handles the climate crisis. The court has been weighing how much power the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  should have to regulate greenhouse gas emissions from power plants.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22Remain in Mexico, the controversial Trump-era policy which sends asylum seekers to Mexico while they wait for their immigration cases to be heard, is also on the table. The Supreme Court is due to decide whether \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  can end the program, which has kept {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wane.com/border-report-tour/migrants-await-supreme-court-ruling-on-remain-in-mexico-program/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thousands}}}\uc2  of would-be immigrants in sometimes dangerous conditions across the US border.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22After the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/29/january-6-donald-trump-mark-meadows-rudy-giuliani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bombshell testimony}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  directed his supporters to march on the Capitol, despite knowing many of them were armed, the Secret Service has begun to push back. Numerous outlets have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/secret-service-jan-6-committee-trump-cassidy-hutchinson-testimony/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that members of the Secret Service are willing to testify that elements of the testimony by Cassidy Hutchinson, an aide to the then White House chief of staff, are inaccurate.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22Away from Washington, Trump-aligned candidates had mixed results in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s primary elections. Mary Miller, who had been criticized after she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/06/26/mary-miller-white-life-trump-rally/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared}}}\uc2  the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision as a \u8220\'20\'1Cvictory for white life\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a spokesman said she had mixed up her words \u8211\'20\'13 won in Illinois, where Darren Bailey also won the Republican gubernatorial primary. But other Trumpist hopefuls {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/06/29/trump-bad-day-hearing-room-good-one-trail/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost}}}\uc2  in Colorado.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220629ei6t001xj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
