\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Leak of Dobbs opinion brought deluge of online searches for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pills, study finds\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 639 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2022\par 15:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Study author suggests public health information should appear prominently in search results\par \par \uc2 Internet searches for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication hit an all-time high in the days after a leaked draft opinion showed the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  was on the verge of overturning Roe v Wade \u8211\'20\'13 a decision the court finalized last week.\par \par \uc2 Increased \uc2 Google\uc2  search volume \u8211\'20\'13 162% more than would have been expected \u8211\'20\'13 was especially pronounced in states hostile to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to a study published in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jamainternalmedicine/fullarticle/10.1001/jamainternmed.2022.2998?guestAccessKey=103c2a31-2c71-4b9a-ab17-d00959290a1b&utm_source=For_The_Media&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=ftm_links&utm_content=tfl&utm_term=062922"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  JAMA Internal Medicine}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a trend the authors said showed how important engaging online is as states quickly move to restrict or ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople ain\u8217\'20\'19t gonna talk about this out in the open and publicly,\u8221\'20\'1D said John Ayers, an adjunct associate professor with the division of infectious diseases and global public health at the \uc2 University of California, San Diego\uc2 , and an author of the study.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we turn to internet searches, we can know what they\u8217\'20\'19re thinking based on the timing and content of their query,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ayers, adding that searches are often predictive of behavior.\par \par \uc2 The new research analyzed searches for the terms \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill\u8221\'20\'1D or specific medications, such as mifepristone (or the brand name Mifeprix) and misoprostol (or Cytotec), originating in the US and specific states from January 2004 to May 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow that we know people are searching, how do we move those searches?,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ayers. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat are we doing to meet those hundreds of thousands, and over the course of weeks and months, millions of women \u8211\'20\'13 to meet their needs?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ayers said search engines should consider creating specialized warnings or boxes for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication in the same way they do for other topics prone to harmful information \u8211\'20\'13 such as Covid-19 or suicide. Doing so could help prevent people from undertaking potentially harmful self-managed abortions.\par \par \uc2 The study closely follows a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seismic ruling from the US supreme court}}}\uc2 , in which the conservative supermajority overturned the landmark 1973 decision in Roe v Wade and found there is no constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The decision left states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/jun/28/tracking-where-abortion-laws-stand-in-every-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 free to regulate the procedure}}}\uc2  as they see fit. That has led {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/25/abortion-banned-in-multiple-us-states-just-hours-after-roe-v-wade-overturned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eight states}}}\uc2  to banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  immediately and almost entirely, including several without exception for rape and incest. Experts predict as many as 26 states in total are certain or likely to seek to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ayers said both the court\u8217\'20\'19s recent decision and forthcoming news about states banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 changes likely to take place over the coming weeks and months \u8211\'20\'13 will probably further drive search traffic. He said public health experts should view that as an opportunity, and push for evidence-based information to appear in search results.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe need has always been among us, people have been searching for this historically, and there will be episodic increases in demand,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ayers. The previous peak in internet searches for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication was in September 2021, when Texas successfully banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at six weeks.\par \par \uc2 Technology companies have quickly become a focus of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate as policies change rapidly across the United States.\par \par \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , both owned by the company \uc2 Meta\uc2 , have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/06/28/1108107718/instagram-and-facebook-begin-removing-posts-offering-abortion-pills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized for removing posts}}}\uc2  that offered to mail \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication to women in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is illegal.\par \par \uc2 Privacy advocates have warned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/29/us-abortion-supreme-court-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 internet searches and other mobile phone data}}}\uc2  could be used against women by zealous police and prosecutors. Further, users of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/28/why-us-woman-are-deleting-their-period-tracking-apps"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 period tracking apps}}}\uc2  have begun to delete software as some worry the data could be used against them.\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s more, \uc2 Google\uc2  has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/09/google-searches-abortion-clinics-pregnancy-crisis-centers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 harshly criticized in the past}}}\uc2  for the way it has regulated searches for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Often, searches for nearby \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics populated results with crisis pregnancy centers, which oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and advertise online in ways some advocates and women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/25/nyregion/crisis-pregnancy-centers-abortion-nyc.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said was deceptive}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220629ei6t002be\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
