\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 TechScape: Can US women trust big tech with their data after Roe v Wade?\b0\par\par\uc2 Alex Hern \par \uc2 967 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2022\par 11:09 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In this week\u8217\'20\'19s newsletter: Calls to delete period tracking apps have gone viral in America \u8211\'20\'13 but the likes of \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Apple\uc2  have questions to answer on user privacy tooDon\u8217\'20\'19t get TechScape delivered to your inbox? Sign up for the full article here\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , the landmark 1973 decision which held that access to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a constitutionally guaranteed right. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/jun/24/what-states-have-abortion-trigger-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 13 states}}}\uc2  with \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger laws\u8221\'20\'1D, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was immediately \u8211\'20\'13 or will imminently be \u8211\'20\'13 outlawed. Others may follow.\par \par \uc2 As Americans grapple with the reality of the repeal, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://foreignpolicy.com/2022/06/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-global-abortion-laws/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of just 11 countries around the world}}}\uc2  to have restricted access in the last three decades, the initial focus has been on how to continue to provide access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and how to guarantee the safety of women.\par \par \uc2 In the moments after the decision was handed down, calls to delete period tracking apps {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jkbibliophile/status/1540345161955385345"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 went}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/doree/status/1540474162262982656"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 viral}}}\uc2 , with users concerned that the data they collect may end up incriminating women; some companies took public stands, committing themselves to defending their users. \u8220\'20\'1CAt this fraught moment, we hear the anger and the anxiety coming from our US community,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://helloclue.com/articles/abortion/clue-s-response-to-roe-vs-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 period tracking app Clue said}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe remain committed to protecting your reproductive health data.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the questions around personal data go far further than the narrow focus on reproductive health apps could suggest. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/25/tech-companies-health-data-security-abortion-prosecution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 From our story by Kari Paul}}}\uc2  :\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and civil rights advocates have warned that there are few federal regulations on what information is collected and retained by tech firms, making it easy for law enforcement officials to access incriminating data on location, internet searches and communication history.\par \par \uc2 Such data has already been used to prosecute people for miscarriages and pregnancy termination in states with strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, including one case in which a woman\u8217\'20\'19s online search for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills was brought against her in court.\par \par \uc2 Digital rights advocacy group the \uc2 Electronic Frontier Foundation (EFF) \uc2 has advised companies in the tech world to pre-emptively prepare for a future in which they are served with subpoenas and warrants seeking user data to prosecute \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  seekers and providers.\par \par \uc2 It recommends companies allow pseudonymous or anonymous access, stop behavioural tracking, and retain as little data as possible. It also advocated for end-to-end encryption by default and refrain from collecting any location information.\par \par \uc2 The ruling has also highlighted the general lack of privacy protections in US law. The connection is more than just tangential: the decision in Roe v Wade is based on the right to privacy, which the supreme court held to be provided by the 14th amendment to the US constitution. That right was first affirmed in an earlier decision, Griswold v Connecticut, which protected a married couple\u8217\'20\'19s rights to contraception; supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  stated, in his concurrence overturning Roe, that that decision should also be re-examined.\par \par \uc2 In Clue\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to protecting its users\u8217\'20\'19 privacy, the company highlighted that, as a Berlin-based organisation, its users are protected by GDPR. \u8220\'20\'1CAs a European company, Clue is obligated under the world\u8217\'20\'19s strictest data privacy law, the European GDPR, to apply special protections to such health data,\u8221\'20\'1D the company said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf we hold your data, our obligation under European law to protect your privately tracked data is the same. No US Court or other authority can override that, since we are not based in the US. Our user data cannot simply be subpoenaed from the US.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 American privacy experts caution that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/10/us-immigration-agency-ice-domestic-surveillance-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cdragnet\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  style surveillance of women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive health, with authorities demanding companies hand over entire databases, is unlikely to occur. Legal pressure could be put on such companies to pro-actively report users, however, and in the meantime the focus should instead be on protecting individual women who have been targeted for investigation. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/25/tech-companies-health-data-security-abortion-prosecution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 From Kari\u8217\'20\'19s article}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Experts are also encouraging individuals seeking abortions to use heightened data security practices, including encrypted communications and disabling location tracking. The Roe decision has highlighted a longstanding privacy crisis affecting users of the most commonly used tech services, said\par \par \uc2 Imran Ahmed, chief executive officer of advocacy group the Center for Countering Digital Hate\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The response of major tech companies to the ruling has been complicated. As a first priority, many have focused inward, announcing policies to protect their own employees. \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 , for instance, have all confirmed they will cover travel expenses for employees who need to leave their home state to access \u8220\'20\'1Clawful medical services where access to care is limited in availability\u8221\'20\'1D, in the words of \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s policy.\par \par \uc2 But major companies have been less forthcoming about their promises to their users. \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , \uc2 Uber\uc2 , \uc2 Apple\uc2  and \uc2 Google\uc2  all failed to respond to queries about how they would handle sensitive data and respond to law enforcement requests in the future.\par \par \uc2 With Texas one of the 13 states with \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger laws\u8221\'20\'1D on the books, the case has also raised questions about the state\u8217\'20\'19s ability to tempt companies to relocate from Silicon Valley. Austin, a leftwing stronghold and the state capital, has been developing a burnishing reputation as a tech hub, and car company \uc2 Tesla\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 owned by \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 moved its headquarters there late last year. \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , Musk\u8217\'20\'19s other company, has a launch facility on the Texas coast.\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  is one of the companies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tesla.com/ns_videos/2021-tesla-impact-report.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promising to cover}}}\uc2  employees for \u8220\'20\'1Chealthcare services that are unavailable in their home state\u8221\'20\'1D. Musk himself has been silent on the ruling, though his \u8220\'20\'1Cpinned tweet\u8221\'20\'1D from 24 May is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/elonmusk/status/1529097667858546689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a screenshot of a Wall Street Journal chart}}}\uc2  showing the declining American birthrate.\par \par \uc2 If you want to read the complete version of the newsletter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/ng-interactive/2021/jun/25/techscape-sign-up"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 please subscribe}}}\uc2  to receive TechScape in your inbox every Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220629ei6t001jo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
