\par\par \uc2 Australia news\par \b \uc2 Victoria names new ministers; \uc2 Penny Wong\uc2  to travel to south-east Asia \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Josh Taylor and Tory Shepherd (earlier) \par \uc2 6,388 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 June 2022\par 01:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Jacinta Allan\uc2  appointed Victoria\u8217\'20\'19s new deputy premier ; Australia records at least 56 Covid deaths and \uc2 Penny Wong\uc2  to travel to Vietnam and Malaysia. This blog is now closedDaniel Andrews names \uc2 Jacinta Allan\uc2  as Victoria\u8217\'20\'19s deputy premierFactions, new blood and \uc2 Jeff Kennett\uc2 : \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 dilemmaJohn Barilaro\u8217\'20\'19s bite of the Big \uc2 Apple\uc2 : the plum posting that set off a firestormVoters have sent \uc2 Peter Dutton\uc2  a clear message; he would be silly to miss the cueGet our free news app ; get our morning email briefing\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.30am BST\par \par \uc2 What we learned today, Saturday 25 June\par \par \uc2 We are wrapping up the blog for now. Thanks for following today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what made the news today:\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2022/jun/25/australia-news-live-updates-us-reacts-to-supreme-court-abortion-ruling-crossbench-anger-as-albanese-cuts-staffing-numbers?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62b661228f0814a0d5d42cfd#block-62b661228f0814a0d5d42cfd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Victorian Labor caucus appointed Jacinta Allan}}}\uc2  as the state\u8217\'20\'19s new deputy premier, with \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2  to announce his new ministry in the next day.\par \par \uc2 * The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2022/jun/25/australia-news-live-updates-us-reacts-to-supreme-court-abortion-ruling-crossbench-anger-as-albanese-cuts-staffing-numbers?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62b66eb78f0814a0d5d42d2c#block-62b66eb78f0814a0d5d42d2c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 foreign minister, Penny Wong}}}\uc2 , announced she will travel to Vietnam and Malaysia this week.\par \par \uc2 * There were at least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2022/jun/25/australia-news-live-updates-us-reacts-to-supreme-court-abortion-ruling-crossbench-anger-as-albanese-cuts-staffing-numbers?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62b6a5c88f0814a0d5d42def#block-62b6a5c88f0814a0d5d42def"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 56 Covid-19 deaths}}}\uc2  reported across Australia.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2022/jun/25/australia-news-live-updates-us-reacts-to-supreme-court-abortion-ruling-crossbench-anger-as-albanese-cuts-staffing-numbers?page=with:block-62b6a0c98f0875bb61abb5b6#block-62b6a0c98f0875bb61abb5b6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Victorian health officials}}}\uc2  expect the Omicron BA.4/BA.5 strain of Covid-19 to become the dominant strain in the next few weeks, leading to more cases, reinfections and hospitalisations.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2022/jun/25/australia-news-live-updates-us-reacts-to-supreme-court-abortion-ruling-crossbench-anger-as-albanese-cuts-staffing-numbers?page=with:block-62b696728f0867712f95f388#block-62b696728f0867712f95f388"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s minister for women }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2022/jun/25/australia-news-live-updates-us-reacts-to-supreme-court-abortion-ruling-crossbench-anger-as-albanese-cuts-staffing-numbers?page=with:block-62b696728f0867712f95f388#block-62b696728f0867712f95f388"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Katy Gallagher}}}\uc2  said the decision by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to overturn Roe v Wade was \u8220\'20\'1Creally disappointing\u8221\'20\'1D, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2022/jun/25/australia-news-live-updates-us-reacts-to-supreme-court-abortion-ruling-crossbench-anger-as-albanese-cuts-staffing-numbers?page=with:block-62b693718f0875bb61abb57e#block-62b693718f0875bb61abb57e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Zealand\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, Jacinda Ardern}}}\uc2 , has described it as \u8220\'20\'1Cincredibly upsetting\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Until tomorrow, stay safe.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Some more reaction from Australian politicians to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturning Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 enltrWomen\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive choice is a fundamental human right.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Tanya Plibersek\uc2  (@tanya_plibersek) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tanya_plibersek/status/1540593586714329088?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWomen have every right to bodily autonomy, and no one should be able to tell us otherwise.\par \par \uc2 Next Saturday, stand in solidarity and defend \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JFfrlKyG9n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JFfrlKyG9n}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mehreen Faruqi (@MehreenFaruqi) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MehreenFaruqi/status/1540593601381793792?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01am BST\par \par \uc2 enltrHeads up, North Brisbane ??\par \par \uc2 You may notice some smoke in the air tonight as our partner agencies are conducting multiple hazard reduction burns.\par \par \uc2 Areas which may be affected include Mount Glorious, Samford, Dayboro, Morayfield, Narangba, Caboolture and Woodford.\par \par \uc2 ??FILE {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Kx7gGNGvYd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Kx7gGNGvYd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Qld Fire & Emergency (@QldFES) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/QldFES/status/1540587099774021632?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43am BST\par \par \uc2 Melbourne man critically wounded after car peppered with bullets\par \par \uc2 A man shot and critically wounded when a car was peppered with bullets in Melbourne\u8217\'20\'19s northern suburbs is believed to be a former member of the Mongols outlaw bikie gang, AAP reports.\par \par \uc2 Former Mongols bikie Suleiman \u8220\'20\'1CSam\u8221\'20\'1D Abdulrahim was driving a Mercedes 4WD when he was gunned down on Saturday, the Age reported.\par \par \uc2 Abdulrahim was driven to Fawkner police station before being taken to the hospital in a critical condition.\par \par \uc2 A Victoria police officer at the crime scene in Fawkner. Photograph: Diego Fedele/AAP\par \par \uc2 The gunmen fled in a \uc2 Mazda\uc2  SUV before losing control, crashing into a fire hydrant and pole on Box Forest Road, near Sydney Road, police said.\par \par \uc2 They then carjacked a Ford Territory, forcing a woman and child from the vehicle before escaping.\par \par \uc2 Abdulrahim remains in critical condition at the Royal Melbourne hospital.\par \par \uc2 Investigators believe the shooting was a targeted attack.\par \par \uc2 Witnesses or anyone with CCTV or dash cam footage or with information is urged to contact Crime Stoppers.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.10am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19am BST\par \par \uc2 David Pocock criticises Albanese government's staff cuts for independents\par \par \uc2 The new independent senator David Pocock continues to express his unhappiness that the Albanese government has cut the staff allocation for independents.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis isn't about parliamentarians or staff, it's about listening to and respecting our communities.\par \par \uc2 Being accessible, consulting widely, challenging the parliament to do better and making politics about people. That\u8217\'20\'19s what I want to do and I need a great team to do that. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZuVQYvpWMo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZuVQYvpWMo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Pocock (@pocockdavid) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/pocockdavid/status/1540580063665479680?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAs an independent you not only have to be accessible and be helping solve problems for your community with electorate staff, you have to be across and decide how to vote on EVERY piece of legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Pocock (@pocockdavid) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/pocockdavid/status/1540580068392460288?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.07am BST\par \par \uc2 National Covid update\par \par \uc2 Here are the latest coronavirus case numbers from around Australia on Saturday, as the country records at least 56 deaths from Covid-19:\par \par \uc2 ACT\par \par \uc2 * Deaths: 0\par \par \uc2 * Cases: 1,116\par \par \uc2 * In hospital: 105 (with 1 person in ICU)\par \par \uc2 NSW\par \par \uc2 * Deaths: 21\par \par \uc2 * Cases: 8,266\par \par \uc2 * In hospital: 1,453 (with 45 people in ICU)\par \par \uc2 Northern Territory\par \par \uc2 * Deaths: 0\par \par \uc2 * Cases: 209\par \par \uc2 * In hospital: 12 (with 0 people in ICU)\par \par \uc2 Queensland\par \par \uc2 * Deaths: 5\par \par \uc2 * Cases: 4,345\par \par \uc2 * In hospital: 556 (with 11 people in ICU)\par \par \uc2 South Australia\par \par \uc2 * Deaths: 1\par \par \uc2 * Cases: 2,565\par \par \uc2 * In hospital: 209 (with 8 people in ICU)\par \par \uc2 Tasmania\par \par \uc2 * Deaths: 0\par \par \uc2 * Cases: 983\par \par \uc2 * In hospital: 49 (with 0 people in ICU)\par \par \uc2 Victoria\par \par \uc2 * Deaths: 24\par \par \uc2 * Cases: 6,634\par \par \uc2 * In hospital: 420 (with 26 people in ICU)\par \par \uc2 Western Australia\par \par \uc2 * Deaths: 5\par \par \uc2 * Cases: 4,394\par \par \uc2 * In hospital: 242 (with 0 people in ICU)\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.08am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Omicron variant likely to be dominant Covid strain in Victoria\par \par \uc2 The Omicron strain BA.4/BA.5 is likely to become the dominant strain of Covid-19 in Victoria, the health department has said.\par \par \uc2 The prevalence of the strain in metropolitan and regional wastewater catchments has increased significantly in recent weeks, after first being identified in catchments in April. It is expected to overtake the BA.2 strain.\par \par \uc2 It is expected to result in an increase in cases, reinfections, and hospital admissions.\par \par \uc2 The health department said:\par \par \uc2 This is in line with similar patterns in NSW and Queensland. In NSW, BA.4/BA.5 represented over one third of Covid-19 variants in isolates from people testing positive by PCR by 11 June. In Queensland, BA.4/BA.5 is expected to become dominant in the next two weeks. Both states have seen a significant rise in the number of people hospitalised with Covid-19 during June.\par \par \uc2 The Department of Health anticipates the prevalence of BA.4/BA.5 in Victoria is likely to result in an increase in cases \u8211\'20\'13 including reinfections \u8211\'20\'13 and hospital admissions. This is because the strain has a greater ability than BA.2 to evade immunity provided by vaccination and earlier Covid-19 infection.\par \par \uc2 There is no evidence at this stage that the BA.4/BA.5 sub-lineage causes more severe disease, but the department is closely monitoring the situation.\par \par \uc2 Of the 24 Covid-19 deaths reported in Victoria today, there were people aged in their 40s, 50s, 60s, 70s, 80s and 90s, the health department has said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43am BST\par \par \uc2 Now it\u8217\'20\'19s my turn to rocket. Josh Taylor will bring it home from here \u8211\'20\'13 so long, and thanks for all the fish!\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.35am BST\par \par \uc2 This is rather cool:\par \par \uc2 enltrI'm at the Arnhem Space Centre! 400m behind me is a rocket that will be taking off tomorrow!\par \par \uc2 And I'll be hosting the live stream here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1FK3v14fe8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/1FK3v14fe8}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zGOctHyGhA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zGOctHyGhA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Brad Tucker (@btucker22) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/btucker22/status/1540523336807383040?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Read all about it here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2022/jun/08/nasa-to-launch-rockets-from-the-northern-territory-for-scientific-research"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nasa to launch rockets from the Northern Territory for scientific research}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24am BST\par \par \uc2 As someone who once wrote an entire news story about the Baklava Races, I probably shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t comment:\par \par \uc2 enltrThere\u8217\'20\'19s gonna be a riot in Bendigo today: \u8220\'20\'1CBallarat teenager\u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/59puUOGAgk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/59puUOGAgk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alexander Darling (@SaveUrDarlings) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SaveUrDarlings/status/1540482710497394688?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.01am BST\par \par \uc2 US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling \u8216\'20\'18really disappointing\u8217\'20\'19, Australia\u8217\'20\'19s minister for women says\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, minister for women Katy Gallagher said the decision by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to overturn Roe v Wade was \u8220\'20\'1Creally disappointing\u8221\'20\'1D. She told the Today show:\par \par \uc2 I think after so many years fighting to maintain rights and to have access to safe and legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clearly this is going to be a very, very divisive issue in America.\par \par \uc2 It will disproportionately affect poor women, women from socially disadvantaged backgrounds.\par \par \uc2 Gallagher said history has shown abortions will always take place, no matter the law:\par \par \uc2 I would argue they should take place in a legal and safe way so, yes, I can see why people are out on the streets today in America.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.05am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Jacinda Ardern\uc2  says US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision is \u8216\'20\'18 incredibly upsetting\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 New Zealand\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Jacinda Ardern\uc2 , has described as \u8220\'20\'1Cincredibly upsetting\u8221\'20\'1D a decision in the United States to wind back women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights, AAP reports.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  on Friday voted to end constitutional protections allowing the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that have been in place for almost 50 years, since the famous 1973 Roe v Wade decision.\par \par \uc2 The move, which was carried by six votes to three in America\u8217\'20\'19s highest court, is expected to lead to bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in about half the nation\u8217\'20\'19s 50 states.\par \par \uc2 Ardern compared the move with New Zealand\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 decriminalisation of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She said:\par \par \uc2 Watching the removal of a woman\u8217\'20\'19s fundamental right to make decisions over their own body is incredibly upsetting.\par \par \uc2 Here in New Zealand we recently legislated to decriminalise \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and treat it as a health rather than criminal issue.\par \par \uc2 That change was grounded in the fundamental belief that it\u8217\'20\'19s a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Correction: this post was amended on Tuesday 28 January. A previous version incorrectly stated the overturning of Roe v Wade was decided by five votes to four\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/25/world-leaders-condemn-us-abortion-ruling-as-backwards-step"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 World leaders condemn US \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ruling as \u8216\'20\'18backwards step\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.19am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Atlassian\uc2  offers support to employees impacted by Roe v Wade decision\par \par \uc2 From the \uc2 Atlassian\uc2  co-founder \uc2 Mike Cannon-Brookes\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Starting today, US employees living in states that have restricted or banned abortions will be offered reimbursement for travel and accommodations for themselves and a companion should they seek care outside their state.\par \par \uc2 enltrAtlassian\u8217\'20\'19s statement on today\u8217\'20\'19s Supreme Court ruling in the USA. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EmXz2fUMaN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/EmXz2fUMaN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Mike Cannon-Brookes\uc2  ????????????? (@mcannonbrookes) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mcannonbrookes/status/1540461694672986112?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.09am BST\par \par \uc2 ACT reports 105 people in hospital with Covid\par \par \uc2 There have been no Covid deaths in the ACT, but 105 people are in hospital, one in intensive care.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.18am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57am BST\par \par \uc2 South Australia records one Covid death\par \par \uc2 One person has died in South Australia and 209 people have been hospitalised with Covid. Eight people are in intensive care.\par \par \uc2 enltrSouth Australian COVID-19 update 25/06/22.\par \par \uc2 For more information, go to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XkVcAmeZ6V"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/XkVcAmeZ6V}}}\uc2  or contact the South Australia COVID-19 Information Line on 1800 253 787. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dhWYNtvs8Y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dhWYNtvs8Y}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SA Health (@SAHealth) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SAHealth/status/1540543497056710658?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.50am BST\par \par \uc2 New details of orange roughy\u8217\'20\'19s life cycle prompt calls to limit fishing\par \par \uc2 Lisa Cox talked to Adrian Meder, the sustainable fisheries manager at the Australian Marine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/conservation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Conservation}}}\uc2  Society, for this story:\par \par \uc2 If the science is correct, we\u8217\'20\'19ve just invited New Zealand-based boats and crews to catch these fish, do decades-lasting damage to our diminished orange roughy stocks and our deep-sea coral reefs, and ship almost all their catch straight to the US and Europe.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jun/25/orange-roughy-campaigners-call-for-limit-to-trawling-of-species-after-breeding-age-of-73-revealed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Breeding at age 73: new details of endangered orange roughy\u8217\'20\'19s life cycle prompt calls to limit fishing}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.17am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Fina bans artistic swimmer who fainted in pool from final\par \par \uc2 Anita Alvarez, the US Olympian artistic swimmer, said yesterday she was feeling better after dramatically fainting and sinking to the bottom of the pool, before being rescued by her coach.\par \par \uc2 But Fina, the water sports federation, has decided that\u8217\'20\'19s not good enough. She won\u8217\'20\'19t be allowed to compete in tonight\u8217\'20\'19s women\u8217\'20\'19s team free final (it\u8217\'20\'19s scheduled for midnight, AEST).\par \par \uc2 A member of Team USA recovers Anita Alvarez from the bottom of the pool during an incident in the women\u8217\'20\'19s solo free artistic swimming finals at the World Aquatics Championships. Photograph: Oli Scarff/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Fina said:\par \par \uc2 Earlier today Fina convened a meeting that included three representatives of Fina\u8217\'20\'19s sports medicine committee, the Fina executive director, the Team USA doctor, the Team USA team leader and the president of USA Artistic Swimming.\par \par \uc2 The meeting lasted an hour. Following these discussions, Fina determined that Anita Alvarez should not compete today.\par \par \uc2 The health and safety of athletes must always come first. While Fina understands why this decision will have been disappointing to the athlete, it was a decision that was made with her best interests in mind. Fina is delighted that Anita Alvarez has already made such a strong recovery, and looks forward to seeing her in competition again soon.\par \par \uc2 You can catch up on what happened at the world championship solo competition here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jun/23/dramatic-rescue-at-world-championships-after-swimmer-faints-and-sinks-to-bottom-of-pool"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dramatic rescue at world championships after swimmer faints and sinks to bottom of pool }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.42am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.18am BST\par \par \uc2 An enlightened Australia:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2022/jun/25/tripping-the-light-fantastic-a-year-round-calendar-of-australias-light-based-festivals"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tripping the light fantastic: a year-round calendar of Australia\u8217\'20\'19s light-based festivals}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Northern Territory reports 12 people in hospital with Covid\par \par \uc2 The Northern Territory hasn\u8217\'20\'19t reported any Covid deaths. Twelve people are in hospital, none of them in intensive care.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Queensland records five Covid deaths\par \par \uc2 Five people have died in Queensland with Covid, while 556 people are in hospital, 11 of them in intensive care:\par \par \uc2 enltrToday we have recorded 4,345 new COVID-19 cases.\par \par \uc2 Sadly, we have reported 5 deaths in the past 24 hours.\par \par \uc2 Full details?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6L6VcCsFY1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/6L6VcCsFY1}}}\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/R7A6j8BmCz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/R7A6j8BmCz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Queensland Health\uc2  (@qldhealth) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/qldhealth/status/1540501264999813120?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.59am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55am BST\par \par \uc2 Thanks, Josh Taylor, for driving while all that was happening!\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53am BST\par \par \uc2 I shall now hand the blog back to Tory Shepherd for the next couple of hours.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19am BST\par \par \uc2 Penny Wong\uc2  to travel to Vietnam and Malaysia\par \par \uc2 The foreign minister, \uc2 Penny Wong\uc2 , has announced she will travel to Vietnam and Malaysia from tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 She says:\par \par \uc2 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s future is tied to the future of south-east Asia, a region we share.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s more than geography that binds us \u8211\'20\'13 we have genuine links in Vietnam and Malaysia: family, business, education and tourism.\par \par \uc2 My visit seeks to deepen these ties, building on our existing partnerships for the benefit of our countries and the region.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s important we work closely together to capitalise on shared economic opportunities, strengthen regional security, and address climate change.\par \par \uc2 In Vietnam I will meet with President \uc2 Nguyen Xuan Phuc\uc2 , Prime Minister \uc2 Pham Minh Chinh\uc2  and Foreign Minister \uc2 B\u249\'00\'F9i Thanh S\u245\'00\'F5n\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ahead of next year\u8217\'20\'19s 50th anniversary of diplomatic relations, our discussions will focus on climate change cooperation, our shared trade and investment ambitions and Australia\u8217\'20\'19s continued support for Vietnam\u8217\'20\'19s Covid-19 recovery.\par \par \uc2 Penny Wong\uc2  at a press conference in Jakarta during a visit to Indonesia in early June. Photograph: Lukas Coch/AAP\par \par \uc2 On 28 July, the foreign minister will go to Malaysia, where she will also visit Sabah, the region Wong is originally from:\par \par \uc2 On the 28th, I will travel on to Malaysia, where I look forward to meeting Minister for Foreign Affairs Dato\u8217\'20\'19 Sri Saifuddin bin Abdullah, as well as Defence Minister Dato\u8217\'20\'19 Seri Hishammuddin Hussein and Minister for International Trade and Investment, Dato\u8217\'20\'19 \uc2 Seri Azmin Ali\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 I will reaffirm our commitment as Comprehensive Strategic Partners and discuss economic recovery, climate action, education ties and health security.\par \par \uc2 I will also travel to Sabah. It\u8217\'20\'19s a region with longstanding ties to Australia, and it\u8217\'20\'19s the region where I am from. Having spent my early years in Kota Kinabalu, I look forward to the great honour of returning to the city as Australia\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.34am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Victorian government unveils frontbench it will take to state election\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the full report on the Victorian Labor caucus vote via AAP.\par \par \uc2 The Victorian government has unveiled the frontbench it expects to take to the November state election and crowned a new deputy premier.\par \par \uc2 The transport infrastructure minister, \uc2 Jacinta Allan\uc2 , will replace \uc2 James Merlino\uc2  as deputy premier, one of four senior Labor ministers to announce their retirement and step down from cabinet on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2  speaks to the media alongside newly elected Victorian deputy premier \uc2 Jacinta Allan\uc2 . Photograph: Diego Fedele/AAP\par \par \uc2 Labor MPs Lizzie Blandthorn, Colin Brooks, Steve Dimopoulos, Sonya Kilkenny and Harriet Shing will fill the ministerial vacancies, although their exact responsibilities are not yet finalised.\par \par \uc2 Maree Edwards was elected to replace Brooks as speaker, while Natalie Suleyman will become deputy speaker.\par \par \uc2 The changes were unanimously backed by the Victorian Labor caucus during a meeting at Parliament House on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 The premier, \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2 , said the new ministry will be sworn in at Government House on Monday and the exact allocation of portfolios could be announced as early as Saturday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59am BST\par \par \uc2 The former Australian prime minister \uc2 Julia Gillard\uc2  responding to the news of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturning Roe v Wade overnight.\par \par \uc2 enltrI fully endorse these words and Michelle Obama\u8217\'20\'19s call to all of us to keep fighting for women\u8217\'20\'19s rights. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/j7x9ua2NXv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/j7x9ua2NXv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Julia Gillard\uc2  (@JuliaGillard) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JuliaGillard/status/1540491941812772864?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.05am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48am BST\par \par \uc2 First non-stop flight from Australia to continental Europe set to depart\par \par \uc2 Stir crazy Australians celebrating the end to travel restrictions will be able to take a direct flight from Perth to Rome, AAP reports.\par \par \uc2 The new route, operating from Saturday night, is the first non-stop flight from Australia to continental Europe on offer.\par \par \uc2 The Western Australian premier, \uc2 Mark McGowan\uc2 , will join the \uc2 Qantas\uc2  boss, \uc2 Alan Joyce\uc2 , on the inaugural flight to Rome.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C(This) represents an incredible milestone for Western Australia,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 The carrier says the route was opened up after the success of its direct Perth to London flight which started in 2018.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Qantas\uc2  terminal at Perth airport. Premier \uc2 Mark McGowan\uc2  will join \uc2 Qantas\uc2  boss \uc2 Alan Joyce\uc2  on the inaugural non-stop flight to Rome. Photograph: Matt Jelonek/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Travellers are demanding more point-to-point travel than ever in the wake of lockdowns and border closures, \uc2 Qantas\uc2  says.\par \par \uc2 The WA tourism minister, R oger Cooke, says it is a \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric moment\u8221\'20\'1D for his state with hopes it will drive a massive boost to local tourism and hospitality industries.\par \par \uc2 Qantas\uc2  has already flagged it will open routes to Johannesburg and Jakarta from Perth later this year.\par \par \uc2 The airline has been grappling with a surge in travel demand as Australians look to reconnect with the world.\par \par \uc2 Airports and airlines are already warning commuters of what may be in store for them as school holidays start across the country.\par \par \uc2 But they\u8217\'20\'19re hoping to avoid a repeat of the travel chaos that gripped airports at Easter with airlines putting on more staff, including customer service personnel and pilots.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.58am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Teenager dies after being stabbed in northern NSW\par \par \uc2 A teenager is dead following a stabbing in northern NSW, AAP reports.\par \par \uc2 Police say the still to be identified victim, thought to be a 17-year-old boy, was found suffering stab wounds at a home in Casino around 1.30am on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 He was treated by paramedics but died at the scene.\par \par \uc2 The residence is to undergo forensic examination, while a search of the surrounding area has been conducted with help from the dog unit and local police.\par \par \uc2 The homicide squad will also assist with the case, with initial inquiries suggesting the incident was targeted.\par \par \uc2 The boy\u8217\'20\'19s death follows that of a 50-year-old man involved in a physical altercation at South Grafton, on the state\u8217\'20\'19s north coast, on Friday morning.\par \par \uc2 Police say a 64-year-old man arrested at the scene will face court charged with manslaughter.\par \par \uc2 Emergency services were called to Phoenix Close following reports of a neighbour dispute shortly after 9.30am.\par \par \uc2 On arrival, they found the man unresponsive and suffering head injuries.\par \par \uc2 He was treated by ambulance paramedics but was unable to be revived.\par \par \uc2 The accused man was expected to appear in Port Macquarie local court on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.45am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Finally Andrews is asked if he is concerned about the institutional knowledge leaving with the four ministers resigning ahead of the state election.\par \par \uc2 He says it has been \u8220\'20\'1Can orderly, professional, seamless process\u8221\'20\'1D to replace the ministers and they\u8217\'20\'19ll be building experience, skills and knowledge:\par \par \uc2 So, of course, there is a lot of experience, but there is also a lot of depth in this team and I\u8217\'20\'19m proud to think that just like the cabinet, the senior leadership group, the coordinating ministers\u8217\'20\'19 group, is now more than 50% women. We\u8217\'20\'19ve got a much more diverse cabinet as a result of these decisions that have been made. Of course I pay tribute to all of those who were leaving yesterday, and that was right to do because they are outstanding people, but they are being replaced by equally outstanding people as well.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Andrews is asked if he discussed a handover with Allan at all. He says \u8220\'20\'1Cnot at all\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 We are focused \u8211\'20\'13 every single member of my team is focused, all of us, on doing the things we said we would do over the next five months and putting a positive and optimistic plan to the Victorian community.\par \par \uc2 Those who know me know I\u8217\'20\'19ve never taken the Victorian community for granted. Never taken any vote, any seat, any contest for granted. The state election will be very close. They always are. It is a handful of votes and a handful of seats.\par \par \uc2 We will put forward a positive, optimistic plan and give Victorians the choice: Keep building, keep the place strong, make it fairer, create jobs, or go a different way \u8211\'20\'13 and closures and all the risks involved in that. But that\u8217\'20\'19s not a choice for me, that\u8217\'20\'19s a choice for the Victorian community.\par \par \uc2 My job, our job together, all of us, is to put forward that optimistic and positive plan, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what we are focused on. We don\u8217\'20\'19t take that outcome for granted. We simply don\u8217\'20\'19t. We never have, we never will.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16am BST\par \par \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2  announces new ministry appointments\par \par \uc2 The Victorian premier, \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2 , is speaking in Melbourne about the new appointments to his ministry, after Labor caucus voted today.\par \par \uc2 He says he will make announcements about portfolios later today or tomorrow, with the new ministry sworn in on Monday.\par \par \uc2 He welcomed the appointment of \uc2 Jacinta Allan\uc2  as deputy premier:\par \par \uc2 Jacinta is someone who came into the parliament in 1999, one of the very youngest MPs in the history of our parliament, and right through her long career, she has been a champion for regional Victorians, Bendigo and has made a such a huge contribution to building our state, to employing hundreds of thousands of Victorians to getting things down. That\u8217\'20\'19s why, I think together with her work ethic and her character, that\u8217\'20\'19s why her colleagues, all of them, have unanimously supported her today. She has big shoes to fill, of course.\par \par \uc2 James Merlino\uc2 , not only our friend, but no one could have asked for a better deputy than \uc2 James Merlino\uc2 . I pay tribute to him and thank him for his amazing work and all he has done, and his great loyalty and support to me at a personal level. But JA is just outstanding and it is fitting that the caucus have elected her unopposed.\par \par \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2  speaks to the media alongside \uc2 Jacinta Allan\uc2  during a press conference at Parliament House in Melbourne. Photograph: Diego Fedele/AAP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11am BST\par \par \uc2 enltrLa Ni\u241\'00\'F1a WATCH activated; negative Indian Ocean Dipole likely\par \par \uc2 While 2021\u8211\'20\'1322 La Ni\u241\'00\'F1a has ended there is ~50% chance of a La Ni\u241\'00\'F1a forming again during 2022\par \par \uc2 Above median rainfall is still likely across E & S Aus during winter & spring\par \par \uc2 More detail: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jGschk9NVB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/jGschk9NVB}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TSaz1WiKFB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/TSaz1WiKFB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bureau of Meteorology, Victoria (@BOM_Vic) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BOM_Vic/status/1540499864953536512?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Jacinta Allan\uc2  appointed Victoria's deputy premier\par \par \uc2 AAP is reporting \uc2 Jacinta Allan\uc2  has been voted by Victorian Labor caucus to be the deputy premier, with Lizzie Blandthorn, Colin Brooks, Steve Dimopoulos, Sonya Kilkenny and Harriet Shing approved to fill ministerial vacancies. Maree Edwards will be the new speaker.\par \par \uc2 enltrJUST IN: \uc2 Jacinta Allan\uc2  has been appointed Victoria\u8217\'20\'19s deputy premier. The decision was unanimous. More on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AAPNewswire?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AAPNewswire}}}\uc2  soon.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Callum Godde (@calgodde) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/calgodde/status/1540497872994459648?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Analysis: \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 dilemma after losing four ministers\par \par \uc2 The next crop of Victorian government ministers to lead Labor\u8217\'20\'19s re-election push is set to be decided, as premier \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2  lobbies for the party to break with convention.\par \par \uc2 The Victorian Labor caucus is meeting to confirm the make-up of its cabinet after the resignation of MPs \uc2 James Merlino\uc2 , \uc2 Martin Foley\uc2 , Lisa Neville and \uc2 Martin Pakula\uc2  from their high-profile portfolios.\par \par \uc2 Current agriculture and regional development minister Mary-Anne Thomas will become health minister, while corrections minister Natalie Hutchins will pick up the education portfolio.\par \par \uc2 It is expected to be the Andrews government\u8217\'20\'19s final cabinet reshuffle before the November election, with new ministers likely to be sworn in early next week.\par \par \uc2 You can read more analysis of the reshuffle in the link below:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/25/factions-new-blood-and-jeff-kennett-daniel-andrews-dilemma-after-losing-four-ministers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Factions, new blood and Jeff Kennett: Daniel Andrews\u8217\'20\'19 dilemma after losing four ministers}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.55am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.35am BST\par \par \uc2 NSW residents urged to ensure they have working smoke alarms\par \par \uc2 NSW residents are being urged to check they have a working smoke alarm after a horror start to the winter, AAP reports.\par \par \uc2 Five people have died since the start of June in house fires, a toll already higher than last year\u8217\'20\'19s total.\par \par \uc2 So far firefighters have attended 202 house fires across NSW with 42% of those homes not having a working smoke alarm and another 16 per cent without one entirely.\par \par \uc2 Fire and Rescue NSW\uc2  deputy commissioner Megan Stiffler reminded people that firefighters can check a household\u8217\'20\'19s smoke alarms and replace them at no cost:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s also a great opportunity to ask for advice from the experts on how you can keep yourself and your family warm but safe.\par \par \uc2 Our firefighters are dedicated to protecting the irreplaceable but it\u8217\'20\'19s important everyone takes steps to safeguard their homes from the threat of fire, especially during winter.\par \par \uc2 Three of the five fatalities are still under investigation with investigators finding a faulty fridge behind the deaths of an elderly couple earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 Emergency services minister Steph Cooke said there was a simple precaution that people could take to keep themselves safe: having a working smoke alarm.\par \par \uc2 Fire can engulf a home in a matter of minutes and while smoke won\u8217\'20\'19t wake you up, a smoke alarm will, which could be the difference between life and death.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.40am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Josh Taylor is going to take over for a bit, while I go and perform some mysterious duties*.\par \par \uc2 *Not that mysterious.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.36am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Victoria records 24 Covid deaths\par \par \uc2 In Victoria, 24 people have died with Covid. 420 have been hospitalised, and 26 are in intensive care:\par \par \uc2 enltrWe thank everyone who got vaccinated and tested yesterday.\par \par \uc2 Our thoughts are with those in hospital, and the families of people who have lost their lives.\par \par \uc2 More data soon: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OCCFTAcOZP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/OCCFTAcOZP}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/COVID19Vic?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #COVID19Vic}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/COVID19VicData?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #COVID19VicData}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ChXDx6Gme5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ChXDx6Gme5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 VicGovDH (@VicGovDH) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VicGovDH/status/1540487820309327873?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.18am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.04am BST\par \par \uc2 This is a lovely tale about a remarkable transformation from Philippa Duncan :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/25/an-elsewhere-world-the-sleepy-tasmanian-mining-town-that-became-an-arts-mecca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 An elsewhere world: the sleepy Tasmanian mining town which became an arts mecca}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Victoria eases mask mandates and lifts Covid restrictions\par \par \uc2 Mask mandates have been relaxed in Victoria, AAP reports:\par \par \uc2 Victorians no longer have to wear masks inside airports as Covid restrictions are lifted across the state.\par \par \uc2 Select vaccine mandates have also been scrapped, including third dose requirements for staff in education, food distribution, meat and seafood processing and quarantine settings.\par \par \uc2 However they remain for health workers and those in emergency services.\par \par \uc2 School staff previously placed on leave without pay for not being fully vaccinated are now free to return to work. Under the new rules, parents will not be informed of a staff member\u8217\'20\'19s vaccination status.\par \par \uc2 Victorian health minister \uc2 Martin Foley\uc2  says the changes are minor and progressive, and have been implemented sensibly.\par \par \uc2 Employers will set their own requirements around vaccines.\par \par \uc2 Rules requiring people to work from home if they\u8217\'20\'19re not double-dosed have also been lifted and aged care and disability care visitor caps have been removed.\par \par \uc2 Positive cases still need to isolate for seven days from the day they took their test but may now leave home to drive a household member directly to or from education or work.\par \par \uc2 With case numbers continuing to rise during winter, Australia\u8217\'20\'19s chief medical officer \uc2 Paul Kelly\uc2  is urging people to get their boosters, along with the flu vaccine:\par \par \uc2 The flu vaccine [is] very important now, and right across Australia, that\u8217\'20\'19s been made free for most people, but particularly those who are vulnerable of severe flu...\par \par \uc2 That includes young kids, actually. That\u8217\'20\'19s a difference to the Covid message. We need to increase that flu shot as well.\par \par \uc2 70% of the eligible population have received their booster.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Once you\u8217\'20\'19ve had a morning coffee or three, Graham Readfearn has an energy quiz for you (I both enjoyed and nailed it):\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/25/capacity-mechanism-fcas-load-shedding-how-much-have-you-learned-from-australias-energy-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Capacity mechanism, FCAS, load shedding: how much have you learned from Australia\u8217\'20\'19s energy crisis? Take our quiz}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Australians should have faith in \u8216\'20\'18narrow path\u8217\'20\'19 back from inflation, \uc2 RBA\uc2  governor says\par \par \uc2 If Australians don\u8217\'20\'19t have faith in the Reserve Bank\u8217\'20\'19s promise of a \u8220\'20\'1Cnarrow path\u8221\'20\'1D to avoid recession, they could end up being the cause of one, the central bank\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Philip Lowe\uc2  has warned, according to a report from AAP.\par \par \uc2 If people start worrying that the path back from 5% inflation to a more normal level is unrealistic, it might push the economy into a downward spiral, he says.\par \par \uc2 Australians are copping increasing costs of living as inflationary pressures rise, leading to higher prices at the supermarket and made worse by high fuel and gas prices.\par \par \uc2 The national minimum wage also recently rose, a move that\u8217\'20\'19s hoped to ease the financial burden on households. Lowe told a central bankers meeting in Zurich on Friday:\par \par \uc2 There is a path to have inflation come down without the economy having too much pain, but it\u8217\'20\'19s a narrow path.\par \par \uc2 But if people start to worry that we can\u8217\'20\'19t show that credible path back... to two to three per cent inflation... then I think that shift in psychology could be quite persistent. And we know where that ends \u8211\'20\'13 it ends in persistent inflation and then you\u8217\'20\'19ve got to have much higher interest rates and an economic downturn to get inflation back down.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.50am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.16am BST\par \par \uc2 There was quite a lot I didn\u8217\'20\'19t know about vaping before I read this piece from Bianca Nogrady :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/25/teens-and-vaping-we-would-have-had-a-nicotine-free-generation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Teens and vaping: \u8216\'20\'18We would have had a nicotine-free generation\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.07am BST\par \par \uc2 NSW records 21 Covid deaths\par \par \uc2 There have been 21 Covid deaths in NSW. 1,453 people have been hospitalised, and 45 are in intensive care:\par \par \uc2 enltrCOVID-19 update \u8211\'20\'13 Saturday 25 June 2022\par \par \uc2 In the 24-hour reporting period to 4pm yesterday:\par \par \uc2 - 96.6% of people aged 16+ have had one dose of a COVID-19 vaccine\par \par \uc2 - 95.1% of people aged 16+ have had two doses of a COVID-19 vaccine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7UrlYkd1ap"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/7UrlYkd1ap}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 NSW Health\uc2  (@NSWHealth) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NSWHealth/status/1540470076100718593?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.03am BST\par \par \uc2 'It just stuns me': \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on the overturning of Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is calling on Americans to vote for officials who will restore \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. This is how he described the overturning of Roe v Wade earlier:\par \par \uc2 So extreme that women could be punished for protecting their health.\par \par \uc2 So extreme that women and girls who are forced to bear their rapist\u8217\'20\'19s child \u8211\'20\'13 of the child of consequence.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a \u8211\'20\'13 it just \u8211\'20\'13 it just stuns me.\par \par \uc2 So extreme that doctors will be criminalised for fulfilling their duty to care.\par \par \uc2 Imagine having a young woman having to carry the child of incest \u8211\'20\'13 as a consequence of incest. No option.\par \par \uc2 Too often the case that poor women are going to be hit the hardest. It\u8217\'20\'19s cruel.\par \par \uc2 enltrIt's a sad day for the country.\par \par \uc2 Nearly 50 years ago, Roe vs. Wade was decided. Today, the \uc2 Supreme Court of the United States\uc2  expressly took away a constitutional right from the American people.\par \par \uc2 Personal freedoms are on the ballot this fall.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1540468564402094080?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Australia has lifesaving antivirals sitting on shelves, but there\u8217\'20\'19s some dithering over getting them out there. Caitlin Cassidy and Josh Butler have talked to the experts:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/25/calls-to-expand-access-to-covid-antivirals-in-australia-splits-experts-and-doctors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Calls to expand access to Covid antivirals in Australia splits experts and doctors}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michael McGowan has tracked the twists and turns that handed former NSW deputy premier \uc2 John Barilaro\uc2  that sweet gig:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/25/john-barilaros-bite-of-the-big-apple-the-plum-new-york-posting-that-set-off-a-firestorm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 John Barilaro\u8217\'20\'19s bite of the Big Apple: the plum New York posting that set off a firestorm}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ooof.\par \par \uc2 enltrSo, to sum up the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s week: life begins at conception and ends in a mass shooting.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Arianna Huffington (@ariannahuff) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ariannahuff/status/1540366118866587648?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve been compromised.\u8221\'20\'1D Please enjoy this read from Nino Bucci on how camouflage failed to make these covert cops invisible:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/25/blockade-australia-how-a-sharp-eyed-hippy-set-off-events-that-cast-a-harsh-light-on-anti-protest-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Blockade Australia: how a \u8216\'20\'18sharp-eyed hippy\u8217\'20\'19 set off events that cast a harsh light on anti-protest laws}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 This is cheating slightly because it\u8217\'20\'19s not today\u8217\'20\'19s news, but I did promise something chirpy. So in case you missed it, here is this week in wildlife pictures:\par \par \uc2 Baby owls being fed at Dicle Wildlife Rescue and Rehabilitation Centre in Diyarbakir, Turkiye. Photograph: Bestami Bodruk/Anadolu Agency/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/gallery/2022/jun/24/the-week-in-wildlife-in-pictures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The week in wildlife \u8211\'20\'13 in pictures}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Unsurprisingly, there are certain Australian elements that will find succour in the US decision:\par \par \uc2 enltrAustralian anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lobby groups and columnists are posting cheerful celebratory statuses this morning. I think they understand better than many that these rights are pretty provisional everywhere.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Gina Rushton (@ginarush) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ginarush/status/1540459294419652610?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Katharine Murphy: voters have sent Dutton a clear message; he would be silly to miss the cue\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re just plugging in, Katharine Murphy will help you fire up. She\u8217\'20\'19s taken a whirlwind trip through the shenanigans in energy policy, and cocked a questioning eyebrow at opposition leader \uc2 Peter Dutton\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s plans:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/25/australian-voters-have-sent-peter-dutton-a-clear-message-he-would-be-silly-to-miss-the-cue"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Australian voters have sent Peter Dutton a clear message; he would be silly to miss the cue | Katharine Murphy}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning\par \par \uc2 Welcome to your Saturday \u8211\'20\'13 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s waking up to the news that the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has overturned the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-decision-reaction-republicans-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18One of our darkest days\u8217\'20\'19: outrage after supreme court overturns Roe v Wade}}}\par \par \uc2 Many in the US are reeling, and protesting, and trying to work out what will happen in each state. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  declared the move \u8220\'20\'1Cso extreme\u8221\'20\'1D. Tory Shepherd here at the wheel, and I\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you the local reaction throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re also talking about that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/25/john-barilaros-bite-of-the-big-apple-the-plum-new-york-posting-that-set-off-a-firestorm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plum New York posting}}}\uc2  for former NSW deputy premier \uc2 John Barilaro\uc2 , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/24/slap-in-the-face-independents-furious-at-pms-decision-to-cut-advisory-staff-from-four-to-one"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crossbench\u8217\'20\'19s anger }}}\uc2  at prime minister Anthony Albanese \u8217\'20\'19s decision on staffing, and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/25/capacity-mechanism-fcas-load-shedding-how-much-have-you-learned-from-australias-energy-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ongoing energy crisis}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And I\u8217\'20\'19m going to find some chirpier news, too, to kick off your weekend. I promise. Let\u8217\'20\'19s go.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220624ei6o003ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
