\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas judge temporarily blocks state ban on abortions up to six weeks\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly in New York \par \uc2 641 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 June 2022\par 17:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Judge sets hearing for 12 July, meaning abortions up to six weeks of pregnancy can resume for at least two weeks\par \par \uc2 A judge in Texas on Tuesday temporarily blocked a state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban linked to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  decision which last week overturned the ruling guaranteeing the right to terminate pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 The Texas case followed stays issued in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/27/louisiana-judge-abortion-ban-roe-v-wade-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/06/25/utah-abortion-ban-planned-parenthood/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Utah}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Across Republican-run states, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates are filing lawsuits seeking to delay implementation of so-called trigger bans, designed to go into effect as soon as the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade, the landmark 1973 ruling granting nationwide access to abortions.\par \par \uc2 A court dominated by conservatives did so on Friday, a seismic event in American history which prompted protest and counter-protest.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit at the center of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s decision in Texas was filed in Harris county, which covers Houston, by \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  and on behalf of local women\u8217\'20\'19s health providers.\par \par \uc2 It concerned a 1925 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban resurrected by the state before its trigger law could pass, and the suit named among its defendants \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , Texas\u8217\'20\'19s Republican attorney general.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.khou.com/article/news/local/texas/texas-trigger-law-abortion-lawsuit/285-a34bc2d2-3e1f-4d37-9ce7-b16d7144bb07"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the ACLU said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1COn Friday, within hours of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, the Texas attorney general put out an advisory stating that the state\u8217\'20\'19s trigger ban, which bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost entirely, will not take effect for approximately two months or longer.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut in that same advisory \u8230\'20\'26 the attorney general said that \u8216\'20\'18\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers could be criminally liable for providing abortions starting today\u8217\'20\'19 based on the state\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  prohibitions predating Roe\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Texas passed a six-week ban in 2021. In January, the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/01/20/us/politics/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 let it stand}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a move many saw as a clear signal of the Roe ruling to come.\par \par \uc2 Under the 1925 law to which Paxton pointed, however, abortions at any stage would only be allowed to save the woman\u8217\'20\'19s life.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, a judge issued a temporary restraining order and set a hearing for 12 July. That meant abortions up to six weeks of pregnancy could resume for at least two weeks.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/profile/marc-hearron/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marc Hearron}}}\uc2 , an attorney for the plaintiffs, told reporters: \u8220\'20\'1CWe all know, Texas has had for 10 months now an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban prohibiting abortions to six weeks of pregnancy, which is before most people know they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant. So we\u8217\'20\'19re still talking about a short window for abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany Texans are still going to have to flee the state, trying to find an appointment in other states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not illegal. But at least for today, we can say that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers cannot be prosecuted for the time being, for providing abortions before six weeks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats across the US are attempting to slow or counter \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans at state and local levels, or to provide assistance to women from states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned. Some prosecutors have said they will not enforce \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in their jurisdictions.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the attorney general of New York, Letitia James, announced the creation of a coalition with \u8220\'20\'1C24 national law firms and eight reproductive rights organisations [of] {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lnks.gd/l/eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJidWxsZXRpbl9saW5rX2lkIjoxMDAsInVyaSI6ImJwMjpjbGljayIsImJ1bGxldGluX2lkIjoiMjAyMjA2MjguNjAwMTgzMjEiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwOi8vYWcubnkuZ292L3JlcHJvZHVjdGl2ZWhlYWx0aCJ9.ZYuQiU5Cd6krDs_AKZsxqdp0nwtSOd5125zgVDyx6PM/s/1163474067/br/134336383900-l"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a legal hotline}}}\uc2  that will provide legal guidance and resources to patients, healthcare providers and supporters seeking information about their legal rights to access and provide abortions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Referring to the Mississippi case which overturned Roe, \uc2 Nancy Northup\uc2 , president of the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2 , said the hotline aimed to \u8220\'20\'1Ccut through the legal chaos left in the wake of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s precedent-breaking and ruinous Dobbs decision\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On the west coast, Democrats in California are seeking to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/27/california-abortion-rights-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enshrine}}}\uc2  the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 In Houston, Hearron, the attorney, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/06/28/texas-abortion-ban-roe-blocks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CEvery hour that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is accessible in Texas is a victory.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220628ei6s002ny\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
