\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: at least 46 people found dead in Texas trailer truck\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,310 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 June 2022\par 10:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Further 16 people in hospital after tragedy in San Antonio. Plus, Louisiana judge blocks \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  banDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Forty-six people were found dead and 16 others were taken to hospital after being found inside a tractor-trailer rig yesterday on a remote back road in south-west San Antonio, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/27/texas-trailer-truck-dead-people-san-antonio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas officials have said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The discovery may prove to be the deadliest tragedy among thousands of people who have died attempting to cross the US border from Mexico in recent decades.\par \par \uc2 A city worker at the scene was alerted by a cry for help shortly before 6pm yesterday, police chief William McManus said. Officers arrived to find a body on the ground outside the trailer and a partially opened gate to the vehicle, he said.\par \par \uc2 Sixteen people were taken to hospital with heat-related illnesses, of which 12 were adults and four were children, said a fire chief, Charles Hood. The patients were hot to the touch and dehydrated, and no water or air conditioning was found in the trailer, he said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Has anyone been arrested? Three people were taken into custody but it was unclear if they were connected to human trafficking, McManus said. \uc2 US Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (ICE) have launched a federal investigation into the deaths, with support of local police and the border force.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else do we know?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/28/san-antonio-what-we-know-about-the-trailer-truck-deaths"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s everything we know}}}\uc2  about the trailer truck deaths so far.\par \par \uc2 Louisiana judge blocks \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban amid uproar after Roe v Wade ruling\par \par \uc2 A Louisiana judge on Monday temporarily stopped the state from enforcing Republican-backed laws banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , about take effect after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ended the constitutional right to the procedure last week.\par \par \uc2 Louisiana is one of 13 states that passed \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger laws\u8221\'20\'1D to ban or severely restrict abortions once the supreme court overturned the 1973 Roe v Wade ruling that recognized a right to the procedure. It did so on Friday, stoking uproar among progressives, with protests and counter-protests on the streets of major cities.\par \par \uc2 In New Orleans on Monday, an Orleans parish civil district court judge, Robin Giarrusso, issued a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3OEBEbG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporary restraining order}}}\uc2 , blocking the state ban.\par \par \uc2 The case before Judge Giarrusso, a Democrat, was brought by Hope Medical Group for Women in Shreveport, one of three \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/louisiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to do what we can,\u8221\'20\'1D Kathaleen Pittman, administrator of Hope Medical Group, told the Associated Press. \u8220\'20\'1CIt [the work of the clinic] could all come to a screeching halt.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s happening in California? California voters will decide in November whether to guarantee the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/27/california-abortion-rights-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in their state constitution}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What has\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\par \par \uc2 said about the supreme court justices? The congresswoman says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/27/alexandria-ocasio-cortez-supreme-court-justices-impeach-kavanaugh-gorsuch-thomas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh and Neil Gorsuch lied under oath}}}\uc2  to Congress about their views on Roe.\par \par \uc2 21 people still missing after Kremenchuk shopping centre attack\par \par \uc2 At least 21 people are still missing after a Russian missile hit a crowded shopping centre in the central Ukrainian city of Kremenchuk yesterday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/jun/28/russia-ukraine-war-rescuers-dig-for-survivors-of-kremenchuk-shopping-centre-attack-amid-global-outrage-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukrainian prosecutors said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 About 18 people are believed to have been killed. Military personnel, volunteers, firefighters and police have been working non-stop to recover bodies from the rubble. Authorities estimated there were between 200 and 1,000 people inside the mall that afternoon. Many managed to flee to a nearby bomb shelter when they heard the air raid sirens but others did not make it in time and remained trapped in the building.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI left the building two minutes before the explosion,\u8217\'20\'19\u8217\'20\'19 said Yevhenia Semyonova, 38, a shop assistant at a sportswear shop. \u8220\'20\'1CMy colleagues who are working in bigger stores, like the supermarket for example, had to wait for the customers to get out before they could leave. We were lucky, because there were no customers in our store during the alarm.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What has Russia said about the attack? Russia\u8217\'20\'19s ministry of defence has claimed that the fire in the shopping mall was caused by \u8220\'20\'1Cthe detonation of stored ammunition for western weapons\u8221\'20\'1D. No evidence was offered to back up the claim.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House select committee investigating the January 6 Capitol attack is closely focused on phone calls and conversations among \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s children and top aides\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/28/january-6-hearings-focus-on-phone-calls-among-trumps-children-and-aides-weeks-before-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 captured by a documentary film-maker}}}\uc2  weeks before the 2020 election, say sources familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ghislaine Maxwell is scheduled to be sentenced this morning in her New York sex-trafficking case, six months after a jury found the British socialite guilty of luring teenage girls into Jeffrey Epstein\u8217\'20\'19s orbit for him to abuse. Maxwell, 60, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/28/ghislaine-maxwell-sentence-sex-trafficking-jeffrey-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faces up to 55 years in prison}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , has urged \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders gathered in Germany to help end the war in Ukraine by\par \par \uc2 winter as they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/27/zelenskiy-meets-g7-leaders-us-plans-air-defence-system-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 planned new economic measures against Russia}}}\uc2  and vowed to \u8220\'20\'1Cstand with Ukraine for as long as it takes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israel has eased its regulations on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, in what the health minister said was a response to last week\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Csad\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ruling overturning Roe v Wade. The new rules, approved by a parliamentary committee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/27/israel-eases-abortion-regulations-in-response-to-sad-roe-v-wade-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 grant women access to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills}}}\uc2  through Israel\u8217\'20\'19s universal health system.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: there have been at least 67 instances in which Scottish bills were vetted by the Queen\par \par \uc2 A Scottish government memo obtained by the Guardian reveals that \u8220\'20\'1Cit is almost certain\u8221\'20\'1D draft laws have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/jun/27/queen-secret-influence-laws-revealed-scottish-government-memo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 secretly changed to secure the Queen\u8217\'20\'19s approval}}}\uc2 . Under an arcane mechanism, the monarch is routinely given advance sight of proposed laws that could affect her personal property and public powers. In Scotland, where the procedure is known as crown consent, research by the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  identified at least 67 instances in which Scottish bills were vetted by the Queen.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: why we love to track our watching and reading habits\par \par \uc2 For millions of people, religiously tracking their cultural intake has become as instinctive as recording their steps, workouts, calorie count or periods. Letterboxd \u8211\'20\'13 dubbed \u8220\'20\'1Cthe social network for film-lovers\u8221\'20\'1D, who can log, review and discuss films with other members \u8211\'20\'13 recently hit 6 million members. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/jun/28/why-we-love-to-keep-tabs-on-what-were-watching-and-reading"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon-owned GoodReads}}}\uc2 , which has been doing the same for books for the past 15 years, has a community of 140 million. But does \u8220\'20\'1Cgamification\u8221\'20\'1D get in the way of actually enjoying the arts?\par \par \uc2 Climate check: climate\par \par \uc2 crisis clear in many extreme events but social factors also key, study finds\par \par \uc2 The climate crisis is to blame for most heatwaves recorded worldwide but its relationship with other extreme events and their effect on society is less clear, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jun/28/climate-change-heatwaves-droughts-study-weather"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a study}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI think on the one hand we overestimate climate change because it\u8217\'20\'19s now quite common that every time an extreme event happens, there is a big assumption that climate change is playing a big role, which is not always the case,\u8221\'20\'1D said Friederike Otto, one of the lead authors of the research.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: blow for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Truth Social as merger company hit by grand jury subpoenas\par \par \uc2 A ??US federal grand jury has issued subpoenas to the board members of the company merging with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s social media company, Truth Social. The disclosure by \uc2 Digital World Acquisition Corporation{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/27/truth-social-merger-trump-subpoenas-digital-world"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is the latest blow to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plans}}}\uc2  to take his Trump Media & Technology Group (TMTG) public. Truth Social was launched after Trump was banned from \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , where he had more than 88 million followers. Trump currently has 3.37 million followers on Truth Social.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220628ei6s001eb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
