\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Democrats hope to tap anger over Roe in November midterms \u8211\'20\'13 will it work?\b0\par\par\uc2 Edward Helmore in New York \par \uc2 1,048 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 June 2022\par 18:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 20\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Analysts say more voters should turn out in the wake of the supreme court ruling \u8211\'20\'13 but that could help Republicans too\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis fall, Roe is on the ballot,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  told American voters in the wake of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to scrap \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The US president was merely echoing a chorus of Democrats urging voters to elect pro \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights lawmakers in November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections in a bid to wrest greater control of Congress and perhaps allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to be enshrined in legislation.\par \par \uc2 But it is also a tactic to try and inject Democratic voters with a sense of urgency and activism as the midterms approach, as currently the political establishment expect Biden and the Democrats to face a defeat at the hands of a resurgent Republican party.\par \par \uc2 Until Roe fell \u8211\'20\'13 triggering a slew of Republican-led states to immediately move to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 Biden and his party have appeared moribund, and down in many polls. Buffeted by immense trouble passing a domestic agenda and hit by soaring inflation, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s popularity has plummeted.\par \par \uc2 But will the fall of Roe help Democrats reverse course on what looks like their current path to defeat? Or could the decision also help motivate the Republican base as the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision revealed the benefits to them of using power?\par \par \uc2 Hank Sheinkopf, a veteran Democrat strategist, said it was too soon to know how far the court\u8217\'20\'19s momentous decision to return the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue to individual US states would go toward shaping voter\u8217\'20\'19s priorities in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn states that Democrats do well generally, this will motivate turnout. In states where they do not do well, it will also motivate turnout \u8211\'20\'13 but not for the Democrats,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. \u8220\'20\'1CThe issue is purple states, like Michigan, Georgia and Nevada, where you have equal numbers of Democrats and Republicans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Four months out from November, voters are signaling that their priorities are rising crime, and inflation that has seen basic living costs shoot up for money, especially when it comes to gas prices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the question is will \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  help swing the election, the answer is probably not, though it could help in states where there\u8217\'20\'19s a reasonable balance between Democrats and Republicans,\u8221\'20\'1D Sheinkopf says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe presumption is that more women will turn out \u8211\'20\'13 but that depends on what\u8217\'20\'19s going in those states at the time. People will make their decisions based on what\u8217\'20\'19s most personal to them,\u8221\'20\'1D he adds. \u8220\'20\'1CSix or seven dollars a gallon of gasoline, a sense that things are out of control as the Democrats run the country, an increase in homicides nationally, may be better motivators for a majority of voters than Roe v Wade.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sonia Ossorio, the president of Now [\uc2 National Organization for Women\uc2 ] New York, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t see how this cannot energize voters. Women are fed up. Formula shortages, childcare shortages, gas prices, losing their jobs in unprecedented numbers during the pandemic, and now having our reproductive freedom gutted by the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe response we\u8217\'20\'19re getting is unprecedented in my two decades in the women\u8217\'20\'19s rights movement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s decision establishes political battlegrounds for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the 50 states. Already, many with conservative-leaning legislatures are banning or poised to ban many or most abortions. Nearly 400 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related laws have been passed across US states since 2009, with 85% designed to restrict, regulate or oppose access, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-06-08/roe-v-wade-abortion-rights-have-been-under-fire-in-these-states-the-past-decade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a Bloomberg News analysis}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kelsy Kretschmer, an associate professor of sociology at \uc2 Oregon State University\uc2 , and co-author of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://journals.sagepub.com/doi/abs/10.1177/1065912917702499"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a study}}}\uc2  examining women\u8217\'20\'19s voting patterns, says it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear that the decision will be help Democrats in a measurable way.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA significant proportion of white women are conservative and form the backbone of the pro-life movement and this is the thing they often care the most about. For Democrats, if you lose half of white women, you don\u8217\'20\'19t have a winning majority of women,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 There are splits, too, over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights even within Democrat-aligned voters, where conservative Democrats may oppose federal funding for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At the same time, Kretschmer says, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have long been part of the Democratic platform. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a core tenet of the Democratic party and most understand that outlawing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  completely is a non-starter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But predicting how Friday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling will affect November\u8217\'20\'19s vote is outside the scope of prior experience. When Roe v Wade was decided in 1973, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not play the public role in plays now.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe research is quite clear that people don\u8217\'20\'19t make voting decisions about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. People tend to have strong opinions one way or the other, but it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t tend to affect their vote choice,\u8221\'20\'1D Kretschmer says.\par \par \uc2 But she points out that this was prior to this moment in which Roe vs Wade may only be among the first of the women\u8217\'20\'19s rights dominos to fall or could open the way to repealing rights around contraception and marriage equality. \u8220\'20\'1CThe hope is among Democrats and the feminist movement in general, this time will be different and enough to shake people out of complacency about it,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve never really had a moment like this, where something so woven into basic political and civic life was ripped out all at once. That moment for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now and we\u8217\'20\'19ve just never seen it before. So the hope is just that \u8211\'20\'13 that this is a watershed moment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , the Democratic speaker of the House, certainly sees it that way. Voting for Democrats in November, she said, is the only way to try and reverse the fall of Roe \u8211\'20\'13 or prevent even worse things happening.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBe aware of this: The Republicans are plotting a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. They cannot be allowed to have a majority in the Congress to do that,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said. \u8220\'20\'1CA woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose, reproductive freedom, is on the ballot in November.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This article was updated on 27 June 2022 to correct Kelsy Kretschmer\u8217\'20\'19s credentials \u8211\'20\'13 she is at \uc2 Oregon State University\uc2 , no \uc2 UC Irvine\uc2 , as we originally said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220625ei6p000me\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
