\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Many US companies move to pay travel costs for employees seeking abortions\b0\par\par\uc2 Edward Helmore in New York \par \uc2 894 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 June 2022\par 15:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Tech firms and banks, including \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 , \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 , \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  and \uc2 JPMorgan Chase\uc2 , add \u8216\'20\'18critical healthcare\u8217\'20\'19 package\par \par \uc2 Many large US corporations have moved swiftly to provide support and financial assistance to employees seeking abortions in states that outlawed the procedure after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision on Friday to overturn its landmark Roe v Wade ruling.\par \par \uc2 With potentially millions of women soon looking to cross state lines for the procedure, many employers have added \u8220\'20\'1Ccritical healthcare\u8221\'20\'1D packages to employees\u8217\'20\'19 benefit packages.\par \par \uc2 The measures reflect, in some cases, elevated responsibility that businesses now feel to respond to pressure from investors, customers and employees at a time when corporate values do not conform with the legislatures of states in which they or their workers are based.\par \par \uc2 Many banks and tech firms have announced they will cover travel expenses for US workers in need of abortions as part of their medical benefits. After the reversal was announced Friday, \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  and \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  joined \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  and \uc2 JPMorgan Chase\uc2  in offering travel benefits.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will continue to provide benefits that support our colleagues\u8217\'20\'19 family planning choices wherever we are legally permitted to do so,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Citi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s head of human resources, \uc2 Sara Wechter\uc2 , wrote in a memo to employees on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Tech firms have also moved to accommodate employees\u8217\'20\'19 needs. \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  extended its financial support for \u8220\'20\'1Ccritical healthcare\u8221\'20\'1D after the draft version of the supreme court opinion overturning Roe was first leaked.\par \par \uc2 Apple\uc2  has said the existing benefits package allows employees to travel out of state for medical care, and \uc2 Facebook\uc2  parent \uc2 Meta\uc2  has said it will offer travel expense reimbursement \u8220\'20\'1Cto the extent permitted by law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In entertainment, \uc2 Disney\uc2 , Cond\u233\'00\'E9 Nast, \uc2 Warner Bros Discovery\uc2  and \uc2 Netflix\uc2  are among those that have said they will offer travel reimbursements.\par \par \uc2 While large companies can mitigate the supreme court ruling, the measures may not address the concerns of employees at firms that have in recent years located to low-tax states that have either enacted restrictions or essentially banned access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Texas, for instance, has been aggressively selling itself as a low-tax- and low-regulation home to companies such as \uc2 Oracle\uc2 , \uc2 Hewlett-Packard\uc2  and \uc2 Tesla\uc2 . \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , \uc2 Amazon\uc2  and \uc2 Apple\uc2  have all increased their presence there.\par \par \uc2 But the commitment of Texas, like Missouri, to a near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could now clash with those companies\u8217\'20\'19 stated values and harm the state\u8217\'20\'19s ability to attract new business, employees and investment.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, Texas state representative \uc2 Briscoe Cain\uc2  sent a cease-and-desist letter to \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 , saying he would propose legislation barring localities in the state from doing business with any company that provides travel benefits for employees seeking abortions.\par \par \uc2 The St Louis mayor, \uc2 Tishaura Jones\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tishaura/status/1540649513551106048"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a post to Twitter}}}\uc2  that she believes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans at the state level are going to make it harder to attract businesses. Kansas City mayor \uc2 Quinton Lucas\uc2  said one business has already backed out of setting up in the city.\par \par \uc2 But many large companies have stayed silent, including \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s, \uc2 PepsiCo\uc2 , \uc2 Coca-Cola\uc2 , \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , and Arkansas-based \uc2 Walmart\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the largest employer in the US with dozens of stores in states that have enacted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 The Business Roundtable, an organization that represents some of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful companies, has said it \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not have a position on the merits of the case\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps a more pressing concern is that for millions of people not employed by a large international or national company, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions present a more onerous challenge.\par \par \uc2 According to the pro-choice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/news-release/2022/us-supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Guttmacher Institute,}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and restrictions don\u8217\'20\'19t reduce unintended pregnancy or demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Rather, they impose significant hurdles to obtaining care, causing stress for people in need of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and leading some to experience forced pregnancy and all its troubling consequences.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvidence also shows the disproportionate and unequal impact \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions have on people who are already marginalized and oppressed \u8211\'20\'13 including Black and Brown communities, other people of color, people with low incomes, young people, LGBTQ communities, immigrants and people with disabilities,\u8221\'20\'1D Dr Hermania Palacio, the institute\u8217\'20\'19s president, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 In response, regional governments and community organizations have started outreach efforts to help anyone in need of the procedure. Baltimore\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, Brandon Scott, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kylegriffin1/status/1541104001520893953"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced }}}\uc2  that the city will provide $300,000 in grants to organizations that offer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and family planning.\par \par \uc2 Some left-leaning states have seen \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedures increase as surrounding states tightened access, even before Roe fell. In Illinois, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased by 25% between 2017 and 2020. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2022/06/long-term-decline-us-abortions-reverses-showing-rising-need-abortion-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Guttmacher said}}}\uc2  in response \u8220\'20\'1Clocal and national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds increased their capacity and helped even more people pay for their abortions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But with an increasingly fragmented and increasingly polarized {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://states.guttmacher.org/policies/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  landscape}}}\uc2 , many companies are likely to find themselves forced to respond to both pro-choice and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists while promising to promote women\u8217\'20\'19s equality and workplace advancement.\par \par \uc2 The issue of freedom to travel to other states for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedure issue has one notable, anti-Roe supporter. In his concurring opinion released Friday, Justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  said it would be unconstitutional for a state to impose travel restrictions. \u8220\'20\'1CIn my view, the answer is no, based on the constitutional right to interstate travel,\u8221\'20\'1D Kavanaugh wrote.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220626ei6q002bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
