\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 World leaders condemn US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ruling as \u8216\'20\'18backwards step\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Farrer and agencies \par \uc2 894 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 June 2022\par 10:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Leaders of UK, Canada, France and New Zealand denounce the overruling of Roe v Wade as WHO chief calls its \u8216\'20\'18disappointing\u8217\'20\'19See all our coverage of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision\par \par \uc2 The end of constitutional protections for abortions in the United States has been described as a \u8220\'20\'1Cbackwards\u8221\'20\'1D move by world leaders and health organisations, while handing a huge boost to anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups around the world.\par \par \uc2 The Canadian prime minister, \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2 , the French president, \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 , and the British prime minister, \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 , all condemned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overruling of the landmark Roe v Wade decision}}}\uc2 , while New Zealand\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Jacinda Ardern\uc2 , said the decision was \u8220\'20\'1Cincredibly upsetting\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWatching the removal of a woman\u8217\'20\'19s fundamental right to make decisions over their own body is incredibly upsetting,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHere in New Zealand we recently legislated to decriminalise \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and treat it as a health rather than criminal issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat change was grounded in the fundamental belief that it\u8217\'20\'19s a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose. People are absolutely entitled to have deeply held convictions on this issue. But those personal beliefs should never rob another from making their own decisions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo see that principle now lost in the United States feels like a loss for women everywhere. When there are so many issues to tackle, so many challenges that face women and girls, we need progress, not to fight the same fights and move backwards.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Johnson described the court ruling as a \u8220\'20\'1Cbig step backwards\u8221\'20\'1D, and hundreds took to the streets of London and Edinburgh to demonstrate against the decision.\par \par \uc2 Nicola Sturgeon\uc2 , leader of the Scottish Nationalist party, the third biggest party in the UK parliament, said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the darkest days for women\u8217\'20\'19s rights in my lifetime... this will embolden anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and anti-women forces in other countries too\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 One of the darkest days for women\u8217\'20\'19s rights in my lifetime. Obviously the immediate consequences will be suffered by women in the US - but this will embolden anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  & anti-women forces in other countries too. Solidarity doesn\u8217\'20\'19t feel enough right now - but it is necessary. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/T1656BPQuL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/T1656BPQuL}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Nicola Sturgeon\uc2  (@NicolaSturgeon) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NicolaSturgeon/status/1540339800338735104?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Trudeau said that \u8220\'20\'1Cno government, politician or man should tell a woman what she can and cannot do with her body\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that he \u8220\'20\'1Ccan\u8217\'20\'19t imagine the fear and anger\u8221\'20\'1D women in the US must be experiencing in the wake of the ruling.\par \par \uc2 No government, politician, or man should tell a woman what she can and cannot do with her body. I want women in Canada to know that we will always stand up for your right to choose.\u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  (@JustinTrudeau) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JustinTrudeau/status/1540362027507634177?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 French foreign ministry\uc2  urged US federal authorities \u8220\'20\'1Cto do everything possible\u8221\'20\'1D to ensure American women have continued access to abortions, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Chealth and survival issue\u8221\'20\'1D. France\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 , added in a tweet that \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a fundamental right of all women\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The former Australian prime minister \uc2 Julia Gillard\uc2  called on women to keep fighting for their rights and retweeted Michelle Obama\u8217\'20\'19s statement in which the former US first lady said she was \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbroken\u8221\'20\'1D about the decision.\par \par \uc2 I fully endorse these words and Michelle Obama\u8217\'20\'19s call to all of us to keep fighting for women\u8217\'20\'19s rights. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/j7x9ua2NXv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/j7x9ua2NXv}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Julia Gillard\uc2  (@JuliaGillard) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JuliaGillard/status/1540491941812772864?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus\uc2 , head of the \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2 , said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cconcerned and disappointed\u8221\'20\'1D by the ruling, and that it reduced both \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen\u8217\'20\'19s rights and access to health care\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN\uc2  agency dealing with sexual and reproductive health said that whether or not \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was legal, \u8220\'20\'1Cit happens all too often\u8221\'20\'1D and global data showed that restricting access made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  more deadly.\par \par \uc2 The United Nations population fund issued a statement following the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision noting that its 2022 report said that nearly half of all pregnancies worldwide were unintended and over 60% of those pregnancies might end in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA staggering 45% of all abortions around the world are unsafe, making this a leading cause of maternal death,\u8221\'20\'1D the agency said.\par \par \uc2 It said almost all unsafe abortions occured in developing countries, and it feared that \u8220\'20\'1Cmore unsafe abortions will occur around the world if access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  becomes more restricted\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s overturning of the landmark Roe v Wade decision \u8220\'20\'1Cshows that these types of rights are always at risk of being steamrolled\u8221\'20\'1D, said Ruth Zurbriggen, an Argentinian activist and member of the Companion Network of Latin America and the Caribbean, a group favouring \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 However, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists cheered the ruling, with legislator Amalia Granata tweeting: \u8220\'20\'1CThere is justice again in the world. We are going to achieve this in Argentina too!!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In El Salvador, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaigner Sara Lar\u237\'00\'EDn expressed hope the ruling would bolster campaigns against the procedure around the globe.\par \par \uc2 Lar\u237\'00\'EDn, president of Fundaci\u243\'00\'F3n Vida SV, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI trust that with this ruling it will be possible to abolish \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the United States and throughout the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 26 June 2022. A reference to \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life groups\u8221\'20\'1D was amended to \u8220\'20\'1Canti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups\u8221\'20\'1D in line with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/guardian-observer-style-guide-a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s style guide}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220627ei6r001jm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
