\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Monday briefing: How the end of Roe v Wade has already transformed America\b0\par\par\uc2 Archie Bland \par \uc2 2,059 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 June 2022\par 05:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In today\u8217\'20\'19s newsletter: in just three days, the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s monumental anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling has torn up old certainties about reproductive rights\u8226\'20\'22 Sign up here for our daily newsletter, First Edition\par \par \uc2 Good morning. It took almost half a century to overturn Roe v Wade, the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  decision that enshrined \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a constitutional right. But in the three days since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the court\u8217\'20\'19s new ruling was published}}}\uc2 , a settlement which Americans once assumed was permanent has been immediately shattered.\par \par \uc2 The conservative-majority court\u8217\'20\'19s decision allows individual states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time since 1973. (For a summary of what it means, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/24/scotus-roe-wade-decision-what-happens-next"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see this explainer by Jessica Glenza}}}\uc2 .) Like any supreme court ruling, the document published on Friday was long and complicated \u8211\'20\'13 but the consequences which flow from it are sweeping, and have proceeded at a pace which belies the court\u8217\'20\'19s claimed solemnity.\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s newsletter takes you through how much has already changed in this sudden new American era. First, here are the headlines.\par \par \uc2 Five big stories\par \par \uc2 Ukraine |\par \par \uc2 Boris Johnson implored world leaders at the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/26/boris-johnson-urges-world-leaders-to-hold-firm-on-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to stand firm in their support of Ukraine,}}}\uc2  after reports that some countries could be persuaded by calls for Ukraine to relinquish control over some territory for peace.\par \par \uc2 Monarchy\par \par \uc2 | Prince Charles {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/jun/26/prince-charles-calls-for-investigations-into-cash-in-bags-controversy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faced fresh controversy over the funding of his charities on Sunday}}}\uc2 , with calls for the government and \uc2 the Charity Commission\uc2  to investigate claims he accepted \u8364\'20\'AC3m in cash from a billionaire Qatari sheikh.\par \par \uc2 Labour |\par \par \uc2 Shadow foreign secretary \uc2 David Lammy\uc2  has said that the Labour party {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2022/jun/26/labour-heathrow-airline-staff-pay-dispute-unions-david-lammy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 should refuse to back airline workers who are demanding a 10% pay rise.}}}\uc2  Unite, Labour\u8217\'20\'19s biggest union donor, accused Lammy and Labour of launching a \u8220\'20\'1Cdirect attack\u8221\'20\'1D on workers.\par \par \uc2 Conservatives\par \par \uc2 | Boris Johnson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2022/jun/26/boris-johnson-tries-to-calm-tory-anger-over-his-third-term-remarks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed on Sunday}}}\uc2  that the record of his government was \u8220\'20\'1Cremarkable\u8221\'20\'1D as he continued to brush aside internal criticism. But he sought to defuse a row triggered by his declaration that he intended to stay in office until the 2030s by saying he simply meant he was focused on his reform agenda.\par \par \uc2 Brazil\par \par \uc2 | The British journalist Dom Phillips {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/26/murdered-british-journalist-dom-phillips-laid-to-rest-in-brazil"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been laid to rest in Brazil}}}\uc2 , exactly three weeks after he was gunned down with the Indigenous expert Bruno Pereira while they journeyed through the Amazon together.\par \par \uc2 In depth: What\u8217\'20\'19s happened since Roe was struck down?\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 In some states, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was banned the moment the court ruled\par \par \uc2 The picture in the immediate aftermath of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision was chaotic. But according to the pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights research group the Guttmacher institute, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/10/26-states-are-certain-or-likely-ban-abortion-without-roe-heres-which-ones-and-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26 states were certain or likely to ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  as quickly as possible after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade. In 10 of those states, \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger laws\u8221\'20\'1D have already been enforced to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  automatically or by rapid certification by officials, with three more expected within 30 days. Eight of those 13 only exclude cases where the mother\u8217\'20\'19s life is in danger \u8211\'20\'13 with no exception for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin and Michigan, two states with Democratic governors and public majorities in favour of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/25/us/abortion-laws-wisconsin-arizona-roe-overturned.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have antiquated laws on the books}}}\uc2  which could now come back into force \u8211\'20\'13 and Republican legislatures unwilling to repeal them. The laws \u8211\'20\'13 instituted in 1931 in Michigan and 1859 in Wisconsin \u8211\'20\'13 again make no exception for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Some states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/25/abortion-banned-in-multiple-us-states-just-hours-after-roe-v-wade-overturned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have promised to protect the right to an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . Lawmakers in California {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sacbee.com/news/politics-government/capitol-alert/article262785293.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are expected}}}\uc2  to enact a new constitutional amendment protecting reproductive rights today. But anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists are already turning towards a larger goal: a national, constitutional amendment banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  completely.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in many states have suspended services or closed completely\par \par \uc2 The New Yorker\u8217\'20\'19s Stephania Taladrid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/news/dispatch/roes-final-hours-in-one-of-americas-largest-abortion-clinics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was in an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  clinic in Houston, Texas}}}\uc2 , at the moment the supreme court ruling was published. Staff wept, hugged, and broke the news to patients in the waiting room. \u8220\'20\'1C Mi amor, the supreme court just ruled that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned in Texas,\u8221\'20\'1D Ivy, a supervisor, told one woman. \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot assist you.\u8221\'20\'1D By the end of the day, the clinic had closed.\par \par \uc2 Chabeli Carrazana {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/25/patients-abortion-texas-clinics-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported for the 19th and the Guardian}}}\uc2  on another clinic in Fort Worth, Texas, where people cried, screamed, and begged for help when they heard the news. In Arizona, where there is confusion over the standing of a 1901 ban, Planned Parenthood {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/25/arizona-planned-parenthood-abortion-state-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 halted procedures at all seven of its clinics}}}\uc2 . Clinics also closed in Alabama, Arkansas, Louisiana, South Dakota, West Virginia and Wisconsin. ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/25/how-to-support-abortion-access-rights-us-roe-wade-funds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 This piece}}}\uc2  sets out some ways to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the new climate, including donating to help keep such clinics open.)\par \par \uc2 One study {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Caitlin_K_Myers/status/1522540905881903104"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 produced in advance of the decision}}}\uc2  estimated that at least 100,000 women would be unable to secure an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  within the first year of a ban, and 75,000 would give birth as a result. The closest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider to New Orleans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/abortion-clinics-close-immediately-scramble-move-appointments-roe-ends-rcna35295"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is now in Illinois}}}\uc2 , more than 800 miles away.\par \par \uc2 Providers are trying to minimise this gap by bringing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as close to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban states as possible. Planned Parenthood {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-health-ontario-planned-parenthood-legislature-2136000ef6581d4a4c8da7399f440e50"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is renting office space in an Oregon town}}}\uc2  on the border with Idaho. Another organisation, Just The Pill, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://npr.org/sections/health-shots/2022/06/25/1107542054/with-just-8-abortion-clinics-minnesota-may-struggle-to-meet-out-of-state-demand"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is organising mobile clinics}}}\uc2  to come to state borders.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills has spiked\par \par \uc2 One significant change in the half-century since Roe v Wade is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/23/opinion/abortion-pills-online-roe-v-wade.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the rise of \u8220\'20\'1Cmedication \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 \u8221\'20\'1D through pills}}}\uc2 . They accounted for more than 50% of US abortions in 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2022/02/medication-abortion-now-accounts-more-half-all-us-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2 . President \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/25/biden-administration-signals-fight-stop-states-banning-abortion-pill-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said he would protect access to those drugs}}}\uc2  in the aftermath of Friday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling.\par \par \uc2 Just The Pill said that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/26/health/abortion-medication-pills.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 orders quadrupled on Friday alone}}}\uc2 , the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reported. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocacy group Plan C meanwhile {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/dozens-of-providers-in-red-states-move-to-prescribe-abortion-pills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Daily Beast}}}\uc2  that it had fielded 100 inquiries from clinicians interested in prescribing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills.\par \par \uc2 The delivery of drugs by post is likely to be difficult for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  states to completely stop, but legitimate providers will be subject to strict regulation, and their use will be limited by fears of the ramifications of a hospital visit for those using them illegally.\par \par \uc2 The haziness of the legal picture over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills is likely to create one of the major flashpoints in the post-Roe era. \u8220\'20\'1CWe haven\u8217\'20\'19t been in a situation where the \uc2 FDA\uc2  has approved a drug as safe and effective and you can use it legally in one state without any problem and then in another state it\u8217\'20\'19s banned,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Alina Salganicoff\uc2 , of the \uc2 Kaiser Family Foundation\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/health/health-news/end-roe-v-wade-access-abortion-pills-rcna34862"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told NBC}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 The legitimacy of the supreme court is more threatened than ever\par \par \uc2 It was one thing to hear progressives argue, as senator and former presidential candidate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/26/elizabeth-warren-democrats-question-supreme-court-legitimacy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elizabeth Warren did}}}\uc2 , that the supreme court has \u8220\'20\'1Cburned whatever legitimacy they may still have had\u8221\'20\'1D, or, as representative \uc2 Alexandra Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  tweeted, that the court now \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1540755944207896576"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has a legitimacy crisis}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D with \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1540755940542119938"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 7 of the 9 justices appointed by a party that hasn\u8217\'20\'19t won a popular vote more than once in 30 years}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 More alarming for defenders of the court were the interventions of pro-choice Republican Susan Collins and conservative pro-choice Democrat Joe Manchin, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/25/gorsuch-kavanaugh-misled-senators-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who said}}}\uc2  that they were misled by Trump appointees \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 . Kavanaugh and Gorsuch claimed they would not overturn Roe in public and (according to notes produced by Collins) private statements before Senate votes on their appointment to the court.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/americans-react-to-roe-v-wade-overturn-opinion-poll-2022-06-26/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a snap poll conducted by CBS}}}\uc2  found that Americans disapprove of the decision by a near-20 point margin. And as David Smith notes in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/jun/26/us-supreme-court-abortion-ruling-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this piece}}}\uc2 , those saying they have faith in the court has dropped to a historic low of 25%.\par \par \uc2 Whatever the status of the court, though, many progressives said that they viewed its future as \u8211\'20\'13 for now \u8211\'20\'13 a secondary concern. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s nothing sacrosanct about nine members of the United States supreme court, but that is a long term question,\u8221\'20\'1D Georgia gubernatorial candidate \uc2 Stacey Abrams{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/videos/politics/2022/06/26/abrams-on-scotus.cnn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN yesterday}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we have to focus on right now is the danger that this decision presents to women \u8230\'20\'26 across the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 What else we\u8217\'20\'19ve been reading\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2022/jun/25/cocaine-class-everyone-in-this-town-takes-drugs-all-the-time"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tabitha Lasley\u8217\'20\'19s memoir}}}\uc2  of cocaine use in the chicken shop where she used to work is a corrective to the idea the drug is a solely middle-class indulgence. \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone takes drugs, all the time,\u8221\'20\'1D she writes. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re part of the civic culture.\u8221\'20\'1D Archie\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hope is not some naive luxury in the face of the supreme court ruling on Roe v Wade, writes Rebecca Traister, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thecut.com/2022/06/rebecca-traister-on-the-necessity-of-hope.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this clarion piece for The Cut}}}\uc2  : it is a \u8220\'20\'1Ctactical necessity\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile it is incumbent on us to digest the scope and breadth of the badness,\u8221\'20\'1D she writes, \u8220\'20\'1Cit is equally our responsibility not to despair.\u8221\'20\'1D Archie\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The rail strikes{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/26/if-rmt-wins-other-workers-will-push-back-quite-right"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have disrupted many people\u8217\'20\'19s lives}}}\uc2 , but Kenan Malik argues that most people understand why unions have decided to strike, adding that, despite significant decline in the last few decades, unions still play a significant role in making the UK a fairer place to live and work. Nimo\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In his parenting column, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2022/jun/26/seamas-oreilly-column-our-four-year-old-is-running-rings-around-me"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 S\u233\'00\'E9amas O\u8217\'20\'19Reilly writes}}}\uc2  about the conversations he\u8217\'20\'19s been having with his highly inquisitive four-year-old. Nimo\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Charlotte Higgins, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s chief culture writer, had never been to Glastonbury : she likes the Proms, Glyndebourne, and functioning sewers. Her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2022/jun/26/a-classicist-at-glastonbury-headbanging-in-rain-coats-its-as-english-as-gardeners-question-time"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first-time dispatch}}}\uc2  is a joy: Glasto, she concludes, is \u8220\'20\'1Ceither a highly advanced form of civilisation, or the opposite\u8221\'20\'1D. Archie\par \par \uc2 Sport\par \par \uc2 Cricket\par \par \uc2 | England {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jun/26/england-new-zealand-third-test-day-four-match-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are on the verge of a 3-0 series win}}}\uc2  against New Zealand after Ollie Pope and Joe Root led their side to 183-2 in pursuit of 296 after Jack Leach took five wickets. Meanwhile, England\u8217\'20\'19s one-day captain Eoin Morgan is understood to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jun/26/eoin-morgan-ponders-international-retirement-amid-form-and-fitness-woes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 considering retirement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Tennis | Emma Raducanu {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jun/26/emma-raducanu-centre-court-debut-wimbledon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will make her centre court debut as Wimbledon gets underway on Monday}}}\uc2 , playing against grass court veteran Alison Van Uytvanck. Andy Murray will also play on centre court.\par \par \uc2 Football\par \par \uc2 | Gabriel Jesus {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2022/jun/26/gabriel-jesus-agrees-five-year-deal-to-join-arsenal-from-manchester-city"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is poised to join Arsenal from Manchester City after agreeing personal terms on a five-year deal}}}\uc2 . The striker will move for a fee of \u163\'00\'A345m following an agreement between the two clubs.\par \par \uc2 The front pages\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lead story is \u8220\'20\'1CDo not give ground on Ukraine, PM tells leaders\u8221\'20\'1D and the FT also goes with the latest from the summit in Germany: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 G7\uc2  aims to hurt Russian war chest with price cap on crude exports\u8221\'20\'1D. The Telegraph has \u8220\'20\'1CBiden to block PM\u8217\'20\'19s answer to food crisis\u8221\'20\'1D while \u8220\'20\'1CLeaders seek united front away from turmoil at home\u8221\'20\'1D is the splash in the i paper. The housing market is the lead in the Express \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1CRush to cash in on homes before \u8216\'20\'18crash\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and the Mail focuses on scammers: \u8220\'20\'1CBritain is \u163\'00\'A33bn fraud capital of the world\u8221\'20\'1D. The Mirror\u8217\'20\'19s lead is \u8220\'20\'1CTrue horror of \uc2 NHS\uc2  dentist crisis\u8221\'20\'1D while the Sun picks up the latest royal travails: \u8220\'20\'1CCharles \u8216\'20\'18cash in bag\u8217\'20\'19 probe\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Today in Focus\par \par \uc2 Can Colombia\u8217\'20\'19s first leftwing president deliver change?\par \par \uc2 Gustavo Petro\uc2  has been elected as the Latin American country\u8217\'20\'19s first leftist leader. But he faces a huge challenge if he is to deliver on his promises, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2022/jun/27/colombia-first-leftwing-president-gustavo-petro-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says Joe Parkin Daniels}}}\par \par \uc2 Cartoon of the day | Nicola Jennings\par \par \uc2 The Upside\par \par \uc2 A bit of good news to remind you that the world\u8217\'20\'19s not all bad\par \par \uc2 Dr Laura Marshall-Andrews (above) loves her job as a general practitioner, but she is acutely aware of the crisis gripping GP clinics across the country. To try and make a difference in one clinic, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2022/jun/26/better-ways-to-get-better-the-radical-gp-changing-lives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marshall-Andrews decided to include different methods for her patients,}}}\uc2  offering dance classes, art and foraging, for holistic treatments that try to improve people\u8217\'20\'19s quality of life more generally.\par \par \uc2 Marshall-Andrew argues that social prescribing reduces pressure on the \uc2 NHS\uc2 , citing a study that showed that every \u163\'00\'A31 spent on arts in health saves the \uc2 NHS\uc2  \u163\'00\'A311. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople, I realised, are not textbooks.\u8221\'20\'1D Marshall-Andrew says, \u8220\'20\'1Cthey are far more complicated than that, and far more interesting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/feb/12/the-upside-sign-up-for-our-weekly-email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up here}}}\uc2  for a weekly roundup of The Upside, sent to you every Sunday\par \par \uc2 Bored at work?\par \par \uc2 And finally, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s crosswords to keep you entertained throughout the day \u8211\'20\'13 with plenty more on the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Puzzles app for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.apple.com/app/id1487780661?mt=8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 iOS}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=uk.co.guardian.puzzles&hl=en_GB&gl=US"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Android}}}\uc2 . Until tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/crosswords/quick/16267"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Quick crossword}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/crosswords/cryptic/28794"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptic crossword}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220627ei6r000p3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
