\par\par \uc2 Australia news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Devastating\u8217\'20\'19: Australian politicians respond to \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Daniel Hurst \par \uc2 521 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 June 2022\par 01:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Some politicians say decision in Roe v Wade will \u8216\'20\'18save lives\u8217\'20\'19 but prime minister emphasises \u8216\'20\'18in Australia, this is not a matter for partisan political debate\u8217\'20\'19Get our free news app ; get our morning email briefing\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to wind back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is \u8220\'20\'1Ca setback for women and their right to control their own bodies and their lives\u8221\'20\'1D, the Australian prime minister, Anthony Albanese, has said.\par \par \uc2 The minister for women, Katy Gallagher, said the \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastating\u8221\'20\'1D decision, while directly affecting people in America, also reinforced the need for Australians \u8220\'20\'1Cto remain vigilant because hard-fought-for wins before our parliaments can be taken away easily\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  on Friday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned a ruling}}}\uc2  that had guaranteed a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for almost half a century, with at least 26 states expected to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  immediately or as soon as practicable.\par \par \uc2 Albanese, who was flying to Spain for a Nato summit on Monday morning, responded to the ruling by saying people were \u8220\'20\'1Centitled to their own views, but not to impose their views on women for whom this is a deeply personal decision\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is, in my view, one for an individual woman to make based upon their own circumstances, including the health implications,\u8221\'20\'1D Albanese told the ABC AM program in an interview broadcast on Monday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis decision has caused enormous distress. And it is a setback for women and their right to control their own bodies and their lives in the United States. It is a good thing that in Australia, this is not a matter for partisan political debate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/guardian-australia-morning-mail/2014/jun/24/-sp-guardian-australias-morning-mail-subscribe-by-email?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up to receive an email with the top stories from Guardian Australia every morning}}}\par \par \uc2 Gallagher echoed Albanese when she said it had been fortunate in Australia that this issue has not been at the \u8220\'20\'1Ccentre of our politics\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the decision over the weekend in America was devastating for many women,\u8221\'20\'1D Gallagher told ABC Radio National.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CObviously it directly affects women in America and we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing some of that on our TVs at the moment and I know that many women who have reached out to me over the weekend feel the impact of this decision here locally and right across the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gallagher underlined the need for termination procedures to remain safe and legal in Australia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVigilance is the message \u8211\'20\'13 to make sure women in Australia have access to safe and legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that that matter is resolved between her and her medical practitioner,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Several Australian politicians cheered the US decision.\par \par \uc2 The Queensland Liberal National party senator \uc2 Matt Canavan\uc2  tweeted: \u8220\'20\'1CA wonderful day to protect human life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bernie Finn, a Victorian state MP who was expelled from the Liberal party over his comments that survivors of rape should not be allowed abortions, said the US decision was \u8220\'20\'1Ca momentous day for humanity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy very warmest congratulations to my friends in the United States who have been fighting for years to overturn Roe,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote on \uc2 Facebook\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis will save lives. This is just the beginning.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220627ei6r0005l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
