\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The Observer view on Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s influence on Roe v Wade ruling\b0\par\par\uc2 Observer editorial \par \uc2 700 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 June 2022\par 07:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s legacy and he must face prosecution for abuse of power\par \par \uc2 The baleful influence of Donald Trump continues to be felt in American life despite his decisive election defeat in 2020 and subsequent disgraceful behaviour. The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s regressive, dangerous and insulting decision to abolish a woman\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was made possible by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s appointment of three highly conservative justices who all voted for the change.\par \par \uc2 This disaster is not all Trump\u8217\'20\'19s doing. A noisy anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lobby of rightwing Republicans and evangelical Christians has fought for decades to scrap the 1973 Roe v Wade ruling giving women the right to choose. But they represent, at most, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2022/06/24/politics/americans-roe-v-wade-polling/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one-third of Americans}}}\uc2 . Trump adopted their minority view for the same reason he champions the gun lobby \u8211\'20\'13 for electoral advantage.\par \par \uc2 Although the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision was anticipated, it is still a tremendous shock \u8211\'20\'13 as ensuing nationwide protests suggest. The speed with which some Republican-controlled states are moving to outlaw or restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also dismaying. The fear is that the other hard-won privacy rights and freedoms, such as the right to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/clarence-thomas-roe-gay-marriage-contraception-lgbtq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contraception and same-sex marriage}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/may/08/the-observer-view-on-us-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may be threatened}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Seeking to limit divisions, the chief justice, \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/24/us/abortion-supreme-court-roberts.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had hoped to limit}}}\uc2  Roe v Wade rather than abolish it outright. The Trump justices\u8217\'20\'19 willingness to take the most extreme option will further undermine public confidence in the court, damaged like other US institutions by the political partisanship of the \u8220\'20\'1Cculture wars\u8221\'20\'1D era.\par \par \uc2 It has long been evident Trump lacks strong religious or moral convictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . As always, his motives are self-serving\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  described the ruling as a \u8220\'20\'1Csad day\u8221\'20\'1D, while outraged Democrats say they will try to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in federal law. To do so, they need to win big in November\u8217\'20\'19s congressional midterm elections. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are thus certain to be a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/us-states-abortion-rights-california-oregon-washington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 central issue}}}\uc2  in the autumn campaign and the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Trump will relish that. As is his wont, he claimed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2022/06/24/roe-v-wade-decision-trump-takes-credit-for-supreme-court-abortion-ruling.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 personal credit}}}\uc2  for the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, saying it was his \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat honour\u8221\'20\'1D to have made it possible. Yet it has long been evident he lacks strong religious or moral convictions about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or anything else. As always, his motives are self-serving. Even erstwhile diehard supporters tire of such cynicism. There is evidence that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/23/trump-january-6-hearings-allies-fallout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump fatigue}}}\uc2  is setting in.\par \par \uc2 Proof of that contention has been on display in recent days on Capitol Hill, where an investigation into the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/09/january-6-hearing-five-key-takeaways-us-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 6 January 2021 insurrection}}}\uc2  is providing jaw-dropping testimony about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s undeniable criminal culpability. From the moment he realised Biden was winning on election night in November 2020, Trump began a concerted, deliberate and illegal effort to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reverse the result}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Abusing the power of his office, Trump intimidated officials in Georgia and other swing states in a move to fiddle the vote, knowingly disseminated false claims of fraud and conspiracy theories, and dangled promises of presidential pardons for those who supported his coup attempt. \u8220\'20\'1CJust say the election is corrupt and leave the rest to me,\u8221\'20\'1D senior justice department officials said Trump told them.\par \par \uc2 When none of that worked, he openly incited white supremacist groups such as the Proud Boys to attack Congress to prevent certification of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory. When they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/12/trump-capitol-attack-rioters-mike-pence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened to hang}}}\uc2  his vice-president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , for refusing to invalidate the election outcome, he applauded. \u8220\'20\'1CMaybe our supporters have the right idea,\u8221\'20\'1D he reportedly told aides. Pence \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/06/10/jan6-trump-pence-deserves-hanged-cheney-capitol/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deserves it}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Like the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate, this is not over. Clinging to his \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D, Trump claims everything else is a hoax. As ever, he subverts American democracy. But he has been weakened and now is not the time to let him off the hook. Trump plainly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/24/opinion/trump-jan-6-prosecution.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broke numerous laws}}}\uc2 . Most Americans agree: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/10-americans-trump-charged-jan-riot-poll/story?id=85482369"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he must face criminal prosecution}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Do you have an opinion on the issues raised in this article? If you would like to submit a letter of up to 250 words to be considered for publication, email it to us at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:observer.letters@observer.co.uk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 observer.letters@observer.co.uk}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220629ei6q002pn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
