\par\par \uc2 Australia news\par \b \uc2 Morning mail: fury over \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ruling, census data due, mystery nightclub deaths\b0\par\par\uc2 Melissa Godin \par \uc2 1,212 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 June 2022\par 21:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Monday : Protesters have taken to the streets of cities across the US to voice their anger at a ruling that overturned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Plus: why teachers are leaving the profession in drovesWant to get the morning mail to your email inbox every weekday? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning. Anger has flared across the US after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade. New census data will show how Covid changed Australia. And 22 young people have been found dead at a bar and nightclub in South Africa.\par \par \uc2 Protests against a supreme court decision that overturned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have continued across the US this weekend. In New York, thousands marched to voice their anger at the ruling that came at the end of a dizzying week surrounding not just reproductive rights but also gun carry laws and the US Capitol attack. \u8220\'20\'1CNot your uterus, not your choice,\u8221\'20\'1D many shouted at demonstrations in Washington DC, Chicago, Los Angeles, Seattle, Atlanta and Austin. In Providence, Rhode Island, tempers flared so much that an off-duty police officer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/26/abortion-rights-protests-across-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was accused of punching a woman at an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  protest}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Australians are about to get a clearer idea of how we are changing as a nation, and how the Covid pandemic changed us, when results from the 2021 census are released. On Tuesday the \uc2 Australian Bureau of Statistics\uc2  will release the first tranche of data covering topics such as population flows between cities and regional areas, how Australians are housed, the languages we use, Indigenous health and education, employment and unpaid rates of work. Demographers are eagerly anticipating the release as a snapshot of mid-pandemic Australia. But they are cautioning that on an initial glance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/27/older-whiter-and-smaller-new-census-data-to-show-how-covid-changed-australia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the results will tell two very different stories}}}\uc2  : on the night the census was taken, 10 August 2021, half the country was in lockdown while other states enjoyed some of the most relaxed rules on internal movement during the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Police forensic teams in South Africa are investigating the deaths of 22 young people at a nightclub and bar in the southern coastal town of East London. Specialists have yet to establish the cause of the tragedy, which occurred during end of school year celebrations by teenagers. Local residents raised the alarm about 4am, officials said. \uc2 Bheki Cele\uc2 , the police minister, tried to calm an angry crowd of relatives and residents at the cordoned-off crime site at Enyobeni Tavern in a poor neighbourhood known as Scenery Park. \u8220\'20\'1CAt first, we were told that this was a stampede, but by the looks of things, there was no stampede that took place,\u8221\'20\'1D Cele said. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/26/south-africa-nightclub-deaths-east-london"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Toxicology tests will established if the casualties were poisoned}}}\uc2 , officials said.\par \par \uc2 Australia\par \par \uc2 Peter Dutton\uc2  has warned the NSW Liberal party it is \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely unacceptable\u8221\'20\'1D to preselect candidates\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/26/peter-dutton-says-nsw-liberal-party-preselection-delays-were-completely-unacceptable"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on the eve of an election}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Experts warn the region\u8217\'20\'19s marine environment is undergoing a \u8220\'20\'1Cdynamic state of change\u8221\'20\'1D due to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/27/oyster-and-kelp-farmers-join-calls-to-future-proof-nsw-south-coasts-blue-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 climate warming}}}\uc2 , freshwater runoff and storms.\par \par \uc2 The education minister has blasted Senator \uc2 Hollie Hughes\uc2  for \u8220\'20\'1Ccrazy\u8221\'20\'1D comments blaming the Liberals\u8217\'20\'19 low youth vote on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/26/education-system-run-by-marxists-jason-clare-takes-aim-at-liberal-senator-over-comments-on-teachers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMarxist\u8221\'20\'1D teachers}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jim Chalmers has warned of \u8220\'20\'1Csignificantly higher\u8221\'20\'1D inflation and suggested a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/26/jim-chalmers-says-inflation-will-go-higher-but-unions-are-right-to-push-for-higher-wages"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 workers\u8217\'20\'19 representative could soon be appointed}}}\uc2  to the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  board.\par \par \uc2 Four frog species in Western Australia that lay their eggs on land have been identified as a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/27/frogs-that-lay-eggs-on-land-new-genus-named-after-wa-teacher-whose-lab-was-a-campervan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new genus}}}\uc2  and named after a retired high school music teacher-turned-scientist.\par \par \uc2 The world\par \par \uc2 Boris Johnson has warned about the likelihood of \u8220\'20\'1Cfatigue\u8221\'20\'1D among western nations over continued support for Ukraine as he began talks at the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit in Germany, where he hopes to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/26/boris-johnson-warns-of-risk-of-fatigue-in-wests-support-for-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 push for renewed sanctions}}}\uc2  against Russia. Kyiv was hit by four Russian missile strikes early yesterday morning for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/26/russian-missiles-strike-kyiv-ukraine-first-time-three-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first time in three weeks}}}\uc2 , during which life had been slowly returning to the Ukrainian capital.\par \par \uc2 Ecuador has been brought to a near standstill after two weeks of tumultuous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/25/ecuador-at-standstill-after-two-weeks-of-protests-over-cost-of-living-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protests over a spike in fuel and food prices }}}\uc2  as global inflation inflames discontent over widening inequality across Latin America.\par \par \uc2 The British journalist Dom Phillips has been laid to rest in Brazil, three weeks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/26/murdered-british-journalist-dom-phillips-laid-to-rest-in-brazil"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after he was gunned down}}}\uc2  while journeying through the Amazon with the Indigenous expert Bruno Pereira.\par \par \uc2 Recommended reads\par \par \uc2 No educator is surprised by the teacher drought Australia is now in. They\u8217\'20\'19ve been watching the landscape change over the years, observing the weather patterns that don\u8217\'20\'19t bode well. And now they\u8217\'20\'19re leaving. Rivers of teachers drying up and no rain in sight. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/27/i-cant-stay-its-not-enough-why-are-teachers-leaving-australian-schools"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why does a teacher shortage occur}}}\uc2  ? Ultimately, it\u8217\'20\'19s because our education system is operating under a business model which treats students and parents as customers and teachers as expendable workers expected to function as told, rather than as autonomous professionals tasked with the unique and complex responsibility of guiding young people\u8217\'20\'19s learning.\par \par \uc2 At first my daughter was excited about visiting the city of my birth \u8211\'20\'13 Karachi, Pakistan, writes Saman Shad. After all, it was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/27/showing-my-daughter-pakistan-the-country-of-my-birth-reminded-me-i-am-part-of-something-bigger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 half her heritage}}}\uc2  and she\u8217\'20\'19d heard about all the family over there she had yet to meet. But I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t hide from her how nervous I felt. It had been 15 years since I was last back; the negative western media headlines rang loudly in my head. How would I be received by the people who last saw me as a young, childless woman?\par \par \uc2 Before her British stage debut in The Seagull, the Game of Thrones star Emilia Clarke\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2022/jun/26/emilia-clarke-games-of-thrones-last-christmas-seagull-the-best-place-in-the-world-is-backstage-at-a-theatre"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 talks about her self-doubt}}}\uc2  as the hit show took off, her decision to write about her brain aneurysms \u8211\'20\'13 and showing her love through baking.\par \par \uc2 Listen\par \par \uc2 After the UK home secretary decided to extradite Julian Assange to face trial and a possible life sentence in the US, Ben Quinn reports on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/audio/2022/jun/27/whats-at-stake-in-the-extradition-of-julian-assange"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what the ruling means}}}\uc2  for the \uc2 WikiLeaks\uc2  founder \u8211\'20\'13 and for press freedom.\par \par \uc2 Full Story is Guardian Australia\u8217\'20\'19s daily news podcast. Subscribe for free on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://podcasts.apple.com/au/podcast/full-story/id1482061243"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Apple Podcasts}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://open.spotify.com/show/7GJod4EyoLywB1AW6zrSHh?si=mbMJnUPiSO2snfF0jNw7jw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Spotify}}}\uc2  or any other podcasting app.\par \par \uc2 Sport\par \par \uc2 Outfoxed by a rookie coach, widely criticised for his team selection and ultimately ambushed and humiliated in front of a record crowd at home, Brad Fittler had both feet in the furnace. But the Blues coach held his nerve all week and now has his mojo back as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jun/26/nathan-cleary-leads-way-as-nsw-roar-back-to-level-state-of-origin-series-with-queensland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NSW dominated their old foes}}}\uc2  to level the State of \uc2 Origin\uc2  series with a thumping 44-12 Game 2 victory.\par \par \uc2 Media roundup\par \par \uc2 The Sydney Morning Herald reports on what overturning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.smh.com.au/national/what-overturning-roe-v-wade-means-for-australia-20220625-p5awk9.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  means for Australia. Accessing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theage.com.au/national/abortion-access-in-parts-of-australia-remains-very-dire-experts-say-20220626-p5awp3.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 postcode lottery}}}\uc2  for women across regional Australia 12 months after South Australia became the final jurisdiction in the country to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal, experts say, according to the Age. And the ABC\u8217\'20\'19s Four Corners {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.abc.net.au/news/2022-06-27/inside-the-thriving-black-market-for-nicotine-vapes/101176544"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigates Australia\u8217\'20\'19s thriving black market }}}\uc2  for nicotine vapes.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 If you would like to receive the Guardian Australia morning mail to your email inbox every weekday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/guardian-australia-morning-mail/2014/jun/24/-sp-guardian-australias-morning-mail-subscribe-by-email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sign up here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Discover Australian Weekend\par \par \uc2 Every Saturday from 6am, enjoy early access to the best journalism planned for the weekend in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/ng-interactive/2021/mar/17/make-sense-of-the-week-with-australia-weekend"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one elegant app}}}\uc2 , plus a curated selection of the week\u8217\'20\'19s news and analysis from Australia and the world.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220626ei6q002e5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
