\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The Guardian view on overturning Roe v Wade: anti-abortionists reign supreme\b0\par\par\uc2 Editorial \par \uc2 619 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 June 2022\par 16:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The removal of women\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will deepen hardship and division in the US\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision}}}\uc2 , when it came on Friday, was not a surprise. Even before the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/may/03/the-guardian-view-on-overturning-roe-v-wade-a-human-rights-catastrophe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dramatic leak}}}\uc2  of Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s draft opinion last month, it was widely predicted that the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  would grab the opportunity presented by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/explainer-mississippi-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization case}}}\uc2  to rescind the decision made in 1973 in Roe v Wade. This, after all, was the purpose of President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s three supreme court selections \u8211\'20\'13 and the culmination of a decades-long campaign by anti-abortionists to return to states the authority to ban the procedure. But the announcement still came as a shock. The US\u8217\'20\'19s global influence means that the decision to remove a woman\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  there {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/may/05/the-guardian-view-on-what-follows-roe-v-wade-it-doesnt-stop-here"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reverberates far beyond its shores}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/abortion-laws-by-state-map-clinics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 speed with which multiple US states reacted}}}\uc2  is disturbing; already, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/us/abortion-laws-roe-v-wade.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outlawed in 10}}}\uc2 , with 11 more expected to follow shortly. While all women should be entitled to control their own lives and bodies, there are instances when denying this is particularly cruel. Americans who oppose forced pregnancy and birth now face the horror of rape and incest victims, including children, being compelled to become mothers. The US is exceptional in its lack of federal maternity provisions; children as well as parents will suffer the consequences of unwanted additions to their families, with poor and black people the worst affected.\par \par \uc2 Early signs are that the most extreme Republican legislatures could try to block girls and women from travelling out of state for treatment, and impose further restrictions on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/07/us-mail-order-abortions-oklahoma"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 care delivered remotely}}}\uc2  including medication sent by mail. The potential for personal data stored online, including on menstrual apps, to be used against women is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/25/abortion-war-against-women-in-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 causing justified alarm}}}\uc2 . Having relied on Roe v Wade to protect access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for half a century, politicians can no longer do so. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now set to become a key issue in this autumn\u8217\'20\'19s midterms.\par \par \uc2 How this pans out will depend on public opinion; polling data suggest that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/1576/abortion.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 85% of Americans}}}\uc2  support legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in some circumstances, and Democrats hope that this could work to their advantage. But the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  right is a formidable force. With hindsight, President Obama\u8217\'20\'19s decision not to codify Roe v Wade into federal law, and Justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2014/feb/14/ruth-bader-ginsburg-retire-liberal-judge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s choice not to retire when he could have nominated a replacement, look like disastrous errors.\par \par \uc2 The three liberal justices who dissented said they did so with sorrow for \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/24/supreme-court-roe-v-wade-breyer-sotomayor-kegan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many millions of American women}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and also for the court itself. With this decision, it has chosen to reopen deep wounds. The 14th amendment on which Roe v Wade rested granted rights to former slaves, and is the basis for other crucial decisions including on same-sex marriage. By dismissing Roe v Wade in the way that they did, and against the wishes of Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  (who argued to retain it, while allowing Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s 15-week rule to stand), the court\u8217\'20\'19s hard-right wing has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/jun/26/us-supreme-court-abortion-ruling-democracy?utm_term=Autofeed&CMP=twt_gu&utm_medium&utm_source=Twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seized control}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Unprecedented division, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/24/overturning-roe-story-is-women-unfreedom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 greatly increased hardship and risk}}}\uc2  for those denied safe healthcare, will be the outcome. While there is reassurance in noting moves elsewhere towards liberalisation, US anti-abortionists are far from unique, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2022/jan/27/protests-flare-across-poland-after-death-of-young-mother-denied-an-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tightened restrictions in Poland }}}\uc2  and the situation in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/may/19/uk-abortion-services-delivery-northern-ireland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Northern Ireland}}}\uc2  show. It is too soon to say whether Trump\u8217\'20\'19s justices and their backers have overreached from an electoral perspective. If there is an early lesson to be drawn, it is that once gained, women\u8217\'20\'19s rights must be constantly defended.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220626ei6q001s0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
