\par\par \uc2 Australia news\par \b \uc2 Australian politicians respond to US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  decision \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Cait Kelly and Graham Readfearn (earlier) \par \uc2 5,832 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 June 2022\par 08:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Sussan Ley\uc2  and Jason Clare react to \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights; Australia to send $1m earthquake relief to Afghanistan ; nation records 26 Covid deaths. This blog is now closedEducation system \u8216\'20\'18run by Marxists\u8217\'20\'19: Jason Clare takes aim at Liberal senator over comments on teachersPeter Dutton says NSW Liberal party preselection delays were \u8216\'20\'18completely unacceptable\u8217\'20\'19Ministers defend cut to crossbenchers\u8217\'20\'19 advisers, despite fury of \uc2 Jacqui Lambie\uc2  and other independentsJim Chalmers says inflation will go higher, but unions are right to push for higher wagesVictorian government\u8217\'20\'19s new frontbenchGet our free news app ; get our morning email briefing\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38am BST\par \par \uc2 What we learned, Sunday 26 June\par \par \uc2 And with that, it is time to put this blog to bed \u8211\'20\'13 it was a rather quiet Sunday. Before we wrap it all up, let\u8217\'20\'19s go through the big stories:\par \par \uc2 * Treasurer \uc2 Jim Chalmers\uc2  flagged that inflation \u8211\'20\'13 at 5.1% in the March quarter \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2022/jun/26/australia-news-live-updates-daniel-andrews-defends-new-ministers-federal-crossbenchers-livid-live?page=with:block-62b79a848f0867712f95f9b5#block-62b79a848f0867712f95f9b5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is likely to keep climbing and could go higher than 7%}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2022/jun/26/australia-news-live-updates-daniel-andrews-defends-new-ministers-federal-crossbenchers-livid-live?page=with:block-62b7a1738f0875bb61abbb95#block-62b7a1738f0875bb61abbb95"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sussan Ley and Jason Clare}}}\uc2  weighed in on the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, with Ley declaring it \u8216\'20\'18a step backwards for women\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2022/jun/26/australia-news-live-updates-daniel-andrews-defends-new-ministers-federal-crossbenchers-livid-live?page=with:block-62b7b7b08f0867712f95fa2b#block-62b7b7b08f0867712f95fa2b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Commonwealth leaders pushed for Covid and climate action}}}\uc2  at a Chogm meeting in Rwanda.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2022/jun/26/australia-news-live-updates-daniel-andrews-defends-new-ministers-federal-crossbenchers-livid-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62b7f5888f0875bb61abbcd2#block-62b7f5888f0875bb61abbcd2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Beekeepers across New South Wales could be banned from moving their honey and hives}}}\uc2  after the detection of a deadly invasive mite in Newcastle.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2022/jun/26/australia-news-live-updates-daniel-andrews-defends-new-ministers-federal-crossbenchers-livid-live?page=with:block-62b7ee608f0814a0d5d4350a#block-62b7ee608f0814a0d5d4350a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A small aircraft with only the pilot on board crashed in a paddock}}}\uc2  near Bowenville in Queensland\u8217\'20\'19s Darling Downs.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2022/jun/26/australia-news-live-updates-daniel-andrews-defends-new-ministers-federal-crossbenchers-livid-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62b7cb818f0867712f95fa6f#block-62b7cb818f0867712f95fa6f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 And the nation recorded 26 Covid deaths}}}\uc2 , with 15 in Victoria, seven in NSW, and two in Queensland and WA respectively.\par \par \uc2 Thank you for spending the day with us \u8211\'20\'13 we will be back tomorrow!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.36am BST\par \par \uc2 I mentioned before that there have been a few comments made online today asking why prime minister Anthony Albanese has not commented on the Roe v Wade decision in the US yet.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s interesting to note, as several world leaders including Ardern, Trudeau and Macron have commented.\par \par \uc2 Former PM \uc2 Julia Gillard\uc2  also tweeted this last night:\par \par \uc2 enltrI fully endorse these words and Michelle Obama\u8217\'20\'19s call to all of us to keep fighting for women\u8217\'20\'19s rights. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/j7x9ua2NXv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/j7x9ua2NXv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Julia Gillard\uc2  (@JuliaGillard) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JuliaGillard/status/1540491941812772864?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.39am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.13am BST\par \par \uc2 I actually can\u8217\'20\'19t describe how beautiful this piece from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/ellen-fanning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ellen Fanning}}}\uc2  is \u8211\'20\'13 just read it:\par \par \uc2 We are hardwired to avoid pain,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are conditioned to make any single unfavourable emotion go away. Minimising [another\u8217\'20\'19s experience] is a protection tool which allows people to pretend that the [difficult situation] isn\u8217\'20\'19t happening.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen someone brings up something uncomfortable, we don\u8217\'20\'19t want a bar of it and/or we want to get the other person out of that pain as quickly as possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/26/dont-worry-hell-be-right-why-do-we-say-all-the-wrong-things-to-parents-of-children-with-a-disability"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Don\u8217\'20\'19t worry!' 'He\u8217\'20\'19ll be right\u8217\'20\'19: Why do we say all the wrong things to parents of children with a disability? | Ellen Fanning}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Dutton has told the NSW Libs they shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be choosing candidates the night before the election \u8211\'20\'13 which, to be fair \u8211\'20\'13 seems quite sensible.\par \par \uc2 Paul Karp has the story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/26/peter-dutton-says-nsw-liberal-party-preselection-delays-were-completely-unacceptable"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peter Dutton says NSW Liberal party preselection delays were \u8216\'20\'18completely unacceptable\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Heading up to the snow this school holidays? Victoria police have some tips here:\par \par \uc2 enltrWhilst driving in the snow, make sure you;\par \par \uc2 ? Drive cautiously with two hands on the wheel and steady pressure on the accelerator\par \par \uc2 ? Brake with steady pressure\par \par \uc2 ? Avoid braking when cornering\par \par \uc2 ? Fit chains to your tyres when advised or if the road looks icy\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Victoria Police (@VictoriaPolice) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VictoriaPolice/status/1540904204994109441?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr? Engage low gear when you drive down a mountain\par \par \uc2 ? If you hit ice, apply the brakes gently to slowly regain traction\par \par \uc2 ? At night only use low beam lights. High beams don't work in high mist areas. If you can\u8217\'20\'19t see, pull over, put your hazards on and keep your engine running\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Victoria Police (@VictoriaPolice) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VictoriaPolice/status/1540904208110563328?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39am BST\par \par \uc2 Tasmania \u8211\'20\'13 where even the road warnings are beautiful:\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Road?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Road}}}\uc2  Weather Alert issued for Monday morning about all districts in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Tas?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Tas}}}\uc2  except the East and the Bass Strait Islands. Icy roads may make {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/driving?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #driving}}}\uc2  conditions dangerous. Check {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6p7uemGHeE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/6p7uemGHeE}}}\uc2  for details. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/klAn2BQHhZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/klAn2BQHhZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Bureau of Meteorology\uc2 , Tasmania (@BOM_Tas) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BOM_Tas/status/1540867125853790209?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.44am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30am BST\par \par \uc2 On \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , some criticism has been levelled at the new PM for not yet making a statement on the Roe v Wade decision in the US.\par \par \uc2 enltrSo our Prime Minister\u8217\'20\'19s really not going to say anything about the Supreme Court decision? Despite many world leaders putting out strong statements condemning the assault on reproductive rights and expressing solidarity with women and LGTBIQ people. Deafening silence says it all.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jill Stark (@jillastark) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jillastark/status/1540921925786288128?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.39am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17am BST\par \par \uc2 The time has come - State of Origin II is just hours away. Here {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/nick-tedeschi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nick Tedeschi}}}\uc2  takes us through the lineup for tonight:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/blog/2022/jun/25/blues-state-of-origin-reputations-on-line-as-weight-of-expectation-falls-on-maroons"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Blues\u8217\'20\'19 State of Origin reputations on line as weight of expectation falls on Maroons | Nick Tedeschi}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.04am BST\par \par \uc2 NSW may impose bans after deadly bee mite discovered in Newcastle\par \par \uc2 Beekeepers across New South Wales could be banned from moving their honey and hives after the detection of a deadly invasive mite in Newcastle.\par \par \uc2 The ABC is reporting the state government could impose the ban as soon as 6pm today, which would prevent any movement of bees, hives, honeycomb and honey.\par \par \uc2 Australia is the only honey producer worldwide to have stopped the mites from becoming established.\par \par \uc2 On {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dpi.nsw.gov.au/biosecurity/seasonal-pests-and-diseases/spring/varroa-mite"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Friday the NSW government}}}\uc2  said it had detected varroa mite in biosecurity surveillance hives in the Port of Newcastle.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dpi.nsw.gov.au/biosecurity/seasonal-pests-and-diseases/spring/varroa-mite"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 50km biosecurity zone was set up}}}\uc2 , preventing any movement or tampering of hives, as well as stopping the removal of honey or comb.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.abc.net.au/news/2022-06-26/nsw-stops-movement-of-bees-due-to-varroa-mite-parasite/101184770"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC is reporting that biosecurity zone}}}\uc2  is to be extended across the entire state.\par \par \uc2 Agriculture minister Dugald Saunders said on Friday an eradication plan had been launched to contain the mites, but warned if it became established it could cost the honey industry $70m a year.\par \par \uc2 Australia is the only honey-producing country to have prevented the Varroa mite from establishing itself. Photograph: Lisa Maree Williams/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 He said Australia was the only honey-producing country to have prevented the mite from establishing itself.\par \par \uc2 There are two types of the pinhead-sized varroa mite \u8211\'20\'13 the Varroa jacobsoni and Varroa destructor \u8211\'20\'13 which are considered the most serious pest for honeybees globally. The mite detected in Newcastle was Varroa destructor.\par \par \uc2 In 2018, Victorian authorities prevented the spread of the mite after a ship from Texas docked in the Port of Geelong with bees infested with the mite.\par \par \uc2 In Queensland, Varroa jacobsoni mites were detected in Townsville in 2019 and 2020 and then eradicated after an initial 2016 detection.\par \par \uc2 The Varroa destructor has been responsible for the collapse of European bee colonies \u8220\'20\'1Cwherever it is present\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.business.qld.gov.au/industries/farms-fishing-forestry/agriculture/land-management/health-pests-weeds-diseases/pests/invasive-animals/prohibited/varroa-mite"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 information from the Queensland Government says}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The mites suck on adult bees, weakening them \u8220\'20\'1Cand new bees are born with deformities\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.19am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53am BST\par \par \uc2 Wealthy Australians are avoiding paying tax by having the family trust pay children (who will be taxed less), who then repay the money to their parents for raising them.\par \par \uc2 A solid story from Ben Butler here about how family trusts are rorting the system:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/26/australian-taxation-office-crackdown-on-family-trust-rorts-causes-alarm-among-tax-advisers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Australian Taxation Office crackdown on family trust rorts causes alarm among tax advisers}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.55am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Andrews out selling new cabinet\par \par \uc2 From AAP :\par \par \uc2 Victorian premier \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2  is selling his new cabinet ahead of incoming ministers being sworn in at Government House.\par \par \uc2 Andrews stepped out with incoming health minister Mary-Anne Thomas and newly promoted cabinet member Sonya Kilkenny on Sunday after unveiling the frontbench he will take to the November state election.\par \par \uc2 Deputy premier and education minister \uc2 James Merlino\uc2 , health minister \uc2 Martin Foley\uc2 , jobs minister \uc2 Martin Pakula\uc2  and police minister \uc2 Lisa Neville\uc2  all resigned on Friday, prompting the reshuffle.\par \par \uc2 Thomas will take over from Foley as health minister \u8211\'20\'13 the state\u8217\'20\'19s fourth in as many years \u8211\'20\'13 while Natalie Hutchins is exchanging her corrections portfolio for education.\par \par \uc2 Five MPs will step into Labor\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet as it seeks a third term in office, including Kilkenny, Lizzie Blandthorn, Steve Dimopoulos, Harriet Shing and speaker Colin Brooks.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.43am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Small plane with only pilot on board crashes in Queensland\par \par \uc2 A small aircraft has hit power lines and crashed in a paddock near Bowenville in Queensland\u8217\'20\'19s Darling Downs.\par \par \uc2 Believed to be an ultralight with only the pilot on board, the plane crashed just before 2.20pm on Sunday, about 20 minutes outside of Oakey.\par \par \uc2 A Queensland Ambulance Service spokesperson said shortly after 3pm that multiple paramedic crews were still waiting for the powerlines to be cut so they could attempt to rescue the patient. Marshy ground was also making access difficult and the rescuers were yet to make contact with the pilot, whose condition was unknown.\par \par \uc2 The Toowoomba Chronicle reported the plane to be upside down and that paramedics only had access by foot to the crash.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.36am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19am BST\par \par \uc2 The education minister has blasted Senator \uc2 Hollie Hughes\uc2  for \u8220\'20\'1Ccrazy\u8221\'20\'1D comments blaming the Liberals\u8217\'20\'19 low youth vote on \u8220\'20\'1CMarxist\u8221\'20\'1D teachers.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday Labor\u8217\'20\'19s Jason Clare responded to the remarks, made by the New South Wales senator at a Sydney Institute federal election postmortem on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/26/education-system-run-by-marxists-jason-clare-takes-aim-at-liberal-senator-over-comments-on-teachers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Education system \u8216\'20\'18run by Marxists\u8217\'20\'19: Jason Clare takes aim at Liberal senator over comments on teachers}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Shelley Allison will never forget the look on her dad\u8217\'20\'19s face after he walked out of the house where her daughter Haley was murdered. \u8220\'20\'1CBefore the crime scene clean-up, my father had to do a walk-through of the house and I never understood why,\u8221\'20\'1D Allison says. \u8220\'20\'1CThis big man, he went white \u8230\'20\'26 It was heartbreaking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/26/scene-clean-up-a-victims-family-wants-queenslanders-to-be-spared-the-trauma"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crime scene clean-up: a victim\u8217\'20\'19s family wants Queenslanders to be spared the trauma}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49am BST\par \par \uc2 ABS to reveal impact on spending of first interest rate in a decade\par \par \uc2 From AAP :\par \par \uc2 Economic figures will show what impact higher interest rates and ongoing cost of living pressures are having on the behaviour of Australians in terms of spending and borrowing.\par \par \uc2 Consumer confidence - a guide to future household spending - has already slumped after consecutive monthly interest rate increases in the cash rate by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Retail trade figures on Wednesday from the \uc2 Australian Bureau of Statistics\uc2  will show the actual impact on spending from May\u8217\'20\'19s first interest rate rise in more than decade.\par \par \uc2 Economists forecasts point to a more modest 0.3 per cent rise in spending in May, coming after a solid run of monthly increases since the start of the year, a worrying sign for the economic outlook more broadly.\par \par \uc2 Their expectations range from a 0.7 per cent rise to a one per cent decline.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBA\uc2  will release monthly credit figures on Thursday, which may also show some softening in demand for loans after a strong run-up, particularly for mortgages when interest rates were at record lows.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.59am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Nasa\uc2  rocket to launch from Arnhem Land space centre tonight\par \par \uc2 From AAP :\par \par \uc2 One of the world\u8217\'20\'19s oldest living cultures is helping scientists understand galaxies and stars with the launch of the first of three \uc2 NASA\uc2  rockets from the Northern Territory.\par \par \uc2 The rocket is scheduled to launch from the Arnhem Space Centre on the Dhupuma Plateau, near Nhulunbuy, about 10.44pm on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 It will carry an X-ray Quantum Calorimeter, allowing \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2  scientists to measure interstellar X-rays with precision to provide new data on the structure and evolution of the cosmos.\par \par \uc2 About 75 \uc2 NASA\uc2  personnel are in Arnhem Land for the launch, which is the agency\u8217\'20\'19s first in Australia in 27 years and first-ever from a commercial spaceport outside the US.\par \par \uc2 The Arnhem Space Centre in the Northern Territory. Photograph: Equatorial Launch Australia/AP\par \par \uc2 The Yolngu helped build Arnhem Space Centre, which is owned by Equatorial Launch Australia, on their land.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re also taking part in the upcoming launch, including retrieving rocket modules when they return to Earth.\par \par \uc2 Gumatj Corporation chairman Djawa Yunupingu says the space industry can provide opportunities for the Yolngu people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe want our young people to see and take up the jobs and business opportunities that come from the growth of the Arnhem Space Centre over time,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 NSA will launch another two rockets from the ELA complex on July 4 and July 12.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.38am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59am BST\par \par \uc2 The northern NSW town finds solace by the banks of a river that has wrought so much destruction on it this year\par \par \uc2 Lismore\u8217\'20\'19s lantern parade is a celebration of nature, to mark the passing of the longest night of winter, but the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/new-south-wales"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New South Wales}}}\uc2  northern rivers town has a troubled relationship with nature.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/26/light-at-the-darkest-time-lantern-parade-a-source-of-healing-for-flood-ravaged-lismore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Light at the darkest time: lantern parade a source of healing for flood-ravaged Lismore}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34am BST\par \par \uc2 In the Moruya North Head campground where about 50 people live, there\u8217\'20\'19s no power and the water in the one private shower is cold. \u8220\'20\'1CSometimes you can\u8217\'20\'19t handle that, so you\u8217\'20\'19ve got to boil up some water and try work it that way,\u8221\'20\'1D says Geoff Pike as the sun dips and the winter chill sets in. Lately, it\u8217\'20\'19s been getting down to 3C at night.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/26/the-changing-face-of-homelessness-in-regional-nsw-im-working-but-everything-is-unaffordable"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The changing face of homelessness in regional NSW: \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m working, but everything is unaffordable\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.43am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19am BST\par \par \uc2 When kids are at school and they\u8217\'20\'19re being taught all this absolute leftwing rubbish, that\u8217\'20\'19s where they\u8217\'20\'19re leaving school and that\u8217\'20\'19s where they\u8217\'20\'19re landing.\par \par \uc2 enltrSenator \uc2 Hollie Hughes\uc2  blames Marxist teachers for the fact that so many young people rejected the Liberal Party at the election. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mr8pdJ6GJU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/mr8pdJ6GJU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Matt Burke (@matttburke) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/matttburke/status/1540622000301178881?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59am BST\par \par \uc2 National Covid summary\par \par \uc2 Here are the latest coronavirus numbers from around Australia today, as the country records at least 26 deaths from Covid-19:\par \par \uc2 ACT\par \par \uc2 * Deaths: 0\par \par \uc2 * Cases: 819\par \par \uc2 * In hospital: 116 (with 1 person in ICU)\par \par \uc2 NSW\par \par \uc2 * Deaths: 7\par \par \uc2 * Cases: 7,461\par \par \uc2 * In hospital: 1,465 (with 48 people in ICU)\par \par \uc2 Northern Territory\par \par \uc2 * Deaths: 0\par \par \uc2 * Cases: 221\par \par \uc2 * In hospital: 16 (with no people in ICU)\par \par \uc2 Queensland\par \par \uc2 * Deaths: 2\par \par \uc2 * Cases: 3,048\par \par \uc2 * In hospital: 556 (with 8 people in ICU)\par \par \uc2 South Australia\par \par \uc2 * Deaths: 0\par \par \uc2 * Cases: 1,996\par \par \uc2 * In hospital: 216 (with 9 people in ICU)\par \par \uc2 Tasmania\par \par \uc2 * Deaths: 0\par \par \uc2 * Cases: 777\par \par \uc2 * In hospital: 48 (with 3 people in ICU)\par \par \uc2 Victoria\par \par \uc2 * Deaths: 15\par \par \uc2 * Cases: 5,824\par \par \uc2 * In hospital: 451 (with 28 people in ICU)\par \par \uc2 Western Australia\par \par \uc2 * Deaths: 2\par \par \uc2 * Cases: 3,544\par \par \uc2 * In hospital: 250 (with 9 people in ICU)\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Victorian MPs to receive 2.75% pay rise\par \par \uc2 From AAP :\par \par \uc2 Victorian Premier \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 yearly pay package will inch closer to half a million dollars as part of a wage rise for state MPs.\par \par \uc2 The annual base and additional salaries of Victorian parliament members, as well as their expense allowance, will lift 2.75 per cent from July 1 after a decision by the Victorian Independent Remuneration Tribunal.\par \par \uc2 That is marginally higher than the 2.5 per cent raise MPs were awarded for this financial year.\par \par \uc2 The latest ruling took into account recent pay adjustments of two to 2.75 per cent for Commonwealth, NSW and Queensland MPs, as well as other factors including Victoria\u8217\'20\'19s fiscal position and economic trends, projected national inflation of seven per cent and the 5.2 per cent minimum wage rise.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn balance... the tribunal has determined to increase the values of the basic salary for Victorian MPs, and the additional salaries and expense allowance for specified parliamentary office holders, by 2.75 per cent for 2022/23,\u8221\'20\'1D VIRT said.\par \par \uc2 The 2.75 per cent rise will take the basic salary for a Victorian MP to $192,115, up about $5200 from 2021/22.\par \par \uc2 Victorian premier, \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2  will receive a 2.75% pay rise after it was approved by the Victorian Independent Remuneration Tribunal. Photograph: Diego Fedele/AAP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Peter Dutton\uc2  calls for increase in income threshold for pensioners to ease labour shortages\par \par \uc2 Opposition leader \uc2 Peter Dutton\uc2  has called on the government to double the amount of income age pensioners and veteran service pensioners can earn without reducing pension payments so they can fill labour shortages.\par \par \uc2 Dutton:\par \par \uc2 Employers can\u8217\'20\'19t find staff \u8211\'20\'13 thousands of jobs across hospitality, agriculture, tourism and retail remain open.\par \par \uc2 This policy ensures that pensioners and veterans, who want to work, are not financially penalised. It puts more money into their pocket.\par \par \uc2 There are around 80,000 age pensioners and veterans who are choosing to work who will likely benefit from this change.\par \par \uc2 Currently, age pensioners and veteran service pensioners can earn $300 of income each fortnight without impacting pension payments. Under the proposed change, age pensioners will be able to earn up to $600 a fortnight and still receive the maximum pension payment.\par \par \uc2 Pensioners will continue to accrue unused pension work bonus amounts up to a maximum of $7,800, which can exempt future earnings from the pension income test.\par \par \uc2 Leader of the opposition, \uc2 Peter Dutton\uc2 . Photograph: Mick Tsikas/AAP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.49am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Vaccine immunity-evading Omicron sub-variant on rise in Victoria\par \par \uc2 Hello everyone \u8211\'20\'13 this is Cait, I will be with you across the afternoon. Let\u8217\'20\'19s start with this:\par \par \uc2 An Omicron subvariant of Covid-19 that can evade vaccine immunity is on the rise in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/victoria"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Victoria}}}\uc2 , with health authorities warning it is on track to be the state\u8217\'20\'19s major strain in line with virus spread in NSW and Queensland.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/26/victoria-says-rising-omicron-subvariant-is-on-track-to-be-the-states-major-covid-strain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Victoria says rising Omicron subvariant is on track to be the state\u8217\'20\'19s major Covid strain}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.36am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Handing over the live news duties now to my colleague Cait Kelly who will guide this good ship for the rest of the day. Thanks and go well.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Commonwealth leaders push for Covid and climate action\par \par \uc2 The Commonwealth Heads of Government meeting has wrapped up in the city of Kigali in Rwanda.\par \par \uc2 Deputy prime minister Richard Marles has been representing Australia.\par \par \uc2 The affects of the Covid-19 pandemic, the importance of sustainable development, action on climate change and radicalism were all highlighted in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thecommonwealth.org/news/chogm-2022-communique-leaders-statement-and-declarations-delivering-common"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 closing leaders\u8217\'20\'19 statement and final communiqu\u233\'00\'E9}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here are some segments from the leaders\u8217\'20\'19 statement from the 54 leaders of Commonwealth countries:\par \par \uc2 We recognised the effects of global insecurities in food, energy and climate, and agreed to strengthen the Commonwealth Secretariat to further focus on these issues and take forward action in support of Commonwealth members.\par \par \uc2 We reaffirmed that radicalisation, leading to violence, violent extremism, and terrorism in all its forms, are serious global threats.\par \par \uc2 We affirmed that the universal, timely, fair and equitable access to and distribution of safe, efficacious, and affordable COVID-19 vaccines, therapeutics and diagnostics, and capacity to administer the same, are key to global recovery from the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 enltrCatching up with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/trussliz?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @trussliz}}}\uc2  on the sidelines of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/CHOGM2022?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #CHOGM2022}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A warm and friendly discussion, looking forward to new areas of cooperation in our long-standing partnership with the UK, including under the AUKUS pillars and working together to tackle climate change. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cb9J0m4ive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cb9J0m4ive}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Richard Marles (@RichardMarlesMP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RichardMarlesMP/status/1540264148323516416?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Australia to send $1m earthquake relief to Afghanistan\par \par \uc2 Foreign minister \uc2 Penny Wong\uc2  has said Australia will top up its aid to Afghanistan after the country suffered a devastating earthquake this week.\par \par \uc2 A statement from Wong says the extra emergency relief was in addition to $140m pledged to the country since last September.\par \par \uc2 The earthquake has caused extensive loss of life, homes and livelihoods, with the full effects still to be determined. This tragedy comes at a time when the humanitarian needs in Afghanistan are greater than ever.\par \par \uc2 Our support will be delivered through \uc2 UN\uc2  agencies already operating in the affected area, and will go towards providing shelter, food and medical support for those in need.\par \par \uc2 The Australian Government extend its deepest condolences to the people of Afghanistan, and the Afghan-Australian community.\par \par \uc2 Afghanistan\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Taliban\uc2  rulers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/25/taliban-say-they-will-not-interfere-with-afghanistan-earthquake-aid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promised not to interfere with the international response to the quake}}}\uc2 , which killed at least 1,000 people.\par \par \uc2 Afghan people try to retrieve a car from the debris of damaged houses after the recent earthquake. Photograph: Ali Khara/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Education minister wants more oversees students to come and stay longer\par \par \uc2 Education minister Jason Clare has been outlining the huge drops in overseas students in the wake of the pandemic, highlighting a 24% drop in the number of Chinese arrivals.\par \par \uc2 According to comments on Sky News, reported by AAP, Clare wants to see the numbers recover, he also wants more students to stay and live in Australia after they\u8217\'20\'19ve finished at university.\par \par \uc2 We train them here, we skill them up. Where we have got skill shortages \u8211\'20\'13 they are chronic across the economy at the moment \u8211\'20\'13 it makes sense to encourage them to stay longer.\par \par \uc2 Only 16% of overseas students stayed behind after finishing their studies, he said. The Covid pandemic had smashed international student numbers.\par \par \uc2 Clare was planning to talk to India\u8217\'20\'19s education minister in the coming weeks to see if more young people from that country could come to Australia to study.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05am BST\par \par \uc2 QLD reports two Covid deaths\par \par \uc2 Queensland\u8217\'20\'19s health department has reported two further deaths of people with Covid-19 and 3,048 new cases of the disease.\par \par \uc2 Those two deaths are added to 15 reported in Victoria and seven in NSW so far today.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday we have recorded 3,048 new COVID-19 cases.\par \par \uc2 Sadly, we have reported 2 deaths in the past 24 hours.\par \par \uc2 Full details?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6L6VcCsFY1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/6L6VcCsFY1}}}\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/eBsAipwsJZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/eBsAipwsJZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Queensland Health\uc2  (@qldhealth) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/qldhealth/status/1540862427868581888?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.12am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Ministers defend cuts to crossbench staffing\par \par \uc2 Paul Karp has the full story on the government\u8217\'20\'19s defence in the face of the fury of crossbench MPs and senators after they had their staffing levels cut.\par \par \uc2 Independent senator David Pocock says it will be hard to vote for government legislation if he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have the resources to get across what it says. Photograph: Mick Tsikas/AAP\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/26/ministers-defend-cut-to-crossbenchers-advisers-despite-fury-of-jacqui-lambie-and-other-independents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ministers defend cut to crossbenchers\u8217\'20\'19 advisers, despite fury of Jacqui Lambie and other independents}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Treasurer defends crossbench staffing cuts\par \par \uc2 A decision by the Albanese government to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/24/slap-in-the-face-independents-furious-at-pms-decision-to-cut-advisory-staff-from-four-to-one"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut the number of advisers available to crossbench MPs and senators}}}\uc2  was described as an \u8220\'20\'1Cattack on democracy\u8221\'20\'1D by some late last week.\par \par \uc2 The treasurer \uc2 Jim Chalmers\uc2  was asked about it on the ABC earlier, and claimed the step wasn\u8217\'20\'19t unprecedented.\par \par \uc2 Well, I think it\u8217\'20\'19s been a surprise to a lot of people. It was a surprise to me, frankly, to learn some backbenchers get twice as many staff as other backbenchers. It\u8217\'20\'19s not unprecedented. It\u8217\'20\'19s not surprising, that members of parliament want to have more resources to help them do their job.\par \par \uc2 What we\u8217\'20\'19ve recognised with the crossbench, is that there are some additional pressures on crossbench members.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s why they get extra staff resources. But I don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s reasonable or fair for one backbench MP in one electorate to get twice as many staff as a backbench MP in the electorate next door. That\u8217\'20\'19s what this commonsense proposal reflects.\par \par \uc2 Chalmers said the government was going to \u8220\'20\'1Cboost investment in the parliamentary library\u8221\'20\'1D to help with workload.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.34am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Sussan Ley: Roe v Wade overturning \u8216\'20\'18a backward step for women\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Deputy Liberal leader \uc2 Sussan Ley\uc2  says the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a \u8220\'20\'1Cbackward step for women in the US\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 AAP is reporting comments made on Sky News by Ley, who is also the shadow minister for women.\par \par \uc2 This has been a step backwards for women in the US. I\u8217\'20\'19m very discomforted by anything that puts a personal and sensitive issue that a woman has to grapple with in many instances, or a family has to grapple with, in the same sentence as criminal.\par \par \uc2 Education minister Jason Clare, AAP reports, said:\par \par \uc2 Thank God we are a country here in Australia where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not an issue that divides the Labor party and Liberal party.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m thinking at the moment for the women who live in some of these states that are basically being told today that if you want to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  then get on a bus and travel a couple of hundred kilometres.\par \par \uc2 Multiple US states made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal within hours of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn the 1973 Roe v Wade judgement. Protests at the decision have erupted across the country.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/25/abortion-banned-in-multiple-us-states-just-hours-after-roe-v-wade-overturned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  banned in multiple US states just hours after Roe v Wade overturned}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.11am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55am BST\par \par \uc2 Changing face of homelessness\par \par \uc2 Talking about rising cost of living, the realities of homelessness in Australia is growing and changing.\par \par \uc2 This important story from my colleague Jordyn Beazley highlights how housing affordability, rising cost of living and \u8220\'20\'1Cno fault evictions\u8221\'20\'1D is seeing people living in tents, mobile homes and sleeping rough in cars on backtrails.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/26/the-changing-face-of-homelessness-in-regional-nsw-im-working-but-everything-is-unaffordable"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The changing face of homelessness in regional NSW: \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m working, but everything is unaffordable\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Inflation could go higher than 7% by July, says treasurer\par \par \uc2 Treasurer \uc2 Jim Chalmers\uc2  has flagged that inflation \u8211\'20\'13 at 5.1% in the March quarter \u8211\'20\'13 is likely to keep climbing and could go higher than 7%.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to the ABC, Chalmers said he was looking to his economic forecast update next month.\par \par \uc2 Inflation will be significantly higher than what was expected in the last government\u8217\'20\'19s most recent budget, what was expected at election time as well. Certainly higher than the 5.1% we saw in the March quarter. This inflation problem will get more difficult.\par \par \uc2 I will update the forecast before the end of July, and we will take in the most recent information, and the Reserve Bank said something around 7% \u8211\'20\'13 that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t seem to me to be wildly off the mark.\par \par \uc2 We will do the work between now and July to give people the most accurate assessment of where we think this inflation challenge is heading.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.27am BST\par \par \uc2 NSW reports seven Covid deaths\par \par \uc2 Health officials in New South Wales have reported seven Covid-19 deaths and 7,461 new cases.\par \par \uc2 enltrCOVID-19 update \u8211\'20\'13 Sunday 26 June 2022\par \par \uc2 In the 24-hour reporting period to 4pm yesterday:\par \par \uc2 - 96.6% of people aged 16+ have had one dose of a COVID-19 vaccine\par \par \uc2 - 95.1% of people aged 16+ have had two doses of a COVID-19 vaccine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/szCNm1Ft7E"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/szCNm1Ft7E}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 NSW Health\uc2  (@NSWHealth) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NSWHealth/status/1540832239902412801?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.33am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Chalmers: Coalition pursued \u8216\'20\'18wage stagnation\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The new treasurer, \uc2 Jim Chalmers\uc2 , is speaking to the ABC\u8217\'20\'19s Insiders program.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s asked if wage growth of 3.5% is sustainable and if it\u8217\'20\'19s not, then where should wage growth be? He claims \u8220\'20\'1Cwage stagnation\u8221\'20\'1D was \u8220\'20\'1Centhusiastically pursued\u8221\'20\'1D by the previous government.\par \par \uc2 We have a common interest, dealing with inflation, boosting wages based on a productive workforce and that\u8217\'20\'19s our focus.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m not interested in nominating a specific number. Our job is to get wages growing sustainably, growing strongly.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.32am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.19am BST\par \par \uc2 Victoria reports 15 Covid deaths\par \par \uc2 Victorian health officials have reported 15 deaths from Covid-19, with 5,824 new cases.\par \par \uc2 enltrWe thank everyone who got vaccinated and tested yesterday.\par \par \uc2 Our thoughts are with those in hospital, and the families of people who have lost their lives.\par \par \uc2 More data soon: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OCCFTAchah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/OCCFTAchah}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/COVID19Vic?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #COVID19Vic}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/COVID19VicData?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #COVID19VicData}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Zm7hMDU8Wp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Zm7hMDU8Wp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 VicGovDH (@VicGovDH) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VicGovDH/status/1540832227516448771?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Exploitation and peril in Sri Lanka\par \par \uc2 With Sri Lanka on the brink of economic collapse, more and more people are looking to escape the country and some are risking perilous journeys on boats.\par \par \uc2 But there are claims of exploitation, particularly in Tamil regions, where the economic crisis comes on top of existing unease at the minority\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing oppression.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has spoken to senior sources, police and the people caught up in human trafficking rings.\par \par \uc2 Devana Senanayake in Colombo, Aliyar Mohammed Geeth in Trincomalee and Guardian Australia\u8217\'20\'19s Ben Doherty in Sydney have the story.\par \par \uc2 A boat with Sri Lankan migrants that tried to reach Australia in 2016. Photograph: Future Publishing/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/26/screened-out-before-arrival-questions-over-legality-of-australias-at-sea-asylum-seeker-rulings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Exploited in a crisis: why are Sri Lankans getting on boats bound for Australia?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.19am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Clare defends crossbenchers\u8217\'20\'19 staff cut\par \par \uc2 The education minister Jason Clare has this morning defended the government\u8217\'20\'19s decision to cut independent MPs and senators staffing allocation.\par \par \uc2 Under the allocation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/24/slap-in-the-face-independents-furious-at-pms-decision-to-cut-advisory-staff-from-four-to-one"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced on Friday}}}\uc2 , independents will have four electorate staff and one extra adviser, down from four extra advisers under the Morrison government.\par \par \uc2 Clare told Sky News:\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re a Labor MP, or Liberal MP or a Nat, you get four staff. If you\u8217\'20\'19re a crossbench MP you get eight. That seems to me to be a bit out of whack. What Albo is saying here is that if your\u8217\'20\'19e a crossbench MP you\u8217\'20\'19ll get an extra member of staff, above what a Labor, Liberal or Nat will get. And we\u8217\'20\'19ll put extra resourcing into the parliamentary library. That seems to me to be pretty fair.\par \par \uc2 Clare revealed that the total salary bill of government staff has been cut by $1.5m and opposition staff by $350,000.\par \par \uc2 People come to this job not for the pay but for the opportunity it provides to make a difference. Everyone is taking a haircut here, whether it is government staff, opposition staff... Most Australians would say you\u8217\'20\'19ve been elected, now knuckle down and do the job.\par \par \uc2 Just some quick maths here. If Labor\u8217\'20\'19s staffing allocation has been cut by $1.5m, if that were spread evenly across its 23 cabinet members, that\u8217\'20\'19s a cut of $65,000 in each office.\par \par \uc2 That sort of cut can be achieved by having one less person at the senior adviser level, and hiring them as a junior adviser.\par \par \uc2 For crossbench MPs and senators losing three staff each, that\u8217\'20\'19s more like a cut of at least $400,000 in salaries in each office, and can\u8217\'20\'19t be achieved without a reduction in head count.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Victoria to have a new cabinet\par \par \uc2 Victorian premier \uc2 Dan Andrews\uc2  finalised his new cabinet and ministry late yesterday with new ministers to be sworn in tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 Andrews\u8217\'20\'19 reshuffle \u8211\'20\'13 sparked by four high-level resignations \u8211\'20\'13 puts 14 women in the state\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet, which he said was the highest of any jurisdiction in Australia.\par \par \uc2 The most senior is new deputy premier, \uc2 Jacinta Allan\uc2 , who replaces \uc2 James Merlino\uc2 . Allan will also have oversight of the delivery of the 2026 Commonwealth Games.\par \par \uc2 Other cabinet appointments are:\par \par \uc2 * Lizzie Blandthorn \u8211\'20\'13 minister for planning and leader of the House\par \par \uc2 * Colin Brooks \u8211\'20\'13 minister for child protection and family services and minister for disability, ageing and carers\par \par \uc2 * Steve Dimopoulos \u8211\'20\'13 minister for tourism, sport and major events and minister for creative industries\par \par \uc2 * Sonya Kilkenny \u8211\'20\'13 minister for corrections, minister for youth justice, minister for victim support and minister for fishing and boating\par \par \uc2 * Harriet Shing \u8211\'20\'13 minister for water, minister for regional development and minister for equality\par \par \uc2 enltrStatement from the Premier on the new Ministry {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fFg1tkbt0G"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fFg1tkbt0G}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Dan Andrews\uc2  (@DanielAndrewsMP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DanielAndrewsMP/status/1540617708701876224?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Morning all.\par \par \uc2 Graham Readfearn here reaching for the cranking handle to get our live news coverage moving for this Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a quick reminder of what happened yesterday.\par \par \uc2 * At least 56 people died after catching Covid-19 across Australia.\par \par \uc2 * In Victoria health officials said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/06/why-are-there-so-many-new-omicron-sub-variants-like-ba4-and-ba5-is-the-virus-mutating-faster"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Omicron BA.4/BA.5}}}\uc2  would become the dominant strain in coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 * Foreign minister \uc2 Penny Wong\uc2  announced visits to Vietnam and Malaysia this week as the Albanese government continues its early diplomatic push in the region.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Jacinta Allan\uc2  is Victoria\u8217\'20\'19s new deputy premier, with the premier \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2  announcing his new ministry after four cabinet resignations. There\u8217\'20\'19s a state election in November.\par \par \uc2 * Minister for women Katy Gallagher said the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  decision to overturn Roe v Wade was \u8220\'20\'1Creally disappointing\u8221\'20\'1D. Environment minister \uc2 Tanya Plibersek\uc2  said reproductive choice was \u8220\'20\'1Ca fundamental human right\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Hope you\u8217\'20\'19re staying warm and safe. Let\u8217\'20\'19s get going with the day.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220625ei6p002p9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
