\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  banned in multiple US states just hours after Roe v Wade overturned\b0\par\par\uc2 Miranda Bryant \par \uc2 763 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2022\par 19:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Utah among first states to outlaw almost all abortions, while mayor of Washington DC declares it \u8216\'20\'18pro-choice city\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was already illegal in multiple US states on Saturday, with bans introduced within hours of Roe v Wade being overturned, as cities erupted in protest at the landmark ruling.\par \par \uc2 It came after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/25/abortion-banned-in-multiple-us-states-just-hours-after-roe-v-wade-overturned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court on Friday abolished the constitutional right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , more than 50 years after it was established, leaving individual states to decide. It is ultimately expected to lead to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in about half of the states.\par \par \uc2 According to a website affiliated with Planned Parenthood, the US sexual healthcare organisation, it remains legal to travel out of state to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Among the first states to outlaw almost all abortions was Utah where, after the ruling, its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban had already come into effect on Friday night.\par \par \uc2 Utah\u8217\'20\'19s Republican state senator, Daniel McCay, who sponsored the state\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger law\u8221\'20\'1D, said it would be wrong for Utah women to seek abortions in neighbouring states but he had no immediate plans to stop them from doing so.\par \par \uc2 Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s ban on most abortions at the first detectable foetal heartbeat \u8211\'20\'13 known as the \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbeat bill\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 also came into effect. The 2019 law has been on hold for nearly three years, but after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s announcement on Friday, a federal judge agreed to remove a federal court injunction blocking it hours later.\par \par \uc2 Alabama quickly stopped abortions as its 2019 state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban took effect \u8211\'20\'13 making it a crime to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any state of pregnancy, including for rape and incest victims. The only exception is for the sake of the mother\u8217\'20\'19s health.\par \par \uc2 Soon after the announcement, Arkansas\u8217\'20\'19s health department told the state\u8217\'20\'19s two \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers that abortions were now banned under a law banning all abortions except to protect the mother\u8217\'20\'19s life in a medical emergency.\par \par \uc2 Facilities were advised that performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now a violation of the law, punishable by up to 10 years in prison and a fine of up to $100,000.\par \par \uc2 West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic stopped performing abortions on Friday. The state has a law that criminalises providing abortions, carrying a three to 10 year prison sentence, but it is unclear how it will proceed on enforcement after the supreme court ruling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRoe has never been enough, but in states like West Virginia, it was the only thing protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access,\u8221\'20\'1D said Katie Quinonez, the executive director of Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Centre of West Virginia.\par \par \uc2 Now, she said, people from the state seeking abortions would be forced to travel hundreds, or even thousands, of miles to do so and marginalised communities would be worst affected.\par \par \uc2 In Missouri, the attorney general, Eric Schmitt, said he was acting immediately to enforce a state law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  except in \u8220\'20\'1Ccases of medical emergency\u8221\'20\'1D. It follows a 2019 law that included a trigger provision bringing it into effect after Roe v Wade was overturned.\par \par \uc2 In some states, including Arizona and Texas, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics temporarily stopped providing abortions while they assessed the legality of continuing.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, multiple states vowed to protect the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In Washington DC, the mayor, Muriel Bowser, responded by declaring it \u8220\'20\'1Ca pro-choice city\u8221\'20\'1D, but warned that as a district, not a state, it was now vulnerable because Congress had oversight of it.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic governors of California, Washington and Oregon have all vowed to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and help women who travel to the west coast from other states for abortions.\par \par \uc2 Anticipating an influx of people seeking abortions, they issued a \u8220\'20\'1Cmulti-state commitment\u8221\'20\'1D and said they would collaborate to defend patients and medical professionals providing abortions and pledged to \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect against judicial and local law enforcement cooperation with out-of-state investigations, inquiries, and arrests\u8221\'20\'1D into abortions in their states.\par \par \uc2 The Massachusetts Republican governor, \uc2 Charlie Baker\uc2 , signed an executive order to protect access to reproductive healthcare.\par \par \uc2 In North Carolina, its Democratic governor, Roy Cooper, also vowed to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, despite the legislature being controlled by Republicans. In response to the ruling, he put out a fundraising appeal on Friday for assistance in preventing Republicans from getting veto-proof majorities in the state in November.\par \par \uc2 In New Mexico, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is readily available, the top public prosecutor and Democratic nominee for attorney general, Ra\u250\'00\'FAl Torrez, urged politicians to take more action to protect women\u8217\'20\'19s access to abortions, including for those from other states.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220625ei6p001gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
