\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We will fight like hell\u8217\'20\'19: US western states band together to protect  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Gabrielle Canon \par \uc2 869 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2022\par 13:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 California, Oregon and Washington pledged to defend access and protect those seeking care as the US came to grips with losing Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 The Democratic state governors of California, Oregon and Washington issued a new commitment to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights across the west coast on Friday, as the US grappled with the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling removing the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Calling their states a \u8220\'20\'1Ca safe haven for all people seeking abortions and other reproductive health care services\u8221\'20\'1D, the California governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , Oregon governor \uc2 Kate Brown\uc2  and Washington governor \uc2 Jay Inslee\uc2  pledged to defend access to reproductive healthcare and protect those who cross their borders from other states seeking care.\par \par \uc2 They vowed to hamper out-of-state investigations or efforts to target those who receive services in their states, including barring local law enforcement from cooperating with outside agencies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCalifornia has banded together with Oregon and Washington to stand up for women, and to protect access to reproductive healthcare,\u8221\'20\'1D Newsom said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not sit on the sidelines and allow patients who seek reproductive care in our states or the doctors that provide that care to be intimidated with criminal prosecution. We refuse to go back and we will fight like hell to protect our rights and our values.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The supreme court decision on Friday to overturn Roe v Wade, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the landmark decision}}}\uc2  that had protected reproductive rights in the US for nearly five decades, paves the way for a slew of states that intend to roll back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/what-states-abortion-clinics-access-trigger-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 At least 26 states}}}\uc2  are expected to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  immediately or as soon as is practical after the decision, affecting 40 million people. Those who are less affluent, the young, Black and brown people, and those with children already are likely to bear the brunt of those rollbacks.\par \par \uc2 But even in liberal states where leaders have consistently voiced strong commitments to reproductive rights and rebuked the Republican-led states that led the charge to dismantle them, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/13/abortion-access-safe-haven-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 key challenges to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access \u8211\'20\'13 and battlegrounds \u8211\'20\'13 remain}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe threat to patient access and privacy has never been more dangerous,\u8221\'20\'1D said Inslee, the Washington governor, noting that even as his state continues to uphold \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, Republicans in the state have introduced at least four dozen billsover the last six years aimed at rolling them back. \u8220\'20\'1CThe right of choice should not depend on which party holds the majority, but that\u8217\'20\'19s where we find ourselves,\u8221\'20\'1D Inslee added.\par \par \uc2 Even in California, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is backed by statute and where legislators are working to enshrine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/billNavClient.xhtml?bill_id=202120220SCA10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reproductive freedoms}}}\uc2  into the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution, some residents still face significant barriers to get care. So-called \u8220\'20\'1Caccess deserts\u8221\'20\'1D cover large swaths of the state, especially in more conservative and rural areas including the central valley and in the far north. In 40% of California counties {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/fact-sheet/state-facts-about-abortion-california#:~:text=In%202017%2C%20some%2040%25%20of%20California%20counties%20had%20no%20clinics%20that%20provided%20abortions%2C%20and%203%25%20of%20California%20women%20lived%20in%20those%20counties."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 there isn\u8217\'20\'19t a single clinic}}}\uc2  that provides abortions. As the state positions itself as a sanctuary for others, some advocates are concerned that residents may struggle to find the care they need.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs more and more people come in from out of state seeking abortions, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to put more pressure on a system that\u8217\'20\'19s already strained,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/13/abortion-access-safe-haven-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said Laura Jim\u233\'00\'E9nez}}}\uc2 , the executive director of California Latinas for Reproductive Justice.\par \par \uc2 Already, some California residents have to travel hours across their county lines in order to receive care.\par \par \uc2 High costs have also hampered access. Even without transportation expenses, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  can run hundreds of dollars for those without insurance. Many, especially those with complicated cases or who are farther along in their pregnancies, aren\u8217\'20\'19t able to afford the costs or coordinate travel quickly. Language barriers and misinformation have only complicated the issues, spurring fear of criminalization and deportation that stops immigrants without legal status from seeking the care they need.\par \par \uc2 Still, important investments have been made in the three states to shore up their pledges, including a $125m reproductive health package proposed by Newsom in California to expand access. Oregon\u8217\'20\'19s Reproductive Health Equity Act offers free reproductive healthcare to some Oregonians and a new bill signed by Inslee this year protects professionals in the state who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.king5.com/article/news/politics/state-politics/washington-state-abortion-law-jay-inslee/281-a2a3e9b9-6c21-4a1e-9c92-f5be7676cbfb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provide abortions}}}\uc2  from out-of-state prosecution. Advocates say there is still a lot more work to be done.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights are expected to be a key issue in future elections in these states and across the country. Already, Democratic lawmakers have used the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lara_korte/status/1540368279088222208"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision}}}\uc2  to fundraise, signifying the fight that lays ahead. Public opinion is on their side \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/1576/abortion.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 roughly 85% of Americans}}}\uc2  support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 But for now, the states along the west coast will continue to offer care and position themselves as a go-to destination.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is healthcare, and no matter who you are or where you come from, Oregon doesn\u8217\'20\'19t turn away anyone seeking healthcare,\u8221\'20\'1D said Brown of Oregon, \u8220\'20\'1CFor all the Americans today feeling scared, angry and disappointed \u8211\'20\'13 for everyone who needs an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and does not know where they can access safe reproductive health care: please know you are not alone, and the fight is not over.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220625ei6p000jl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
