\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  ruling highlights the war against women in America. Time to fight back\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,157 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2022\par 13:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The post-Roe US will be a nightmare of digital authoritarianism where even Googling \u8216\'20\'18\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill\u8217\'20\'19 could be used against you\par \par \uc2 The end of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US\par \par \uc2 Well, it finally happened. The fact that we all expected it, that we have spent the last few weeks waiting for this to happen, didn\u8217\'20\'19t blunt the shock of it. On Friday the supreme court issued a decision in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 . Six unelected supreme court justices stripped bodily autonomy away from tens of millions of women and ended nearly 50 years of legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s wrong to say that the US is going backwards. It\u8217\'20\'19s wrong to say that the US is being transported back to the 70s, to a pre-Roe era. No. We are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2022/07/04/we-are-not-going-back-to-the-time-before-roe-we-are-going-somewhere-worse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moving forward}}}\uc2  into something far more sinister. The pre-Roe era didn\u8217\'20\'19t have the widespread {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/07/will-anti-abortionists-use-uterus-surveillance-against-women-in-the-us-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surveillance mechanisms}}}\uc2  that exist today. Regressive laws can now be enforced with the help of modern technology: if you even so much as \uc2 Google\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill\u8221\'20\'1D, there is a chance your online {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/05/05/tech/abortion-laws-phone-privacy/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 search history}}}\uc2  could be used against you. If you leave your state to try to get a safe and legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a state where it is still permitted, your location data could be used against you. For the past decade we have been sleepwalking into a new era of digital authoritarianism. Now we are in the middle of a nightmare.\par \par \uc2 This nightmare, of course, is not evenly distributed. Friday\u8217\'20\'19s decision will not affect everyone equally: \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, it should be stressed, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Health/abortion-restrictions-disproportionately-impact-people-color/story?id=84467809"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disproportionately harm}}}\uc2  poor people and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/05/06/1097065368/an-upcoming-supreme-court-ruling-may-disproportionately-impact-on-people-of-colo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 women of colour}}}\uc2 . Male Republican politicians, on the other hand, will probably still be able to get their mistresses an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/aug/25/a-republican-theme-on-abortions-its-ok-for-me-evil-for-thee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when it\u8217\'20\'19s convenient for them}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The end of Roe is just the beginning of an all-out assault on civil rights in America. There have been signs for a while now that, emboldened by their progress on restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, conservatives are going to come after things like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/may/25/banning-abortions-is-just-the-start-next-the-us-right-want-to-outlaw-contraception"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 birth control}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/apr/09/republicans-are-coming-after-same-sex-marriage-and-wont-stop-there"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gay marriage}}}\uc2 . On Friday Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  issued a concurring opinion acknowledging that the supreme court was not going to stop with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Now that Roe has been overturned, the supreme court, Thomas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/06/24/thomas-constitutional-rights-00042256"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in his opinion}}}\uc2 , should reconsider the landmark cases that protect the right to contraception, same-sex relationships and same-sex marriage. (Just to refresh your memory, Thomas is the guy who has been accused of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2017/dec/17/anita-hill-clarence-thomas-sexual-harassment-hollywood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sexual harassment}}}\uc2 , and whose wife tried to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/11/ginni-thomas-wife-supreme-court-justice-clarence-arizona-republicans-undermining-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overthrow the government}}}\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 There is a war on women going on in America. There is a war on trans people. There is a war on gay people. There is a war on people of colour. There is a war on democracy. And guess what? Only one side of the government is really fighting. Roe v Wade wasn\u8217\'20\'19t overturned just like that: it was the result of the Republicans spending decades consolidating power and working towards advancing their vision of America. Democrats need to stop their milquetoast simpering about \u8220\'20\'1Ccivility\u8221\'20\'1D, their obsession with taskforces and polite bipartisan agreements, and start properly fighting back.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US government\uc2  regulates women more than guns\par \par \uc2 Roe v Wade was overturned the day after the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/jun/23/new-york-gun-ruling-supreme-court-reactions-democrats-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down}}}\uc2  100-year-old New York gun restrictions that made it tough to carry a concealed handgun outside the home. In the same week, then, the supreme court ruled that states don\u8217\'20\'19t have the right to pass their own gun-control laws but do have the right to pass their own women-control laws. Time to get uteruses reclassified as assault rifles, I guess.\par \par \uc2 Former chambermaid elected to French parliament\par \par \uc2 Rachel Keke, who used to be a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/17/cleaner-who-led-pay-strike-runs-to-be-mp-in-french-elections-rachel-keke"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hotel housekeeper}}}\uc2  and led a strike for better pay and conditions at a Paris hotel, beat President \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former sports minister in Sunday\u8217\'20\'19s legislative elections in France. She is now one of France\u8217\'20\'19s few working-class MPs. While that\u8217\'20\'19s exciting it should be noted that although Keke is on the left now, she has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.france24.com/en/france/20220623-maid-turned-mp-rachel-keke-new-star-of-french-left-admits-previously-backing-marine-le-pen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 admitted sharing posts}}}\uc2  supporting the far-right leader \uc2 Marine Le Pen\uc2  during the 2017 elections.\par \par \uc2 Women are credited less in science than men\par \par \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s contributions to research are \u8220\'20\'1Coften not known, not appreciated or ignored\u8221\'20\'1D, say the authors of a new study {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-022-01725-9?error=cookies_not_supported&code=0cdf3fe6-ab52-4b67-8eee-a45bce7bcb1b&utm_medium=Social&utm_campaign=nature&utm_source=Twitter#Echobox=1655917038"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published in Nature}}}\uc2 . The study shows that in order to be credited on scientific articles, women need to work harder than men. The research focused on women, but the authors \u8220\'20\'1Csaw similar patterns for people from other groups that are marginalized in science\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine begins first trial of Russian soldier charged with rape\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the first of what could be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/23/ukraine-to-begin-first-trial-of-russian-soldier-charged-with-rape-mikhail-romanov"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dozens of such cases}}}\uc2 . Although the soldier is being tried in absentia, this trial is still incredibly important. Rape has always been a weapon of war (Christina Lamb describes it as the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/apr/15/rape-weapon-ukraine-war-crime-sexual-violence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cheapest weapon known}}}\uc2  to man\u8221\'20\'1D) and there is all-too-rarely any accountability.\par \par \uc2 Chinese city stripped of \u8216\'20\'18civilised\u8217\'20\'19 title after attack on female diners\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month a group of women were viciously attacked at a restaurant in the northern Chinese city of Tangshan. The attack was caught on video and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/21/chinese-police-investigated-over-handling-of-restaurant-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made headlines}}}\uc2  around the world. Nine men have since been arrested and now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/22/chinese-city-tangshan-stripped-of-civilised-title-assault-four-women-restaurant-china"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tangshan has been removed}}}\uc2  from China\u8217\'20\'19s list of \u8220\'20\'1Cnational civilised cities\u8221\'20\'1D. If you\u8217\'20\'19re wondering what on earth a civilised city is, there\u8217\'20\'19s an explainer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uts.edu.au/about/faculty-arts-and-social-sciences/research/fass-research-projects/spatial-research-cities-china/national-civilised-city"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Abhorrent and systemic\u8217\'20\'19 culture of sexual abuse in Australian mining\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/06/23/business/western-australia-mining-sexual-abuse-intl-hnk/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 parliamentary inquiry published on Thursday}}}\uc2  found that mining in Western Australia is rife with misogyny and \u8220\'20\'1Csexual harassment is generally accepted or overlooked\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Israeli gunfire killed journalist Shireen Abu Aqleh, \uc2 UN\uc2  says\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/06/24/1107254898/israeli-gunfire-shireen-abu-akleh-un-human-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UN office for human rights}}}\uc2  is the latest body to say that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/11/shireen-abu-akleh-killing-al-jazeera-voice-events-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Abu Aqleh}}}\uc2  was killed by Israeli forces. How many more investigations do there need to be before someone is held accountable?\par \par \uc2 The website saving home sewing history from the trash\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CScholarship around patterns and home sewing is still relatively underappreciated, often dismissed as women\u8217\'20\'19s work or insignificant to fashion and art,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theverge.com/23169321/commercial-pattern-archive-home-sewing-database"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes the Verge}}}\uc2 . The Commercial Pattern Archive is trying to change that; it has preserved about 65,000 home sewing patterns going back to the 1800s.\par \par \uc2 The week in parasite-archy\par \par \uc2 Ninety percent of us are home to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2022/jun/22/tiny-mites-demodex-folliculorum-parasites-gene-loss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 horny little mites called }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2022/jun/22/tiny-mites-demodex-folliculorum-parasites-gene-loss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Demodex folliculorum}}}\uc2 . Every night when we go to sleep, the tiny parasites emerge to have sex on our faces. And while that sounds pretty disgusting it turns out they probably keep our pores unplugged and our skin nice and fresh. Now, however, the mites are facing extinction. Perhaps not the most important threat we face at the moment, but a dermatological mite-mare nonetheless.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Arwa Mahdawi\u8217\'20\'19s new book, Strong Female Lead, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://linktr.ee/ARWAMAHDAWI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 available for order}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220625ei6p001gu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
