\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s important to fight\u8217\'20\'19: US cities erupt in protest as Roe v Wade falls\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levin in Los Angeles and Victoria Bekiempis in New York \par \uc2 1,255 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2022\par 12:47 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Soon after the supreme court struck down \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protection, pro-choice demonstrators took to the streets\par \par \uc2 Massive protests swept across the US in response to the supreme court decision overturning the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Soon after the decision was released on Friday, reversing federal reproductive protections that have been in place for half a century, pro-choice demonstrators began gathering in major cities and smaller towns in a wide range of communities and regions.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/demonstrators-supreme-court-protest-dobbs-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 large demonstration}}}\uc2  outside the supreme court in Washington DC \u8211\'20\'13 where activists shouted, \u8220\'20\'1CThis decision must not stand! Legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand!\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CWe won\u8217\'20\'19t go back!\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 protesters rallied in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Reuters/status/1540447904837402624"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York City}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Reuters/status/1540426827943931904"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Los Angeles}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abc7chicago.com/chicago-abortion-protest-roe-v-wade-near-me-federal-plaza/11993602/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chicago}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BettieCrossTV/status/1540457147179335684"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Austin}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JohnWFerguson/status/1540476486158880770?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1540476486158880770%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fus-news%2Flive%2F2022%2Fjun%2F24%2Froe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Houston}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RebeccaWSMV/status/1540456839267192832"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nashville}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/narwhallington/status/1540463466418429952"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas City}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b65e858f0867712f95f2c8#block-62b65e858f0867712f95f2c8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Topeka}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/chasitymaynard0/status/1540441867778760704"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tallahassee}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/32BJSEIU/status/1540485813485568000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Miami}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PhotoJFish/status/1540456820497596416"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oklahoma}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KatieTerhuneID/status/1540499240819904512"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Boise}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wgno.com/news/local/crowds-protest-roe-overturn-outside-new-orleans-courthouse/?utm_campaign=socialflow&utm_source=t.co&utm_medium=referral&utm_content=Louisiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Orleans}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/detroitnews/status/1540408833209688064"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Detroit}}}\uc2 . Solidarity protests also erupted overseas in London and Berlin.\par \par \uc2 In Arizona, people protesting the decision in Phoenix were sent fleeing when police fired tear gas from the state capitol building after demonstrators banged on the doors of the senate, according to eyewitness reports.\par \par \uc2 NOW This is what's going on outside the Arizona State Senate building: tear gas fired at people on Capitol mall protesting Roe decision. Tear gas fired from windows of the Old Capitol building. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/sfCm5xpYRd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/sfCm5xpYRd}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Brahm Resnik (@brahmresnik) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/brahmresnik/status/1540544973967224832?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m in a state of mourning and also very angry, and I want to turn that feeling into something where I can contribute to the solution,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary McNamara, a San Francisco attorney who was heading out to protest in the northern California city. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to go to the streets and raise our voices, even in blue states where our rights are protected. This is one of the most consequential decisions of the past 50 years \u8230\'20\'26 and we\u8217\'20\'19re entering into a very dark era.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McNamara is president of the \uc2 Bar Association of San Francisco\uc2 , which is organizing to provide free legal services to people affected by the end of Roe v Wade protections. She added: \u8220\'20\'1CI have no faith that the supreme court is going to stop here. I think this is the start of a massive retrenchment on individual rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Washington Square park in New York, Lucy Schneider, 101, arrived with her granddaughter and carried a sign that said, Centenarian for Choice. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m very much opposed to the current supreme court and everything they\u8217\'20\'19re doing. It\u8217\'20\'19s just awful,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding, \u8220\'20\'1CI want her to be free to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary. I hope it won\u8217\'20\'19t come to that, but I want her to be able to.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Her granddaughter, Emily Savin, 36, said she has been advocating for choice since high school.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was important to me to fight for this. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think I could fully grasp that it could really be taken away \u8230\'20\'26 I\u8217\'20\'19m heartbroken and angry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meet Lucy Schneider, 101, who is in the park with her granddaughter, Emily Savin, 36, to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hlpWrClX9M"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hlpWrClX9M}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Victoria Bekiempis (@vicbekiempis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vicbekiempis/status/1540467249647067138?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Nearby, Kelsey Clough, 29, said, \u8220\'20\'1CIt wasn\u8217\'20\'19t an option not to be here. It kind of feels like my whole life\u8217\'20\'19s falling apart when I see little kids get shot in a classroom and all I see is politicians trying to control what I do. I feel pretty helpless, but if me being here, holding my sign, is going to help people, I want to be.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 By the evening, protesters had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vicbekiempis/status/1540497698922577921"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 taken over}}}\uc2  Park Avenue in Manhattan, shouting, \u8220\'20\'1CWhose streets? Our streets!\u8221\'20\'1D before marching toward Times Square where demonstrators shouted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vicbekiempis/status/1540512103433379841"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chants against Fox News}}}\uc2  outside its offices.\par \par \uc2 In Washington DC, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/demonstrators-supreme-court-protest-dobbs-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outside the supreme court}}}\uc2 , where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1540362945921785856"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 officers in riot gear}}}\uc2  were deployed, protester Sara Kugler said, \u8220\'20\'1CThis has been a fight 30 years in the making to overturn women and people\u8217\'20\'19s fundamental rights to make decisions about their body. There is no coming back from this. There is no response other than outrage and action.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists also gathered outside the court celebrating the decision soon after it was announced, while critics {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP/status/1540364971619524609"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chanted}}}\uc2  that the court was \u8220\'20\'1Cillegitimate\u8221\'20\'1D. Elsewhere in the nation\u8217\'20\'19s capital city, a pro-choice demonstrator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/regulation/court-battles/3536331-dc-bridge-shuts-down-after-pro-abortion-rights-activist-scales-arch/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shut down}}}\uc2  a bridge after climbing its arch, and called on others to engage in nonviolent civil resistance.\par \par \uc2 Kelsey Clough, 29, holds a sign that reads: "If I put a gun up my pussy, will you give me your rights back?" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Y4HTF4haDB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Y4HTF4haDB}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Victoria Bekiempis (@vicbekiempis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vicbekiempis/status/1540481135637143553?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 In Missouri, one of the states with a \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger law\u8221\'20\'1D to automatically ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Roe decision, an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-decision-reaction-republicans-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  clinic escort in the city of Jackson}}}\uc2  told a reporter, \u8220\'20\'1CWe are looking at suffering and death. How should we feel? We see what\u8217\'20\'19s coming. Those with means, they will get what they need. Those without it, they will suffer. America is not ready for what\u8217\'20\'19s about to happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2 , the Missouri congresswoman who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RebXsll-awc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoken out}}}\uc2  about her own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a teenager, tweeted: \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care IS healthcare. It was so before this. And it will remain so after this. We don\u8217\'20\'19t care what a far-right extremist supreme court that is in a crisis of legitimacy says. Your racist, sexist, classist ruling won\u8217\'20\'19t stop us from accessing the care we need.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Indra Lusero, the director of Elephant Circle, a birth justice organization, who was heading to a protest in Grand Junction, Colorado, said the decision was not surprising, but still painful to absorb: \u8220\'20\'1CIt hits some of us directly in our bodies. I felt it physiologically. This implicates our physical autonomy so fundamentally.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lusero said they were thinking of the disparate harms of the decision as more pregnant people are unable to get abortions: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen people are coerced into carrying a pregnancy to term, that comes with risks, and those risks aren\u8217\'20\'19t equally borne because of inequities built into our system. Black and Indigenous folks in particular are more likely to experience mortality.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Boise, Idaho, a demonstrator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KatieTerhuneID/status/1540500406807105536"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held}}}\uc2  a sign that read, \u8220\'20\'1CI shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have to fight a fight my mom already won.\u8221\'20\'1D In Charlotte, North Carolina, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BHAMonTV/status/1540485027644973056?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1540485027644973056%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fus-news%2Flive%2F2022%2Fjun%2F24%2Froe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 activists shouted}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CMy body, my choice!\u8221\'20\'1D And in downtown Los Angeles, marchers took over the streets, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PplsCityCouncil/status/1540500215643262976"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chanting}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not your incubators. Fuck the court and the legislature!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In some liberal cities, progressive activists said they wanted to see a more aggressive response from Democratic elected officials. In San Francisco, Jackie Fielder, a former candidate for state senate, said she was frustrated to see Democrats like the House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , fundraising off of the decision given her recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/news/2022/05/in-case-youre-wondering-nancy-pelosi-is-still-supporting-the-only-antiabortion-house-democrat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support}}}\uc2  of an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Democrat, and the lack of action to expand the supreme court or abolish the filibuster: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s hard to believe that Democratic leadership are going to do anything.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fielder was heading to the annual Trans March in the city\u8217\'20\'19s Dolores Park where marchers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nananastia/status/1540506045268733957"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shouted}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CWhen our community is under attack, what do we do? Rise up, fight back!\u8221\'20\'1D and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nananastia/status/1540507652060356611"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held signs}}}\uc2  saying, \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are trans rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re very privileged in California to have access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other reproductive justice means, but we really gotta dig deep to figure out how to support people in other states. This is a matter of life and death.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lauren Burke contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220625ei6p0005l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
