\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturns  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights, upending Roe v Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza and Martin Pengelly in New York, and Sam Levin in Los Angeles \par \uc2 1,221 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2022\par 12:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 12\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Biden calls ruling in pivotal case Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization \u8216\'20\'18a tragic error\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has ruled there is no constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the United States, upending the landmark Roe v Wade case from nearly 50 years ago in a rare reversal of long-settled law that will fracture reproductive rights in America.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  called the ruling a \u8220\'20\'1Ctragic error\u8221\'20\'1D and the Republicans celebrating it \u8220\'20\'1Cwrong, extreme and out of touch\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The court, the president said, had pointed America down \u8220\'20\'1Can extreme and dangerous path\u8221\'20\'1D. Sounding an alarm over a concurring opinion by the conservative justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , Biden said key rights including same-sex marriage and access to contraception could now be targeted by the rightwing court.\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1CJustice Thomas said as much today. He explicitly called to reconsider the right of marriage equality. The right of couples to make their choices on contraception.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an extreme and dangerous path the court has now taken us on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The ruling, handed down a day after the court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/23/us-supreme-court-new-york-law-gun-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned a New York gun control law}}}\uc2 , came in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/explainer-mississippi-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 case}}}\uc2  Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, in which the last \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Mississippi opposed state efforts to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks and overturn Roe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe hold that Roe and Casey must be overruled,\u8221\'20\'1D said the majority opinion, written by \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and joined by four other conservatives, referring also to a 1992 ruling which buttressed Roe. \u8220\'20\'1CThe constitution makes no reference to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and no such right is implicitly protected by any constitutional provision.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  said he would have upheld Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s law but not overruled Roe.\par \par \uc2 The three liberal justices dissented, saying the majority opinion \u8220\'20\'1Csays that from the very moment of fertilization, a woman has no rights to speak of\u8221\'20\'1D, and that conservatives well knew states would enact \u8211\'20\'13 and in many cases had already enacted \u8211\'20\'13 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions to the moment of conception.\par \par \uc2 Under state restrictions, \u8220\'20\'1Ca woman will have to bear her rapist\u8217\'20\'19s child or a young girl her father\u8217\'20\'19s \u8211\'20\'13 no matter if doing so will destroy her life\u8221\'20\'1D, the liberal justices wrote.\par \par \uc2 At least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/what-states-abortion-clinics-access-trigger-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26}}}\uc2  states are expected to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  immediately or as soon as practicable. The Republican attorney general of Texas, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , celebrated the ruling and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texasattorneygeneral.gov/news/releases/ag-paxton-celebrates-end-roe-v-wade-announces-abortion-now-illegal-texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is illegal here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Dobbs decision is one of the most consequential in generations. It will have profound, immediate and enduring consequences for tens of millions of women and other people who can become pregnant. Ripple effects could play out over decades.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven if it\u8217\'20\'19s not completely unprecedented it\u8217\'20\'19s extremely rare,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Ziegler, a visiting professor of constitutional law at Harvard Law School, professor at the University of California, Davis School of Law and a historian of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s also extraordinary to do something like this so quickly, with no kind of advance notice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/supreme-court-abortion-law-leak-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 draft opinion}}}\uc2 , in which Alito laid out a caustic argument for reversing Roe v Wade, was leaked in May.\par \par \uc2 Swaths of the south and midwest are expected to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or impose severe restrictions, possibly forcing patients to travel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/05/abortion-deserts-clinics-access-closed-map"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hundreds of miles}}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/07/abortion-pill-at-home-activists-future-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 self-manage abortions}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://cmyers.middcreate.net/scholarship/#repropolicy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one economist}}}\uc2  has estimated such bans could result in 60,000 births a year among women unable to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , affecting 41% of women of reproductive age and hitting young, poor, Black and brown women and people who already have children hardest.\par \par \uc2 As Biden indicated, the decision could also herald restrictions in other areas of private life. In his opinion, Thomas explicitly encouraged fellow justices to \u8220\'20\'1Creconsider all of this court\u8217\'20\'19s\u8221\'20\'1D cases that establish rights to contraception and gay marriage and sex.\par \par \uc2 Thomas did not mention interracial marriage, another right many fear could be targeted. Thomas is Black. His wife, the far-right activist Ginni Thomas, is white.\par \par \uc2 Massive protests erupted outside the courthouse and in major cities and smaller towns across the US after the decision was announced. Democratic-run states and cities have vowed to uphold \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and welcome people from neighboring states with bans, and some district attorneys have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b625708f0867712f95f1c2#block-62b625708f0867712f95f1c2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pledged}}}\uc2  not to prosecute people for abortions even if new laws criminalize the procedure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBacklash to the decision is really unpredictable, and part of the reason we know that is because backlash to Roe was unpredictable,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ziegler.\par \par \uc2 Dr Iffath A Hoskins, president of the \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s decision is a direct blow to bodily autonomy, reproductive health, patient safety and health equity in the United States.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe principle of shared decision-making is founded on respect for people\u8217\'20\'19s expertise in their own bodies and lives and clinicians\u8217\'20\'19 expertise in science and medicine. There is no room within the sanctuary of the patient-physician relationship for individual lawmakers who wish to impose their personal religious or ideological views on others.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democratic-led states have enacted laws to aid patients who travel for abortions. Republican-led states have worked to further restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Some have debated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/29/us-abortion-supreme-court-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prosecuting women}}}\uc2  who seek abortions under homicide statutes.\par \par \uc2 Although an estimated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/1576/abortion.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 85% of Americans}}}\uc2  support legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under certain circumstances, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2021/nov/12/gerrymander-redistricting-map-republicans-democrats-visual"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 partisan manipulation}}}\uc2  of electoral districts has insulated Republican leaders from popular opinion.\par \par \uc2 Biden pointed to the midterm elections in November.\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis fall, Roe is on the ballot. Personal freedoms are on the ballot. The right to privacy, liberty, equality. They are on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUntil then, I will do all my power to protect a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right in states where they will face the consequences of today\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThough the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision cast a dark shadow over large swaths of the land, many states still recognize a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose. So if a woman lives in a state that restricts \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision does not prevent her from traveling from her home state to the state that allows it. It does not prevent a doctor in that state from treating her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs the attorney general has made clear, women must remain free to travel safely to another state to seek care they need. My administration will defend that bedrock right. If any state or local official, high or low, tries to interfere with a woman exercising her basic right to travel, I will do everything in my power to fight that deeply un-American attack.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The leak of the draft Roe decision prompted protests, some near justices\u8217\'20\'19 homes. Biden called for protests to remain peaceful, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CNo intimidation. Violence is never acceptable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Among Republican-led states , Missouri {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AGEricSchmitt/status/1540338042413944832?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1540338042413944832%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.kcur.org%2Fnews%2F2022-06-24%2Fmissouri-abortion-laws-roe-v-wade-birth-control-iud-ectopic-pregnancy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed to be first}}}\uc2  to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . South Dakota announced a special session to consider more restrictions.\par \par \uc2 In Illinois, the Democratic governor, JB Pritzker, called the general assembly into special session \u8220\'20\'1Cto further enshrine our commitment to reproductive healthcare rights and protections\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The US is one of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/01/22/upshot/abortion-us-roe-global.html?utm_term=6270c444daca2b8b1e81bcc53ad95514&utm_campaign=FirstEdition&utm_source=esp&utm_medium=Email&CMP=firstedition_email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only four countries}}}\uc2  since 1994 to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to the Center for Reproductive Rights, the others being Poland, Nicaragua and El Salvador. This will further set America apart from peer countries as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.news.vcu.edu/article/2022/04/us-life-expectancy-continued-to-fall-in-2021#:~:text=U.S.%20life%20expectancy%20decreased%20from,not%20yet%20been%20peer%20reviewed."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 life expectancy falls}}}\uc2 . It could also damage efforts to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/14/dr-tlaleng-mofokeng-roe-v-wade-reversal-un"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 advocate for the rights of women and girls globally}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220624ei6o002bi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
