\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Companies scramble to protect  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  access for employees after court ruling\b0\par\par\uc2 Dominic Rushe \par \uc2 556 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2022\par 05:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Disney\uc2 , \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 , \uc2 Levi Strauss\uc2 , \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  and others are offering to cover travel expenses but face a Republican backlash\par \par \uc2 Some of America\u8217\'20\'19s largest companies moved swiftly to protect their employees\u8217\'20\'19 access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Friday\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court decision to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 end the constitutional right}}}\uc2  to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US. The moves are likely to deepen an expanding rift between conservative Republicans and corporate America.\par \par \uc2 Disney\uc2 , \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 , \uc2 Levi Strauss\uc2  and \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  were among the companies to tell staff they would cover employee travel expenses for abortions in light of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to strike down Roe v Wade, the 1973 ruling that the constitution generally protects the right to choose an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe recognize the impact of the ruling and that we remain committed to providing comprehensive access to quality and affordable care for all of our employees, cast members and their families, including family planning and reproductive care, no matter where they live,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Disney\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 In a statement \uc2 Levi Strauss\uc2  said: ?? \u8220\'20\'1C We stand strongly against any actions that hinder the health and well-being of our employees, which means opposing any steps to restrict access to the full range of reproductive health care, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProtection of reproductive rights is a critical business issue impacting our workforce, our economy, and progress toward gender and racial equity. Given what is at stake, business leaders need to make their voices heard and act to protect the health and well-being of our employees.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The upending of Roe has left businesses scrambling to reassess their policies.\par \par \uc2 Jen Stark, co-director of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bsr.org/en/expertise/diversity-equity-and-inclusion-dei#overview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Center for Business and Social Justice}}}\uc2 , said the ruling was \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply destabilizing\u8221\'20\'1D for companies and their employees and the situation would probably get worse.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fall of Roe is just the end of the beginning. We will see more extreme public policy, unfortunately, at the state level and with even more extreme policy if there is a willingness at the federal level,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Republican legislators are already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/08/us-companies-abortion-travel-assistance-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatening companies}}}\uc2  that have said they will offer staff assistance in getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . After \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  revealed it would give staff travel assistance, conservatives in Congress {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/abortion-citi-republicans-bank/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked}}}\uc2  House and Senate administrators to cancel its contract with the company.\par \par \uc2 Legal scholars said Friday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling could open the way for attacks on other rights, including same-sex marriage, at a time when companies are facing Republican backlash for supporting the LGBTQ community.\par \par \uc2 Disney\uc2  is at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/09/ron-desantis-disney-republican-culture-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 loggerheads with Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 , Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor and a potential Republican presidential candidate, over his \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D bill, which bans teachers ??from holding classroom instruction about sexual orientation or gender identity.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProponents of extreme policy do issue a lot of punitive rhetoric,\u8221\'20\'1D said Stark. \u8220\'20\'1CUltimately a larger story is that these moves are economically destabilizing [for corporations] and sow a lot of chaos. On that issue alone, companies\u8217\'20\'19 antennas are up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Stark said companies may have tolerated extreme rhetoric in the past because they got what they needed in terms of tax and regulatory issues. Now \u8220\'20\'1Cthe collateral damage has increased, making it harder for companies to say one thing and do another, and the cost of that is going to be higher than the perception of backlash,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220625ei6p000jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
