\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Protests sweep across nation as supreme court overturns Roe v Wade \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh and Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 11,451 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2022\par 02:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Outrage pours over into streets as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are stripped awayDecision split on political lines, with six conservatives in favorFull story: \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturns Roe v WadeThe court just overturned Roe v Wade \u8211\'20\'13 what happens next?Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04am BST\par \par \uc2 A recap\par \par \uc2 * President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  condemned the ruling, calling it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b5e8b78f0814a0d5d429bb#block-62b5e8b78f0814a0d5d429bb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ca sad day for the court and for the country\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who as president installed three of the justices that voted to strike down Roe v Wade, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b5ef888f0814a0d5d42a1c#block-62b5ef888f0814a0d5d42a1c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly doesn\u8217\'20\'19t think the ruling is a good idea}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * States nationwide are scrambling to react to the decision, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b5e5f28f0875bb61abb16d#block-62b5e5f28f0875bb61abb16d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with many Republican-led governments moving to ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  immediately}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * West coast governors pledged {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b6143d8f0875bb61abb331#block-62b6143d8f0875bb61abb331"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their states would be havens for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * A Republican senator said she was duped by two of the supreme court justices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b5e31c8f0814a0d5d42979#block-62b5e31c8f0814a0d5d42979"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who she supported while insisting they would respect Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Protesters gathered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b5f6758f0814a0d5d42a62#block-62b5f6758f0814a0d5d42a62"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at the supreme court building in Washington DC}}}\uc2 , in cities and towns around the country \u8211\'20\'13 and even at the American embassy in London.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic staff in states like Texas has to abruptly stop providing care this morning.\par \par \uc2 * Among the conservative justices, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b5da528f0875bb61abb0c3#block-62b5da528f0875bb61abb0c3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 there was a slight difference of opinion in how far the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ruling should go}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Congress approved the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b601378f0814a0d5d42ab9#block-62b601378f0814a0d5d42ab9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bipartisan gun control compromise}}}\uc2 , sending the bill to Biden for his signature.\par \par \uc2 * House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said \u8220\'20\'1Cthe path forward will depend on the outcome of the upcoming midterm elections\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Chris Stein, Maanvi Singh\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/24/us-cities-protest-roe-v-wade-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s important to fight\u8217\'20\'19: US cities erupt in protest as Roe v Wade falls}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.19am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Contraception, gay marriage: \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  signals new targets for supreme court\par \par \uc2 Many Americans reacted to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to reverse {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  and remove federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US with shock, but many also asked a terrified question: what might be next?\par \par \uc2 The conservative justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  appeared to offer a preview of the court\u8217\'20\'19s potential future rulings, suggesting the rightwing-controlled court may return to the issues of contraception access and marriage equality, threatening LGBTQ+ rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn future cases, we should reconsider all of this court\u8217\'20\'19s substantive due process precedents, including Griswold, Lawrence, and Obergefell,\u8221\'20\'1D Thomas wrote in his concurring opinion to the ruling on Roe.\par \par \uc2 Griswold v Connecticut established a married couple\u8217\'20\'19s right to use contraception without government interference in 1965. The court ruled in the 2003 case of Lawrence v Texas that states could not criminalize sodomy, and Obergefell v Hodges established the right for same-sex couples to marry in 2015.\par \par \uc2 In the decision written by Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , the conservative majority makes it clear that the decision in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization should not be interpreted as a threat to other major precedent cases. But the court\u8217\'20\'19s three liberal justices \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2 , \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  and Elena Kagan \u8211\'20\'13 dismissed that logic as a farce in their fiery dissenting opinion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEither the mass of the majority\u8217\'20\'19s opinion is hypocrisy or additional constitutional rights are under threat,\u8221\'20\'1D the liberal justices wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is one or the other.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/clarence-thomas-roe-gay-marriage-contraception-lgbtq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Contraception, gay marriage: Clarence Thomas signals new targets for supreme court}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.18am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31am BST\par \par \uc2 In states across the US, staff at \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics faced confusion and chaos as they tried to decipher the implications of the supreme court ruling in each state.\par \par \uc2 In several state\u8217\'20\'19s, bans on abortions in most cases were triggered immediately \u8211\'20\'13 in others, like Idaho, a law triggering an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban will take effect in 30 days.\par \par \uc2 Here the \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/us/abortion-laws-roe-v-wade.html?name=styln-abortion-us&region=TOP_BANNER&block=storyline_menu_recirc&action=click&pgtype=LegacyCollection&variant=show&is_new=false"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 captures}}}\uc2  the scene at a Texas clinic where abortions came too an abrupt stop today:\par \par \uc2 The phones started ringing, as they always did, moments after Houston Women\u8217\'20\'19s Reproductive Services opened for business at 9 a.m. on Friday \u8212\'20\'14 with patients in need of abortions calling to secure a spot on the schedule.\par \par \uc2 Then, 12 minutes later, it all came to a stop. The Supreme Court had overturned Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCan we still do abortions today?\u8221\'20\'1D asked patient advocate Marjorie Eisen, thinking about the 20 women they had booked for appointments.\par \par \uc2 Several were already in the waiting room, scrolling through their phones as they waited.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19am BST\par \par \uc2 More scenes from around the country.\par \par \uc2 In Miami, the mayor of Miami-Dade county \uc2 Daniella Levine Cava\uc2  joined a rally:\par \par \uc2 Daniella Levine Cava\uc2  at a Miami protest. Photograph: Anadolu Agency/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, crowds from coast to coast are marching in the streets and gathering outside government buildings.\par \par \uc2 In Boise, Idaho.\par \par \uc2 enltrSeveral hundred people are in front of Boise City Hall right now protesting against the overturning of Roe v. Wade. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cBF7Q036h6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cBF7Q036h6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Katie Terhune (@KatieTerhuneID) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KatieTerhuneID/status/1540499240819904512?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 And Charlotte, North Carolina:\par \par \uc2 enltrProtesters shouting \u8220\'20\'1Cmy body, my choice\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 we are nearing the EpiCentre in uptown {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Charlotte?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Charlotte}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CXixp1f5Sz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CXixp1f5Sz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Brandon Hamilton (@BHAMonTV) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BHAMonTV/status/1540485027644973056?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 And New Orleans, Louisiana:\par \par \uc2 enltrCrowds protest Roe overturn outside New Orleans courthouse {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nQqeyrQiGF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/nQqeyrQiGF}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OAVq8kRq7o"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/OAVq8kRq7o}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 WGNO-TV (ABC) New Orleans (@WGNOtv) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WGNOtv/status/1540485496375222272?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 And Houston, Texas:\par \par \uc2 enltrMore than 100 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights demonstrators gathered outside the federal courthouse in downtown Houston. Speakers expected to begin in a few minutes. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/M7rOnSlFQ7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/M7rOnSlFQ7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 John Wayne Ferguson (@JohnWFerguson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JohnWFerguson/status/1540476486158880770?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 And Topeka, Kansas:\par \par \uc2 Pro-choice advocates gather outside a the Kansas statehouse. Photograph: Charlie Riedel/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05am BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Victoria Bekiempis is on the ground in New York City where the streets are filled with demonstrators.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a view through her eyes:\par \par \uc2 enltrTo give a sense of how many people are here, this is the scene up Park Avenue South.... {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VsuVEM0mLu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VsuVEM0mLu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Victoria Bekiempis (@vicbekiempis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vicbekiempis/status/1540497698922577921?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.26am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.54am BST\par \par \uc2 The decision to overturn Roe v Wade has sparked outrage and concern around the world.\par \par \uc2 In London, protesters gathered outside the US embassy holding signs and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sianabradley/status/1540407375655538689?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1540407375655538689%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fmetro.co.uk%2F2022%2F06%2F24%2Fprotesters-gather-outside-us-embassy-in-london-angry-at-abortion-ruling-16889136%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chanting}}}\uc2 . Demonstrations also took place in Edinburgh, the Independent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.independent.co.uk/news/uk/boris-johnson-united-states-jeremy-corbyn-vauxhall-mayor-b2109142.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 , while sympathy protests were also reported in Berlin.\par \par \uc2 A protest at the embassy in London on Friday. Photograph: Guy Smallman/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has rounded up some reactions from international figures and world leaders, as well as activists who fear the reverberations of the US decision in their own countries:\par \par \uc2 The head of the \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2 , \uc2 Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus\uc2 , said he\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cconcerned and disappointed\u8221\'20\'1D. Writing on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , he called the ruling was \u8220\'20\'1Cboth reducing women\u8217\'20\'19s rights and access to health care.\u8221\'20\'1D He said there was \u8220\'20\'1Cirrefutable\u8221\'20\'1D evidence that restricting legal abortions can drive women and girls to unsafe and sometimes deadly procedures.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the French president Emmanuel Macron tweeted that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Ca fundamental right for all women\u8221\'20\'1D that must be protected. The \uc2 French Foreign Ministry\uc2  urged US federal authorities \u8220\'20\'1Cto do everything possible\u8221\'20\'1D to ensure American women can have continued access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , calling it \u8220\'20\'1Ca health and survival issue for young girls and women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The end of constitutional protections for abortions in the United States on emboldened \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents around the world, while advocates for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights worried it could threaten recent moves toward legalization in their countries.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s overturning of the landmark decision \u8220\'20\'1Cshows that these types of rights are always at risk of being steamrolled,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ruth Zurbriggen, an Argentinian activist and member of the Companion Network of Latin America and the Caribbean, a group favoring \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 In Kenya, Phonsina Archane watched news of Friday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling and said she froze for a while in a state of panic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is being done in America, which should be an example when it comes to the women\u8217\'20\'19s rights movement,\u8221\'20\'1D said Archane, an activist for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. \u8220\'20\'1CIf this is happening in America, what about me here in Africa? It\u8217\'20\'19s a very, very sad day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.26am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.59am BST\par \par \uc2 How Americans lost their right to abortions: a victory for conservatives, 50 years in the making\par \par \uc2 The short version of how Americans lost their right to terminate a pregnancy might be summed up in one name: Trump.\par \par \uc2 The real estate tycoon and reality-TV star first shocked the world by winning the US presidency, then rewarded his base by confirming three supreme court justices to a nine-member bench, thus rebalancing the court to lean conservative for a generation to come.\par \par \uc2 That short road led to Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, an opinion released this week in which supreme court justices voted to overturn the landmark case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , which in 1973 granted a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The end of federal protection for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/05/abortion-deserts-clinics-access-closed-map"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lead to 26 states}}}\uc2  banning the procedure immediately or as soon as practicable, affecting tens of millions of US women and people who can become pregnant.\par \par \uc2 The decision comes even though about 85% of Americans favor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/1576/abortion.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legal \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in at least some circumstances. Why, and how, a decision opposed by a majority of Americans came about has everything to do with political power, experts said.\par \par \uc2 The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe best organized faction in American politics\u8221\'20\'1D, said Frederick Clarkson, an expert on the Christian right and a senior research analyst at Political Research Associate, a progressive thinktank in Massachusetts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey understand they\u8217\'20\'19re a minority of the population, of the electorate, and certainly a minority set of views on reproductive rights issues,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut because they know that, they\u8217\'20\'19ve found effective ways of maximizing their political clout by being better organized than numerically greater factions who are less well organized.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Put another way, he said, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement \u8220\'20\'1Cmastered the tools of democracy to achieve undemocratic outcomes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The currents that led to the Dobbs decision are among the most powerful in American politics today. Over decades, a religious movement prevailed by harnessing the forces of polarization, the erosion of constitutional norms and the manipulation of US democracy, scholars said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not like we\u8217\'20\'19ve had this slow erosion of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights,\u8221\'20\'1D said Neil Siegel, an expert in constitutional law and professor at \uc2 Duke University\uc2  who clerked for former liberal Justice \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2 . Instead, justices issued an opinion that \u8220\'20\'1Cis utterly dismissive of what has been constitutional law for literally five decades\u8221\'20\'1D, and was \u8220\'20\'1Crepeatedly affirmed by justices appointed by both parties\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/24/how-americans-lost-federal-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How Americans lost their right to abortions: a victory for conservatives, 50 years in the making}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the scene in Philly:\par \par \uc2 enltrBig ol crowd of protestors out here in front of Philadelphia\u8217\'20\'19s City Hall (and a lot of cute dogs) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/l5pUaEcHxl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/l5pUaEcHxl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kim \u8220\'20\'1CFIGHT LIKE HELL??Out Now!\u8221\'20\'1D Kelly (@GrimKim) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GrimKim/status/1540470524643508224?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates demonstrate in Philadelphia. Photograph: Matt Slocum/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.36am BST\par \par \uc2 What was \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  like before Roe v Wade?\par \par \uc2 In 1968, Ann Hill discovered she was pregnant while a law student. With \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal, she was forced to have a backstreet operation. She explains how it inspired her to become a women\u8217\'20\'19s rights campaigner.\par \par \uc2 As told to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/eminesaner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Emine Saner}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Somehow, I got the name and number of one of the most well-known doctors in the area who performed abortions illegally, Nathan Rappaport. A man with a deep gravelly voice told me that it would be $500 upfront, and scheduled the procedure for a Saturday morning, so I didn\u8217\'20\'19t miss any law school classes. A friend lent me the money and I went with another friend, Steve, to Rappaport\u8217\'20\'19s apartment in a brownstone on New York\u8217\'20\'19s Upper West Side.\par \par \uc2 It looked like a home: you first walked into a living area, where Steve had to stay, then I was taken into a room that looked like a dentist\u8217\'20\'19s office, which had a chair with stirrups. I was nervous \u8211\'20\'13 you do not go for medical procedures at an apartment \u8211\'20\'13 but it was just a matter of immediacy. Get it done, and then I\u8217\'20\'19ll breathe again. I was frightened about the procedure, but I knew I was doing the right thing. Fortunately, I hadn\u8217\'20\'19t known beforehand that he had been imprisoned for manslaughter, after a woman whom he had given \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to had died.\par \par \uc2 When I came round from the anaesthesia \u8211\'20\'13 I think he had given me ether \u8211\'20\'13 still groggy and trying to deal with everything, he foisted legal papers on me about his case. He knew I was a law student and wanted me to help him overturn his conviction and get his medical licence back.\par \par \uc2 I took the documents and left. I felt relief, but I was also in a lot of pain. Back in my dorm room at Yale, I was bleeding. I was worried about what would happen \u8211\'20\'13 was I going to bleed to death? I hadn\u8217\'20\'19t given much thought to the safety of it before because I knew I was going to do it. It may have been denial on my part. But that weekend, dealing with the pain and bleeding, I worried I had been permanently mutilated or would die.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, I went back to the original doctor I had seen, and told him I\u8217\'20\'19d had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He told me that he could admit me to the hospital to be \u8220\'20\'1Ccleaned out\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 that it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t illegal. Fortunately, the pain and bleeding stopped after a few days; I think he gave me antibiotics, concerned about infection.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/abortion-before-roe-v-wade-illegal-ann-hill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I was worried I had been permanently mutilated\u8217\'20\'19: what \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  was like before Roe v Wade}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.09am BST\par \par \uc2 The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Health, Education, Labor, and Pensions Committee will be holding a hearing next month to discuss the impact of the Dobbs decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am not going to stand idly by while Republicans rip away \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, drag this country back by half a century, and gear up for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban,\u8221\'20\'1D said committee chair Patty Murray. \u8220\'20\'1CI will use my gavel as chair of the health committee to shed light on the devastating harm this supreme court decision will have on women\u8217\'20\'19s health in this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But once again, it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear what this hearing could do, other than \u8220\'20\'1Cshed light\u8221\'20\'1D. In a divided Senate, it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear that there are 60 votes needed to move past a filibuster and pass any sort of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.40am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.00am BST\par \par \uc2 In New York\u8217\'20\'19s Washington Square Park, Lucy Schneider, 101, and her granddaughter, Emily Savin, were among those in the park in opposing the decision. Schneider held a side that read \u8220\'20\'1CCentenarian for Choice\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrMeet Lucy Schneider, 101, who is in the park with her granddaughter, Emily Savin, 36, to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hlpWrClX9M"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hlpWrClX9M}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Victoria Bekiempis (@vicbekiempis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vicbekiempis/status/1540467249647067138?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m very much opposed to the current supreme court and everything they\u8217\'20\'19re doing it\u8217\'20\'19s just awful,\u8221\'20\'1D Schneider said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want her to be free to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary. I hope it won\u8217\'20\'19t come to that, but I want her to be able to,\u8221\'20\'1D Schneider said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.40am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez was escorted by police on Friday as she walked the short distance separating the Capitol and the supreme court buildings to join pro-choice rights groups protesting there.\par \par \uc2 The New York representative addressed the crowd amid chaos through a bullhorn calling for people to go \u8220\'20\'1Cinto the streets\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ckeep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  safe and legal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.46am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are looking at suffering and death,\u8221\'20\'1D said an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic escort in Jackson, Missouri. \u8220\'20\'1CHow do you think we feel?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York City \u8217\'20\'19s Washington Square park was packed with what appeared to be more than 1,000 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights protesters early Friday evening as the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  handed down a decision this morning that overturned the landmark court decision Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re very upset about what\u8217\'20\'19s going on in the world, and I\u8217\'20\'19m feeling more and more and more like we\u8217\'20\'19re sliding to theocracy and it\u8217\'20\'19s hard to wake up thinking that women are lesser citizens,\u8221\'20\'1D said Erin, 49. Erin, a non-profit sector worker who asked that her surname not be used, was visiting the city from Arizona.\par \par \uc2 In that state, advocates are preparing for officials to crack down on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Erin said she wasn\u8217\'20\'19t shocked by the decision.\par \par \uc2 It was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot surprising, honestly\u8221\'20\'1D, Erin said. \u8220\'20\'1CI know a lot of my friends and family were holding out hope that it wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t come down the way it did.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s devastating,\u8221\'20\'1D Erin said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really hard.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.42am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some more scenes from protests around the country:\par \par \uc2 People gathered at Union Square in New York to protest against the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision. Photograph: Spencer Platt/Getty Images Protestors take part in a \u8220\'20\'1Cdie in\u8221\'20\'1D in Norman, Oklahoma. Photograph: Sue Ogrocki/AP Protesters gathered outside the courthouse in Los Angeles. Photograph: David McNew/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 During a press conference held this afternoon, California governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  signed new legislation codifying the state\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to ensure safe access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care for those outside its borders.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Friday, Newsom also joined the governors of Washington and Oregon, who together, pledged to secure \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights across the west coast for residents and those across the country who will be impacted by the ruling.\par \par \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s new law quashes civil judgements from states hostile to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that have sought to bar their residents from traveling to places where reproductive care is legal. Signaling that this is just the first of a dozen pieces of legislation that will cross the governor\u8217\'20\'19s desk in the coming weeks, Newsom emphasized that the state will do all it can to serve as a safe-haven while protecting its own residents from what he cast as profound hypocrisy from the highest court in the nation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not just about women. This is not just about choice,\u8221\'20\'1D Newsom said, nodding to the erosion of rights outlined for by Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  in his concurring opinion, calling for reevaluation of precedents upholding same-sex marriage and contraception. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a serious moment in American history,\u8221\'20\'1D Newsom continued. \u8220\'20\'1CThis moment punctuates what is really going on this country and they are just winding up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the scene at the supreme court:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe scene at the Supreme Court this afternoon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DvUQbCc51s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DvUQbCc51s}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kirsten Appleton (@kirstenappleton) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kirstenappleton/status/1540426336925360130?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights demonstrators protest outside the supreme court building as the court rules in the Dobbs v Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case. Photograph: Jim Bourg/Reuters Protestors outside the supreme court. Photograph: Evelyn Hockstein/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Amanda Gorman, first national youth poet laureate, wrote this in reaction to today\u8217\'20\'19s ruling:\par \par \uc2 enltrWe will not be delayed.\par \par \uc2 We will not be masquerade\par \par \uc2 To the tale of a handmade.\par \par \uc2 We will not let Roe v. Wade slowly fade.\par \par \uc2 Because when we show up today,\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re already standing up\par \par \uc2 With the tomorrow we made.\par \par \uc2 Let's get to work: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BNVLVLM6Ji"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/BNVLVLM6Ji}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Amanda Gorman (@TheAmandaGorman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheAmandaGorman/status/1540403105182846976?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lisa Murkowski, one of two Senate Republicans who supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, said she would \u8220\'20\'1Cwork with a broader group\u8221\'20\'1D to restore rights.\par \par \uc2 The Alaska senator said:\par \par \uc2 I am continuing to work with a broader group to restore women\u8217\'20\'19s freedom to control their own health decisions wherever they live. Legislation to accomplish that must be a priority.\par \par \uc2 But the sentiment is unlikely to get her very far. Encoding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections will require support from all the Senate Democrats and 10 Republicans.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Dozens of elected prosecutors across the US have signed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fairandjustprosecution.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/FJP-Post-Dobbs-Abortion-Joint-Statement.pdf?utm_content=&utm_medium=email&utm_name=&utm_source=govdelivery&utm_term="}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  pledging not to prosecute abortions, including officials in states with \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger laws\u8221\'20\'1D that are in the process of banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrDAs pledging not to prosecute \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in states with trigger laws + bans include officials in St Louis, MO; Jefferson Co in Alabama; Dallas, Travis, Bexar, Nueces, Fort Bend counties in Texas; Genesee, Hinds, Washtenaw, Ingham, Marquette counties in Mich; and Hinds County, Miss {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vGkUKnGJnG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vGkUKnGJnG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levin (@SamTLevin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SamTLevin/status/1540412070809567233?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 A total of 83 district attorneys and state attorneys general agreed to the commitment, saying they were united in their belief that \u8220\'20\'1Cprosecutors have a responsibility to refrain from using limited criminal legal system resources to criminalize personal medical decisions\u8221\'20\'1D, adding, \u8220\'20\'1CAs such, we decline to use our offices\u8217\'20\'19 resources to criminalize reproductive health decisions and commit to exercise our well settled discretion and refrain from prosecuting those who seek, provide, or support abortions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In addition to commitments from officials in blue states that have laws defending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, the signatories include local district attorneys in Missouri, Texas, Michigan and Mississippi. Even with Roe in effect, prosecutors across the US have brought criminal charges against people for pregnancy loss and other outcomes, and advocates say this kind of criminalization will significantly escalate with the Roe decision overturned.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/03/california-stillborn-prosecution-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 She was jailed for losing a pregnancy. Her nightmare could become more common}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Where are abortions now banned?\par \par \uc2 In nine states, bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  took effect today, following the ruling. These states include: Alabama, Arkansas, Kentucky, Louisiana, Missouri, Oklahoma, South Dakota, Utah and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 In other states, bans on abortions in most cases will take effect in 30 days. And in some others, legislatures and legal bodies will determine how to proceed \u8211\'20\'13 convening to legislate new restrictions, or provide guidance on previously unenforceable \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/abortion-laws-by-state-map-clinics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  deserts: America\u8217\'20\'19s new geography of access to care \u8211\'20\'13 mapped}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a letter to Democratic colleagues, House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  acknowledged that Thomas\u8217\'20\'19 concurring opinion was \u8220\'20\'1Cof special concern\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She also said that when it comes to gun control and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, \u8220\'20\'1CIt is clear that the path forward will depend on the outcome of the upcoming midterm elections.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe contrast between our parties could not be clearer: while Democrats are the party of freedom and safety, Republicans are the party of punishment and control,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe must \u8216\'20\'18Remember in November\u8217\'20\'19 that the rights of women, and indeed all Americans, are on the ballot.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 The repercussions from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling overturning the constitutional right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  continue to be felt across the country. Here is what has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 * President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  condemned the ruling, calling it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b5e8b78f0814a0d5d429bb#block-62b5e8b78f0814a0d5d429bb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ca sad day for the court and for the country\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who as president installed three of the justices that voted to strike down Roe v Wade, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b5ef888f0814a0d5d42a1c#block-62b5ef888f0814a0d5d42a1c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly doesn\u8217\'20\'19t think the ruling is a good idea}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * States nationwide are scrambling to react to the decision, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b5e5f28f0875bb61abb16d#block-62b5e5f28f0875bb61abb16d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with many Republican-led governments moving to ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  immediately}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * West coast governors pledged {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b6143d8f0875bb61abb331#block-62b6143d8f0875bb61abb331"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their states would be havens for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * A Republican senator said she was duped by two of the supreme court justices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b5e31c8f0814a0d5d42979#block-62b5e31c8f0814a0d5d42979"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who she supported while insisting they would respect Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Protesters are gathering {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b5f6758f0814a0d5d42a62#block-62b5f6758f0814a0d5d42a62"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at the supreme court building in Washington DC}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Among the conservative justices, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b5da528f0875bb61abb0c3#block-62b5da528f0875bb61abb0c3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 there was a slight difference of opinion in how far the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ruling should go}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Congress approved the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b601378f0814a0d5d42ab9#block-62b601378f0814a0d5d42ab9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bipartisan gun control compromise}}}\uc2 , sending the bill to Biden for his signature.\par \par \uc2 The US politics blog is now in the hands of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maanvi-singh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maanvi Singh}}}\uc2  on the west coast, who will take you through the final hours of a day with massive consequences for the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Dubbing it the \u8220\'20\'1CWest Coast Offense\u8221\'20\'1D, the Democratic governors of California, Oregon and Washington have announced a push to preserve \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access for their residents and people who come from neighboring states to seek the procedure.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Supreme Court has stripped women of their liberty and let red states replace it with mandated birth.\par \par \uc2 This is an attack on American freedom.\par \par \uc2 CA, OR and WA are creating the West Coast offensive. A road map for other states to stand up for women.\par \par \uc2 Time to fight like hell. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jBrJcTQVa8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jBrJcTQVa8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  (@GavinNewsom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GavinNewsom/status/1540368627144089600?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The three governors {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kpic.com/news/local/oregon-governor-you-cannot-ban-abortion-you-can-only-ban-safe-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.losangelesblade.com/2022/05/04/newsom-on-supreme-court-abortion-leak-its-about-controlling-women/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 been}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opb.org/article/2022/05/03/washington-governor-inslee-promises-to-defend-abortion-rights/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vocal}}}\uc2  about the issue {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/chief-justice-roberts-abortion-leak-investigation-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ever since the leak of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s draft opinion overturning Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 . In 2021, California governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  signed new laws protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and patients in the country\u8217\'20\'19s most-populous state:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/23/gavin-newsom-california-reproductive-freedom-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Governor vows to make California a \u8216\'20\'18reproductive freedom state\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 In the end, there weren\u8217\'20\'19t enough of them to stop the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority from overturning Roe v Wade, but the dissenting opinion from the court\u8217\'20\'19s three liberal justices \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2 , \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  and Elena Kagan acts as a requiem of sorts for the 49-year-old constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , now overturned:\par \par \uc2 Earlier this Term, this court signaled that Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s stratagem would succeed. Texas was one of the fistful of states to have recently banned abortions after six weeks of pregnancy. It added to that \u8220\'20\'1Cflagrantly unconstitutional\u8221\'20\'1D restriction an unprecedented scheme to \u8220\'20\'1Cevade judicial scrutiny.\u8221\'20\'1D And five justices acceded to that cynical maneuver. They let Texas defy this court\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional rulings, nullifying Roe and Casey ahead of schedule in the Nation\u8217\'20\'19s second largest state.\par \par \uc2 And now the other shoe drops, courtesy of that same five-person majority. (We believe that the chief justice\u8217\'20\'19s opinion is wrong too, but no one should think that there is not a large difference between upholding a 15-week ban on the grounds he does and allowing states to prohibit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the time of conception.) Now a new and bare majority of this court \u8211\'20\'13 acting at practically the first moment possible \u8211\'20\'13 overrules Roe and Casey. It converts a series of dissenting opinions expressing antipathy toward Roe and Casey into a decision greenlighting even total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. It eliminates a 50-year-old constitutional right that safeguards women\u8217\'20\'19s freedom and equal station. It breaches a core rule-of-law principle, designed to promote constancy in the law. In doing all of that, it places in jeopardy other rights, from contraception to same-sex intimacy and marriage. And finally, it undermines the court\u8217\'20\'19s legitimacy.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/24/supreme-court-roe-v-wade-breyer-sotomayor-kegan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Fewer rights than their grandmothers\u8217\'20\'19: read three justices\u8217\'20\'19 searing \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  dissent | Stephen Breyer, Sonia Sotomayor and Elena Kagan}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy, leader of the Republicans in the House of Representatives, has cheered the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most important pro-life ruling in American history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The people have won a victory. The right to life has been vindicated. The voiceless will finally have a voice. This great nation can now live up to its core principle that all are created equal. Not born equal. Created equal.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cookpolitical.com/ratings/house-race-ratings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans are viewed as favorites to take control of the House following this year\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections}}}\uc2 , and McCarthy would be a top contender for the job of speaker. In his speech, he alluded to what his priorities might be, should the GOP ascend to the majority.\par \par \uc2 As encouraging as today\u8217\'20\'19s decision is, our work is far from done. America remains one of only seven countries on earth that allows elective abortions in the third trimester, including China and North Korea. This is radical \u8211\'20\'13 but House Democrats continue to support it against the wishes of the American people. This Congress, every House Democrat has voted for extreme policies like taxpayer-funded \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , on demand, until the point of birth. But Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 radical agenda does not have Americans\u8217\'20\'19 support.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 The largest association of African American physicians in the United States has warned that the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights will harm racial minorities, particularly Black women.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, president of the \uc2 National Medical Association\uc2  Rachel Villanueva said:\par \par \uc2 This decision is unconstitutional, dangerous and discriminatory. It will not stop abortions from being performed, it will unfortunately only make the procedure more dangerous. Women of color, poor women and other disadvantaged individuals who don\u8217\'20\'19t have the resources to travel to obtain the medical care they need will be disproportionately impacted. At a time when maternal mortality rates are worsening, particularly for Black women, it is deeply disappointing that our institutions are actively harming \u8212\'20\'14 not helping \u8212\'20\'14 women\u8217\'20\'19s health. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is part of total health care for a woman. Doctors should be able to provide medical care based on scientific fact and evidence-based medicine, and free from any political interference. The entire medical community should be gravely concerned about the precedent this decision sets.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/volumes/70/ss/ss7009a1.htm#T6_down"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention data from 2019}}}\uc2 , the most recent year available, Black women have the highest rates of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with 23.8 per 1,000 people. Hispanic women had 11.7 abortions per 1,000 people, while for white women, the ratio was 6.6.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Will the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative justices stop with Roe v Wade? As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joan-greve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joan E Greve}}}\uc2  reports, today\u8217\'20\'19s decision in the Dobbs case contains signs that the Republican-appointed majority would like to go after other rights the court has established, such as same-sex marriage and access to contraception:\par \par \uc2 Many Americans reacted to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to reverse {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  and remove federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US with shock, but many also asked a terrified question: what might be next?\par \par \uc2 The conservative justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  appeared to offer a preview of the court\u8217\'20\'19s potential future rulings, suggesting the rightwing-controlled court may return to the issues of contraception access and marriage equality, threatening LGBTQ rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn future cases, we should reconsider all of this court\u8217\'20\'19s substantive due process precedents, including Griswold, Lawrence, and Obergefell,\u8221\'20\'1D Thomas wrote in his concurring opinion to the ruling on Roe.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/clarence-thomas-roe-gay-marriage-contraception-lgbtq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Contraception, gay marriage: Clarence Thomas signals new targets for supreme court}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congress passes gun control bill\par \par \uc2 The House of Representatives {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/24/senate-breakthrough-clears-way-for-toughening-us-gun-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has passed the bipartisan gun control measure}}}\uc2  that the Senate approved yesterday. It now awaits action from President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who said he will sign it.\par \par \uc2 enltr234-193, House sends guns package to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s desk. 14 Rs broke with their leadership: \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , Tom Rice, John Katko, Maria Salazar, Chris Jacobs, \uc2 Brian Fitzpatrick\uc2 , Peter Meijer and Fred Upton; and \uc2 Steve Chabot\uc2 , Mike Turner, David Joyce and Anthony Gonzalez\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1540389076490227720?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 While the bill tightens gun access for some Americans and funds mental health services, it is being passed just a day after a supreme court ruling that expanded the right to carry a concealed weapon nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/23/us-supreme-court-new-york-law-gun-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court overturns New York handgun law in bitter blow to gun-control push}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Medical experts have also decried the Dobbs opinion as threatening the health and autonomy of patients nationwide.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists\uc2  released a statement condemning the supreme court opinion from its president, Iffath A Hoskins, MD, FACOG, reading in part:\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s decision is a direct blow to bodily autonomy, reproductive health, patient safety and health equity in the United States.\par \par \uc2 Reversing the constitutional protection for safe, legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  established by the Supreme Court nearly fifty years ago exposes pregnant people to arbitrary, state-based restrictions, regulations, and bans that will leave many people unable to access needed medical care.\par \par \uc2 The restrictions put forth are not based on science nor medicine; they allow unrelated third parties to make decisions that rightfully and ethically should be made only by individuals and their physicians.\par \par \uc2 ACOG\uc2  condemns this devastating decision, which will allow state governments to prevent women from living with autonomy over their bodies and their decisions.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American Medical Association{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ama-assn.org/press-center/press-releases/ruling-egregious-allowance-government-intrusion-medicine?utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=social_ama&utm_term=7161024113&utm_campaign=Advocacy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also released a statement }}}\uc2  denouncing the Dobbs opinion, with its president Jack Resneck Jr MD, writing:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American Medical Association\uc2  is deeply disturbed by the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn nearly a half century of precedent protecting patients\u8217\'20\'19 right to critical reproductive health care\u8212\'20\'14representing an egregious allowance of government intrusion into the medical examination room, a direct attack on the practice of medicine and the patient-physician relationship, and a brazen violation of patients\u8217\'20\'19 rights to evidence-based reproductive health services.\par \par \uc2 States that end legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14they will end safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , risking [devastating] consequences, including patients\u8217\'20\'19 lives.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 CEOs are starting to react to the Dobbs news. \uc2 Mike Bloomberg\uc2  has called the decision \u8220\'20\'1Cthe worst attack on the rights of American women in generations \u8211\'20\'13 but it will not be the final word. We must make our voices heard at the ballot box.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling is the worst attack on the rights of American women in generations \u8211\'20\'13 but it will not be the final word. We must make our voices heard at the ballot box.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Mike Bloomberg\uc2  (@MikeBloomberg) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MikeBloomberg/status/1540345352796180485?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Yelp\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s co-founder Jeremey Stoppelman said the ruling puts \u8220\'20\'1Chealth in jeopardy, denies them their human rights, and threatens to dismantle the progress we\u8217\'20\'19ve made toward gender equality in the workplace since Roe. Business leaders must speak out now and call on Congress to codify Roe into law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many large US companies including \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 , Amazon, \uc2 Apple\uc2  and \uc2 Tesla\uc2  have pledged to provide travel assistance to employees who are in states that restrict abortions. The reaction from Republicans has been fierce with some threatening to cancel government contracts if they follow through with the plans.\par \par \uc2 The Walt Disney Company\uc2  said it would cover employee travel expenses for abortions in light of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 You can read more about the clash here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/08/us-companies-abortion-travel-assistance-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Corporate America buckles down for culture war on Roe v Wade}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 As 150 or so Democratic lawmakers joined angry protesters in front of the supreme court in Washington, plans emerged for scores of marches in towns and cities across the country.\par \par \uc2 From coast to coast, and border to border, pro-choice and women\u8217\'20\'19s rights groups jumped into action to organise civil action in parks, squares and outside government buildings as a way for ordinary people to express their anger at the ruling that will force pregnancy and parenthood on women and girls in half the country. You can find the map of \u8220\'20\'1Cwe won\u8217\'20\'19t go back\u8221\'20\'1D protests {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://map.wewontgoback.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  here. }}}\par \par \uc2 After years of political failure, some activists are preparing for direct action and civil disobedience targeting the country\u8217\'20\'19s economy.\par \par \uc2 The feminist group Women\u8217\'20\'19s March Action is calling on people to walk out of their workplaces and homes, and gather in front of their local courthouse wearing red. \u8220\'20\'1CThe vast majority of this country supports the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . When we walk out together, our collective power will shut down the nation and say loud and clear that we will not go back,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EmilianaGuereca/status/1540342299254595584?s=20&t=6vAQMUwY4FquP9fE-08UqQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  said organiser Emiliana Guereca.}}}\par \par \uc2 Also expect to see plenty of green pa\u241\'00\'F1uelos or bandannas \u8211\'20\'13 the symbol of the pro-choice movement in Latin America known as the green wave which has led to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans being overturned or relaxed in Argentina, Chile, Colombia and Mexico.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 America is reeling from the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision striking down the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with foes of the procedure cheering the justices\u8217\'20\'19 ruling and supporters calling it a calamity. It\u8217\'20\'19s the sort of political earthquake that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t happen in the United States that often.\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the main takeaways:\par \par \uc2 * President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  condemned the ruling, calling it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b5e8b78f0814a0d5d429bb#block-62b5e8b78f0814a0d5d429bb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ca sad day for the court and for the country\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who as president installed three of the justices who voted to strike down Roe v Wade, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b5ef888f0814a0d5d42a1c#block-62b5ef888f0814a0d5d42a1c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly doesn\u8217\'20\'19t think the ruling is a good idea}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * States nationwide are scrambling to react to the ruling, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b5e5f28f0875bb61abb16d#block-62b5e5f28f0875bb61abb16d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with many Republican-led governments moving to ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  immediately}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * A Republican senator said she was duped by two of the supreme court justices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b5e31c8f0814a0d5d42979#block-62b5e31c8f0814a0d5d42979"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who she supported while insisting they would respect Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Protesters are gathering at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b5dc868f0814a0d5d42922#block-62b5dc868f0814a0d5d42922"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the supreme court in Washington DC}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Among the conservative justices, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-decision-latest-updates?page=with:block-62b5da528f0875bb61abb0c3#block-62b5da528f0875bb61abb0c3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 there was a slight difference of opinion in how far the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ruling should go}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling might not have happened without \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . During his time in office, the Republican president appointed three of the conservative justices who voted to overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 But as the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reports, Trump is apparently not a fan of what the justices have handed down. Ever since a draft opinion of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision leaked last month, he\u8217\'20\'19s worried about what it will mean for the support of voters who were decisive in his election loss in 2020, and who he would need to turn to should he run again in 2024.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/24/us/trump-roe-wade-republicans.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 From the report}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Privately, Mr. Trump has told people repeatedly that he believes it will be \u8220\'20\'1Cbad for Republicans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The decision, Mr. Trump has told friends and advisers, will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/13/us/roe-overturned-women-republican-voters.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anger suburban women}}}\uc2 , a group who helped tilt the 2020 presidential race to \uc2 Joseph R. Biden Jr\uc2 ., and will lead to a backlash against Republicans in the November midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 His advisers had encouraged Mr. Trump to keep quiet about the issue until a ruling was issued, in part to ensure he was not accused of trying to influence the decision. Still, the contrast between Mr. Trump and conservatives who have heralded the decision and who worked in his administration, such as former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , has been striking. On Friday morning, Mr. Pence issued a statement saying, \u8220\'20\'1CLife won,\u8221\'20\'1D as he called for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents to keep fighting \u8220\'20\'1Cin every state in the land.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for Mr. Trump did not immediately respond to a request for comment about his private remarks, or his view of the ruling. But in an interview that Fox News published after the decision on Friday, Mr. Trump, asked about his role, said, \u8220\'20\'1CGod made the decision.\u8221\'20\'1D He said the decision was \u8220\'20\'1Cfollowing the Constitution, and giving rights back when they should have been given long ago.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think, in the end, this is something that will work out for everybody,\u8221\'20\'1D Mr. Trump told Fox News.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden closed his speech by denouncing the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority and appealing for his supporters to act at the ballot box.\par \par \uc2 The conservative majority of the supreme court shows how extreme it is, how far removed they are from the majority of this country. It made the United States an outlier among developed nations in the world. But this decision must not be the final word. My administration will use all of its appropriate lawful powers. Congress must act. But with your vote, you can act. You can have the final word. This is not over.\par \par \uc2 It remains to be seen how much the ruling will animate voters, particularly Democrats, in the upcoming midterm elections:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/abortion-midterms-election-scotus-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  to become key fight in US midterms after stunning court leak}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden has vowed to do whatever his administration can to allow people to access abortions where the procedure is legal, and warned states against effort to hinder people seeking reproductive health care.\par \par \uc2 I will do all in my power to protect a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right in states where they will face the consequences of today\u8217\'20\'19s decision. Now, the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision casts a dark shadow over large swaths of the land, many states in this country still recognize a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose. So a woman lives in a state that restricts \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision does not prevent her from traveling from her home state to the state that allows it, does not prevent a doctor in that state from treating her.\par \par \uc2 Biden warned that, \u8220\'20\'1CAny state or local official, high or low, tries to interfere with a woman\u8217\'20\'19s exercising their basic right to travel, I will do everything in my power to fight that deeply unamerican attack.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also said he was directing the health and human services department to ensure \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills \u8220\'20\'1Care available to the fullest extent possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden is connecting the court\u8217\'20\'19s action against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the upcoming midterm elections, saying Americans must choose politicians who back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights if they want to see the conservative justices\u8217\'20\'19 ruling undone.\par \par \uc2 Voters need to make their voices heard. This fall, they must elect more senators and representatives who codify woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose in the federal law once again, elect more state leaders to protect this right at the local level. We need to restore the protections of Roe as law of the land. We need to elect officials who will do that. This fall, Roe is on the ballot. Personal freedoms are on the ballot. The right to privacy, liberty equality. They\u8217\'20\'19re all on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Overturning Roe 'a sad day for the court and for the country' \u8211\'20\'13 Biden\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has decried the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision overturning the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , warning that it risks the health of women nationwide.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe court has done what it has never done done before: expressly take away a constitutional right that is so fundamental to so many Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a speech from the White House. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a sad day for the court and for the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow with Roe gone, let\u8217\'20\'19s be very clear, the health and life of women in this nation are now at risk.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 States nationwide are continuing to act in the wake of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s Dobbs decision, with Republican governors and officials moving to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the day the Lord has made; let us rejoice in it and be glad. Today, along with millions across Louisiana and America, I rejoice with my departed Mom and the unborn children with her in Heaven!\u8221\'20\'1D, Louisiana attorney general \uc2 Jeff Landry{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.ag.state.la.us/Article/13044"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a statement where he announced a law banning \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  in the state was now in effect}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 South Dakota has a similar such \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger law\u8221\'20\'1D banning the procedure, but governor \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  and the leaders of the state legislature also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.sd.gov/newsitem.aspx?id=30323"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced a special session \u8220\'20\'1Cto save lives and help mothers impacted by the decision\u8221\'20\'1D.}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe must do what we can to help mothers in crisis know that there are options and resources available for them. Together, we will ensure that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not only illegal in South Dakota \u8211\'20\'13 it is unthinkable,\u8221\'20\'1D Noem said.\par \par \uc2 The second-in-command of the state senate Lee Schoenbeck elaborated on the reasons for calling the legislature back into session: \u8220\'20\'1CA special session is necessary because we could not have known this winter in session that we would have this opportunity and new responsibility to protect lives presented by the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s decision. Also, there will be more work to do on the many challenges a post-Roe world presents in regular session next January\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In Illinois, Democratic governor JB Pritzker announced a special legislative session to make the state a haven for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in a region where many of its neighbors will do the opposite.\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OnMVD2BCFB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/OnMVD2BCFB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Governor JB Pritzker (@GovPritzker) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovPritzker/status/1540352556240871431?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A slap in the face to women\u8217\'20\'19: \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  reacts to the overturning of Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican senator Susan Collins supported justices \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  and \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  during the confirmation hearings and repeatedly reassured the public that they would not vote to overturn Roe v Wade. But both men joined in today\u8217\'20\'19s opinion doing just that, and now the Maine lawmaker says she was duped.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis decision is inconsistent with what Justices Gorsuch and Kavanaugh said in their testimony and their meetings with me, where they both were insistent on the importance of supporting long-standing precedents that the country has relied upon,\u8221\'20\'1D Collins said.\par \par \uc2 She elaborated further on her thoughts regarding the decision:\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court has abandoned a fifty-year precedent at a time that the country is desperate for stability. This ill-considered action will further divide the country at a moment when, more than ever in modern times, we need the Court to show both consistency and restraint. Throwing out a precedent overnight that the country has relied upon for half a century is not conservative. It is a sudden and radical jolt to the country that will lead to political chaos, anger, and a further loss of confidence in our government.\par \par \uc2 Collins noted she supported legislation that would codify the rights previously established by Roe v Wade into law, though its unclear if such legislation would win enough support from her Republican colleagues to make it through the senate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur goal with this legislation is to do what the Court should have done \u8212\'20\'14 provide the consistency in our \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws that Americans have relied upon for 50 years,\u8221\'20\'1D Collins said.\par \par \uc2 Susan Collins with \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  in 2018. Photograph: Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Luis Maga\u241\'00\'F1a/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court will issue more opinions on Monday 27 June, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to its website}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If today\u8217\'20\'19s ruling on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling expanding gun rights are any indication, the conservative majority may continue making major shifts to US law in the seven cases it has yet to issue opinions on.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Justice department condemns supreme court \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision\par \par \uc2 Attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  has denounced the supreme court ruling overturning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, warning it will harm people nationwide, particularly the poor and racial minorities.\par \par \uc2 From his statement:\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court has eliminated an established right that has been an essential component of women\u8217\'20\'19s liberty for half a century \u8211\'20\'13 a right that has safeguarded women\u8217\'20\'19s ability to participate fully and equally in society. And in renouncing this fundamental right, which it had repeatedly recognized and reaffirmed, the Court has upended the doctrine of stare decisis, a key pillar of the rule of law.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department strongly disagrees with the Court\u8217\'20\'19s decision. This decision deals a devastating blow to reproductive freedom in the United States. It will have an immediate and irreversible impact on the lives of people across the country. And it will be greatly disproportionate in its effect \u8211\'20\'13 with the greatest burdens felt by people of color and those of limited financial means.\par \par \uc2 Garland said the department would work to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  accessible, and in particular counter efforts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/07/us-mail-order-abortions-oklahoma"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to restrict access to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  drug mifepristone}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The Department strongly supports efforts by Congress to codify Americans\u8217\'20\'19 reproductive rights, which it retains the authority to do. We also support other legislative efforts to ensure access to comprehensive reproductive services. And we stand ready to work with other arms of the federal government that seek to use their lawful authorities to protect and preserve access to reproductive care. In particular, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  has approved the use of the medication Mifepristone. States may not ban Mifepristone based on disagreement with the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s expert judgment about its safety and efficacy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Protestors gathered on the steps of the supreme court after the ruling today. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t care what that vote is today. They cannot stop us. They cannot control our lives. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to do everything that we can possibly do, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to continue to organize,\u8221\'20\'1D said Representative \uc2 Maxine Waters\uc2 , a Democrat representing California\u8217\'20\'19s 43rd district.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to turn out a huge vote of women. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to see if we can get something on the ballot real soon. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to do everything we can possibly do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Exactly how did the supreme court justices vote in their decision ending the nationwide right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? While the ruling represents the successful conclusion of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement\u8217\'20\'19s quest to overturn Roe v Wade, the exact breakdown of the vote elaborates on some of the differences among the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative justices.\par \par \uc2 At issue in the case, Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/explainer-mississippi-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Mississippi law}}}\uc2  that banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks gestation. The justices ruled both on that law\u8217\'20\'19s validity, and the Roe v Wade precedent. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scotusblog.com/2022/06/supreme-court-overturns-constitutional-right-to-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SCOTUSblog has a breakdown looking at how they each voted}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The vote to overturn Roe was 5-4, with Justices \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 , and Amy Coney Barrett joining Alito\u8217\'20\'19s opinion. Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  filed a separate opinion, agreeing with the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to uphold the Mississippi law but arguing that the court should not have decided the broader question of whether the Constitution protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all. The court\u8217\'20\'19s three liberals, Justices \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2 , \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2 , and Elena Kagan, filed a joint dissent.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s decision has shocked many, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/chief-justice-roberts-abortion-leak-investigation-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it\u8217\'20\'19s no surprise}}}\uc2  and hundreds of protesters descended on the supreme court building in Washington DC within minutes of the decision\u8217\'20\'19s publication, chanting, \u8220\'20\'1CWe trust women, we won\u8217\'20\'19t go back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There are plans for protests in cities across the country \u8211\'20\'13 and world \u8211\'20\'13 including in New York, where pro-choice activists, human rights groups and trade unions will gather in Washington Square Park in Lower Manhattan at 6.30pm. Illinois\u8217\'20\'19s governor has pledged to make the state a haven for women who need an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as have the leaders of Chicago, where a protest organized by a coalition of local groups including ACLU of Illinois, the Chicago \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund and Planned Parenthood Illinois Action is planned for 5pm at Federal Plaza.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists react outside the supreme court in Washington on Friday, June 24, 2022. Photograph: Jacquelyn Martin/AP\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Abortion_RCScot/status/1540346184757288960?s=20&t=-VklrCnuuM3K79ZrtM12Sw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Expect to see protests}}}\uc2  outside US embassies and consulates in cities across the world, including in Edinburgh, Scotland, at 1pm Eastern time (6pm local time)\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will address the nation at 12.30pm eastern time following the supreme court decision overturning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, the White House has announced.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of his speech, take a look at the the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s map detailing where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  can likely still be accessed, and where it will no longer be available:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/05/abortion-deserts-clinics-access-closed-map"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  deserts: America\u8217\'20\'19s new geography of access to care \u8211\'20\'13 mapped}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Just how big of a deal is the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling? To Lawrence Gostin, faculty director of the O\u8217\'20\'19Neill Institute for National and Global Health Law at Georgetown Law, its decision to strike down the 49-year old Roe ruling is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe single greatest reversal of women\u8217\'20\'19s rights in American history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 From his statement:\par \par \uc2 This Court\u8217\'20\'19s blatant disregard for settled precedent, along with the previously leaked draft opinion, undermines the Court\u8217\'20\'19s legitimacy and America\u8217\'20\'19s trust in the federal judiciary. But even more troubling are the impacts on women who live in states banning or restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. We are going to see \u8216\'20\'18Two Americas,\u8217\'20\'19 one that protects women\u8217\'20\'19s health and rights and one where women will have few, if any, reproductive rights. The Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s decision will widen racial and health disparities across America. The Supreme Court has made the United States an outlier among peer countries that safeguard the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Tarah Demant, interim national director for programs, advocacy and government affairs at \uc2 Amnesty International USA\uc2 , said the ruling marked a \u8220\'20\'1Cgrim milestone\u8221\'20\'1D in US history:\par \par \uc2 People will be forced to give birth. They\u8217\'20\'19ll be forced to seek unsafe abortions. This is the outcome of a decades-long campaign to control the bodies of women, girls, and people who can become pregnant. And it paves the way for unprecedented state legislation to criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as well as other bills that will aim to strip human rights from people in the United States, including the potential for bills that will affect access to birth control, gender, and marriage equality as well as other anti-discrimination laws... Regardless of what the Supreme Court says, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains a human right and states all over the world are still obligated to uphold that right.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Missouri is claiming to be the first state in the country to end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  entirely, with an opinion from attorney general Eric Schmitt:\par \par \uc2 enltr?? BREAKING ?? Following the \uc2 SCOTUS\uc2  ruling overturning Roe v. Wade, Missouri has just become the first in the country to effectively end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with our AG opinion signed moments ago. This is a monumental day for the sanctity of life. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Jphy72R4rq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Jphy72R4rq}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Attorney General Eric Schmitt (@AGEricSchmitt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AGEricSchmitt/status/1540338042413944832?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Schmitt, a Republican, has also made a lengthy post about his efforts to stop the procedure:\par \par \uc2 enltrTHREAD: Today is a historic day, but we also remember over 60 million innocent lives lost. There was a lot of work behind the scenes before we achieved this incredible victory. Here are some of our efforts to protect all, including the unborn. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rI8GTLgr5r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rI8GTLgr5r}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Attorney General Eric Schmitt (@AGEricSchmitt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AGEricSchmitt/status/1540339949550981121?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Conservative groups are cheering the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision overturning Roe v Wade as the successful culmination of decades of work to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Jeanne Mancini, president of March for Life, put it:\par \par \uc2 For nearly fifty years, the Supreme Court has imposed an unpopular and extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy on our nation, but as the annual March for Life gives witness to, Roe\u8217\'20\'19s allowance of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -on-demand, up-until-birth has never represented where most Americans stand on life! Today, the ability to determine whether and when to limit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was returned to the American people who have every right to enact laws like Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s which protect mothers and unborn babies after 15 weeks - when they have fully formed noses, can suck their thumb, and feel pain.\par \par \uc2 President and CEO \uc2 Brooke Rollins\uc2  of the America First Policy Institute noted the role of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who appointed three of the conservative justices whose votes were crucial in the ruling:\par \par \uc2 It should also be noted that this historic day for democracy, nearly 50 years in the making, would not have been possible without the leadership and commitment to life of President \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 . Thank you, Mr. President!\par \par \uc2 Another key player in laying the groundwork for Roe to fall was \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , who as top Senate Republican in 2016 stopped then-president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  from installing a justice of his choosing for a vacant seat on the supreme court. Trump ended up filling that opening with \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , who voted to strike down Roe.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what McConnell had to say about the ruling:\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s landmark ruling in Dobbs is courageous and correct. This is an historic victory for the Constitution and for the most vulnerable in our society.\par \par \uc2 For 50 years, states have been unable to enact even modest protections for unborn children. More than 90% of Europe restricts \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand after 15 weeks, but every state in America has been forced to allow it more than a month past that, after a baby can feel pain, yawn, stretch, and suck his or her thumb. Judicial activists declared that every state had to handle \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  like China and North Korea and no state could handle it like France or Germany.\par \par \uc2 Not anymore. Now the American people get their voice back.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  has condemned the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling overturning Roe v Wade, calling it an attack on \u8220\'20\'1Cthe essential freedoms of millions of Americans\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, the Supreme Court not only reversed nearly 50 years of precedent, it relegated the most intensely personal decision someone can make to the whims of politicians and ideologues\u8212\'20\'14attacking the essential freedoms of millions of Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Barack Obama (@BarackObama) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BarackObama/status/1540340642848690176?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAcross the country, states have already passed bills restricting choice. If you're looking for ways to respond, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PPFA?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PPFA}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/USOWomen?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @USOWomen}}}\uc2 , and many other groups have been sounding the alarm on this issue for years\u8212\'20\'14and will continue to be on the front lines of this fight. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PpXBEcbL2S"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PpXBEcbL2S}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Barack Obama (@BarackObama) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BarackObama/status/1540340648972279813?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrFor more than a month, we\u8217\'20\'19ve known this day was coming\u8212\'20\'14but that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t make it any less devastating. Here are my thoughts from when we first saw the draft ruling: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aegHc7AoTm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/aegHc7AoTm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Barack Obama (@BarackObama) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BarackObama/status/1540340651610497031?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is expected to address the nation:\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden has been prepared to address the nation when the Supreme Court ruling on Roe v. Wade came down. It remains to be seen when he\u8217\'20\'19ll do so but the White House has been bracing for this decision, meeting with stakeholders and preparing their own actions.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1540339023046230018?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 The ruling overturning Roe v Wade is the culmination of decades of work by conservatives \u8211\'20\'13 assisted by a president named \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/jessica-glenza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jessica Glenza}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 The short version of how Americans lost their right to terminate a pregnancy might be summed up in one name: Trump.\par \par \uc2 The real estate tycoon and reality-TV star first shocked the world by winning the US presidency, then rewarded his base by confirming three supreme court justices to a nine-member bench, thus rebalancing the court to lean conservative for a generation to come.\par \par \uc2 That short road led to Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, an opinion released this week in which supreme court justices voted 6-3 to overturn the landmark case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , which in 1973 granted a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/24/how-americans-lost-federal-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How Americans lost their right to abortions: a victory for conservatives, 50 years in the making}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 With the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling overturning Roe v Wade, conservatives have struck a major blow against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the United States. The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/jessica-glenza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jessica Glenza}}}\uc2  breaks down what it means:\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has ruled there is no constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the United States, upending a precedent set nearly 50 years ago in the landmark {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  case \u8211\'20\'13 a rare reversal of long-settled law that will fracture the foundations of modern reproductive rights in America.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling came in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/explainer-mississippi-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pivotal case}}}\uc2  Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, in which the last \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Mississippi opposed the state\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks and overturn Roe in the process.\par \par \uc2 The reversal of the 1973 opinion will again allow individual US states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/what-states-abortion-clinics-access-trigger-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26 states}}}\uc2  are expected to do so immediately or as soon as practicable.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court overturns \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights, upending Roe v Wade}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court overturns Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has overturned Roe v Wade, ending nearly a half-century of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the United States.\par \par \uc2 enltrTHE SUPREME COURT HAS OVERTURNED ROE V. WADE, ELIMINATING THE CONSTITUTIONAL RIGHT TO \b \highlight22\uc2 ABORTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZNYRs3QnpJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ZNYRs3QnpJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1540336880188801026?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The decision split along ideological lines, with the six conservative justices voting for it and the three liberals dissenting.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court will issue its first opinion of the day in one minute, at 10am eastern time. Assuming there\u8217\'20\'19s more than one, subsequent decisions will come in 10-minute intervals.\par \par \uc2 Follow the US politics live blog for updates, or check out the opinions on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 court\u8217\'20\'19s website}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 If the supreme court issues a ruling today that weakens the government\u8217\'20\'19s ability to regulate greenhouse gas emissions, one wonders what that would mean for places like Phoenix. As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/nina-lakhani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nina Lakhani }}}\uc2  reports, the city is struggling with the opioid epidemic, and extreme heat is making it worse:\par \par \uc2 Andy Brack was out cold with his head slumped back on the driver\u8217\'20\'19s seat of a white pickup truck, a faint blue tinge around his lips. His friend, Ellen, had called 911 after the 50-year-old lost consciousness while driving to the store.\par \par \uc2 Brack had been smoking fentanyl for two days straight, according to Ellen, who managed to stop the vehicle from crashing. It was around 4.30pm and boiling outside, almost 108F (42C), and the pickup didn\u8217\'20\'19t have air conditioning. She was doing CPR compressions when the paramedics arrived.\par \par \uc2 Unable to rouse him, the paramedics administered the drug naloxone via an injection into his upper left arm. The drug, widely known by the brand name Narcan, is an emergency treatment for opioid overdose that temporarily reverses the depressive and potentially fatal effects on the cardiovascular and respiratory systems.\par \par \uc2 Brack came to abruptly. He refused to be taken to hospital and became angry as the opioid withdrawals set-in. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sober, I need a cigarette,\u8221\'20\'1D he said to Ellen as they drove off.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/24/arizona-excessive-heat-opioid-crisis-phoenix"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A deadly combination\u8217\'20\'19: excessive heat adds to Arizona opioid epidemic\u8217\'20\'19s toll}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Another takeaway from the January 6 hearings is that a number of Republicans were worried enough about their conduct after the 2020 election to ask for pardons from Trump before he left office, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/23/republicans-election-overturn-trump-presidential-pardon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 The Republicans \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  and Mo Brooks sought a blanket pardon of members of Congress involved in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempt to overturn his defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  through lies about electoral fraud, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/23/capitol-attack-panel-trump-pressured-doj-overturn-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House January 6 committee}}}\uc2  revealed on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 A witness said Andy Biggs of Arizona, \uc2 Louie Gohmert\uc2  of Texas and Scott Perry of Pennsylvania also contacted the White House about securing pardons. The same witness, former Trump White House aide Cassidy Hutchinson, said she heard \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , an extremist from Georgia, wanted a pardon too.\par \par \uc2 The committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NikkiMcR/status/1540081340757966850?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1540082440521359364%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es2_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rollingstone.com%2Fpolitics%2Fpolitics-news%2Fmo-brooks-matt-gaetz-pardons-overturn-election-1373475%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 displayed an email}}}\uc2  written by Brooks, of Alabama, on 11 January 2021, five days after the deadly attack on the US Capitol by Trump supporters.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/23/republicans-election-overturn-trump-presidential-pardon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans who aided coup attempt sought blanket presidential pardons}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee won\u8217\'20\'19t meet for another few weeks but it\u8217\'20\'19s worth reading this story of the hearing\u8217\'20\'19s revelations and what we know about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s reaction, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Somewhere in Bedminster, New Jersey, on Thursday afternoon, it seems quite possible that an elderly man was sitting in front of a television howling with rage.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who spends summers at his Bedminster golf club, is a TV guy, a ratings guy. So the widely televised hearings of the congressional committee investigating the January 6 attack on the US Capitol {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/17/donald-trump-january-6-hearings-witch-hunt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hit him where it hurts}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former US president has reportedly been glued to them \u8211\'20\'13 and has not liked what he\u8217\'20\'19s seen. As the panel has presented a carefully crafted case against Trump as the leader of a failed coup, he is said to be livid that there is no one in the room to speak up for him.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/23/trump-january-6-hearings-allies-fallout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump feeling fallout of Capitol attack hearings as allies abandon ship}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/what-states-abortion-clinics-access-trigger-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the case in which the supreme court could overturn \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2 , is not the only one in which the justices could make a ruling that touches on a contentious issue in American society.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s also Kennedy v Bremerton School District, which deals with a football coach\u8217\'20\'19s practice of praying after games and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/sports-football-religion-prayer-washington-7490d215c8b1ead529299ac92114dbab"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could end up expanding the types of religious activities allowed at public schools}}}\uc2 . A ruling in that direction would come just days after the court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/jun/21/sonia-sotomayor-supreme-court-separation-church-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opened the door to religious schools receiving public funds}}}\uc2  in a decision that liberal justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  warned weakened the separation between church and state.\par \par \uc2 Then there\u8217\'20\'19s West Virginia v \uc2 EPA\uc2 . The justices are considering a plan announced by former president Barack Obam a to lower power plants\u8217\'20\'19 emissions \u8212\'20\'14 but which never took effect. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/feb/25/supreme-court-west-virgina-epa-nondelegation-doctrine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The fear is that}}}\uc2  the conservative majority will use the case as an opportunity to take away major regulatory powers from the government.\par \par \uc2 Finally, there\u8217\'20\'19s a case that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t affect Americans but rather people on its borders. Biden v. Texas represents the sitting president\u8217\'20\'19s attempt {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/26/biden-trump-supreme-court-remain-in-mexico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to end the \u8220\'20\'1Cremain in Mexico\u8221\'20\'1D policy}}}\uc2  implemented by his predecessor \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , which forced many asylum seekers to stay south of the border while their cases were heard.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court could today release their opinions on all of these, or none, or some combination in between.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 America braces for more conservative rulings from supreme court\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog reader. Today could be one for the history books. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court}}}\uc2  will announce more rulings at 10am eastern time, and among the cases outstanding is one in which the conservative majority is widely expected to strike down the nationwide right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  established by the Roe v Wade decision. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/chief-justice-roberts-abortion-leak-investigation-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A draft opinion that leaked last month showed}}}\uc2  the court prepared to overturn it and yesterday, the conservative bloc ruled against a New York law regulating concealed weapons in a decision expected to make it more difficult to control guns nationwide \u8211\'20\'13 a sign of the court\u8217\'20\'19s pronounced rightward drift.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 * The House of Representatives is expected to take up a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/24/senate-breakthrough-clears-way-for-toughening-us-gun-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  bipartisan gun control compromise that passed the Senate last night}}}\uc2 , and will probably approve it. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has said he is ready to sign it.\par \par \uc2 * White House press secretaryKarine Jean-Pierre briefs reporters at 2pm eastern time, though Biden has nothing public on his scheduled today.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2022/jun/24/campaign-strip-fox-news-site-of-ad-revenue"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A campaign has kicked off}}}\uc2  to deprive Fox News of ad revenue over claims that the network is \u8220\'20\'1Cworking overtime to fuel the next insurrection\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220624ei6o00236\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 atleast5(abortion)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trle